  :source-forms 1
  :current-authority-seat "INTERFACE-AND-SCHEMA-REGISTRY.sexp, file tail after the v1.8 candidate block (last preceding section header ';; § RA-JUR-NS jurisdiction namespace (candidate)' at ISR:172); the single form :ISR-V6-closure at ISR:177-180. Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:7 (source-class INTERFACE-AND-SCHEMA-REGISTRY__define-invariant :source-count 1 :status DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE :batch DDI-4). File role CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT via classification-rule R-010 (classification-rules.sexp:48-50)."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "NEW:invariants.sexp — one-seat reason: the 92 define-invariant forms of the six registries (ISR 1, SR 2, V1.5 22, V1.6 21, V1.7 23, V1.8 23; classes.md rows 3,8,13,26,37,50) are ONE concept ('a named normative constraint on the architecture') and today have six file seats; putting them in an existing module would attach them to a module whose concept is different (interfaces-and-types = types/components; seats = seat universe) and would create a second concept inside that module. The two existing candidates are both worse: files-and-roles.sexp and deferred-imports.sexp are GENERATED artefacts (generation-order.sexp:38-41), so hand-authored facts cannot live there; rationale-references.sexp is hand-authored and could hold a POINTER (:doc :anchor) but cannot hold the text or the enforcing-law binding. Cost: a NEW *.sexp under ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/ is auto-classified CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT by classification-rule R-008 (classification-rules.sexp:39-41) and auto-pinned by build_root.py:57 (directory listing), so ROOT.sexp :module-count 14 (ROOT.sexp:12) becomes 15 and every module SHA is re-derived (law L7)."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "NEW fact type `invariant` :id-space TOKEN-SPACE :required (source-file source-line text) :optional (enforced-by scope-subsystem status) :types ((source-file STRING) (source-line INTEGER) (text STRING) (enforced-by SYMBOL) (scope-subsystem SYMBOL) (status SYMBOL)) :enum ((enforced-by law-id) (status invariant-status)) :ref ((scope-subsystem subsystem)). Flattening rule: the form is docstring-only (one keyword id + one prose STRING, ISR:177-180) so the TEXT is already an L1-legal value; but the docstring carries FOUR independent clauses ('defined here exactly once', 'with an owner and a definition seat', 'no adapter-specific (vendor) type is a canonical interface', 'no interface has two owners', 'referenced-but-undefined => architecture-gate FAIL' — ISR:178-180), of which two are already laws (L2, L3) and one has no enforcement anywhere in the model, so a one-fact import silently mixes enforced and unenforced clauses. Alternative flattening: `invariant` + `invariant-clause` (:invariant ref, :ordinal INTEGER, :text STRING, :enforced-by law-id or NONE). Id rendering: keyword ids (`:V5I-01`, `:SR-V6-one-seat`, …) are not TOKEN-SPACE ids — TOKEN excludes ':' (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:41,17) — so a colon-stripping id-rendering convention must be declared once for all 92 define-invariant forms (orchestrator-notes.md N12) -> ISR-V6-closure. L1 permits only quoted string / integer / bare plain symbol [A-Za-z0-9_.+/-]+ — no keywords, no nested lists, no NIL (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6)."
  :owner "UNKNOWN — the form carries no :owner and no subsystem governs 'architecture governance' (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:35-127 has no such subsystem; subsystems.sexp:5-30 has none either). The dossier records the same: owner_subsystem.id = UNKNOWN (dossier-INTERFACE-AND-SCHEMA-REGISTRY.sexp/dossier.json, class define-invariant). Not invented here."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — `writer` is a field of `store` only (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:155-158) and this class creates no store. Imported facts would be authored by hand in the target module (cf. interfaces-and-types.sexp:2 'thereafter EDIT HERE'); rationale-references.sexp has no generator (it is absent from the gen-artifact universe, generation-order.sexp:38-61)."
  :classification "PUBLIC — governance prose over the whole interface universe; no private member. Evidence: the form quantifies over all 60 define-interface forms (ISR:11-175), of which 6 are PRIVATE types in the model (interfaces-and-types.sexp:24,41,44,51,58,59) — it CONSTRAINS private types but carries no private datum, so importing it does not create a public->private edge under L5 (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:47,164-170)."
  :dependencies ("DECISION: the `invariant` fact family (shape, module, one-seat policy) — shared prerequisite of classes 1,4,5,9,12,14 (92 forms) [schema dependency]" "DECISION: the keyword-id rendering convention (colon strip) — shared with all 92 invariant forms [id-space dependency, orchestrator-notes.md N12]" "EXISTING model facts: laws L2 and L3 already mechanize two of the four clauses (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:34-36 define-unique; :164-170 consumes closed refs; falsifier K14 vc:152-154 'resolves to no declared subsystem') [law dependency, not a fact reference]" "NOT-A-DEPENDENCY (verified): dag.json records 0 out-edges and 0 in-edges for this class — it references no other source class by symbol and no source class references it")
  :consumers ("NONE in the canonical model: grep of the 14 modules for 'ISR-V6-closure' = 0 hits; rationale-references.sexp:3-5 anchors RAT-V6I-17/RAT-ONE-SEAT/RAT-WP-HONESTY at SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp, never at ISR" "legacy: V1.6-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh:172-181 (V6S6/V6S7/V6S8) — HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:440), 'never a blocking or sufficient acceptance gate' (LEGACY-AUDIT-DISPOSITION.md:10)" "build_deferred.py -> the ledger row deferred-imports.sexp:7 (the only mechanical consumer)" "concept siblings that restate it: SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:136 :SR-V6-one-seat; V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp:348 :V6I-17-one-source-of-truth (names ISR at :350); V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp:158 :V6I-REF-single-source-of-truth; V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp:26 :RA-I-5-one-seat-per-concept; V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp:20 :V8I-03-one-seat")
  :identity-version-rule "ONLY-VERSION by id: the name :ISR-V6-closure occurs in exactly one registry (ISR:177; classes.md row 3; version-chains.md lists no chain for it). BUT the CONCEPT is a five-seat family with divergent text and divergent scope (ISR:177-180 interfaces; SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:136-140 subsystem seats; V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp:348-352 generated tables; V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp:26-28 concepts; V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp:20-22 concepts+registries) — under the model's own one-seat law that family is SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT with no declared winner. No winner is picked here."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION — becomes IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL (1 `invariant` fact + 4 `invariant-clause` facts) once (a) the invariant fact family exists, (b) the id-rendering convention is fixed, and (c) the family question (retire-as-subsumed-by-L2/L3 vs import) is answered. If the answer is 'retire', the rule becomes SKIP-WITH-PROOF and the proof must name which law subsumes each of the four clauses — for clause 3 ('no adapter-specific vendor type is a canonical interface') no such law exists (grep of the 14 modules for ONNX / vendor / adapter = 0 in a law or check position), so SKIP-WITH-PROOF is NOT currently provable for the whole form."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "HIGH at concept level, NONE at id level. Importing this form alone creates the sixth statement of 'one seat per concept' — inside the model whose L2 already IS that law (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:34-36, 106-107, 308, 319-321) — i.e. the import would itself violate the invariant it imports. Second risk: the imported text would become a prose seat competing with the mechanised law, with nothing declaring which wins (dossier-INTERFACE-AND-SCHEMA-REGISTRY A12; dossier-SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY A12-SR-ONE-SEAT-INVARIANT-FAMILY names seven such forms)."
  :requirement "UNKNOWN — no requirement id is attached to this form at source and none of the model's 24 `requirement` facts (rtw:5-28) covers architecture governance. TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md registers no row for :ISR-V6-closure (the ISR rows it carries are per-interface). A NEW requirement would have to be minted, which is itself the open question of where the requirement universe is seated (orchestrator-notes.md N1/N8)."
  :invariant "Model laws L1 (string value legality, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6), L2 (one id owned by one fact type, :106-107), L7 (exact module/hash universe, ROOT.sexp:12-27) if a NEW module is added. Source invariant: the form IS the invariant; its own clauses map to L2 ('exactly once', 'no two owners') and L3 ('referenced-but-undefined => FAIL'), with clause 3 (vendor types) unmapped."
  :qualification-test "NEW — QT-DDI4-ISR-CLOSURE: no existing model `test` fact covers it (rtw:30-50 lists 21 test ids, none about invariants). Executable one-liner: `python3 SEXP-READER.py --model . | jq -e '[.facts[]|select(.type==\"invariant\")]|length==92'` after import — i.e. the invariant universe has exactly the 92 source forms, and a companion property-family `PF-INVARIANT-CLAUSE-LAW` asserting that every `invariant-clause` :enforced-by value is either a declared law-id or the explicit token NONE (so an unenforced clause is declared, never silent)."
  :falsifier "APPEND to the target module `(fact invariant ISR-V6-closure :source-file \"INTERFACE-AND-SCHEMA-REGISTRY.sexp\" :source-line 177 :text \"…\" :enforced-by :L2)` — must be REJECTED on BOTH paths: kernel-reason 'illegal value kind', checker-reason 'MALFORMED-FACT' (the keyword value :L2; exact precedent X27 vc:172-174). Second falsifier, REPLACE `:enforced-by L2` with `:enforced-by L9` — must be REJECTED as outside the law-id enum (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:64), checker-reason 'L1'. Third, APPEND a second `(fact invariant ISR-V6-closure …)` — must be REJECTED as a duplicate id (L2, cf. FX-L2-DUPLICATE-STORE vc:28-29)."
  :rollback "Delete the imported facts; delete `invariant`/`invariant-clause` (and the `invariant-status` enum) from MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp and move :version \"4\" (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:37) — the schema version is cross-checked against ROOT.sexp:9 and is itself falsified (X74-X76 vc:354-372 per orchestrator notes); delete invariants.sexp if it was created and re-run build_root.py so ROOT.sexp:12-27 returns to 14 modules and the original digests; build_deferred.py then regenerates deferred-imports.sexp:7 as DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT :batch DDI-4. The source registry is never edited: authority stays AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE until the batch is independently reviewed (deferred-imports.sexp:73-76)."
  :batch-reason "DDI-4 because build_deferred.py:101 maps the head `define-invariant` to DDI-4 ('normative invariants / rules / prose', :108); the ledger reason string (deferred-imports.sexp:7) is the generic per-batch template, not a per-class judgement. AGREES — with the caveat that there is NO mechanical dependency evidence in either direction: dag.json records 0 in-edges and 0 out-edges for this class, so its placement is a naming convention, not a derived order."
  :decision-kind "SCHEMA_EXTENSION"
  :decision-question "What is the `invariant` fact family (fields, module, id rendering), and is :ISR-V6-closure imported as text or retired as subsumed by L2+L3 — noting clause 3 (no vendor type is a canonical interface) is subsumed by nothing in the model? (Recorded as UNKNOWN at source: the dossier states the creator's intent is not written down anywhere.)"
  :adjudication-items ("A11 (ISR dossier): no invariant fact type; keyword ids violate TOKEN-SPACE; clause 3 has no enforcing check" "A12 (ISR dossier) = A12-SR-ONE-SEAT-INVARIANT-FAMILY (SR dossier): five (SR dossier counts seven) prose forms state 'one seat per concept' — ISR:177, SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:136, V1.6:348, V1.7:26, V1.7:337, V1.8:20, V1.8:296" "ADJ-MX4-INV-SEAT (new, spans classes 1/4/5/9/12/14): the 92 define-invariant forms need ONE declared module and ONE declared policy (latest-only / all-as-history / pointer-only) before any of the six classes can be imported; today the model anchors two of the chains at SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp (rationale-references.sexp:4-5) and none at V1.8" "ADJ-MX4-ANCHOR-UNCHECKED (new, spans every pointer-style import): no counted check opens a `rationale` :doc and greps its :anchor — RAT-PUBPRIV (rationale-references.sexp:7) points at an anchor string that occurs 0 times in deployment/LAWMAX-THREAT-MODEL.md and passes every gate (orchestrator-notes.md N17)")
  :topological-position 36 :atomic-groups ()
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "hash-pinned model fact in a module under ROOT.sexp composition (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:170-184 root-composition/load-facts; L7) | invariant: L7 exact module/hash universe (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:64 law-id L7) | fallback: existing `rationale` pointer fact (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:182-184; pattern rationale-references.sexp:3-7) — no text copy" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart "NOT-APPLICABLE (a gate failure is a kernel violation record `v!` ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:25, not a signalled condition)" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE (registry forms are DATA read under *read-eval* nil (deferred-imports.sexp:4; ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:56; safe-read.lisp:152-165) — never a macro expanded over the registry file)" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE" :package-asdf-boundary "NOT-APPLICABLE" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE" :compile-time-validation "kernel laws already evaluated at gate time over the ISR-derived type/component/consumes facts (deferred-imports.sexp:6 maps-to): L2 duplicate seat / id under two types (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:124,126; law2-unique :190 over define-unique data ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:34-36) + L3 closed refs (law3-closed-refs :200) | invariant: :ISR-V6-closure clauses 'DEFINED here exactly once with an owner' and 'Referenced-but-undefined ⇒ FAIL' (ISR:178-180) | fallback: none needed for those clauses (already mechanized — dossier A11/A12); the 'no adapter-specific (vendor) type is canonical' clause has NO mechanism: `type` has fields owner-subsystem/classification/consumer-role only (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:148-152) — UNKNOWN whether an origin enum is wanted" :runtime-validation "NOT-APPLICABLE" :python-in-cl-risk "YES — a naive import writes `(fact invariant ISR-V6-closure :text \"...\")`: a string blob that duplicates two laws already mechanized (L2/L3) and invites a Python regex 'check' of the prose. CL-native alternative: no text fact at all — a `rationale` pointer (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:182-184; rationale-references.sexp:4 RAT-ONE-SEAT pattern) and, for the one unmechanized clause (vendor type), a NEW closed enum field on `type` (e.g. :origin CANONICAL|ADAPTER declared with define-enum ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:18) that the generic kernel enum path (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:152-155) validates — never a per-invariant checker." :future-freedom "NONE — restates L2/L3 over the interface universe. The vendor clause PROTECTS S20/V8I-02 (adapters stay replaceable, V1.8:17-19) provided it is mechanized as an origin enum, not as a closed list of vendor names (which would freeze the adapter roster). No S04/S19/JTMS constraint.")
