(ddi-class SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY__define-wp-purpose
  :batch DDI-4 :source-file "SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp" :fact-class "define-wp-purpose" :source-count 16 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms (("WP-00" :line 15 :sha16 "eb218434677c55fe") ("WP-01" :line 16 :sha16 "5065e11e66c162dc") ("WP-02" :line 17 :sha16 "a880c58b4d9541ba") ("WP-03" :line 18 :sha16 "0f613bd3214041cd") ("WP-04" :line 19 :sha16 "5dadac926e47d353") ("WP-05" :line 20 :sha16 "01130836597f2782") ("WP-06" :line 21 :sha16 "c2d52bc4b60320b0") ("WP-07" :line 22 :sha16 "99e6ae6bb0f351bc") ("WP-08" :line 23 :sha16 "1bc9a29d9d9995b5") ("WP-09" :line 24 :sha16 "cce56cd3f4dddcaa") ("WP-10" :line 25 :sha16 "71a18eba12cfea96") ("WP-11" :line 26 :sha16 "1501a2fc412e0337") ("WP-12" :line 27 :sha16 "b5539ce022277683") ("WP-13" :line 28 :sha16 "13f66e65771dd6ff") ("WP-14" :line 29 :sha16 "2b2d7412d0dac9e6") ("FUTURE_BOOK_REVISION" :line 30 :sha16 "9e5a579c41684dce"))
  :source-file "SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp"
  :source-forms 16
  :current-authority-seat "SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp section ';; ---- Implementation-Book Work-Packet purposes (EVIDENCE: IMPLEMENTATION-BOOK/WORK-PACKETS/WP-NN.md:1/5/6) ----' (header SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:11-14), forms L15-L30 (WP-00..WP-14 at :15-29 plus the sentinel FUTURE_BOOK_REVISION at :30). The header itself declares this the seat: 'This is the audit's WP-assignment cross-check source of truth' (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:12) and 'Grounded, not asserted' (:14). Grounding evidence: IMPLEMENTATION-BOOK/WORK-PACKETS/WP-NN.md:5 (15 tracked files, AUTHORED_NORMATIVE_PROSE, files-and-roles.sexp:378-392). Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:12 (:source-count 16 :status DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE :batch DDI-4)."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp (EXISTING) — the `wp` fact type is already seated there (rtw:52-65, 14 facts) together with `requirement`, `test` and `req-map`; a second module for WP purposes would split one concept across two files, which is exactly what the source's own :SR-V6-one-seat forbids (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:136-140). CONDITIONAL: the module is hand-authored ('thereafter EDIT HERE', rtw:2) so it can receive facts, but its current content was DERIVED from a different class (define-subsystem :future-wp, build_model.py:73-78) — importing define-wp-purpose into it gives `wp` a SECOND ORIGIN unless that derivation is retired in the same change (orchestrator-notes.md N2)."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "EXTEND the existing `wp` fact type (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:175 — today :required () :optional () :types (), i.e. a bare id) with :optional (purpose) :types ((purpose STRING)); the closed field set (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:9-13) makes this a schema change, not an added key. PLUS a NEW fact type `wp-owns` :id-space TOKEN-SPACE :required (wp requirement) :types ((wp SYMBOL) (requirement SYMBOL)) :ref ((wp wp) (requirement requirement)). Flattening rule: :owns is a STRING encoding a list of ids AND RANGES ('R-01..R-13 R-132', SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:16; 'R-57..R-70 R-89 R-90 R-92 R-94 R-125..R-128 R-130 R-134', :21) — a range is not a value kind under L1 (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6), so each range must be EXPANDED into one `wp-owns` fact per requirement id and each expanded id must exist as a `requirement` fact. That expansion mints roughly 130 requirement ids against the 24 that exist today (rtw:5-28) — the single largest fact-count consequence in DDI-4. Id normalisation is required first: WP-00 writes 'R-1..R-6' unpadded (:15) where WP-01 writes 'R-01..R-13' padded (:16) — two spellings of one id space (A17-SR-R-ID-FORMAT). The sentinel FUTURE_BOOK_REVISION (:30) carries :owns \"none\", which must become an ABSENCE (zero wp-owns facts) or an explicit token, not the literal string 'none'."
  :owner "UNKNOWN — no form carries an owner; the class is cross-cutting and the source header attributes it to the Implementation Book (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:11; files-and-roles.sexp:378-392). The model's `wp` fact type has no owner field at all (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:175). Dossier records the same value ('none (cross-cutting; owner is the Implementation Book)'). Not invented here."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — `writer` is a field of `store` only (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:155-158). rtw is hand-authored after migration (rtw:2), so the writer question is 'who edits the module', not a store authority."
  :classification "UNKNOWN — no form carries a classification and `wp` has no classification field (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:175). By content the 16 packets are PUBLIC design prose, but the model never asserts a classification for a wp and L5 (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:47, 164-170) applies to types/consumers, not to work packets. Reported as UNKNOWN rather than guessed."
  :dependencies ("FIRST: `requirement` facts for the whole R-universe named by :owns (~130 ids across SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:15-29; TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md carries 134 distinct R-nnn ids per orchestrator-notes.md N8) — otherwise every `wp-owns` fact is a dangling typed reference [L3 closed-reference dependency]" "FIRST: the requirement-id normalisation decision (padded vs unpadded, A17-SR-R-ID-FORMAT) [id-space dependency]" "FIRST: the sentinel-token decision — FUTURE_BOOK_REVISION (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:30, model wp rtw:53) vs FUTURE_IMPLEMENTATION_BOOK_PACKET_REQUIRED (V1.7:394-399, V1.8:315-319, ISR:112,115,129,138,142,145,160,164,175) vs DEFERRED (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:110,113,116,126; model wp rtw:52, which has NO define-wp-purpose at source) vs 'FUTURE_BOOK' (TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:347,391,394,397) [enum/id dependency, shared with classes 13 and 15]" "FIRST (authority): retire the derivation that currently mints `wp` facts from define-subsystem :future-wp (build_model.py:73-78 — HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, classification-rules.sexp:15-17) or this import creates a second origin for one fact family [one-seat dependency, orchestrator-notes.md N2]" "NOT a dependency of anything earlier: this class references only requirement ids that live outside all six registries (dag.json records 0 out-edges for it)")
  :consumers ("IMPORTED SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-subsystem — 29 symbol references (dag.json class_edges 'SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp define-subsystem -> SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp define-wp-purpose': 29; examples SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:100 S20 -> :22 WP-07, :104 S21 -> :15 WP-00, :119 S25 -> :30 FUTURE_BOOK_REVISION)" "IMPORTED INTERFACE-AND-SCHEMA-REGISTRY define-interface — 10 references (dag.json; examples ISR:117 ClarifiedInterpretation/1 -> WP-08, ISR:130 MultiCommitment/1 -> WP-06)" "DDI-1 V1.8-SCHEMAS define-write-authority — 7 references (V1.8:286-292 -> WP-03/06/01/13/11); DDI-1 V1.7 define-write-authority — 7 references (V1.7:327-333)" "DDI-2 V1.6-SCHEMAS define-reference — 6 references (V1.6:92,96,127,131,143,147)" "DDI-4 siblings: SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-invariant 8 refs (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:139-145); V1.7 define-wp-reconciliation 10 refs (V1.7:379-399); V1.8 define-wp-reconciliation 10 refs (V1.8:303-319); V1.6/V1.7/V1.8 define-invariant 1 ref each" "CANONICAL MODEL (live): 12 of the 16 ids are already `wp` facts (rtw:54-65) and are reference targets of 29 `req-map` :wp values (rtw:67-95) and of 6 `seat` :packet values (seats.sexp:77,79,81,83,85,87) — the model already depends on this class's id vocabulary" "legacy: V1.6-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh:192-202 (V6S11) and V1.8-VERIFY.py:821 — both HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:440,453)")
  :identity-version-rule "LIVE-REFERENCE-TARGET + ONLY-VERSION. ONLY-VERSION: define-wp-purpose exists in no other registry (classes.md row 5; version-chains.md). LIVE-REFERENCE-TARGET: 12 of its ids are already model `wp` facts (rtw:54-65) pointed at by 29 req-map facts and 6 seat :packet fields, so the model's L6 closure (requirement->seat->test->WP) already stands on this deferred class's vocabulary. The two universes DIVERGE: WP-00 (:15), WP-05 (:20) and WP-10 (:25) exist at source and are NOT model facts; `wp DEFERRED` (rtw:52) is a model fact with NO define-wp-purpose at source (admitted only by prose SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:139 and by legacy audit V1.6-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh:194). Import therefore cannot be a pure add: 16 source forms vs 14 model facts with 3 in and 1 out."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION — the class cannot be imported while `wp` has two origins. Once the derivation is retired the rule becomes MERGE-INTO-EXISTING-FACT for the 12 overlapping ids (add :purpose to the existing `wp` facts), IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL for WP-00/WP-05/WP-10 (3 new `wp` facts) plus ~130 new `requirement` facts and the `wp-owns` edges, and a separate ruling on `wp DEFERRED` (a model fact with no source form: either SKIP-WITH-PROOF that it is a disposition token rather than a WP, or a new define-wp-purpose is required at source)."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "HIGHEST in DDI-4. (i) Two origins for one fact family: `wp` facts derived from define-subsystem :future-wp (build_model.py:73-78) vs define-wp-purpose as the declared cross-check source of truth (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:12) — orchestrator-notes.md N2. (ii) Three competing seats for WP ASSIGNMENT: :owns here (requirement-keyed), req-map (subsystem-keyed, rtw:67-95), define-wp-reconciliation (concept-keyed, V1.7:379, V1.8:303) — and they already disagree: LEGAL_IR -> WP-03 (V1.8:307) vs LegalIR/1 owner S04 -> WP-08 (rtw:70). (iii) The :owns ranges CONTRADICT existing req-map rows: S12 maps R-118 to WP-12 (rtw:78) while WP-14 owns R-112..R-118 (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:29); S13/S15 map R-124 to WP-12/WP-13 (rtw:79,81) while WP-11 owns R-119..R-124 (:26) — A2-SR-WP-OWNS-CONFLICT. Importing :owns makes three live model facts contradict a fourth. (iv) S20/S21 composite WPs were SPLIT at migration into 5 req-map rows citing :SR-V6-one-seat as the governing invariant (MODEL-MIGRATION-CONFLICT-LEDGER.md:25-26) — that invariant is itself in DDI-4 (class 4)."
  :requirement "The class IS the requirement-ownership statement, but no model `requirement` fact covers it and none of the ~130 ids it names exists as a fact except the 24 at rtw:5-28. UNKNOWN which requirement authorises the import; TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md is the R-universe seat (134 ids, orchestrator-notes.md N8) and is AUTHORED_NORMATIVE_PROSE, not a model input."
  :invariant "Source invariants :SR-V6-one-seat (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:136-140, 'every :future-wp token resolves to a define-wp-purpose WP id') and :SR-V6-wp-honesty (:141-145) — both in class 4 of this same batch. Model laws: L3 (wp-owns.requirement must resolve to a declared requirement), L6 (requirement->seat->test->WP closure — today satisfied by sentinel WPs, A4-SR-SENTINEL-WPS), L1 (the range strings are not values)."
  :qualification-test "NEW — QT-DDI4-WP-OWNS: no model `test` fact covers WP ownership (rtw:30-50). Executable one-liner: after import, `for every req-map R: assert exists wp-owns(R.wp, R.requirement)` — i.e. the WP a subsystem is mapped to must be the WP that owns that subsystem's requirement. Run today against the source strings this test FAILS for S12/S13/S15 (rtw:78,79,81 vs SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:26,29), which is the point: the test is what makes A2-SR-WP-OWNS-CONFLICT visible instead of silent."
  :falsifier "APPEND to requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp `(fact wp-owns WP-01__R-999 :wp WP-01 :requirement R-999)` — must be REJECTED on both paths: kernel-reason 'resolves to no declared requirement', checker-reason 'L3' (exact precedent FX-L3-DANGLING-WP vc:30-31). REPLACE `:wp WP-01` with `:wp WP-00` before WP-00 is minted — must be REJECTED for the same law. APPEND `(fact wp WP-01 :purpose \"duplicate\")` — must be REJECTED as a duplicate id under L2 (precedent FX-L2-DUPLICATE-STORE vc:28-29). CHECK-class: mutate the :purpose of one wp so it no longer matches WP-NN.md:5 and require the new grounding check to name it (there is no such check today — that absence is itself the finding, cf. no counted check opens a `rationale` :doc and greps its :anchor — RAT-PUBPRIV (rationale-references.sexp:7) points at an anchor string that occurs 0 times in deployment/LAWMAX-THREAT-MODEL.md and passes every gate (orchestrator-notes.md N17))."
  :rollback "Delete the `wp-owns` facts, the ~130 minted `requirement` facts and the WP-00/05/10 `wp` facts; strip :purpose from the 12 merged `wp` facts; revert the `wp` fact-type declaration in MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:175 and move the schema :version (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:37 / ROOT.sexp:9); re-run build_root.py (module digests) and build_deferred.py (deferred-imports.sexp:12 returns to DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT :batch DDI-4). NOTE the rollback is NOT symmetric if the define-subsystem derivation was retired in the same change: restoring it means re-running a HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE program (build_model.py, classification-rules.sexp:15-17), which the model declares 'not on the live path' — so the derivation retirement needs its own rollback statement."
  :batch-reason "DDI-4 because build_deferred.py:103 maps the head `define-wp-purpose` to DDI-4; the ledger reason (deferred-imports.sexp:12) is the generic template. DISAGREES — the dependency evidence contradicts last placement, three ways: (1) two IMPORTED classes already reference it 39 times (define-subsystem 29, define-interface 10) and dag.json lists both as order violations (from_rank 0 -> to_rank 4); (2) two DDI-1 classes (V1.7/V1.8 define-write-authority, 7 refs each) and one DDI-2 class (V1.6 define-reference, 6 refs) reference it — order violations from_rank 0/1/2 -> to_rank 4; (3) the LIVE model already carries 12 of its ids as `wp` facts consumed by 29 req-map and 6 seat facts, i.e. the model's L6 closure stands on a class scheduled to be imported LAST. On dependency order this class belongs at the FRONT of DDI-1, not at the end of DDI-4."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "Which seat owns WP assignment — define-wp-purpose (:owns, requirement-keyed, declared source of truth at SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:12), req-map (subsystem-keyed, rtw:67-95, derived from :future-wp), or define-wp-reconciliation (concept-keyed, V1.8:303) — and, once chosen, is the define-subsystem-derived `wp` universe retired? Sub-questions: one sentinel token for 'no WP owns this'; whether WP-00/05/10 enter the model; whether `wp DEFERRED` (a model fact with no source form) is legitimate; and how ~130 requirement ids enter a model that today holds 24."
  :adjudication-items ("A2-SR-WP-OWNS-CONFLICT (SR dossier): S12 R-118->WP-12 vs WP-14 :owns R-112..R-118; S13/S15 R-124->WP-12/WP-13 vs WP-11 :owns R-119..R-124 (rtw:78,79,81 vs SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:26,29)" "A3-SR-COMPOSITE-WP-UNOWNED (SR dossier): S20/S21 composite WP tokens assign WPs to requirements no :owns covers; split at migration under :SR-V6-one-seat (MODEL-MIGRATION-CONFLICT-LEDGER.md:25-26)" "A4-SR-SENTINEL-WPS (SR dossier): FUTURE_BOOK_REVISION has :owns \"none\"; DEFERRED has no define-wp-purpose yet is a model `wp` fact (rtw:52) — L6 closure is satisfied by sentinels" "A5-SR-WP-UNREFERENCED (SR dossier): WP-00/WP-05/WP-10 exist at source with no subsystem reference and no model fact" "A14-SR-FUTURE-TOKEN-NAMING (SR dossier) = ADJ-V17-WP-2 = ADJ-V18-WP-1: four tokens for one disposition" "A17-SR-R-ID-FORMAT (SR dossier): 'R-1..R-6' vs 'R-01..R-13' — normalise before minting requirement ids" "ADJ-MX4-WP-ORIGIN (new) = orchestrator-notes.md N2: importing define-wp-purpose gives the `wp` family a second origin unless the build_model.py:73-78 derivation is retired — and retiring it means the model's current `wp` universe was produced by a program the model classifies HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE" "ADJ-MX4-WP-BATCH (new): batch placement contradicted by 39 IMPORTED-class references + 14 DDI-1 + 6 DDI-2 references and by 29 live req-map / 6 live seat dependencies (dag.json order_violations)")
  :topological-position 3 :atomic-groups ()
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "hash-pinned `wp` fact extended with :purpose STRING (schema extension — `wp` has no fields, ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:175) + NEW `wp-owns` facts (:wp ref wp, :requirement ref requirement), one fact per owned requirement | invariant: L7 hash pin + L3 closed refs (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:24-25) | fallback: keep :purpose in WP-NN.md (AUTHORED_NORMATIVE_PROSE files-and-roles.sexp:386) and import only wp-owns edges" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart "NOT-APPLICABLE" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE (the range syntax 'R-1..R-6' at SR:15 is data the generator expands into one fact per requirement — not a reader macro; the model reader admits only string/integer/plain symbol, ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5)" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE" :package-asdf-boundary "NOT-APPLICABLE" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE" :compile-time-validation "L3 closed refs (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:200 law3-closed-refs) over wp-owns → requirement and L6 requirement→seat→test→WP closure (req-map ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:176-181; verification-corpus.sexp:42-44 PF-L6) at gate time | invariant: :SR-V6-one-seat 'every :future-wp token resolves to a define-wp-purpose WP id' (SR:139-140) + :SR-V6-wp-honesty 'grounded in WP-NN.md, not asserted' (SR:142-145) | fallback: today's 14 bare `wp` facts (requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:52-65) with no ownership check" :runtime-validation "NOT-APPLICABLE" :python-in-cl-risk "YES — naive import keeps :owns as an opaque STRING ('R-1..R-6 R-85..R-88 R-99 R-100' SR:15): a JSON-shaped range list nobody resolves, with two id formats in one file (R-1 at SR:15 vs R-01 at SR:16; dossier A17-SR-R-ID-FORMAT) and an ad-hoc range parser hidden in build_model.py. CL-native alternative: expand every range into typed `wp-owns` facts whose :requirement is an L3 closed ref into a FULL `requirement` universe (today only 24 requirement facts exist, requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:5-28; R-1..R-134 has no model seat — it lives in prose: TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md, IMPLEMENTATION-BOOK WP-NN.md:5), and declare the range grammar as DATA (as classification-rules.sexp declares its match grammar, ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:80-83) so the generic kernel ref check validates it." :future-freedom "SCHEDULE ONLY — binds concept→WP ownership, not mechanisms. S19 memory = FUTURE_BOOK_REVISION (SR:30; SR:98-99 'FUTURE BOOK REVISION REQUIRED before construction') is a construction block, not a design constraint; WP-07 :purpose pins 'Python+ONNX … MUST become optional adapter' (SR:22), which is freedom-preserving w.r.t. V8I-02. Importing WP-00/WP-05/WP-10 (absent from model `wp` facts) widens the wp universe (L3/L6 effects). No JTMS/S04/S20 mechanism constraint.")
  )

(ddi-class SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY__define-file-disposition
  :batch DDI-4 :source-file "SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp" :fact-class "define-file-disposition" :source-count 1 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms (("\"legal-casegrammar.lisp\"" :line 130 :sha16 "8482bb1f8585e90a"))
  :source-file "SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp"
  :source-forms 1
  :current-authority-seat "SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp section ';; ---- casegrammar SPLIT (a file-level disposition surfaced for the migration map) ----' (header :129), form :130-134 for \"legal-casegrammar.lisp\" (:was DEFER_PRIVATE :now SPLIT :public :private :no-copy). Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:9 (:source-count 1, DDI-4, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE). COMPETING SEAT of the same rule: V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp:247-250 define-rule casegrammar-split, also DDI-4 (deferred-imports.sexp:39) — identical :public/:private/:no-copy triple, without :was/:now and without the S04/S22 targets."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "NEW:file-dispositions.sexp — one-seat reason: the only existing module that speaks about files is files-and-roles.sexp, and it is a GENERATED artefact (gen-artifact ART-INVENTORY, generation-order.sexp:40-41, producer build_inventory.py), so a hand-authored disposition fact cannot live there without creating a second author for one file. The `file` fact type also has a CLOSED field set :required (role rule reason) :optional () (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:88-91), so a :disposition key is a typed L1 violation, not an added field. ALTERNATIVE (no new module): express the split as two `component` facts in interfaces-and-types.sexp — (fact component legal-casegrammar.lisp :owner-subsystem S04) plus a private counterpart under S22 — but `component` ids are TOKEN-SPACE (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:144-147) and two components for one physical path re-creates the duplicate-seat shape that SEAT-PATH-UNIQUE (:308) exists to forbid for seats. The choice is the decision, not a preference; both options are recorded. Cost of the NEW module: a NEW *.sexp under ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/ is auto-classified CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT by classification-rule R-008 (classification-rules.sexp:39-41) and auto-pinned by build_root.py:57 (directory listing), so ROOT.sexp :module-count 14 (ROOT.sexp:12) becomes 15 and every module SHA is re-derived (law L7)."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "NEW fact type `file-disposition` :id-space TOKEN-SPACE :required (path was now) :optional (public-subsystem private-subsystem no-copy public-note private-note) :types ((path STRING) (was SYMBOL) (now SYMBOL) (public-subsystem SYMBOL) (private-subsystem SYMBOL) (no-copy SYMBOL) (public-note STRING) (private-note STRING)) :enum ((was migration-disposition) (now migration-disposition) (no-copy yes-no)) :ref ((public-subsystem subsystem) (private-subsystem subsystem)). Flattening rule: the form is a flat plist already; the three prose values (:public/:private/:no-copy, SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:132-134) stay STRINGs (L1-legal). BLOCKER: :now SPLIT is NOT a member of the model's migration-disposition enum, which holds only (KEEP EXTEND DEFER_PRIVATE) (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:51), while the source header declares six dispositions KEEP|EXTEND|SPLIT|MOVE|DEFER_PRIVATE|REMOVE (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:6) — the enum must grow (a closed-enum change is a schema change) or the value must be re-expressed. The id must be synthesised: the form's name is the quoted path \"legal-casegrammar.lisp\" and PATH-SPACE ids are already owned by `file` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:88), so under L2 (one id owned by one fact type, :106-107) the disposition needs its own token id, e.g. FD-legal-casegrammar."
  :owner "SPLIT, therefore NOT a single owner — S04 for the public part and S22 for the private part (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:132-133; subsystems.sexp:8 S04 PUBLIC, :26 S22 PRIVATE). This is itself the finding: the model's ownership families are single-valued (`component :owner-subsystem`, `type :owner-subsystem`, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:144-152), so a two-owner file has no representable shape today. Reported as MIXED-OWNER, not resolved."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — no store is declared by this form (`writer` is a store field, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:155-158). The file itself, source/legal-casegrammar.lisp, is tracked and classified PRODUCTION_CODE by a bulk dir-rule (files-and-roles.sexp:1077 via DR-0060; classification-rules.sexp:111-113 R-031) and is named by NO `component` or `seat` fact (grep 'casegrammar' in the 14 modules = 0)."
  :classification "MIXED — private members named: the private half is 'client-fact schemas + matter-solving -> S22 PrivateMatterProfile (DEFER_PRIVATE)' (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:133), and S22 is PRIVATE (subsystems.sexp:26) with type PrivateMatterProfile/1 PRIVATE (interfaces-and-types.sexp:41) and seat SEAT-PRIVATE-MATTER-PROFILE DEFERRED_PRIVATE (seats.sexp:91-92). The public half is 'general Greek morphology / case frames / ambiguity detection -> S04' (:132), S04 PUBLIC (subsystems.sexp:8). One tracked path carrying both halves is the L5 question (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:47,164-170; deployment/LAWMAX-THREAT-MODEL.md is the cited boundary doc)."
  :dependencies ("FIRST: the migration-disposition enum must admit SPLIT (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:51 vs SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:6) [closed-enum / L1 dependency]" "FIRST: the duplicate-seat ruling against V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp:247-250 define-rule casegrammar-split (same batch, class 11) [one-seat dependency]" "FIRST: an L5 ruling on whether one tracked path may be owned by a PUBLIC and a PRIVATE subsystem without a physical split of the file [law dependency]" "EXISTING model facts: subsystem S04 (subsystems.sexp:8) and S22 (:26) are the ref targets [typed reference]" "EXISTING but unusable: `file` legal-casegrammar.lisp exists only inside a bulk dir-rule count (files-and-roles.sexp :1077 DR-0060), not as an individual `file` fact — so a :ref to a `file` id is not available [reference-target gap]")
  :consumers ("DDI-1 V1.6-SCHEMAS define-construction-order cognition-stage-dag (V1.6:217-221, :seat \"legal-casegrammar.lisp[general]\") — dag.json order violation from_rank 1 -> to_rank 4, 1 ref" "DDI-1 V1.7-SCHEMAS define-construction-order cognition-stage-dag-v7 (V1.7:80,85) — dag.json order violation from_rank 1 -> to_rank 4, 1 ref" "DDI-2 V1.6-SCHEMAS define-mapping cognition->existing-lisp-seat (V1.6:231,234-235 'legal-casegrammar.lisp[general] (SPLIT->public)') — dag.json order violation from_rank 2 -> to_rank 4, 1 ref" "DDI-4 sibling V1.6-SCHEMAS define-rule casegrammar-split (V1.6:247-250) — restates the same triple" "SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-subsystem (IMPORTED) — 2 refs (dag.json), the S04/S22 endpoints" "CANONICAL MODEL: none — 0 hits for 'casegrammar' in the 14 modules; the only model trace is the ledger row deferred-imports.sexp:9")
  :identity-version-rule "SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT (two live seats, neither retired): SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:130-134 and V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp:247-250 state the same :public/:private/:no-copy triple with divergent key sets — SR adds :was DEFER_PRIVATE :now SPLIT and names S04/S22, V1.6 names neither. Both rows are DDI-4 and both are AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE (deferred-imports.sexp:9 and :39). Neither file declares the other superseded. Also ONLY-VERSION for the head define-file-disposition (1 form in the whole corpus, classes.md row 7)."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION — an import today would (a) add an enum value, (b) instantiate one of two competing seats, and (c) assert a two-owner file that the model's ownership families cannot express. None of the three is a mechanical consequence of the source."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "CERTAIN duplicate seat: two forms in two registries, both deferred, both authoritative at source, stating one rule (A11-SR-CASEGRAMMAR-SPLIT-SEAT; A14 CASEGRAMMAR SPLIT TWICE in the V1.6 dossier). A third statement of the same rule sits in a V1.6 section comment (V1.6:167). Importing both yields two `file-disposition`/`rule` facts for one file; importing either silently retires the other."
  :requirement "UNKNOWN — no requirement id is attached at source; S04's model requirement is R-129 (rtw:70) and S22's is R-V6-PRIV (rtw:91), neither of which is about file disposition. No V-series requirement row names define-file-disposition."
  :invariant "L5 (public/private isolation, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:47,164-170) — a shared file straddles the boundary the law protects; L1 (SPLIT outside the migration-disposition enum, :51); L2 (id collision with the PATH-SPACE `file` id space, :88,106-107). Source invariant: :SR-V6-one-seat (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:136-140) — which the duplicate seat itself violates."
  :qualification-test "NEW — QT-DDI4-SPLIT-NO-COPY: no model test covers dispositions (rtw:30-50). Executable one-liner: `assert count(file-disposition where path=P) == 1 and (public-subsystem.classification == PUBLIC) and (private-subsystem.classification == PRIVATE) and no-copy == YES` for every disposition fact — i.e. exactly one disposition per path, the two halves land on opposite sides of the boundary, and the no-second-implementation clause is a declared value rather than prose."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact file-disposition FD-legal-casegrammar :path \"source/legal-casegrammar.lisp\" :was DEFER_PRIVATE :now SPLIT :public-subsystem S04 :private-subsystem S99 :no-copy YES)` — must be REJECTED: kernel-reason 'resolves to no declared subsystem', checker-reason 'L3' (precedent K14 vc:152-154, the S99 mutation). REPLACE `:now SPLIT` with `:now MOVE` — must be REJECTED as outside the migration-disposition enum until that enum is extended (L1). APPEND a SECOND disposition fact for the same :path — must be REJECTED by a new define-unique DISPOSITION-PATH-IS-ONE (modelled on SEAT-PATH-UNIQUE, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:308); without that uniqueness law the duplicate passes, which is precisely the duplicate-seat defect this class carries."
  :rollback "Delete the disposition fact(s); revert the migration-disposition enum in MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:51 and the schema :version (:37 / ROOT.sexp:9); delete file-dispositions.sexp if created and re-run build_root.py (module-count back to 14, ROOT.sexp:12); build_deferred.py restores deferred-imports.sexp:9. source/legal-casegrammar.lisp is never touched — no physical split is performed by a model import."
  :batch-reason "DDI-4 because build_deferred.py:103 maps `define-file-disposition` to DDI-4. DISAGREES — three earlier classes reference it and dag.json records all three as order violations: V1.6 define-construction-order (DDI-1, from_rank 1 -> to_rank 4), V1.7 define-construction-order (DDI-1, from_rank 1 -> to_rank 4), V1.6 define-mapping (DDI-2, from_rank 2 -> to_rank 4). The '[general]' seat token those three classes consume is DEFINED by this form, so on dependency order it belongs no later than DDI-1."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "Which form is the seat of the casegrammar split — SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:130-134 define-file-disposition or V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp:247-250 define-rule casegrammar-split? Does the model grow a `file-disposition` family (with SPLIT/MOVE/REMOVE in migration-disposition) or express the split as two `component` facts? And may one tracked file be owned by a PUBLIC and a PRIVATE subsystem under L5 without a physical split of the file?"
  :adjudication-items ("A11-SR-CASEGRAMMAR-SPLIT-SEAT (SR dossier) = A14 CASEGRAMMAR SPLIT TWICE (V1.6 dossier): two seats, one rule" "ADJ-MX4-SPLIT-ENUM (new): SPLIT/MOVE/REMOVE are declared dispositions at source (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:6) and absent from the model enum (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:51) — the model's disposition vocabulary is a strict subset of the registry's and nothing records the reduction" "ADJ-MX4-SPLIT-L5 (new): a single tracked path with a PUBLIC and a PRIVATE owner has no representable shape in the model's single-valued ownership families and is the first case where L5 must rule on a FILE rather than a type" "ADJ-MX4-SPLIT-BATCH (new): DDI-1 and DDI-2 classes consume the '[general]' seat token this class defines (3 dag.json order violations)")
  :topological-position 14 :atomic-groups ()
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "NEW `file-disposition` fact (:file PATH, :was/:now closed enum incl. SPLIT, :public-subsystem/:private-subsystem refs subsystem, :no-copy yes-no) hash-pinned, define-unique on :file | invariant: L1 closed enums (SPLIT is absent from migration-disposition = KEEP EXTEND DEFER_PRIVATE, ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:51) + L2 one disposition per path | fallback: two `component` facts under S04/S22 (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:144-147)" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart "NOT-APPLICABLE" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE" :package-asdf-boundary "the FUTURE execution of SPLIT is a package/ASDF split: the general mechanisms stay in :orchestrator.casegrammar (legal-casegrammar.lisp:29-37, exports parse-narrative/parse-definition/parse-provision) inside the public system; client-fact schemas + matter-solving move to a private package in a system that no public system :depends-on (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:31 'package boundary = capability boundary'; [0146]-claude.md:18 '16 systems, 53 edges, cycle NONE') | invariant: :no-copy 'no second implementation; private consumes the public general mechanisms' (SR:134) + V6I-16 acyclic public→private boundary (V1.6:334-338) + model L5 (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:243 law5-isolation) | fallback: one package with export discipline and a documented private section — which is today's state: every cognition seat lives in ONE serial system (orchestrator-infrastructure.asd:44 :serial t; :105 legal-casegrammar, :113 constitutional-gate, :114 cognition, :115 memory) — no ASDF-level seat for the split exists" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE" :compile-time-validation "ASDF dependency-graph cycle check (contract test 'ASDF graph cycle check (exit 0)', LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:31) + kernel L5 over consumes once the private package's types are PRIVATE `type` facts (verification-corpus.sexp:45-47 PF-L5) | invariant: public system never depends on the private system (V6I-07 V1.6:38-40) | fallback: runtime package-export check" :runtime-validation "NOT-APPLICABLE" :python-in-cl-risk "YES — SPLIT rendered as a free string (or dropped because it is not in the enum), and :public/:private carried as prose blobs ('general Greek morphology … -> S04 …') instead of typed subsystem refs. CL-native alternative: L3 refs to S04/S22, yes-no enum for :no-copy (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:71), and the SPLIT member added to a disposition enum AS DATA in MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp — never a Python special case in the generator." :future-freedom "CONSTRAINS S04 (cognition) file/package layout: the morphology/case-frame layer must be a public package consumed by the private layer (COG-3/COG-4 seats 'legal-casegrammar.lisp[general]' V1.6:220-221; V1.7:85). This PRESERVES the public/private one-way boundary and S22's deferral. No S19/JTMS/S20 constraint. Precondition: the duplicate seat (SR:130-134 vs V1.6:247-250) must be adjudicated to ONE (dossier A11-SR-CASEGRAMMAR-SPLIT-SEAT).")
  )

(ddi-class SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY__define-invariant
  :batch DDI-4 :source-file "SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp" :fact-class "define-invariant" :source-count 2 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms ((":SR-V6-one-seat" :line 136 :sha16 "9d1e26c9190fc024") (":SR-V6-wp-honesty" :line 141 :sha16 "56f977329acaa948"))
  :source-file "SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp"
  :source-forms 2
  :current-authority-seat "SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp file tail, forms :SR-V6-one-seat at :136-140 and :SR-V6-wp-honesty at :141-145 (no section header of their own; the preceding header is the casegrammar block at :129). Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:10 (:source-count 2, DDI-4, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE). LIVE MODEL ANCHORS pointing INTO this deferred class: rationale-references.sexp:4 (RAT-ONE-SEAT :doc \"SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp\" :anchor \":SR-V6-one-seat\") and :5 (RAT-WP-HONESTY :anchor \":SR-V6-wp-honesty\")."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "NEW:invariants.sexp for the TEXT (same seat as classes 1/5/9/12/14 — the 92-form invariant family), OR rationale-references.sexp (EXISTING) if the decision is pointer-only. This is the one class where the pointer option is already exercised: the model ALREADY holds two `rationale` facts for these two forms (rationale-references.sexp:4-5), consumed by seven seat facts — SEAT-COVERAGE-LEDGER (seats.sexp:77), SEAT-SECURITY-CELLS (:79), SEAT-OBSERVATORY-COLLECTOR (:81), SEAT-COVERAGE-OWNER (:83), SEAT-RA-T-SIGNER (:85), SEAT-MLTP-THRESHOLD-CUSTODY (:87) all :rationale RAT-WP-HONESTY, and SEAT-NO-WRITER (:99) :rationale RAT-ONE-SEAT. So 'pointer-only' is not a proposal for this class; it is the status quo, and the import decision is whether the text joins the model or the pointer stays alone."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "Either (a) EXISTING `rationale` (:doc STRING :anchor STRING, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:182-184) — already instantiated, PURE pointer, carries no text and no mechanisation binding; or (b) NEW `invariant` (as in class 1) with :text, :source-file, :source-line, :enforced-by law-id, plus :mechanized-by naming the define-unique / conditional that implements it. Flattening rule: both forms are docstring-only (keyword id + one prose STRING), so the text is already an L1-legal value; the ids render as SR-V6-one-seat / SR-V6-wp-honesty after colon stripping (keyword ids (`:V5I-01`, `:SR-V6-one-seat`, …) are not TOKEN-SPACE ids — TOKEN excludes ':' (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:41,17) — so a colon-stripping id-rendering convention must be declared once for all 92 define-invariant forms (orchestrator-notes.md N12)). :SR-V6-one-seat carries FOUR clauses (one owner seat; no dual/orphan/multi-writer; S19/S04 named examples; every :future-wp resolves to a define-wp-purpose id) of which the first is mechanised by define-unique SEAT-PATH-UNIQUE / STORE-OWNER-IS-ONE-SEAT (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:308,319) and the last by L3 on req-map :wp — so a single-fact import again mixes mechanised and unmechanised clauses. :SR-V6-wp-honesty is NOT mechanised at all: `wp` facts carry no :owns, so no law checks that req-map.wp owns req-map.requirement."
  :owner "UNKNOWN — registry-level normative prose with no :owner field; the dossier records 'none (registry-level normative prose)'. No subsystem in SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:35-127 or subsystems.sexp:5-30 governs architecture invariants."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — no store (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:155-158). rationale-references.sexp is hand-authored (absent from the gen-artifact universe, generation-order.sexp:38-61)."
  :classification "UNKNOWN — no classification field at source; `rationale` has none either (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:182-184). By content the two forms govern PUBLIC and PRIVATE subsystems alike (they quantify over all 26 subsystems, 4 of which are PRIVATE: subsystems.sexp:26-28,30) and carry no private datum. Reported as UNKNOWN rather than guessed; the dossier records the same."
  :dependencies ("DECISION: the shared invariant-family decision (ADJ-MX4-INV-SEAT) [schema dependency, spans 92 forms]" "DEPENDS ON class 2 in the same batch: :SR-V6-one-seat's WP clause quantifies over define-wp-purpose ids (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:139-140; dag.json 'SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp define-invariant -> define-wp-purpose': 8 refs) — an intra-DDI-4 ordering constraint [symbol reference]" "REFERENCES the IMPORTED class: 4 refs to define-subsystem (dag.json; S19 at SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:96, S04 at :45 as named examples) [symbol reference, already satisfied — subsystems.sexp:8,23]" "REFERENCES a token with no source definition: DEFERRED is named as a legal :future-wp value (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:139) but has no define-wp-purpose form; it exists as a model fact (rtw:52) admitted only by legacy audit code V1.6-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh:194 [dangling enum member]")
  :consumers ("CANONICAL MODEL (live, unique in DDI-4): rationale RAT-ONE-SEAT (rationale-references.sexp:4) and RAT-WP-HONESTY (:5) are `rationale` facts whose :anchor strings ARE these two form names; 7 `seat` facts reference them (seats.sexp:77,79,81,83,85,87,99) and those seats are in turn reference targets of subsystem :owner-seat, store :owner/:writer and req-map :seat" "MODEL-MIGRATION-CONFLICT-LEDGER.md:25-26 names :SR-V6-one-seat as the governing invariant of the S20/S21 composite-WP split that produced 5 req-map facts (rtw:86-90)" "legacy: V1.6-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh:166-170 (V6S4/V6S5) and :192-202 (V6S11) — HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:440)" "DDI-4 siblings restating the same two concepts: one-seat at ISR:177, V1.6:348, V1.7:26, V1.7:337, V1.8:20, V1.8:296; wp-honesty at V1.7:400, V1.8:320")
  :identity-version-rule "LIVE-REFERENCE-TARGET (both forms) — the model's `rationale` facts point at these exact anchors (rationale-references.sexp:4-5) and 7 seat facts depend on them; the model's seat universe therefore already rests on a class that is AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE and scheduled for the last batch. Additionally SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT at concept level: :SR-V6-one-seat is restated with divergent scope by :RA-I-5-one-seat-per-concept (V1.7:26-28, concepts), :V7I-OWN-single-writer (V1.7:337-340, stores/writers), :V8I-03-one-seat (V1.8:20-22), :V8I-OWN-universal (V1.8:296-299), :V6I-17-one-source-of-truth (V1.6:348-352, generated tables) and :ISR-V6-closure (ISR:177-180, interfaces); :SR-V6-wp-honesty by :V7I-WP-honest (V1.7:400-403) and :V8I-WP-real (V1.8:320-323). The model anchors the SR versions, i.e. it has de facto chosen SR as the seat for these two chains — but nothing declares that choice and the later registries do not defer to it."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION. Note the asymmetry: SKIP-WITH-PROOF is NOT available for this class even if the family decision is 'retire as mechanised', because the model's own `rationale` facts would then point at anchors in a file whose class was skipped — and no check verifies that a :doc/:anchor pair resolves (no counted check opens a `rationale` :doc and greps its :anchor — RAT-PUBPRIV (rationale-references.sexp:7) points at an anchor string that occurs 0 times in deployment/LAWMAX-THREAT-MODEL.md and passes every gate (orchestrator-notes.md N17)), so the breakage would be silent. If the decision is 'pointer-only', the rule is MERGE-INTO-EXISTING-FACT (the two rationale facts stay and gain nothing) and the class must then be marked SKIP-WITH-PROOF with an explicit statement that the model carries the pointer, not the text."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "HIGH. (i) Seven prose forms state 'one seat per concept' across four registries (A12-SR-ONE-SEAT-INVARIANT-FAMILY) and three state WP honesty (A13-SR-WP-HONESTY-FAMILY). (ii) Importing the text creates a prose seat beside the MECHANISED law (define-unique, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:308,319; the seat conditionals :293-304) with nothing declaring which governs — the ADJ-V18-INV-5 shape. (iii) The `rationale` pointer and an `invariant` text fact would themselves be two seats for one form unless the import replaces rather than supplements the pointer."
  :requirement "UNKNOWN — no requirement id at source. The two invariants are the stated justification of six DESIGN_TARGET seats, so the closest thing to a requirement is the seat conditionals SEAT-DESIGN-TARGET (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:297-298, ':rationale and :packet REQUIRED') — a law, not a requirement fact. None of the 24 model requirement facts (rtw:5-28) covers architecture governance."
  :invariant "L2 (define-unique SEAT-PATH-UNIQUE MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:308, STORE-OWNER-IS-ONE-SEAT :319 — the mechanised half of :SR-V6-one-seat), L3 (req-map :wp -> wp closed reference — the mechanised half of the WP clause), L6 (requirement->seat->test->WP closure, which today is satisfied by sentinel WPs), L1 (string values). :SR-V6-wp-honesty has NO mechanisation: `wp` carries no :owns (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:175)."
  :qualification-test "NEW — QT-DDI4-RATIONALE-RESOLVES: for every `rationale` fact, open :doc and require :anchor to occur in it. Executable one-liner: `for r in facts(rationale): grep -F -q -- \"$anchor\" \"$doc\" || fail(r.id)`. Run today it FAILS on RAT-PUBPRIV (rationale-references.sexp:7; orchestrator-notes.md N17) and PASSES on the four others including RAT-ONE-SEAT and RAT-WP-HONESTY — which is why this test is the entry criterion for any pointer-style DDI-4 import. No existing model `test` fact covers it (rtw:30-50) and gate_checks.py has no rationale resolver."
  :falsifier "REPLACE in rationale-references.sexp `:anchor \":SR-V6-one-seat\"` with `:anchor \":SR-V6-no-such-anchor\"` — must be REJECTED by the new anchor-resolution check, reason 'anchor does not occur in :doc'. Today this mutation PASSES every counted check, which is the held-out defect this class exposes. Second: APPEND `(fact rationale RAT-ONE-SEAT :doc \"x\" :anchor \"y\")` — must be REJECTED as a duplicate id (L2, precedent FX-L2-DUPLICATE-STORE vc:28-29). Third (if the text is imported): APPEND `(fact invariant SR-V6-one-seat :text \"…\" :enforced-by NONE :mechanized-by SEAT-PATH-UNIQUE)` while RAT-ONE-SEAT still exists — must be REJECTED by a new one-seat check that forbids a `rationale` and an `invariant` naming the same source anchor."
  :rollback "Delete any `invariant` facts and restore rationale-references.sexp to its 5 facts; if the pointer was replaced, restore lines 4-5 verbatim (the 7 seat facts reference them by id and would otherwise become L3 violations — a rollback that must be done in one step, not two); re-run build_root.py (module digest of rationale-references.sexp, ROOT.sexp:22) and build_deferred.py (deferred-imports.sexp:10). The source registry is not edited."
  :batch-reason "DDI-4 because build_deferred.py:101 maps `define-invariant` to DDI-4. DISAGREES — not on symbol order (its 12 out-edges point at define-subsystem, IMPORTED, and define-wp-purpose, same batch) but on LIVE MODEL DEPENDENCE: the canonical model already carries two `rationale` facts whose anchors are these two forms (rationale-references.sexp:4-5) and seven `seat` facts that reference them (seats.sexp:77,79,81,83,85,87,99). A class the model's seat universe already depends on is not 'deferred to last' in any meaningful sense; its authority split (AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE, deferred-imports.sexp:10) is contradicted by the model's own use of it. Intra-batch: it must follow class 2 (define-wp-purpose) because of the 8 WP references."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "Is :SR-V6-one-seat retired as mechanised by L2 + define-unique (leaving RAT-ONE-SEAT pointing at a source anchor whose class is skipped), or imported as an `invariant` fact together with its six sibling one-seat forms — and which single form is then the seat? Same question for :SR-V6-wp-honesty, which is mechanised by nothing. Secondary: is DEFERRED a legitimate :future-wp token when it has no define-wp-purpose at source?"
  :adjudication-items ("A12-SR-ONE-SEAT-INVARIANT-FAMILY (SR dossier): seven prose forms for one law" "A13-SR-WP-HONESTY-FAMILY (SR dossier): three prose forms; unmechanised in the model; anchored only by RAT-WP-HONESTY under six DESIGN_TARGET seats" "A4-SR-SENTINEL-WPS (SR dossier): DEFERRED is named as a legal token by this invariant but defined nowhere at source" "ADJ-MX4-INV-SEAT (new, shared with classes 1/5/9/12/14): one module and one policy for the 92 invariant forms" "ADJ-MX4-ANCHOR-DEPENDENCE (new): the model's `rationale`/`seat` closure already depends on a DEFERRED class; either the ledger's AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE claim or the model's use of the anchors is wrong")
  :topological-position 37 :atomic-groups ()
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "the EXISTING `rationale` pointer facts (rationale-references.sexp:4-5) are already the seat; the prose stays in SR (V6I-17: prose not duplicated, rationale-references.sexp:1-2) | invariant: one seat per concept (the invariant's own first clause, SR:137) + constitution :no-duplicate (LAWMAX-ARCHITECTURE-CONSTITUTION.sexp:26) | fallback: a NEW invariant fact carrying :text — which would be a second seat for the same prose" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart "NOT-APPLICABLE" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE (registry forms are DATA read under *read-eval* nil (deferred-imports.sexp:4; ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:56; safe-read.lisp:152-165) — never a macro expanded over the registry file)" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE" :package-asdf-boundary "NOT-APPLICABLE" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE" :compile-time-validation "one-seat: kernel L2 (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:124 duplicate seat; :190 law2-unique reading define-unique data ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:308 SEAT-PATH-UNIQUE, :319 STORE-OWNER-IS-ONE-SEAT) — ALREADY enforced; wp-honesty: a NEW data-declared closure rule 'every req-map.wp owns req-map.requirement via wp-owns' (needs C2 facts) evaluated by the generic kernel | invariant: SR:139-140 'the architecture gate rejects a dangling or invented WP'; SR:142-145 'grounded, not asserted' | fallback: audit V6S11 in V1.6-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh — HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, NON_AUTHORITATIVE (files-and-roles.sexp:440)" :runtime-validation "NOT-APPLICABLE" :python-in-cl-risk "YES if the two docstrings become :text blobs beside the pointers (duplicate seat) or if wp-honesty is 'checked' by a hand-written Python loop over strings. CL-native alternative: keep the pointer facts; mechanize wp-honesty as a declared rule in MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp data (define-unique/define-conditional style, ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:26-36) that both verification paths evaluate generically (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:1-2 forbids shared evaluator code, permits shared specification)." :future-freedom "NONE — the invariant FIXES the one-seat identity of S19 memory (memory.lisp EXTEND, SR:138 = SEAT-MEMORY seats.sexp:56) and S04 cognition ('existing engine EXTEND' = SEAT-LEGAL-AST seats.sexp:32); that is the intended guard against a second engine/memory (contract JTMS row LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:28). No S20/V8I-02 constraint.")
  )

