  :dependencies ("SCHEMA FIRST: MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp version bump ('4' -> '5', X76 positive control verification-corpus.sexp:365-370) declaring `enum` + `enum-value` (reference kind: fact-type declaration)" "subsystem facts S01/S03/S04/S10 (subsystems.sexp:5,7,8,14) for :owner-subsystem — EXIST (reference kind: L3 ref)" "V1.5-SCHEMAS__define-record (same batch) for the field->enum binding of 9 enums (V1.5:34,38,199,200,279,280,305,316,326,364,412,413,416,417,463,498,507) — the enum must exist BEFORE the field facts (reference kind: field-type)" "decision on the enum owner field (A19: owner optional or mandatory) before StateEventKind / admission_obligation_state can be written")
  :consumers ("V1.5 define-record fields (same batch) — 9 of 16 enums are field types (own parse of V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp: unreferenced-by-any-field = StateEventKind acquisition_state admission_obligation_state availability_state negative_evidence_validity observation_state validation_state)" "DDI-1 V1.5 define-required-refs keys are enumerability_class VALUES (V1.5:210-214) — enum-value ids must exist before that DDI-1 class can be L3-closed" "DDI-3 census-coverage-decision (V1.5:229-244) and census-coverage-decision-v7 (V1.7:259-276) test enum VALUES of 8 enums by input NAME convention only (V1.5:230)" "DDI-1 V1.5 define-cardinality-matrix columns are SemanticAdmissionAssuranceProfile values (V1.5:46-62)" "DDI-4 invariants :V5I-01/:V5I-04/:V5I-05/:V5I-D3-unknown and gate SA-2-canonical-admission (V1.5:115-137,246-260,406-408); SR:56 S07 interface string names the D1.5 event distinction" "prose: deployment/LAWMAX-SECURE-SEMANTIC-INGRESS-CONTRACT.md:175-181, deployment/LAWMAX-PUBLIC-SOURCE-TYPE-AUTHORITY-REGISTRY.md:168-189, MACHINE-LEGAL-TRUST-PROTOCOL.md:1473-1544, deployment/LAWMAX-LEGAL-IR-SEMANTIC-CONTRACT.md:169-207; no tracked source/ or systems/ file names any record/enum id of the six registries (git grep at RO = 0); the only mechanical readers are the legacy audits/harness classified HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:436,440,444,450,453)")
  :identity-version-rule "id = the enum name as written (all 16 are TOKEN-legal; two use snake_case, e.g. enumerability_class); enum-value id = <enum>__<VALUE> after colon-strip (V1.5:14 ':SA-0' -> SA-0). Version relation: ONLY-VERSION for 14 (no same-name define in V1.6/V1.7/V1.8, grep); LIVE-REFERENCE-TARGET for availability_state (V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp:257 define-reference :canonical \"V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp:188\" :identity \"lawmax/availability-state\") — V1.7 adds identity, changes no member; DIVERGENT-BY-VALUE for negative_evidence_validity: V1.7:274 tests :VALID_AUTHORITATIVE_FRESH which is no member of V1.5:223-224 (V5-A3); DivergenceState omits INDEPENDENCE_UNKNOWN used as a result token at V1.5:99,290,340 (V5-A17)"
  :migration-rule "IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL for 14 forms once the enum family exists (SCHEMA_EXTENSION); BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION for StateEventKind (owner S03 vs S07, V5-A5) and negative_evidence_validity (V1.5 vocabulary vs V1.7:274 undeclared value, V5-A3); the per-member attributes (:label/:obligation V1.5:14-16, :binding L267-269, :sa L22-31) are imported as enum-value fields, not dropped (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:12 'a parsed-but-ignored field is silent loss')"
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "(1) availability_class (V1.5:172) and availability_state (V1.5:188) share three member names (ACCESS_RESTRICTED LICENSING_RESTRICTED UNKNOWN) — two enums, no stated mapping; under <enum>__<VALUE> ids they do not collide but the concept 'availability' has two seats; (2) the 8 decision-input enums are bound to census-coverage-decision inputs by NAME only (V1.5:230) — importing them without the binding fact leaves the DDI-3 function untyped; (3) the model's own `define-enum classification (PUBLIC PRIVATE)` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:47) is a schema domain, not a fact — no id collision with domain enums, but the word 'enum' must not be reused for both in prose"
  :requirement "EXISTING via owner req-maps only: R-25 (S03__WP-07 requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:69), R-132 (S01__WP-01 :67; S16__WP-01 :82), R-130 (S10__WP-06 :76), R-129 (S04__WP-08 :70); the class-specific requirements V5R-D1-06/07/08, V5R-D2-06/07/08, V5R-D3-07/11, V5R-R8 (TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:250-262,289) are NEW — not model `requirement` facts (requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:5-28; V5-A15)"
  :invariant "L1 (closed value domain: an out-of-domain enum-value is a typed L1 violation once `enum-value :enum` is an L3 ref and the value set is the fact set); L3 (field :domain -> enum id); L2 (one enum id, one seat); source invariants :V5I-01 (V1.5:115-118), :V5I-04 (:246-252), :V5I-05 (:254-260), :V5I-D3-unknown (:406-408), :V5I-D1-unregistered-event (:152-154)"
