  :falsifier "(fact falsifier D2-ENUM-VALUE-ORPHAN :harness COMPONENT :intent \"an enum-value naming an enum that does not exist\" :mutation APPEND :module \"interfaces-and-types.sexp\" :form \"(fact enum-value NoSuchEnum__X :enum NoSuchEnum :value X :ordinal 1)\" :kernel-reason \"resolves to no declared enum\" :checker-reason \"L3\"); (fact falsifier D2-ENUM-VALUE-KEYWORD :harness COMPONENT :intent \"a member value written as a keyword instead of a symbol\" :mutation APPEND :module \"interfaces-and-types.sexp\" :form \"(fact enum-value DivergenceState__AGREED2 :enum DivergenceState :value :AGREED)\" :kernel-reason \"illegal value kind\" :checker-reason \"MALFORMED-FACT\")"
  :rollback "delete the imported facts of this class and the fact-type/enum declarations added to MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp for it, re-run build_root.py so ROOT.sexp re-pins the 14 modules (ROOT.sexp:12-27; L7), and restore the ledger row to DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT / AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE (deferred-imports.sexp) so the source file is authoritative again; the source registry is never edited by the import (V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp:256 'v1.5 files are NOT edited' is the precedent)"
  :batch-reason "ledger: 'prior-version (may be superseded by v1.8) class ... scheduled for batch DDI-2 (type / record / enum / reference schema detail)' (deferred-imports.sexp:16; build_deferred.py:92-95 batches by head name only). Dependency evidence DISAGREES with the DDI-1 -> DDI-2 order: DDI-1 V1.5 define-required-refs (deferred-imports.sexp:27) keys are enumerability_class values (V1.5:210-214) and DDI-1 V1.7 define-pipeline :node-types names census_coverage_state (V1.7:315); the batch matrix shows 137 DDI-1 -> DDI-2 references (WORK/dag-fragment.md:5-12). Within DDI-2 the enums must precede the records that type fields with them"
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "(a) Does the `enum` fact carry a mandatory :owner-subsystem (then StateEventKind needs S03 or S07 decided — V1.5:10-11/ISR:59 vs SR:56 — and admission_obligation_state S01 or S03) or is owner optional for closed domains (A19)? (b) Which vocabulary is canonical for the negative-evidence input: V1.5:223-224 {FRESH_QUALIFYING INSUFFICIENT EXPIRED ABSENT UNKNOWN} or V1.7:274 :VALID_AUTHORITATIVE_FRESH (declared nowhere) (V5-A3)? (c) Are INDEPENDENCE_UNKNOWN (V1.5:99,290,340) and UNVERIFIED_FOR_MACHINE_RELIANCE (V1.5:405) to be declared as enum members, or mapped (V5-A17)?"
  :adjudication-items ("V5-A5 StateEventKind owner: S03 (D1 seat, V1.5:10-11; ISR:59) vs S07 (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:56 'later-treatment (v1.5 D1.5)'); no record field has this type (grep V1.5:20,149,150,153 only)" "V5-A3 negative_evidence_validity: V1.5:223-224 members vs V1.7:274 :VALID_AUTHORITATIVE_FRESH (defined in no registry)" "V5-A17 INDEPENDENCE_UNKNOWN / UNVERIFIED_FOR_MACHINE_RELIANCE result tokens (V1.5:99,290,340,405; MLTP.md, deployment/LAWMAX-THREAT-MODEL.md:47) are members of no closed enum" "A19 (V1.6 dossier) enum fact family shape: owner mandatory/optional; classification of enums for L5 (L5 today ranges over `type`+`consumes` only, KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:243-254)" "V5-A15 requirement/test universe: V5R-*/V5Q-* (TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:241-293) are not model facts; L6 chain for imported V1.5 facts undefined" "UNKNOWN: whether :obligation/:binding/:sa attributes are machine-consumed anywhere (only membership is read by V1.5-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh:175,193)" "UNKNOWN: the availability_class (V1.5:172) vs availability_state (V1.5:188) relation — three shared member names, no registry mapping")
  :topological-position 1 :atomic-groups (4 9)
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "NOT-APPLICABLE" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE (an enum is a closed VALUE DOMAIN, not a domain object; CL-native form is a `deftype` member type + one exported constant list per enum — source/version-graph.lisp:148-149 deftype legal-date / legal-instant; source/capability-registry.lisp:59 +param-types+ closed list + :169 %type-ok-p ecase (unknown type errors structurally, no fail-open))" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE (exhaustive dispatch over a closed set is `ecase` over the declared members — source/capability-registry.lisp:59 +param-types+ closed list + :169 %type-ok-p ecase (unknown type errors structurally, no fail-open); no open dispatch is wanted: an enum must not grow by adding a method)" :condition-restart "out-of-domain value => typed condition at the decoding boundary (fail-closed; pattern source/safe-read.lisp:68 safe-read-error; :28-30 INTERNAL-ONLY (forbids Internet/HTML/PDF/OCR/LLM raw input); :203 read-data-form; source/capability-registry.lisp:59 +param-types+ closed list + :169 %type-ok-p ecase (unknown type errors structurally, no fail-open)) | invariant: closed enum + fail-closed unregistered kinds (V1.5:148-151 define-rule unregistered-state-event: never downgraded to SA-0/SA-1; MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:18 out-of-domain value is L1) | fallback: return a typed error value (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:24)" :macro-dsl "ONE `define-closed-enum`-shaped Lisp macro expanding at compile time to deftype+constant+predicate is admissible ONLY with the macroexpand golden test (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:25); the registry form itself stays DATA read by the kernel (AM/interfaces-and-types.sexp:3 'No eval. Read with *read-eval* nil' (model facts are DATA, never loaded as code)) | invariant: macros expand at compile time only, never over external bytes (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:25) | fallback: hand-written deftype + defparameter list (source/version-graph.lisp:148-149 deftype legal-date / legal-instant; source/capability-registry.lisp:59 +param-types+ closed list + :169 %type-ok-p ecase (unknown type errors structurally, no fail-open))" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE (values are arguments of protocols, never protocol owners; SemanticAdmissionAssuranceProfile/DivergenceState are consumed by the S03 admission seat source/legal-extraction-verify.lisp:17-23 V1-V4 deterministic checks (V4 consistency in the JTMS); :340 verdict)" :package-asdf-boundary "each enum lives in the package of its owner subsystem's seat (subsystem :owner-seat -> seat :path, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:132-143); owners are UNKNOWN for StateEventKind (V5-A5) and the six decision-input enums (V1.5:186-224 typed by no record field) so placement is undecidable today | invariant: package boundary = capability boundary (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:31) | fallback: monolith package (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:31)" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE (values are not events; StateEventKind CLASSIFIES journal events by SA level, V1.5:18-31, but is itself static data)" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE (DivergenceState/unknown_handling are LABEL domains of TMS-like outcomes; the mechanism belongs to the records/gate that carry them — source/legal-inference-engine.lisp:238 make-jtms; :385 fact-status (:in/:undefined/:out/:unknown); :395 tms-retract-premise)" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE" :compile-time-validation "member list of every deftype must equal the model's enum-value facts (set equality both directions, the corpus discipline of AM/verification-corpus.sexp:11-14) at build; per-value attributes (:label/:obligation/:sa/:binding V1.5:14-16,22-31,267-269) become one flat fact per (enum,value,attribute) — never a nested list (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:4-7) | invariant: L1 closed value domain enforced by the kernel (AM/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:1-3 (*read-eval* nil, standard readtable, no eval), :23 *enums*, :24 *conds*, :56-60 reader, :243-257 law5-isolation *enums*) | fallback: runtime check (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:32)" :runtime-validation "`typep`/`ecase` against the declared member type inside the typed decoder of the record that carries the field (source/legal-ast.lisp:1704-1717 form-to-ast (typed decoder: closed+mandatory key-set, no duplicate keys, deep type check, class allowlist, no eval); :1071 ast-decode-error); out-of-domain => typed condition, never coercion | invariant: fail-closed, no silent downgrade (V1.5:148-154) | fallback: reject input (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:35)" :python-in-cl-risk "HIGH. Naive import: per-value attributes (:SA-0 :label \"STRUCTURAL\" :obligation ...) become nested plists/dicts or a single STRING listing members; decision-input enums (V1.5:217-224) become an ad-hoc `if value in [...]` validator inside a decision function. CL-native: deftype member type per enum (source/version-graph.lisp:148-149 deftype legal-date / legal-instant) + closed constant list checked by ecase (source/capability-registry.lisp:59 +param-types+ closed list + :169 %type-ok-p ecase (unknown type errors structurally, no fail-open)); attributes as flat typed facts (enum-value :label STRING :obligation SYMBOL) so the kernel's L1 (AM/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:1-3 (*read-eval* nil, standard readtable, no eval), :23 *enums*, :24 *conds*, :56-60 reader, :243-257 law5-isolation) and SBCL's type system both see the domain; the registry form remains data (AM/interfaces-and-types.sexp:3 'No eval. Read with *read-eval* nil' (model facts are DATA, never loaded as code))." :future-freedom "NO problematic constraint. ArgumentScheme closes with :OTHER (V1.5:448-450) and StatementTargetKind (:Norm :Fact, V1.5:454) references the frozen Legal-IR node set (V1.5:452-453) — vocabularies are versioned and fail-closed (V1.5:148-151), none mandates a model/vendor (V8I-02 V1.8:17). Binding to the reasoning engine is by value only; no JTMS/S04/S19/S20 technique is fixed. Cross-registry divergence negative_evidence_validity vs V1.7:274 :VALID_AUTHORITATIVE_FRESH (V5-A3) is a vocabulary adjudication, not a freedom loss.")
  )

