  :cl-native (:immutable-record "content-addressed immutable BODY: *_id = hex(sha256(id_domain || 0x1F || canonical(BODY))), BODY excludes id+signatures+detached refs (V1.5:141-142, :456-458); canonical(BODY) MUST be the ONE serialization seat source/journal.lisp:61 canon-sexp (ONE canonical value serialization; admissible domain NIL/keyword/string/integer/list, :65-66) + source/journal.lisp:88 sha256-hex (as source/memory.lisp:96-110 record-episode (chained-append + body hash via journal:canon-sexp, :hv 2) already does), which bounds every field value to canon-sexp's domain (keyword/string/integer/list) | invariant: identity = content-address; lifecycle detached (V5I-A2-immutable-id V1.5:554-558; V6I-11 V1.6:151-154; deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:27) | fallback: copy-on-write (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:27)" :clos-class "CLOS class ONLY where inheritance/dispatch is real: the C1 records (CanonRule/ClaimRecord/ArgumentRecord/ArgumentRelation) are Legal-IR objects consumed by the S04 engine (pattern source/knowledge-graph.lisp:69-84 assertion-class metaclass + initialize-instance :after (no assertion without source+justification); :116 knowledge-graph; source/legal-ast.lisp:291-338 ast-node with :type slot declarations); D1/D2/D3 evidence records are flat signed bodies -> immutable defstruct with :read-only slots (source/capability-registry.lisp:40-47 defstruct capability (:read-only t slots, immutable after registration)) | invariant: one class per concept (constitution :no-duplicate deployment/LAWMAX-ARCHITECTURE-CONSTITUTION.sexp:26; deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:20) | fallback: plain structs (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:20)" :generic-function "C1 records enter the reasoning engine through the existing generic seats (rule-matches source/legal-inference-engine.lisp:538; source/cognition.lisp:92 plan / :96 execute-step / :101 synthesize / :107 triage / :113 critique (defgeneric, open dispatch per frame)); no per-record generic is added | invariant: dispatch is total or errors typed (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:21) | fallback: single dispatch fn (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:21)" :condition-restart "typed decode condition per record family (source/legal-ast.lisp:1704-1717 form-to-ast (typed decoder: closed+mandatory key-set, no duplicate keys, deep type check, class allowlist, no eval); :1071 ast-decode-error); missing/expired/revoked/out-of-scope evidence => typed INDEPENDENCE_UNKNOWN outcome, never silent (V1.5:98-99, :382-383, :406-409) | invariant: every error is a typed condition; never a guess (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:24; V1.5:161-164 V5I-02) | fallback: return typed error value (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:24)" :macro-dsl "a record-declaration macro (immutable struct/class + typed decoder + canonical field order for canon-sexp hashing) is admissible only if its expansion is golden-tested against the model's `field` facts; the registry `define-record` forms stay DATA (AM/interfaces-and-types.sexp:3 'No eval. Read with *read-eval* nil' (model facts are DATA, never loaded as code)) | invariant: macros expand at compile time only (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:25); single seat of the field list (V6I-REF V1.6:158-162) — see CL2-A1 | fallback: hand-written defstruct/defclass + decoder (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:25)" :protocol "NOT