ployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:32)" :runtime-validation "table-driven typed decoder (one engine + `field` data, the design principle of MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:26-30) with closed+mandatory key-set and deep type check (source/legal-ast.lisp:1704-1717 form-to-ast (typed decoder: closed+mandatory key-set, no duplicate keys, deep type check, class allowlist, no eval); :1071 ast-decode-error); signed bodies verified against a LocalTrustState-pinned registry (V1.5:367-375) before use | invariant: no forgery-by-omission (source/legal-ast.lisp:1705-1706); VALID := signature AND issuer AND scope AND freshness AND not revoked (V1.5:95-97) | fallback: reject input (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:35)" :python-in-cl-risk "HIGH. Naive import: (a) field types `(list anchor)`, `(or instant null)`, `(member :true :false)` stored as opaque STRINGS parsed by regex (exactly deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/V1.6-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh:151-152 `re.finditer(r':type\\s+...')` — the anti-pattern the kernel forbids, AM/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:9 'No regex, no grep, no substring is structural proof'); (b) records as hash-tables/alists with string keys validated by an imperative walker (pattern deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/V1.8-VERIFY.py:1050-1075); (c) TrustedIssuerRegistry/1 embedding record lists (V1.5:357-359) as nested blobs. CL-native: decompose every type expression into typed closed fields (:domain <type|enum id> :cardinality ONE|LIST :nullable YES|NO) — one fact per field, L3-closed :domain; inline (member ...) sets promoted to named enums (as V1.8:31 MergeSemanticsV8 did); composition as ref fields to content-addressed ids (V1.5:466-470 CanonPolicy canon_id_refs already does this); immutable defstruct/CLOS per record with hashing through source/journal.lisp:61 canon-sexp (ONE canonical value serialization; admissible domain NIL/keyword/string/integer/list, :65-66) + source/journal.lisp:88 sha256-hex." :future-freedom "NO new constraint, conditional on ONE reading: the C1 records REPRESENT the existing :argument primitive and add 'NO engine, NO seat' (V1.5:487-493, :630-638), i.e. they must bind to the existing JTMS (source/legal-inference-engine.lisp:238 make-jtms; :385 fact-status (:in/:undefined/:out/:unknown); :395 tms-retract-premise) — importing them as a separate argument store would be a second reasoning seat (V5I-C1-canon). Undefined primitive types (uncertainty 'typed lawmax/uncertainty/1' V1.5:509, quorum-spec V1.5:418 — 0 occurrences in source/*.lisp) and prose targets (LocalTrustState, ConflictPolicyBundle V5-A7) are UNKNOWN seats, not technique locks. No adapter/model dependency (D1 admission is symbolic: V1.5:64-69).")
