nditional shape (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:26-30; kernel *conds* AM/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:1-3 (*read-eval* nil, standard readtable, no eval), :23 *enums*, :24 *conds*, :56-60 reader, :243-257 law5-isolation) | invariant: exactly one code per (field x {SA-0,SA-1,SA-2}) (V1.5:44) | fallback: runtime check (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:32)" :runtime-validation "at decode of a SemanticAdmissionEvidence/1: for its assurance_profile, :R fields present, :F fields absent, :C fields evaluated by the gate — one data-driven evaluator (the CL twin of MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp define-conditional; declarative shapes as in source/shacl-validator.lisp:6-10 (shapes are data, not a bespoke checker); :115-130 property-shape / node-shape structs) | invariant: V5I-01 (V1.5:115-120) | fallback: reject input (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:35)" :python-in-cl-risk "HIGH. Naive import: nested dict field->profile->code, or a hand-coded if/elif chain per profile (the imperative pattern of deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/V1.8-VERIFY.py:1058-1069 for the sibling table); or a STRING cell 'R R R'. CL-native: one flat fact per cell (cardinality record field profile code) with :field an L3 ref to a `field` fact and :profile an enum-value ref, consumed by ONE evaluator whose specification is the data — the exact discipline of AM/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:26-30 define-conditional; the kernel already evaluates such rules generically (AM/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:1-3 (*read-eval* nil, standard readtable, no eval), :23 *enums*, :24 *conds*, :56-60 reader, :243-257 law5-isolation *conds*)." :future-freedom "NO constraint on S04/S19/JTMS/S20. It constrains ingress admission (S03) only and is symbolic (V1.5:64-69). Two cardinality dialects exist (this matrix vs V1.8:394-397 table, ADJ-V18-CARD-1): one fact family expressing both keeps one evaluator; two families = two evaluators (a mediocrity risk, not a freedom loss).")
