  :current-authority-seat "V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp — inline, each invariant closing the definition it constrains, distributed over the file's delta sections: D1 8 forms (:70,:100,:105,:115,:152,:155,:161 and :246 is D2), D2 2 (:246,:254), D3 5 (:287,:293,:346,:406,:433 plus :437), C1 6 (:487,:522,:554,:610,:618,:622) and one GLOBAL under the header ';; ============================ GLOBAL TRUST INVARIANT (unchanged wording) ===' (V1.5:640) at :641. Full id list and lines: classes.md row 13. The same 22 ids are the 'Type/Invariant' column of TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:250-289 (AUTHORED_NORMATIVE_PROSE, files-and-roles.sexp:414). Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:22 (:source-count 22, DDI-4, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE)."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "NEW:invariants.sexp — same seat as classes 1/4/9/12/14; one-seat reason as in class 1 (one concept, six file seats today). Cost: a NEW *.sexp under ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/ is auto-classified CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT by classification-rule R-008 (classification-rules.sexp:39-41) and auto-pinned by build_root.py:57 (directory listing), so ROOT.sexp :module-count 14 (ROOT.sexp:12) becomes 15 and every module SHA is re-derived (law L7). rationale-references.sexp is the pointer-only alternative and cannot carry the text or the subsystem scope."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "NEW `invariant` (as in class 1) with :optional (scope-subsystem) :ref ((scope-subsystem subsystem)) — 15 of the 22 forms have an inferable owner (S03 7, S01 2, S10 6, S04 6 per the dossier's per-form owner_subsystem) so the scope field is usable, and 3 are UNKNOWN. Flattening rule: every form is docstring-only (keyword id + one prose STRING), so the text is L1-legal as-is; ids render by colon stripping (keyword ids (`:V5I-01`, `:SR-V6-one-seat`, …) are not TOKEN-SPACE ids — TOKEN excludes ':' (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:41,17) — so a colon-stripping id-rendering convention must be declared once for all 92 define-invariant forms (orchestrator-notes.md N12)) giving V5I-D1-both, V5I-01, V5I-A2-immutable-id, … all inside TOKEN charset. NO nested list appears in this class (unlike define-rule/gate), so this is the one DDI-4 class whose 22 values are already representable. What is NOT representable is the SEMANTIC content: the invariants quantify over record fields, enum members and lifecycle states that are DDI-2/DDI-3 facts or are declared nowhere at all (V5-A6), so a typed :about reference field cannot be closed under L3 today."
  :owner "MIXED / partly UNKNOWN — no form carries an :owner; the dossier infers per form from the section: S03 (D1: :V5I-D1-both :70, :V5I-D1-indep :100, :V5I-01 :115, :V5I-D1-no-assumption-canonical :155, :V5I-02 :161), S01 (D2: :V5I-04 :246 via SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:36, :V5I-05 :254), S10 (D3: :V5I-D3-bind :287, :V5I-D3-issuer-signing :293, :V5I-D3-domainassertion :346, :V5I-D3-unknown :406, :V5I-06 :433, :V5I-07 :437), S04 (C1: :V5I-C1-canon :487, :V5I-C1-relation-detached :522, :V5I-A2-immutable-id :554, :V5I-C1-acyclic :610, :V5I-08 :618, :V5I-09 :622). UNKNOWN for :V5I-F7-derivation-trust (:105, spans S03 and S10), :V5I-D1-unregistered-event (:152, owner of StateEventKind undetermined — V5-A5) and :V5I-10 (:641, global). Only :V5I-04's owner is DECLARED (S01 owns census-coverage-decision per SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:36); the other 21 are inferences and are labelled as such."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — `writer` is a store field only (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:155-158); this class declares no store."
