  :identity-version-rule "ONLY-VERSION for 21 of 22 ids (no form of the same name exists in the other five registries — dossier lineage 'V1.5-only' for every form; classes.md; version-chains.md lists no V5I chain). TWO exceptions at CONCEPT level: (a) :V5I-04 (V1.5:246) asserts totality/determinism of census-coverage-decision, a function V1.7:259-260 declares SUPERSEDED by census-coverage-decision-v7 and whose properties V1.7:280-284 restates as :V7I-COV-availability-live — SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT with the v1.5 form still live because SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:36 still names census-coverage-decision as S01's interface (V5-A2); (b) :V5I-10 (V1.5:641) is a principle restated by :RA-I-1 (V1.7:14) and :V8I-01 (V1.8:14) under different ids — a principle chain without a name chain. The header calls :V5I-10's wording 'unchanged' (V1.5:640) but git grep finds no v1.4/MLTP origin for that text in RO (dossier unknowns) — the claim of unchanged-ness is unverifiable here."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION for the class. Per-form: 21 of 22 would be IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL once the invariant family exists (their ids are unique and their text is L1-legal); :V5I-04 (:246) is IMPORT-AS-HISTORICAL-VERSION or SKIP-WITH-PROOF depending on the census-coverage-decision supersession ruling (V5-A2), which is a DDI-3 decision this class cannot make."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "MODERATE. No id collides. The risks are: (i) :V5I-04 and :V7I-COV-availability-live become two live invariant facts about two versions of one decision function, with SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:36 still naming the older one; (ii) importing text whose vocabulary is undeclared (V5-A6/A7/A17) puts prose in the model that no law can check — a parsed-but-unenforced fact, which the model's own doctrine calls silent loss (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:12); (iii) the 30 V5R/V5Q/V5KW ids in TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md would become a second requirement/test universe beside rtw:5-50 if imported with the text (V5-A15)."
  :requirement "NEW — TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:250-289 declares one V5R-* requirement per invariant (e.g. V5R-D2-06 at :254, V5R-F2 at :273, V5R-F7 at :288), but no V5R-* id is a model `requirement` fact (rtw:5-28 holds 24 ids, none of them V5R-*). Whether the V5 universe enters the model is the open question orchestrator-notes.md N8 states for the whole R-space."
  :invariant "L1 (prose STRING values are legal; keyword ids are not — MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6,41), L2 (one id per fact type, :106-107), L3 (any typed :about reference must resolve — today impossible for the lifecycle-state and LocalTrustState vocabulary), L7 (module universe if a new module is added). Source invariants: the 22 forms ARE the invariants; their own enforcement lives in the legacy audit V1.5-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE) and in predeclared UNEXECUTED tests."
  :qualification-test "NEW — QT-DDI4-INV-V15-COUNT + QT-DDI4-INV-VOCAB. Executable one-liner (count): `assert len([f for f in facts('invariant') if f.source_file=='V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp']) == 22` — a silently smaller universe is the exact defect universe-floors exist to catch (vc:58-71), so the import must also add `(fact universe-floor UF-INVARIANT :family invariant :minimum 92 …)`. Executable one-liner (vocabulary): for every invariant fact, every capitalised token in :text that looks like a declared id must resolve to a model fact OR be listed in an explicit :undeclared-vocabulary field — turning V5-A6/A17 from an invisible gap into a declared one."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact invariant V5I-01 :source-file \"V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp\" :source-line 115 :text \"…\" :scope-subsystem S99)` — must be REJECTED on both paths: kernel-reason 'resolves to no declared subsystem', checker-reason 'L3' (precedent K14 vc:152-154). REPLACE `:source-line 115` with `:source-line \"115\"` — must be REJECTED as a type violation (INTEGER declared), checker-reason 'L1'. DROP one of the 22 imported facts — must be REJECTED by UF-INVARIANT (floor), reason 'universe below floor' (precedent: the floors exist because a coherent deletion previously read as a smaller success, vc:58-61)."
  :rollback "Delete the 22 imported facts and the UF-INVARIANT floor; remove the `invariant` fact type and its enums from MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp and move :version (:37 / ROOT.sexp:9); delete invariants.sexp and re-run build_root.py (ROOT.sexp:12 back to 14 modules); build_deferred.py restores deferred-imports.sexp:22. Because the floor is base-anchored (universe-authorization, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:268-279), lowering it back requires a base-anchored authorization — the rollback of a floor is NOT symmetric with its introduction and must be planned before the import, not after."
