  :current-authority-seat "V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp inline, 7 forms totalling 27 clauses: derivation-independence-trust-root (:87-99, 5 clauses), candidate-id-discipline (:140-145, 2), unregistered-state-event (:148-151, 1), domain-namespace-comparison (:333-345, 6), trusted-issuer-registry-pinning (:367-375, 4), revocation-semantics (:378-383, 3), lifecycle-overlay (:544-553, 6). Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:28 (:source-count 7, DDI-4, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE)."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "NEW:invariants.sexp (shared with the invariant family — a rule and an invariant are the same concept 'named normative constraint' at two grammars) OR NEW:rules.sexp if the decision is that a multi-clause rule is a distinct concept. Recorded as a choice, not resolved: putting rules and invariants in one module is the one-seat reading; splitting them is the grammar reading. Cost either way: a NEW *.sexp under ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/ is auto-classified CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT by classification-rule R-008 (classification-rules.sexp:39-41) and auto-pinned by build_root.py:57 (directory listing), so ROOT.sexp :module-count 14 (ROOT.sexp:12) becomes 15 and every module SHA is re-derived (law L7)."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "NEW `rule` :id-space TOKEN-SPACE :required (source-file source-line) :optional (owner-subsystem) :ref ((owner-subsystem subsystem)) PLUS NEW `rule-clause` :required (rule key text) :types ((rule SYMBOL) (key SYMBOL) (text STRING)) :ref ((rule rule)). Flattening rule is MANDATORY here: each form is a list of nested (clause-key \"prose\") sublists (e.g. V1.5:87-99), and a nested list is not a permitted value kind under L1 (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6) — so the 7 forms become 7 `rule` facts + 27 `rule-clause` facts, one per clause, with the clause key rendered as a colon-stripped plain symbol. Clause ids must be synthesised (<rule>__<key>) because a clause has no name of its own. All 7 rule names are already TOKEN-legal (no keyword ids in this class)."
  :owner "MIXED / partly UNKNOWN — no form carries an :owner. Dossier inferences: S10 for domain-namespace-comparison (:333), trusted-issuer-registry-pinning (:367) and revocation-semantics (:378) (D3 section, MLTP trust root, SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:65-66); S03 for candidate-id-discipline (:140) (D1 section); UNKNOWN for derivation-independence-trust-root (:87 — spans S03's evidence and S10's trust root and neither registry names an owner), unregistered-state-event (:148 — inherits the undetermined owner of StateEventKind, V5-A5) and lifecycle-overlay (:544 — inherits the undetermined owner of LifecycleRecord/1, S04 vs S05, V5-A12). Three of seven owners are UNKNOWN and are not guessed."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — no store declared (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:155-158)."
  :classification "PUBLIC — all seven govern public admission/trust/lifecycle mechanics; the inferred owners S03 and S10 are PUBLIC (subsystems.sexp:7,14). No private member."
  :dependencies ("DECISION: rule/rule-clause family and module (shared with the invariant family question) [schema dependency]" "DDI-2 V1.5-SCHEMAS define-record — 1 symbol reference (dag.json); the clauses in fact name many more record FIELDS (e.g. evidence_issuer, valid_from/valid_to, freshness_policy_ref, revocation_ref, candidate_id, event_ref at V1.5:77-84) which are DDI-2 facts that do not exist yet [field references]" "DDI-2 V1.5-SCHEMAS define-closed-enum — 1 reference [enum-value reference]" "NOT AVAILABLE: LocalTrustState and its field independence_issuer_registry_ref exist only as MLTP prose (MACHINE-LEGAL-TRUST-PROTOCOL.md:869, :1514) and in a SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY :interface string (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:66) — no define-record, no model type (V5-A7); 'MLTP qualification registry' likewise; InstitutionalAct (lifecycle-overlay) exists only in deployment/LAWMAX-LEGAL-IR-SEMANTIC-CONTRACT.md prose [dangling reference targets — two of the seven rules cannot be L3-closed at all]" "NOT AVAILABLE: QUARANTINED / the candidate lifecycle vocabulary (unregistered-state-event, V1.5:150) — V5-A6")
