  :identity-version-rule "ONLY-VERSION — no define-rule of any of these seven names exists in another registry (dossier lineage 'V1.5-only' for all seven; the only sibling define-rule forms in the corpus are V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp:247 casegrammar-split and :251 common-lisp-cognition-usage, different names and different subject matter). INTERNAL duplication instead: candidate-id-discipline's hash formula (V1.5:141) is restated verbatim twice more in the same file at :356 (TrustedIssuerRegistry/1.registry_id) and :456 (C1 records) — one concept, three prose seats inside one registry, with no define-rule owning the other two."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION — two of the seven rules (derivation-independence-trust-root, trusted-issuer-registry-pinning) pin to a type (LocalTrustState) that exists in no registry and no model fact, so they cannot be imported as typed facts and can only be imported as unenforceable prose; that admission is the decision. The other five would be IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL (5 `rule` + 18 `rule-clause` facts) once the family exists."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "MODERATE-HIGH: (i) the content-addressing formula has three prose seats inside V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp alone (:141, :356, :456) and no single content-addressing rule exists anywhere — importing candidate-id-discipline alone canonises one of three statements; (ii) mesh-independence-quorum's 'ONE seat' claim is contradicted by MACHINE-LEGAL-TRUST-PROTOCOL.md:1541-1544 holding an identical text (V5-A16) — the same pattern applies to these rules' MLTP overlaps (MLTP:1509-1514 for trusted-issuer-registry-pinning); (iii) revocation-semantics requires a field ('the issuer declares revocation support') that exists on neither IssuerEntry/1 (V1.5:362-366) nor IndependencePolicy/1 (:411-418) — importing it asserts a constraint over a field that does not exist."
  :requirement "NEW — TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md rows V5R-F7 (:288), V5R-R8 (:289), V5R-F4 (:275), V5R-D3-10 (:260), V5R-C1x (:286), V5R-D1x (:287); none is a model `requirement` fact (V5-A15). UNKNOWN which model requirement, if any, authorises the import."
  :invariant "L1 (the nested clause lists are NOT legal values — this is the hard blocker and the reason a flattening rule is mandatory, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6), L2 (synthesised clause ids must not collide), L3 (rule-clause -> rule, and any typed :about field), L6 (requirement->seat->test->WP for the new facts). Source invariants: :V5I-F7 (V1.5:105), :V5I-D1-unregistered-event (:152), :V5I-D3-domainassertion (:346) each assert the corresponding rule."
  :qualification-test "NEW — QT-DDI4-RULE-CLAUSE-CLOSURE. Executable one-liner: `assert every rule-clause.rule resolves to a rule fact AND count(rule-clause) == 27 AND every rule has >= 1 clause` — the cardinality is the point: a rule imported with its clauses silently dropped would otherwise read as a successful import (the coherent-deletion shape, vc:58-61). No existing model `test` fact covers rules (rtw:30-50)."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact rule-clause derivation-independence-trust-root__ghost :rule no-such-rule :key r7.2 :text \"x\")` — must be REJECTED: kernel-reason 'resolves to no declared rule', checker-reason 'L3'. APPEND a rule fact whose :text value is a nested list, e.g. `(fact rule probe :source-file \"V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp\" :source-line 87 :text (a b))` — must be REJECTED, kernel-reason 'illegal value kind', checker-reason 'MALFORMED-FACT' (precedent X27 vc:172-174 for the keyword case; the nested-list case is the L1 clause at MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6). DROP the 5 clauses of derivation-independence-trust-root while keeping the rule fact — must be REJECTED by the clause cardinality check."
  :rollback "Delete the 7 rule + 27 rule-clause facts; remove the fact types from MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp and move :version (:37 / ROOT.sexp:9); delete the module if created and re-run build_root.py; build_deferred.py restores deferred-imports.sexp:28. Source unedited."
