  :decision-question "Are the two MLTP-anchored rules (derivation-independence-trust-root :87, trusted-issuer-registry-pinning :367) importable as prose while LocalTrustState and the MLTP qualification registry are defined in no registry and no model fact (V5-A7) — or must LocalTrustState be seated as a type (owner S10) first? Who owns each rule (S03 vs S10 for the first; the undetermined owners of StateEventKind and LifecycleRecord/1 for two more)? And which of the three statements of the content-addressing formula (V1.5:141, :356, :456) is the seat?"
  :adjudication-items ("V5-A5 (V1.5 dossier): StateEventKind is an orphan enum with an undeterminable owner — inherited by unregistered-state-event" "V5-A6 (V1.5 dossier): QUARANTINED and the candidate lifecycle vocabulary are undeclared" "V5-A7 (V1.5 dossier): LocalTrustState, MLTP qualification registry, InstitutionalAct, ConflictPolicyBundle — reference targets with no definition anywhere" "V5-A12 (V1.5 dossier): owner of LifecycleRecord/1 and lifecycle-overlay (S04 vs S05)" "V5-A15 (V1.5 dossier): V5R-*/V5Q-* are not model requirement/test facts" "ADJ-MX4-RULE-FAMILY (new): are `rule` and `invariant` one family or two — and, if two, what distinguishes a multi-clause rule from a multi-clause invariant, given both are docstrings at source" "ADJ-MX4-CONTENT-ADDRESS-SEAT (new): the candidate_id formula has three prose seats inside one file (V1.5:141, :356, :456) and no single rule owns it")
