  :cl-native (:immutable-record "NEW `rule` (id, owner-subsystem) + `rule-clause` (rule, key SYMBOL, text STRING) facts, hash-pinned; candidate-id-discipline's identity formula hex(sha256(id_domain‖0x1F‖canonical(BODY))) (V1.5:141-142) IS the content-address rule whose CL seat is journal.lisp:61-86 canon-sexp + :88 sha256-hex (the ONE canonical serialization boundary, LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:34) | invariant: candidate-id-discipline :target 'no ambient/implicit candidate' (V1.5:143-145) + :V5I-A2 | fallback: explicit encoder per record (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:34 fallback)" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart "the :fail-closed clauses yield typed outcome VALUES (INDEPENDENCE_UNKNOWN, 'evidence does NOT count'); a condition only if a bundle verification must abort mid-way — pattern safe-read.lisp:68-70 safe-read-error caught into (values nil :unreadable) at :214 | invariant: revocation-semantics :fail-closed 'treated as UNKNOWN (never silently counted)' (V1.5:382-383); derivation-independence-trust-root :fail-closed (98-99) | fallback: typed error value (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:24)" :macro-dsl "ONLY IF these rules are to be EXECUTED by the engine (not merely anchored): the admitted DSL is `defrule` (legal-inference-engine.lisp:491-506 → a legal-rule class :456-465 with STATIC legality at instantiation :473-489; exemplar legal-event-calculus.lisp:43-64 ec-initiation/ec-clipping/ec-holds) — 'rules as inspectable data' expanded at compile/load time, never over registry bytes | invariant: 'rules are data, not opaque code' (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:26) + 'macros expand at compile time only; NEVER over external bytes' (:25) | fallback: procedural branch (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:26) — NOTE: defrule rule DISCOVERY uses sb-mop:class-direct-subclasses (legal-inference-engine.lisp:514-520) while the contract's MOP row says 'NOT USED in the trusted path — (none)' (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:23) → ADJ-CL4-01" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE" :package-asdf-boundary "NOT-APPLICABLE" :persistent-event "lifecycle-overlay (V1.5:544-553): each transition (:propose/:adopt/:withdraw/:correct/:revoke/:supersede) is an appended LifecycleRecord whose :supersedes is the back-link — journal.lisp:507 chained-append (:back-link/:identity keys :507, stale-chain-link :534-541); trusted-issuer-registry-pinning :update 'monotonic: new registry_id with supersedes = the pinned one' (V1.5:371-372) is the same idiom | invariant: lifecycle-overlay :revocation 'historical records survive; no retroactive identity change' (V1.5:550-551) | fallback: full replay (journal.lisp:544 read-lines)" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE (validity predicates and state overlays, not belief revision)" :temporal-index-projection "lifecycle-overlay 'withdrawn-by-revocation from audit_time forward' (V1.5:550) and the validity windows [valid_from, valid_to] + freshness in derivation-independence-trust-root :validity (V1.5:95-97) are as-of predicates over the bitemporal seat (version-graph.lisp:1030 version-at; legal-temporal.lisp:48-53 date-in-interval-p, half-open) | invariant: :validity 'now in [valid_from, valid_to] AND fresh … AND not revoked' (V1.5:95-97) | fallback: linear scan" :compile-time-validation "the clause-key set of each rule becomes a CLOSED field set (L1: per-rule fact type or a closed enum of clause keys) so a missing/misspelled clause is a typed L1 violation (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:137,157) | invariant: L1 'a parsed-but-ignored field is silent loss' (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:12) | fallback: free text" :runtime-validation "derivation-independence-trust-root :validity/:issuer-scope/:self-issued, trusted-issuer-registry-pinning, revocation-semantics :verify, domain-namespace-comparison are production verifier predicates in the MLTP seat (SEAT-KERNEL-VERIFY seats.sexp:44); their consumer control-domain-partition (V1.5:387-400) is DDI-3 — fail-closed | invariant: :fail-closed clauses (V1.5:98-99, 338-340, 382-383) | fallback: reject" :python-in-cl-risk "YES — 27 clauses as a JSON dict {clause-key: text} per rule, then the 'VALID :=' formula (V1.5:95-97) re-typed as an imperative Python validator in the V1.x-VERIFY lineage (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE files-and-roles.sexp:453). CL-native alternative: clause facts with closed keys (L1) and, where a rule is executable, `defrule`-style declarative patterns whose :where guards are typed :bool at load time (legal-inference-engine.lisp:477-479) and recorded in the proof (:495-496) — the rule is inspectable data, its evaluation is the ONE engine." :future-freedom "CONSTRAINS S10 (trust): two rules bind to LocalTrustState / MLTP qualification registry (V1.5:88-89, 368) which no registry declares (dossier V5-A7). lifecycle-overlay binds InstitutionalAct + event-ledger (existing seats). candidate-id-discipline fixes the content-address formula that compiler B must mirror semantically (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:10-15) — a permanent cross-language constraint by design. No S04/S19/S20 mechanism constraint; no mandatory model.")
  )

(ddi-class V1.5-SCHEMAS__define-gate
  :batch DDI-4 :source-file "V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp" :fact-class "define-gate" :source-count 1 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms (("SA-2-canonical-admission" :line 123 :sha16 "5dd9666348f770b4"))
  :source-file "V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp"
  :source-forms 1
  :current-authority-seat "V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp D1 section, comment ';; F2 — SA-2 canonical-promotion gate. residual_independence_assumption is NEVER an alternative to evidence.' (V1.5:122), form SA-2-canonical-admission at :123-137. Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:21 (:source-count 1, DDI-4, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE). It is the ONLY define-gate form in the whole corpus (classes.md row 15)."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "NEW:invariants.sexp (with the rule/invariant family — the gate is a normative constraint on a state transition) OR dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp (EXISTING) if the decision is to model it as a typed transition beside the `stage`/`stage-edge` graph (dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:5-21). The second option is tempting and WRONG without a ruling: `stage`/`stage-edge` are PIPELINE stages (ACQUIRE..PUBLISH), not record lifecycle states, and L4 acyclicity applies to them; a lifecycle transition ADOPTED->CANONICAL in the same family would silently join two different graphs under one law. Recorded as a choice, not resolved."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "NEW `gate` :id-space TOKEN-SPACE :required (from to) :optional (verify-rule forbids-alternative source-file source-line note) :types ((from SYMBOL) (to SYMBOL) (verify-rule SYMBOL) (forbids-alternative SYMBOL) (source-file STRING) (source-line INTEGER) (note STRING)) :enum ((from lifecycle-state) (to lifecycle-state)) :ref ((verify-rule rule)) PLUS NEW `gate-requires` (:gate ref, :field SYMBOL, :is-value SYMBOL optional) and `gate-disposition` (:gate ref, :state SYMBOL). Flattening rule is MANDATORY: :requires is a list of 5 items one of which is itself a nested list `(divergence_state :is :AGREED)` (V1.5:127), :verify is a list containing one multi-line string (:130-132), :assumption-disposition is a nested pair whose value is a list of three keywords (:134) — none of these is an L1-legal value (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6). The import is therefore 1 `gate` + 5 `gate-requires` + 3 `gate-disposition` facts, with keyword values (:ADOPTED, :CANONICAL, :AGREED, :CANDIDATE, :UNKNOWN, :QUARANTINED) colon-stripped to plain symbols. BLOCKER: a NEW closed enum `lifecycle-state` must be declared to hold those states — and they are declared in NO registry (V5-A6), so its membership would be minted here rather than migrated, which is exactly what the migration is not allowed to do."
  :owner "UNKNOWN — the form carries no owner. Three candidates, none declared: S03 by section (D1 is the ingress/admission delta, V1.5:10-11; ISR:59 registers SemanticAdmissionEvidence/1 to S03); S10 as the verifier of the independence evidence the gate demands (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:65-66); or the adoption seat source/adoption-decision.lisp, which is tracked but appears in NO `seat` fact (seats.sexp) and no SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY :owner string. Since the transition is an institutional adoption act (:adoption_act_ref, V1.5:129; :V5I-09 'InstitutionalAct adoption', :622), S12's approval plane (SEAT-APPROVAL-POLICY seats.sexp:46) is a fourth candidate. Not resolved here."
  :writer "UNKNOWN — this is the one DDI-4 class where NO_WRITER is NOT the honest answer: the gate governs promotion INTO a canonical store, and the model's canonical store for the promoted artefact is legal-ir (stores-and-authorities.sexp:9, :owner SEAT-LEGAL-AST :writer SEAT-WRITE-AUTHORITY). But the source form names no store and no writer, and nothing in the six registries says the SA-2 gate is enforced by SEAT-WRITE-AUTHORITY. Reported UNKNOWN rather than inferred; if the decision is that the gate belongs to the legal-ir write path, the writer is SEAT-WRITE-AUTHORITY and that must be DECLARED, not deduced."
  :classification "PUBLIC — governs promotion of public canonical legal state (legal-ir store, stores-and-authorities.sexp:9); no private member named in the form."
  :dependencies ("FIRST: a closed enum for the candidate lifecycle (CANDIDATE/ADOPTED/CANONICAL/PUBLISHED/QUARANTINED/UNKNOWN) — declared in NO registry (V5-A6); without it :from/:to are unconstrained symbols and the gate is unenforceable [enum dependency, and the enum's membership has no source]" "FIRST: the owner ruling (S03 / S10 / adoption seat / S12) [ownership dependency]" "DDI-4 class 6 (same batch): :verify names the rule derivation-independence-trust-root (V1.5:130-132) — an intra-batch order [typed reference to a `rule` fact]" "DDI-2 V1.5-SCHEMAS define-record — 1 reference (dag.json); in detail the 5 :requires items are FIELDS of SemanticAdmissionEvidence/1 (V1.5:37-40) and derivation_independence_evidence_ref must resolve to a VALID DerivationIndependenceEvidence/1 (:76) [field references, DDI-2 facts that do not exist]" "DDI-2 V1.5-SCHEMAS define-closed-enum DivergenceState :AGREED (V1.5:112) [enum-value reference]")
  :consumers ("DDI-4 class 5 (same batch): :V5I-01 (V1.5:115-120) and :V5I-D1-no-assumption-canonical (:155-159) are the invariants that assert this gate; :V5I-F7-derivation-trust (:105) asserts its verify clause" "DDI-4 class 6: candidate-id-discipline (V1.5:140-145) binds the candidate identity the gate promotes" "deployment/LAWMAX-SECURE-SEMANTIC-INGRESS-CONTRACT.md:178 (F2/R7 prose) — AUTHORED_NORMATIVE_PROSE" "TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:273 (V5R-F2 'define-gate'); PUBLIC-OBSERVATORY-QUALIFICATION-TESTS.md:1104 (V5Q-F2) — predeclared, UNEXECUTED" "legacy: V1.5-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh:323 (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, files-and-roles.sexp:436)" "CANONICAL MODEL: none — no `gate`/`transition` fact type; grep of the 14 modules for 'SA-2' = 0")
  :identity-version-rule "ONLY-VERSION — define-gate occurs once in the whole corpus (classes.md row 15; version-chains.md lists no chain). The model's `stage`/`stage-edge` family (dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:5-21) is NOT a prior version of it: those are pipeline stages, not record lifecycle states, so there is no supersession relation to record."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION — the gate cannot become an L3-closed fact while its :from/:to states are declared nowhere. Two exits: (a) declare the lifecycle enum at SOURCE first (a change to a registry, which the migration does not do), or (b) import the gate as prose with :from/:to as free symbols and accept that the model carries an unenforceable transition. Neither is a mechanical consequence."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "MODERATE. No second define-gate exists. The risk is a NEW duplicate seat created by the import: if the gate is modelled beside `stage`/`stage-edge`, the model gains two meanings of 'transition' in one family; if a `lifecycle-state` enum is minted here, the model becomes the SEAT of a vocabulary that the registries never declared, inverting the migration direction (the model would be authoring, not importing)."
  :requirement "NEW — TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:273 registers V5R-F2 for this form; V5R-F2 is not a model `requirement` fact (rtw:5-28) and is predeclared UNEXECUTED (V5-A15)."
  :invariant "L1 (the nested :requires / :verify / :assumption-disposition lists are not legal values — flattening mandatory; MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6), L3 (:verify-rule must resolve to a declared rule; gate-requires fields must resolve to declared record fields once DDI-2 exists), L2 (synthesised ids). Source invariants: :V5I-01 (V1.5:115), :V5I-D1-no-assumption-canonical (:155), :V5I-F7-derivation-trust (:105)."
  :qualification-test "NEW — QT-DDI4-GATE-NO-ASSUMPTION-PATH. Executable one-liner: `assert no gate-requires or gate-disposition fact of gate SA-2-canonical-admission permits residual_independence_assumption as a :field on the path to :to CANONICAL, and gate.forbids-alternative == residual_independence_assumption` — i.e. the structural claim of :V5I-D1-no-assumption-canonical (V1.5:155-159) is checked as data rather than asserted in prose. No existing model `test` fact covers it (rtw:30-50)."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact gate-disposition SA-2-canonical-admission__CANONICAL :gate SA-2-canonical-admission :state CANONICAL)` — must be REJECTED: it would place the assumption-only disposition on the CANONICAL state, which the gate forbids; reason 'assumption disposition names a state outside (CANDIDATE UNKNOWN QUARANTINED)'. APPEND `(fact gate probe :from ADOPTED :to PUBLISHED :verify-rule no-such-rule)` — must be REJECTED: kernel-reason 'resolves to no declared rule', checker-reason 'L3'. REPLACE `:to CANONICAL` with `:to :CANONICAL` — must be REJECTED, checker-reason 'MALFORMED-FACT' (keyword value, precedent X27 vc:172-174)."
  :rollback "Delete the 1 gate + 5 gate-requires + 3 gate-disposition facts and the `lifecycle-state` enum from MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp; move the schema :version (:37 / ROOT.sexp:9); re-run build_root.py and build_deferred.py (deferred-imports.sexp:21 restored). Source unedited."
  :batch-reason "DDI-4 because build_deferred.py:101 maps `define-gate` to DDI-4. AGREES — its single recorded out-edge is to DDI-2 define-record (dag.json) and no order violation names it as a target. Intra-batch constraint: it must follow class 6 (its :verify-rule) and precede nothing."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "Where is the candidate lifecycle state machine (CANDIDATE/ADOPTED/CANONICAL/PUBLISHED/QUARANTINED/UNKNOWN) seated as a closed enum, given it is declared in no registry — and does minting it in the model invert the migration direction? Which seat owns the gate (S03 ingress, S10 verifier, source/adoption-decision.lisp which has no seat fact, or S12 approval)? Is 'PUBLISHED machine-reliance' (V1.5:136-137) a state of the same machine or of the static-site store?"
  :adjudication-items ("V5-A6 (V1.5 dossier): the gate's own :from/:to states are declared in no closed enum" "V5-A15 (V1.5 dossier): V5R-F2 / V5Q-F2 are predeclared UNEXECUTED, not model facts" "ADJ-MX4-GATE-OWNER (new): four candidate owners, none declared; source/adoption-decision.lisp is tracked but has no `seat` fact (seats.sexp) — importing the gate with an inferred owner would create a seat by inference" "ADJ-MX4-GATE-WRITER (new): the gate governs promotion into the legal-ir store (stores-and-authorities.sexp:9) but no source form binds it to SEAT-WRITE-AUTHORITY — writer UNKNOWN, and a guess here would silently extend a write authority")
  :topological-position 10 :atomic-groups (10)
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "NEW `gate` fact (:from/:to symbols of a lifecycle-state enum, :verify-rule ref to the C6 rule fact, :forbids-alternative field SYMBOL) + `gate-requires` facts (:gate, :field, optional :value from DivergenceState) + `gate-disposition` facts — hash-pinned; the gate's subject is content-addressed (candidate-id-discipline V1.5:140-145) so it binds an immutable candidate | invariant: :V5I-01 (V1.5:115-120) + :V5I-D1-no-assumption-canonical (155-160) | fallback: prose in the D1 contract (LAWMAX-SECURE-SEMANTIC-INGRESS-CONTRACT.md, named V1.5:11)" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE (no invariant requires dispatch on assurance profile; the per-profile decision is a data table — the cardinality matrix V1.5:45-62, DDI-2)" :condition-restart "gate failure ⇒ QUARANTINED VALUE (:V5I-01 'a schema-valid but wrong SA-2 event is QUARANTINED' V1.5:119-120); NO restart is admissible — a restart offering 'use the assumption' would be the structural error the gate exists to exclude (:forbids-alternative V1.5:133) | invariant: :V5I-D1-no-assumption-canonical 'contains NO assumption alternative' (V1.5:155-160) | fallback: typed error value" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE (the gate is a data table evaluated by a generic evaluator; no invariant requires a `define-gate` macro in the image; registry forms are DATA read under *read-eval* nil (deferred-imports.sexp:4; ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:56; safe-read.lisp:152-165) — never a macro expanded over the registry file)" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE" :package-asdf-boundary "NOT-APPLICABLE" :persistent-event "the ADOPTED→CANONICAL transition is itself a journaled adoption event (adoption_act_ref REQUIRED, V1.5:129) through the ONE write seat (write-authority.lisp:53 with-write-authority; adoption-decision.lisp:85 record-adoption!) | invariant: V6I-08 'journaled adoption + rollback' (V1.6:41-42) + :V5I-09 | fallback: replay" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE" :compile-time-validation "gate-time: every gate-requires :field must be a declared field of SemanticAdmissionEvidence/1 (V1.5:33-41) with SA-2 cardinality :R or :C in the matrix (V1.5:45-62, DDI-2) — an L3 closed ref to a record-field fact; :forbids-alternative must NOT occur among gate-requires (define-conditional :forbid, ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:26-30) | invariant: :V5I-D1-no-assumption-canonical 'STRUCTURAL' (V1.5:156) | fallback: prose review" :runtime-validation ":verify (V1.5:130-132): resolve derivation_independence_evidence_ref and VERIFY signature / issuer in qualification registry / scope / freshness / revocation / candidate binding — a production verifier in the MLTP seat (SEAT-KERNEL-VERIFY seats.sexp:44); presence of the reference is NOT sufficient (R7.6) | invariant: :V5I-F7 'the gate VERIFIES the evidence, not merely the presence of a reference' (V1.5:108) | fallback: reject (fail-closed) — a source seat for the ADOPTED/CANONICAL/CANDIDATE/QUARANTINED states: NOT FOUND (adoption-decision.lisp exposes can-adopt :23 / record-adoption! :85 only; grep 'SA-2|:ADOPTED' over source/ and systems/ = no hit)" :python-in-cl-risk "YES — the nested :requires item (divergence_state :is :AGREED) and :assumption-disposition (:candidate-only (...)) are flattened into strings or silently dropped (L1 forbids nested lists, ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:6), and the :verify prose becomes an imperative Python function. CL-native alternative: one `gate-requires` fact per requirement (:field ref + optional :value validated against the DivergenceState enum), the disposition as a closed enum, and the verifier obligation as an L3 ref to the C6 rule fact derivation-independence-trust-root — all validated by the kernel's generic ref/enum paths." :future-freedom "CONSTRAINS the ADMIT stage (dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:7 stage ADMIT; edges :15 ACQUIRE→ADMIT and :16 ADMIT→IR) to evidence-only promotion — no S04/S19/JTMS mechanism constraint; it STRENGTHENS V8I-02 (no proposer can promote). Precondition: the lifecycle states ADOPTED/CANONICAL/CANDIDATE/UNKNOWN/QUARANTINED are declared in no registry (dossier V5-A6) — importing the gate forces that enum to be seated first (ADJ-CL4-11).")
  )

