  :owner "S01 — evidence: SR:36 ':interface \"CensusSpaceClassification/1 + census-coverage-decision\"' (S01 define-subsystem SR:35-37); model subsystem S01 PUBLIC owner-seat SEAT-COVERAGE-LEDGER (AM/subsystems.sexp:5; DESIGN_TARGET, AM/seats.sexp:77-78, packet WP-01). NOT a fact of the form itself (no :owner key, V1.5:229-245); the dossier's S01 is the same interface-string inference."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — the form is a normative decision table, not a store; no registry names an executing seat. The store whose values it decides (coverage-ledger) has writer SEAT-COVERAGE-OWNER (AM/stores-and-authorities.sexp:6, DESIGN_TARGET AM/seats.sexp:83-84) — an inference, not a declaration; not asserted as the writer of this fact."
  :classification "PUBLIC — S01 PUBLIC (AM/subsystems.sexp:5); output enum census_coverage_state is the frozen public v1.4 state (V1.5:182-185); all 8 input enums are public D2/R3 dimensions (V1.5:111-113,169-173,186-189,217-224); no private member."
  :dependencies "(1) DDI-2 V1.5-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum — enum-value refs of every condition and of :result: DivergenceState V1.5:111, observation_state :186, availability_state :188, acquisition_state :217, validation_state :219, admission_obligation_state :221, negative_evidence_validity :223, enumerability_class :169 (dag.json edge V1.5 define-decision-function -> V1.5 define-frozen-enum-reference =1; the closed-enum refs are string matches inside clauses, not head-level symbols); (2) DDI-2 V1.5-SCHEMAS__define-frozen-enum-reference census_coverage_state V1.5:182-185 — :output ref-target; also V1.7:258 define-reference census_coverage_state (dag.json edge -> V1.7 define-reference =1); (3) SCHEMA: enum/enum-value fact family (ADJ-DDI3-ENUM-1) — without it no L3 closure; (4) decision-input binding declared as data (V1.5:230 vs the enum lines above; V1.5 dossier unknown #5); (5) L6: requirement V5R-B1 / test V5Q-B1 (TM:284; QT:1110) are NOT model facts (AM/requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:5-50); (6) LINEAGE: V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-decision-function (V1.7:259-279) — the same concept, divergent."
  :consumers "SR:36 S01 :interface string (IMPORTED class; the model dropped :interface at import, orchestrator N15, so no L3 obligation today); :V5I-04 V1.5:246-253 and :V5I-05 V1.5:254-260 (DDI-4) restate the clauses; V1.7:259-260 names it in :supersedes; SUPERSEDED-REGISTER.md:257-258; V1.7-ARCHITECTURE-IDEA-SURVIVAL-LEDGER.md:13 (row 1, EXTEND); TM:284 V5R-B1; QT:1110 V5Q-B1 (UNEXECUTED, QT:1119); V1.5-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, AM/files-and-roles.sexp:436). Model: stage CENSUS (AM/dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:6) binds no function; 0 canonical-model consumers."
  :identity-version-rule "id = `census-coverage-decision` (TOKEN charset OK, AM/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:17,41). Versions: V1.5:229 -> V1.7:259 SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT: V1.7:260 ':supersedes' declared; divergences — new guard clause 4 (V1.7:269), ':availability :PUBLIC_PRESENT' added to the INGESTED clause (V1.7:272 vs V1.5:238-240), ':negative_evidence :VALID_AUTHORITATIVE_FRESH' (V1.7:274) replaces ':FRESH_QUALIFYING' (V1.5:242), key ':ordered-clauses' (V1.5:232) renamed ':clauses' (V1.7:263), ':total t :single-valued t' added (V1.7:279), precedence text changed (V1.5:245 vs V1.7:278). No V1.6 or V1.8 form (classes.md rows 18,42; version-chains.md has no entry because the names differ). ALSO LIVE-REFERENCE-TARGET: SR:36 and TM:284 still name the V1.5 id; TM:367 names the -v7 id."
