  :falsifier "(fact falsifier D3-01-DECISION-RESULT-NOT-IN-ENUM :harness COMPONENT :intent \"a decision clause whose result renames the frozen coverage state\" :mutation APPEND :module \"decision-functions.sexp\" :form \"(fact decision-clause census-coverage-decision__C7 :decision census-coverage-decision :ordinal 7 :result PRESENT :otherwise NO)\" :kernel-reason \"resolves to no declared enum-value\" :checker-reason \"L3\") — PRESENT is the rename :V5I-05 forbids (V1.5:255-256); requires the enum-value family."
  :rollback "Drop the `decision*` facts (or the whole NEW module) and re-run build_root.py so ROOT.sexp pins the previous module set (L7, AM/ROOT.sexp:12-28); flip AM/deferred-imports.sexp:19 back to DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT (build_deferred.py IMPORTED map :60-79); the source form stays AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE. No existing module references decision facts, so rollback has no inbound-ref fallout."
  :batch-reason "DDI-3 by the BATCH map (AM/build_deferred.py:98 'define-decision-function':'DDI-3'; ledger AM/deferred-imports.sexp:19 'cognition graph / decision / projection layer'). Dependency evidence AGREES with DDI-2 -> DDI-3 ordering (all inputs are DDI-2 enums), with two caveats: an IMPORTED class already names it (SR:36; dag-fragment.md order violation 'SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:35 S01 -> V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp:229') and no batch imports the V5R-*/V5Q-* requirement universe it needs for L6 (orchestrator N1/N8)."
