  :decision-question "Which census-coverage decision is the ONE canonical seat — census-coverage-decision (V1.5:229-245) or census-coverage-decision-v7 (V1.7:259-279, ':supersedes' at V1.7:260; SUPERSEDED-REGISTER.md:257-258)? If V1.7: are SR:36 (S01 :interface) and :V5I-04 (V1.5:246) re-pointed or retired, and is the V1.5 form imported as a historical version or skipped with proof? In either case: which enum declares V1.7's ':VALID_AUTHORITATIVE_FRESH' (V1.7:274; negative_evidence_validity V1.5:223-224 has only FRESH_QUALIFYING/INSUFFICIENT/EXPIRED/ABSENT/UNKNOWN), and is the 8-input→8-enum binding (V1.5:230) declared as `decision-input` data?"
  :adjudication-items ("V5-A2 (superseded decision kept live: SR:36 names V1.5 id; V1.7:260 supersedes)" "V5-A3 / ADJ-V17-DF-2 (V1.7:274 :VALID_AUTHORITATIVE_FRESH is a member of no enum)" "ADJ-V17-DF-1 (canonical coverage decision = V1.5:229 or V1.7:259)" "V5-A15 (V5R-*/V5Q-* universe not in model — L6 for every V1.5 fact)" "ADJ-V18-AGG-2 (one fact family for all three DDI-3 decision dialects: V1.5/V1.7 define-decision-function vs V1.8 define-reliance-aggregation)" "ADJ-DDI3-INPUT-1: the 8 decision inputs (V1.5:230) bind to enums only by naming convention (V1.5 dossier unknown #5) — a `decision-input :enum` declaration must be authored, by whom?" "ADJ-DDI3-MOD-1: module NAME for the DDI-3 function layer is stated three ways by the dossiers — 'decisions-and-projections.sexp' (V1.5 dossier) vs 'decision-functions' (V1.7 and V1.8 dossiers) vs 'cognition-graph' (V1.8 dossier, for the graph) — one name per module must be fixed once; every NEW module is auto-classified CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT by AM/classification-rules.sexp:39-41 (R-008) and must be pinned in AM/ROOT.sexp:12-28 (:module-count 14 today) under L7." "ADJ-DDI3-ENUM-1: no enum / enum-value fact family exists in AM/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:84-288 (34 fact types); every DDI-3 clause value, :output, :failure, :order and :result-when-insufficient is an enum member of a DDI-2 define-closed-enum / define-frozen-enum-reference form. Until DDI-2 seats enums as facts, DDI-3 values can only be bare SYMBOLs with no L3 closure (KERNEL:196-210 checks :ref targets only)." "ADJ-DDI3-EXEC-1 (= dossier ADJ-V18-EXEC-1, widened to every DDI-3 class): the only program that has ever executed a DDI-3 contract is V1.8-VERIFY.py / V1.5-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, AM/files-and-roles.sexp:436,453; AM/LEGACY-AUDIT-DISPOSITION.md:10 'never a blocking or sufficient acceptance gate'); the model's harness universe executes laws L1-L7 only (AM/verification-corpus.sexp:24-58,122-125; KERNEL:346). Which harness (existing COMPONENT harness with new schema-derived checks, or a NEW harness fact) executes imported decision/graph contracts, or are they imported as inert data with a declared reason?")
