  :dependencies "(1) V1.5-SCHEMAS__define-algorithm control-domain-partition V1.5:387 — invoked at V1.5:425 (same batch; dag.json edge = 1); (2) DDI-2 V1.5-SCHEMAS__define-record IndependencePolicy/1 V1.5:411-418 fields quorum(.n), required_distinct_dimensions, prohibited_shared_dimensions, unknown_handling, min_independence_assurance (V1.5:424-431) — field refs; `quorum-spec` (V1.5:418) has no definition seat (V1.5 dossier unknown); (3) DDI-2 closed-enum unknown_handling V1.5:403-405 (:FAIL_CLOSED at V1.5:429); (4) SCHEMA: an independence-result enum declaring INDEPENDENCE_UNKNOWN (V5-A17; also used at V1.5:99,290,340,342,350,435 and MLTP/THREAT-MODEL) — none exists; (5) L6: V5R-D3-12 / V5Q-D3-12 (TM:262; QT:1098) not model facts."
  :consumers ":V5I-06 V1.5:433-436 and :V5I-07 V1.5:437-440 (DDI-4); MLTP.md:1540-1546 (restates the predicate); V1.7-ARCHITECTURE-IDEA-SURVIVAL-LEDGER.md:31 (row 19, REUSE, WP-06); TM:262 V5R-D3-12, TM:289 V5R-R8 ('MLTP quorum τετρα-συζευκτικό'); QT:1098 V5Q-D3-12; V1.5-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh:208-209 (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE). 0 canonical-model consumers."
  :identity-version-rule "id = `mesh-independence-quorum` (TOKEN OK). ONLY-VERSION (define-quorum-predicate exists only in V1.5, classes.md row 20). :was names the replaced v1.4 predicate `distinct-valid-kids` (V1.5:422; MLTP.md:1541) which has no registry form — a historical name, not a version."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION — the body is only importable as a joined STRING; the result token has no enum; the 'ONE seat' claim (V1.5:420) is contradicted by the identical MLTP.md:1540-1546 text; importing creates a third copy unless the institutional seat is decided."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "Two normative texts already exist for one predicate (V1.5:421-432 CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT vs MLTP.md:1540-1546 AUTHORED_NORMATIVE_PROSE, AM/files-and-roles.sexp:438,406); a model `predicate` fact would be the third. No model id collides."
  :requirement "R-130 (S10, AM/requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:76). Source V5R-D3-12 (TM:262) / V5R-R8 (TM:289) NOT model facts — NEW."
  :invariant "L1 (no control characters; symbol rendering), L3 (:algorithm, :policy-type refs). Source guards: :V5I-06 V1.5:433-436 (distinct kid ≠ independence; insufficient ⇒ INDEPENDENCE_UNKNOWN) and :V5I-D3-unknown V1.5:406-409. No model law can evaluate the predicate body."
  :qualification-test "Existing: Q28 (:76). Source: V5Q-D3-12 (QT:1098 'quorum-predicate fixtures counting components') UNEXECUTED. NEW executable statement: T-DDI3-QUORUM-COMPONENTS — with a fixture of N actors in K control-domain components (from T-DDI3-PARTITION-DETERMINISTIC) and policy.quorum.n, the predicate holds iff K >= n and required dimensions are covered and no prohibited dimension is shared; under unknown_handling FAIL_CLOSED an actor with UNKNOWN evidence never raises K."
  :falsifier "(fact falsifier D3-03-RETIRED-PREDICATE-REENTERS :harness COMPONENT :intent \"the replaced v1.4 predicate distinct-valid-kids re-bound as the partition\" :mutation REPLACE :module \"decision-functions.sexp\" :replace-from \":algorithm control-domain-partition :policy-type IndependencePolicy/1\" :replace-to \":algorithm distinct-valid-kids :policy-type IndependencePolicy/1\" :kernel-reason \"resolves to no declared algorithm\" :checker-reason \"L3\") — distinct-valid-kids is exactly what V1.5:420 says the seat 'replaces'."
  :rollback "Drop the `predicate` fact, rebuild ROOT.sexp (L7), flip AM/deferred-imports.sexp:24 back to DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT; no inbound model refs; MLTP.md:1540-1546 remains the prose seat exactly as today."
  :batch-reason "DDI-3 by BATCH map (AM/build_deferred.py:98 'define-quorum-predicate':'DDI-3'; ledger :24). AGREES: dependencies are the same-batch algorithm and DDI-2 record/enum forms."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "Where is the ONE normative seat of the mesh-independence quorum predicate after import — the model `predicate` fact (with MLTP.md:1540-1546 demoted to a `rationale` anchor), or MLTP.md §15 (with the model carrying only a pointer), given V1.5:420 'ONE seat' and MLTP.md:1477 'Μία quorum έδρα' while both texts exist today (V5-A16)? And which closed enum declares the result token INDEPENDENCE_UNKNOWN (V1.5:432; V5-A17)?"
  :adjudication-items ("V5-A16 (duplicate statement of the 'ONE seat' predicate: V1.5:421-432 vs MLTP.md:1540-1546)" "V5-A17 (INDEPENDENCE_UNKNOWN / UNVERIFIED_FOR_MACHINE_RELIANCE in no closed enum)" "V5-A15 (V5R-D3-12 / V5Q-D3-12 not model facts)" "ADJ-DDI3-OWN-1 (owner S10 vs S11, shared with define-algorithm)" "ADJ-DDI3-HELPER-1: independence-evidence-valid / distinct-components / covers / no-prohibited-shared-dimension (V1.5:423-430) are defined nowhere — define, or accept the :now body as opaque?" "ADJ-DDI3-STEP-1 (inert prose strings as canonical values)" "ADJ-DDI3-EXEC-1 (= dossier ADJ-V18-EXEC-1, widened to every DDI-3 class): the only program that has ever executed a DDI-3 contract is V1.8-VERIFY.py / V1.5-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, AM/files-and-roles.sexp:436,453; AM/LEGACY-AUDIT-DISPOSITION.md:10 'never a blocking or sufficient acceptance gate'); the model's harness universe executes laws L1-L7 only (AM/verification-corpus.sexp:24-58,122-125; KERNEL:346). Which harness (existing COMPONENT harness with new schema-derived checks, or a NEW harness fact) executes imported decision/graph contracts, or are they imported as inert data with a declared reason?" "ADJ-DDI3-MOD-1: module NAME for the DDI-3 function layer is stated three ways by the dossiers — 'decisions-and-projections.sexp' (V1.5 dossier) vs 'decision-functions' (V1.7 and V1.8 dossiers) vs 'cognition-graph' (V1.8 dossier, for the graph) — one name per module must be fixed once; every NEW module is auto-classified CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT by AM/classification-rules.sexp:39-41 (R-008) and must be pinned in AM/ROOT.sexp:12-28 (:module-count 14 today) under L7.")
  :topological-position 41 :atomic-groups ()
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "`predicate` fact (id, was, result-when-insufficient) — the :now body (V1.5:423-431) cannot be a model value except as an opaque string (dossier); the CL-native form is the FOUR conjuncts (|INDEP| >= n, covers, no-prohibited-shared-dimension, FAIL_CLOSED exclusion) as four `predicate-conjunct` facts referencing the IndependencePolicy/1 fields they read (V1.5:412-418) | invariant: 'ONE seat' (V1.5:420; MACHINE-LEGAL-TRUST-PROTOCOL.md:1477 'Μία quorum έδρα') — today two textual seats (V5-A16); a structured record makes the second prose copy derivable rather than authored | fallback: opaque string value + rationale pointer" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart "NOT-APPLICABLE" :macro-dsl "the τετρα-συζευκτική predicate (MLTP.md:1542) as an inspectable data conjunction evaluated by ONE evaluator — the pattern of legal-inference-engine.lisp:491 defrule (:when support list, :unless defeaters) where the rule is data, NOT a runtime parse of the :now string and NOT cl:read/eval of it (contract:35; safe-read.lisp:6-8 'Κανένα bare read') | invariant: contract:26 'rules are data, not opaque code'; one quorum seat | fallback: procedural `and` of four plain functions" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE" :package-asdf-boundary "S10 package — same UNKNOWN code seat as control-domain-partition (SEAT-KERNEL-VERIFY seats.sexp:44-45 holds no quorum code; grep = 0; CL-DDI3-A4); the helper predicates independence-evidence-valid / distinct-components / covers / no-prohibited-shared-dimension are 'defined nowhere' (dossier) and must be exported from that one package | invariant: contract:31; one seat | fallback: monolith package" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE" :temporal-index-projection "VALID := fresh AND non-revoked ... (V1.5:423-424) is as-of an explicit instant against evidence_freshness (V1.5:415) via legal-temporal.lisp:28-46; the verdict carries its as-of | invariant: determinism of the quorum verdict per (members, evidence, policy, as-of); revocation fail-closed (THREAT-MODEL.md:47) | fallback: recompute at query time" :compile-time-validation "L1 closed-enum membership of :result-when-insufficient at model build (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:18 'an out-of-domain value is L1') — FAILS TODAY: :INDEPENDENCE_UNKNOWN (V1.5:432) is in no closed enum (V5-A17); plus L3 refs of the four conjuncts into the IndependencePolicy/1 fields (quorum, required_distinct_dimensions, prohibited_shared_dimensions, unknown_handling V1.5:412-418) | invariant: L1/L3; the build makes V5-A17 structurally visible | fallback: runtime check" :runtime-validation "unknown_handling dispatch inside the one evaluator over the closed enum (:FAIL_CLOSED | :DEGRADE, V1.5:403-405): under :FAIL_CLOSED no UNKNOWN member is counted in INDEP (V1.5:430-431); insufficient evidence ⇒ the declared result VALUE, never a pass | invariant: :V5I-06 (V1.5:433-436) + :V5I-D3-unknown (V1.5:406-409) | fallback: always FAIL_CLOSED" :python-in-cl-risk "HIGH. The :now field is pseudo-code in a string (V1.5:423-431); a naive import stores it and someone later 'parses' it or writes a boolean function beside it — which is already the state of play: MACHINE-LEGAL-TRUST-PROTOCOL.md:1540-1545 restates the predicate as a second authored text (V5-A16). CL-native alternative: four `predicate-conjunct` facts + one evaluator; the :now string survives only as a `rationale` (doc, anchor) pointer (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:182-184), and MLTP §15 becomes a rendering of the facts, not a second seat." :future-freedom "S04/S19/JTMS: NONE. S20 / V8I-02: NONE (trust layer, no model). Freedom-reducing by OMISSION: the four helper predicates are undefined anywhere, so whoever implements first fixes MLTP §10 semantics without a registry seat; and the result token :INDEPENDENCE_UNKNOWN is undeclared (V5-A17) — importing the string as-is would freeze an undeclared vocabulary into the model.")
  )

