the :hash-bearing graph is the JTMS justification skeleton (class 2) | invariant: recomputation deterministic + replayable (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:29); projections carry no identity (V1.5:484-486) | fallback: full recompute (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:29)" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE (SubjectCurrentStatus is a fold in time but the classification only names it :derived; the fold seat is class 2)" :compile-time-validation "build-time set equality: ref-bearing fields of the C1 records == classified rows (V1.5:566-568), plus L4 acyclicity over :hash-bearing edges and L3 closure of every target (9 targets are undeclared today: AuthorityBasis, ConflictPolicyBundle, InstitutionalAct, Evidence, Norm, Fact, anchor, scope, StatementTargetKind-as-target — V5-A7/V5-A9) | invariant: V5I-C1-acyclic; L3 closed typed references (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:24-25) | fallback: runtime check (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:32)" :runtime-validation "at construction: a :hash-bearing ref must resolve to an ALREADY-constructed immutable id before the body is hashed (V1.5:512-514, :523-525; order = define-construction-order legal-ir-interpretive V1.5:597-609, DDI-1) | invariant: relation constructed after both endpoints exist (V5I-C1-relation-detached V1.5:522-525) | fallback: reject (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:35)" :python-in-cl-risk "MEDIUM. Naive import: list of tuples with STRING targets ('AuthorityBasis', 'anchor') and a string kind; the acyclicity audit then re-parses field names by regex. CL-native: one fact per row (ref-class :record TYPE :field FIELD :kind HASH_BEARING|DETACHED|DERIVED :target TYPE-or-enum) with :record/:field/:target L3-closed refs; acyclicity computed by the kernel's generic