  :consumers (":V5I-C1-acyclic (V1.5:610-616, DDI-4) — 'Claim is built before Argument (legal-ir-interpretive)' (:615)" "deployment/LAWMAX-LEGAL-IR-SEMANTIC-CONTRACT.md §12 (:199-200 per dossier V1.5)" "TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:272 V5R-F1 ('ρητή construction order (Claim πριν Argument)'); PUBLIC-OBSERVATORY-QUALIFICATION-TESTS.md:1103 V5Q-F1 (predeclared, UNEXECUTED)" "no canonical-model consumer (0 hits for 'legal-ir-interpretive' in ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/*.sexp)")
  :identity-version-rule "ONLY-VERSION of the NAME legal-ir-interpretive (no other registry defines it; version-chains.md has no entry). SAME HEAD, DIFFERENT GRAMMAR as V1.6:217 / V1.7:80 cognition orders — numbered `(n Name)` pairs vs `(:stage ID :in :out :seat :symbolic-only)` plists (V5-A10): a head chain, not a name chain; no later version supersedes this form. Id: the atomic name is TOKEN-legal; per-step ids must be synthesised (`legal-ir-interpretive__01` …)."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION — (a) the fact-family/grammar decision V5-A10; (b) the 7 DDI-2 records and 3 DDI-3 projections must be facts first (L3); (c) steps 2 and 5 name undeclared external ids (V5-A7). After those: IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL (this is the only seat of the C1 construction order)."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "If imported into `stage`/`stage-edge` it would be a second, unrelated graph inside the pipeline family (dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:5-21; ADJ-V17-CO-1 raises the same for the cognition orders). The order is also restated in prose inside :V5I-C1-acyclic (V1.5:615) and Legal-IR §12 — prose, not a second fact seat."
  :requirement "NEW — V5R-F1 (TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:272) and V5R-C1-05..08 (:263-266) are not model requirement facts (V5-A15); S04's model requirement R-129 (req-map S04__WP-08 requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:70) does not name a construction order."
  :invariant "L4 (acyclicity of every from/to relation — the model's only enforcement shape for an order) + L3; source :V5I-C1-acyclic (V1.5:610-616)."
  :qualification-test "NEW — V5Q-F1 (PUBLIC-OBSERVATORY-QUALIFICATION-TESTS.md:1103: 'inject a ClaimRecord→ArgumentRecord back-edge ⇒ cycle detected') is predeclared UNEXECUTED and not a model test. Executable statement: the construction-edge graph over construction-step is acyclic and every step :target resolves to a declared type or projection fact."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact construction-edge legal-ir-interpretive__07__06 :from legal-ir-interpretive__07 :to legal-ir-interpretive__06)` (Argument→Claim back-edge, the V5Q-F1 mutation) — kernel-reason 'cycle in the construction-edge graph over construction-step', checker-reason 'L4' (mirrors FX-L4-PIPELINE-CYCLE verification-corpus.sexp:32-33 and X29 :179-181). REPLACE `:target CanonRule/1` of step 1 with `:target ConflictPolicyBundle` — must be rejected 'resolves to no declared type' (L3) until that id has a seat."
  :rollback "Delete the imported facts and any new fact-type/field declaration from MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp (schema-version must move, X74-X76 verification-corpus.sexp:354-372); re-run build_root.py so ROOT.sexp pins the restored modules (L7); build_deferred.py regenerates the ledger row as DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT :batch DDI-1. The source registry is never edited (authority stays AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE until the batch is independently reviewed, deferred-imports.sexp:73-76)."
  :batch-reason "DDI-1 by build_deferred.py:90 (head define-construction-order → 'pipeline+authority topology'). DISAGREES: the form references 7 DDI-2 records and 3 DDI-3 projections (dag.json out-edges; dag-fragment.md:39,79) plus two undeclared external ids — nothing in DDI-1 can close it before DDI-2 and DDI-3 content exists."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "(a) One fact family for define-construction-order across V1.5 (numbered record order) and V1.6/V1.7 (typed :stage plists), or two (V5-A10)? (b) May steps 2 (ConflictPolicyBundle) and 5 (statement) reference ids that have no seat in any registry or the model (V5-A7) — seat them as types (owner? file?) or admit a typed external-reference fact class? (c) Is DDI-1 an import GATE (then this class must move after DDI-2/DDI-3) or a grouping (then the batch order is not a dependency order)?"
  :adjudication-items ("V5-A7" "V5-A10" "V5-A15" "ADJ-MX1-CO5-1 (new): batch placement DISAGREES with dependency evidence (7 DDI-2 + 3 DDI-3 references from a DDI-1 class)")
  :topological-position 17 :atomic-groups ()
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "The 9 ordered record kinds are hash-bearing immutable bodies (V1.5:598 'immutable; refs only AuthorityBasis/anchors'; :V5I-A2-immutable-id V1.5:554); a construction order over content-addressed records IS the dependency order of their identities — an object can only be hashed after everything it references exists (journal.lisp:507 chained-append :identity :hash; canon-sexp journal.lisp:61) | invariant: :V5I-C1-acyclic (V1.5:610-616) 'the content-addressing dependency graph over ALL hash-bearing ref fields … is ACYCLIC'; contract L27 'identity = content-address; lifecycle detached' | fallback: copy-on-write; keep prior version" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart "typed condition `construction-order-violation` (from-kind, to-kind, ref-field) when a hash-bearing ref would target an unbuilt identity; no restart that fabricates the dependency | invariant: :V5I-C1-acyclic 'Any cycle … ⇒ kill (V5KW-C1-9)'; contract L24 | fallback: typed error value (fail-closed)" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE" :package-asdf-boundary "Owner S04 (V1.6:97 declares the canonical seat of 'v1.5 C1 records' as legal-ast.lisp + LAWMAX-LEGAL-IR-SEMANTIC-CONTRACT.md; seats.sexp:32 SEAT-LEGAL-AST; package :orchestrator.legal-ast legal-ast.lisp:57). The order is Legal-IR SEMANTICS and therefore must remain language-independent data that compiler B (Rust, WP-05) can read — no CL mechanism (class precedence, load order, ASDF :serial) may become the seat of the order | invariant: contract §1 (L10-15) 'no CL mechanism may leak into the IR contract such that a non-Lisp compiler cannot conform'; §3 (L42-44) | fallback: monolith package" :persistent-event "Step 9 LifecycleRecord/1 (V1.5:606 'detached overlay keyed to any immutable subject') is an EVENT over an identity, journal-shaped: appended, hash-chained, never mutating the subject (journal.lisp:507 chained-append; memory.lisp:79 record-episode :prev) | invariant: contract L27 'lifecycle detached (v1.5 R2)'; V1.5 define-rule lifecycle-overlay (V1.5:544, DDI-4) | fallback: full replay" :truth-maintenance-dependency "Steps 10-12 are DERIVED projections over (7),(3),(9) (V1.5:607-609): dependency-directed recomputation targets — a projection is a JTMS-style consequent of its base records so that a new ArgumentRecord/CanonPolicy/LifecycleRecord recomputes exactly the dependent projection (legal-inference-engine.lisp:227 jtms, :347 recompute-beliefs; corpus-diff.lisp:66 corpus-diff for deltas) | invariant: contract L29 'recomputation is deterministic + replayable'; L28 'belief revision is monotone-audited' | fallback: full recompute of the three projections" :temporal-index-projection "Step 12 SubjectCurrentStatus (V1.5:609, define-projection V1.5:540 DDI-3) is a current-time projection over the LifecycleRecord/1 overlay — the same shape as version-graph's bitemporal text-version (version-graph.lisp:7, :221) where valid-time is a PROJECTION (version-graph.lisp:334) | invariant: valid-time vs recorded-time separation (version-graph.lisp:7); :V5I-C1-relation-detached (V1.5:522) | fallback: full scan of the overlay" :compile-time-validation "Kernel-law time: (i) every step target is a declared id (L3, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:24-25) — steps 2 ConflictPolicyBundle and 5 statement are UNDECLARED today (dossier V5-A7: CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.4.md:871 prose / LAWMAX-LEGAL-IR-SEMANTIC-CONTRACT.md:55) so L3 cannot close; (ii) the order is CONSISTENT with the typed ref graph (define-ref-classification V1.5:569, DDI-2) — i.e. derived by topological sort and compared, never authored twice | invariant: L3 + L4 (acyclicity of every from/to relation); V1.8:266 VR-01 'edges are DERIVED FROM REAL SOURCES, never from manual restatement' | fallback: runtime check at build" :runtime-validation "At record construction: a hash-bearing ref to an identity not yet in the store signals the typed condition above; the store is the journal/legal-ir store (stores-and-authorities.sexp:9 store legal-ir :owner SEAT-LEGAL-AST :writer SEAT-WRITE-AUTHORITY) | invariant: :V5I-C1-acyclic; V7I-OWN-single-writer (V1.7:337-340) | fallback: fail-closed" :python-in-cl-risk "HIGH. Naive import yields an ordered Python list [(1,'CanonRule/1'),…,(12,'SubjectCurrentStatus')] and a build script that iterates it (the build_*.py shape) — an authored SECOND seat of a truth already carried by the records' hash-bearing ref fields, which V6I-REF (V1.6:158-162) and V8I-03 (V1.8:20-22) reject as duplicate source of truth. CL-native alternative: the order is DERIVED (topological sort of `ref-classification`/field-type facts, DDI-2) and the authored 12-step list becomes an EXPECTATION — a `fixture :expect PASS :law L4` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:217-220) or `construction-step`/`construction-edge` facts whose agreement with the derived order is a kernel-law property. Source shape is nested (n Name) pairs (V1.5:598-609) — L1 forbids nested values, so flattening is mandatory in any case (N4)." :future-freedom "NO CONSTRAINT on S19/S20/LLM. S04: the order fixes Legal-IR construction semantics (Claim before Argument, V1.5:614-615) — legitimate because it is IR contract semantics (LAWMAX-LEGAL-IR-SEMANTIC-CONTRACT.md §12 per dossier) that both compilers must share; it would become a constraint only if imported as a CL-specific mechanism (contract §1). JTMS: steps 10-12 should be JTMS consequents rather than a hand-ordered rebuild, otherwise future incremental reasoning (contract L28-29) is pre-empted by a full-rebuild order. Grammar clash with V1.6/V1.7 same-head forms (dossier V5-A10) must not be 'solved' by a union type that carries both shapes.")
  )

(ddi-class V1.5-SCHEMAS__define-constitution-reference
  :batch DDI-4 :source-file "V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp" :fact-class "define-constitution-reference" :source-count 1 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms (("v1.5-interpretive-binding" :line 630 :sha16 "202e856f97dfb0a3"))
  :source-file "V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp"
  :source-forms 1
  :current-authority-seat "V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp C1 section, comment ';; C1.5 — FORMAL machine-readable Constitution reference/invariant (replaces the inert comment)… Mirrored in the constitution .sexp as a (v1.5-interpretive-binding) reference form.' (V1.5:627-629), form v1.5-interpretive-binding at :630-638. Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:17 (:source-count 1, DDI-4, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE). COMPETING SEAT: deployment/LAWMAX-ARCHITECTURE-CONSTITUTION.sexp:353-368 carries the mirror form with EXTRA keys (:status :not-frozen :frozen-baseline :second-seat :machine-readable :spec) and points back at V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp (:367); that file is AUTHORED_NORMATIVE_PROSE (files-and-roles.sexp:20), i.e. NOT a migration input, so the two seats are not even in the same authority class."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "rationale-references.sexp (EXISTING) if the import is pointer-only — the model's `rationale` family is exactly a (doc, anchor) pointer into authored prose (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:182-184) and the Constitution is authored prose; the fact would be e.g. (fact rationale RAT-C1-ARGUMENT :doc \"deployment/LAWMAX-ARCHITECTURE-CONSTITUTION.sexp\" :anchor \"v1.5-interpretive-binding\"). NEW:invariants.sexp if the three boolean flags (:adds-primitive :adds-engine :adds-gate) and the :invariant string are to be carried. The pointer option is the only one that needs NO schema change — but it drops the flags, which are the substantive content."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "EXISTING `rationale` (:doc STRING :anchor STRING) for the pointer, OR NEW `constitution-binding` :required (represents-primitive by-record adds-primitive adds-engine adds-gate) :optional (claims-record profile-record invariant source-file source-line) :types (… all SYMBOL/STRING) :enum ((adds-primitive yes-no) (adds-engine yes-no) (adds-gate yes-no)) :ref ((by-record type) (claims-record type) (profile-record type)). Flattening rule: the form is FLAT (V1.5:630-638) — no nested lists — but it carries THREE `nil` values (:adds-primitive nil :adds-engine nil :adds-gate nil, V1.5:635) and NIL is explicitly not a permitted value kind (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:6). They must render as the existing yes-no enum (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:71) NO/NO/NO. The three record refs would be L3-closable TODAY: ArgumentRecord/1 is NOT a model type but ClaimRecord/1 is not either — checked: interfaces-and-types.sexp:5-64 contains neither ArgumentRecord/1 nor ClaimRecord/1; InterpretiveProfile/1 IS a model type (interfaces-and-types.sexp:28). So 1 of 3 refs closes today and 2 wait for DDI-2 (V1.5:496,502)."
  :owner "S04 — inferred, not declared. Evidence chain: the C1 section's seat is named as 'LAWMAX-LEGAL-IR-SEMANTIC-CONTRACT.md §12 + InstitutionalAct + L2 event-ledger' (V1.5:442-446); V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp:97 declares the canonical seat of 'v1.5 C1 records' to be 'legal-ast.lisp + LAWMAX-LEGAL-IR-SEMANTIC-CONTRACT.md', which is SEAT-LEGAL-AST (seats.sexp:32-33) = S04 (subsystems.sexp:8); the ISR-registered sibling InterpretiveProfile/1 carries :owner S04 (ISR:65; interfaces-and-types.sexp:28). The Constitution file itself has no subsystem (files-and-roles.sexp:20). Marked as an inference."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — no store (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:155-158). If the pointer form is chosen, the fact is hand-authored in rationale-references.sexp, which has no generator (generation-order.sexp:38-61)."
  :classification "PUBLIC — binds PUBLIC S04 records to the public Constitution; InterpretiveProfile/1 is PUBLIC (interfaces-and-types.sexp:28). No private member."
  :dependencies ("FIRST: the two-seat ruling (V1.5:630-638 vs LAWMAX-ARCHITECTURE-CONSTITUTION.sexp:358-368) [one-seat dependency; the two forms have DIVERGENT key sets, so 'identical duplicate' is not available as an answer]" "DDI-2 V1.5-SCHEMAS define-record — 3 references (dag.json): ArgumentRecord/1 (V1.5:502), ClaimRecord/1 (:496), InterpretiveProfile/1 (:476) [typed record references; 2 of 3 are not model types yet]" "IMPORTED ISR define-interface — 1 reference (dag.json): InterpretiveProfile/1 (ISR:65) [already satisfied]" "EXISTING: deployment/LAWMAX-ARCHITECTURE-CONSTITUTION.sexp:14 declares :argument among :primitives — the represents-primitive target; it is prose, not a model fact, so a typed ref to it is not available [reference-target gap]" "yes-no rendering of the three nil flags (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:6,71) [L1 dependency]")
  :consumers ("TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:266 (V5R-C1-08 'define-constitution-reference'); PUBLIC-OBSERVATORY-QUALIFICATION-TESTS.md:1102 (V5Q-C1-08) — predeclared, UNEXECUTED, not model facts" "legacy: V1.5-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh:222 (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, files-and-roles.sexp:436)" "deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.5.md:351 (prose copy of the form) and AI-DIALOGUE.md:247 ([0148] C1.5)" "CANONICAL MODEL: none — grep of the 14 modules for 'v1.5-interpretive-binding' = 0; the only trace is deferred-imports.sexp:17")
  :identity-version-rule "SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT / two live seats: V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp:630-638 (CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT, classification-rule R-011 classification-rules.sexp:51-52) and deployment/LAWMAX-ARCHITECTURE-CONSTITUTION.sexp:358-368 (AUTHORED_NORMATIVE_PROSE, files-and-roles.sexp:20) hold the same binding with divergent keys, and each points at the other (V1.5:629 'Mirrored in the constitution .sexp'; Constitution:367 points back). Neither declares itself the seat; the Constitution copy calls itself ':second-seat', which names the problem without resolving it. ONLY-VERSION for the head define-constitution-reference (1 form in the corpus, classes.md row 24)."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION — pointer-only would be MERGE-INTO-EXISTING-FACT (one `rationale` fact, no schema change, but the flags are dropped); full import would be IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL of a NEW `constitution-binding` fact but must wait for the two DDI-2 record types and must first settle which of the two live seats is canonical."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "CERTAIN two-seat conflict (V5-A11), and importing either version canonises one without retiring the other — the Constitution copy is AUTHORED_NORMATIVE_PROSE and therefore outside the migration's authority to retire. Secondary risk: a pointer-only import creates a THIRD statement (the rationale fact) unless it explicitly replaces one of the two, and no check verifies that its anchor resolves (no counted check opens a `rationale` :doc and greps its :anchor — RAT-PUBPRIV (rationale-references.sexp:7) points at an anchor string that occurs 0 times in deployment/LAWMAX-THREAT-MODEL.md and passes every gate (orchestrator-notes.md N17))."
  :requirement "NEW — V5R-C1-08 (TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:266) names this form; it is not a model `requirement` fact (rtw:5-28; V5-A15). UNKNOWN which model requirement authorises the import."
  :invariant "L1 (the three `nil` flags are illegal values and must render as the yes-no enum, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:6,71), L3 (the three record refs must resolve to declared types — 2 of 3 do not yet), L2 (one id per fact type). Source invariant: the form's own :invariant string (V1.5:636-638) 'ArgumentRecord/1 REPRESENTS the existing Constitution :argument primitive; it does not extend :primitives, create a reasoning engine, or add a gate.'"
  :qualification-test "NEW — QT-DDI4-CONSTITUTION-BINDING-NO-GROWTH. Executable one-liner: `assert binding.adds-primitive == NO and adds-engine == NO and adds-gate == NO and every by-record/claims-record/profile-record resolves to a declared type` — i.e. the 'adds nothing' claim becomes a checked property instead of a prose promise. A companion anchor test (QT-DDI4-RATIONALE-RESOLVES from class 4) is required if the pointer option is chosen. No existing model `test` fact covers it (rtw:30-50)."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact constitution-binding v1.5-interpretive-binding :represents-primitive argument :by-record ArgumentRecord/1 :adds-primitive NO :adds-engine NO :adds-gate NO)` BEFORE DDI-2 seats ArgumentRecord/1 — must be REJECTED: kernel-reason 'resolves to no declared type', checker-reason 'L3'. REPLACE `:adds-gate NO` with `:adds-gate nil` — must be REJECTED, checker-reason 'MALFORMED-FACT' (NIL is not a value kind, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:6). REPLACE `:adds-gate NO` with `:adds-gate MAYBE` — must be REJECTED as outside the yes-no enum (:71), checker-reason 'L1'."
  :rollback "Delete the binding (or the rationale pointer); remove `constitution-binding` from MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp and move :version (:37 / ROOT.sexp:9); re-run build_root.py and build_deferred.py (deferred-imports.sexp:17 restored). Neither V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp nor LAWMAX-ARCHITECTURE-CONSTITUTION.sexp is edited."
  :batch-reason "DDI-4 because build_deferred.py:102 maps `define-constitution-reference` to DDI-4. AGREES — its 4 out-edges go to DDI-2 define-record (3) and IMPORTED define-interface (1); dag.json records no order violation naming it. Its DDI-2 dependency is satisfied by DDI-4 being later."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "Which of the two forms is the seat of the interpretive binding — V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp:630 (CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT) or LAWMAX-ARCHITECTURE-CONSTITUTION.sexp:358 (AUTHORED_NORMATIVE_PROSE, richer key set, self-labelled ':second-seat')? And does the model carry only a `rationale` pointer or the :adds-primitive/:adds-engine/:adds-gate flags themselves — noting that a pointer drops exactly the content that makes the form normative?"
  :adjudication-items ("V5-A11 (V1.5 dossier): two seats with divergent key sets for one binding" "V5-A15 (V1.5 dossier): V5R-C1-08 / V5Q-C1-08 are not model facts" "ADJ-MX4-NIL-RENDERING (new, shared with class 16): `nil` appears as a value in DDI-4 source forms (V1.5:635 three flags; V1.8:405 :provenance-preserved nil) and is forbidden by L1 (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:6) — the yes-no rendering (:71) must be declared once, with the rename recorded, not applied silently per class")
  :topological-position 39 :atomic-groups ()
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "pointer fact: existing `rationale` (:doc \"deployment/LAWMAX-ARCHITECTURE-CONSTITUTION.sexp\" :anchor \"v1.5-interpretive-binding\") — PURE_DATA under ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:182-184 | invariant: V6I-17 prose not duplicated (rationale-references.sexp:1-2) + constitution :no-duplicate (LAWMAX-ARCHITECTURE-CONSTITUTION.sexp:26) | fallback: NEW `constitution-binding` fact carrying the three record refs (L3 → type) and the three flags as yes-no (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:71)" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart "NOT-APPLICABLE" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE" :package-asdf-boundary "NOT-APPLICABLE" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE" :truth-maintenance-dependency "the binding's :invariant says L6 Adversarial Parliament consumes ArgumentRecords 'as typed arguments with proof/counterproof' and :adds-engine nil (V1.5:635-638): the CL consumer is the EXISTING jtms (legal-inference-engine.lisp:227-238) read dialectically (legal-dialectic.lisp:6-11 'Dung grounded semantics = the well-founded fixpoint the engine already runs') — ArgumentRecord → tms-node datum, ArgumentRelation → justification in/out lists | invariant: :adds-engine nil / :adds-gate nil (V1.5:635) + :SR-V6-one-seat 'S04 cognition has ONE seat (existing engine EXTEND)' (SR:138) | fallback: full recompute" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE" :compile-time-validation "gate-time: :by-record/:claims-record/:profile-record resolve to declared `type` facts (L3) and the three flags are NO (yes-no enum); :represents-primitive resolves to a member of the Constitution :primitives list (LAWMAX-ARCHITECTURE-CONSTITUTION.sexp:14) if that list is imported as a define-enum | invariant: :adds-primitive/:adds-engine/:adds-gate nil (V1.5:635) | fallback: prose review — the two seats disagree in key set (8 vs 12 keys); adjudicate V5-A11 first (ADJ-CL4-10)" :runtime-validation "NOT-APPLICABLE" :python-in-cl-risk "MODERATE — the nil flags become NIL (forbidden, ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:6) or Python False, and :represents-primitive :argument (a keyword) is stringified. CL-native alternative: yes-no enum values and a plain symbol ARGUMENT validated against a closed enum of Constitution primitives (LAWMAX-ARCHITECTURE-CONSTITUTION.sexp:14) — or, simpler and one-seat, only the rationale pointer." :future-freedom "NONE (preserving) — it forbids a second reasoning engine and a new gate (V1.5:635), binding interpretation to the existing JTMS/L5-L6 seat; no S19/S20/V8I-02 constraint.")
  )

