  :current-authority-seat "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp, one invariant closing each section: §0 (header V1.6:14) 9 global forms :V6I-01..:V6I-09 at :15,17,25,29,32,35,38,41,43; §1 (header :48) :V6I-10-proposer-never-authority at :75; §2 (header :80) :V6I-11-contracts-closed-noncircular :151, :V6I-12-no-vendor-in-core :155, :V6I-REF-single-source-of-truth :158; §3 (header :164) :V6I-13-cognition-one-seat :261, :V6I-COG-symbolic-only :265, :V6I-COG-one-to-one :270; §4 (header :274) :V6I-14 :297, :V6I-15 :301, :V6I-MEM-public-base-clean :305; §5 (header :310) :V6I-16-extension-isolation :334; §6 (header :340) :V6I-17-one-source-of-truth :348. Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:33 (:source-count 21, DDI-4, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE). LIVE MODEL ANCHOR into this class: rationale RAT-V6I-17 (rationale-references.sexp:3, :doc \"SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp\" :anchor \":V6I-17\") — note the :doc names the WRONG FILE: :V6I-17-one-source-of-truth is defined at V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp:348, and SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp only MENTIONS it in a header comment (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:3). The anchor string ':V6I-17' does occur in that comment, so the pointer resolves textually while pointing away from the definition."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "NEW:invariants.sexp — shared seat with classes 1/4/5/12/14; one-seat reason as in class 1. Cost: a NEW *.sexp under ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/ is auto-classified CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT by classification-rule R-008 (classification-rules.sexp:39-41) and auto-pinned by build_root.py:57 (directory listing), so ROOT.sexp :module-count 14 (ROOT.sexp:12) becomes 15 and every module SHA is re-derived (law L7)."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "NEW `invariant` (as class 1) with :optional (scope-subsystem) — 12 of 21 forms have an inferable owner and 9 are global/UNKNOWN. Flattening rule: all 21 are docstring-only (keyword id + one prose STRING), L1-legal as values; ids colon-stripped (keyword ids (`:V5I-01`, `:SR-V6-one-seat`, …) are not TOKEN-SPACE ids — TOKEN excludes ':' (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:41,17) — so a colon-stripping id-rendering convention must be declared once for all 92 define-invariant forms (orchestrator-notes.md N12)) to V6I-01-lock-meanings-not-tools … V6I-17-one-source-of-truth, all TOKEN-legal. A typed :about reference field would need the DDI-2 record/enum universe (9 record refs, 9 reference refs, 5 enum refs per dag.json) plus the DDI-1 V1.8 canonical-identity facts (7 refs), so an untyped text-only import is the only shape available at DDI-4 time unless those batches land first — which the batch order already guarantees."
  :owner "MIXED / partly UNKNOWN — no form carries an :owner. Dossier inferences with evidence: S21 for :V6I-03-symbolic-only-complete (SafetyState/SYMBOLIC_ONLY, SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:104-107); S19 for :V6I-05-memory-owned-by-lawmax (:96-99), :V6I-14, :V6I-15, :V6I-MEM-public-base-clean; S03 for :V6I-10-proposer-never-authority (:41-44); S04 for :V6I-13-cognition-one-seat, :V6I-COG-symbolic-only, :V6I-COG-one-to-one (:45-48); S20/S03 for :V6I-04 and S20/S19 for :V6I-12 (both marked 'not stated' by the dossier); S18 for :V6I-07 ('not stated'); S22/S23/S24 for :V6I-16-extension-isolation (subsystems.sexp:26-28). UNKNOWN (global, no subsystem) for :V6I-01, :V6I-02, :V6I-06, :V6I-08, :V6I-09, :V6I-11, :V6I-REF-single-source-of-truth, :V6I-17. Nine of 21 owners are UNKNOWN and are not guessed."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — no store (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:155-158)."
  :classification "MIXED — private members named: :V6I-16-extension-isolation (V1.6:334-338) is ABOUT PrivateMemoryEvent/1, PrivateMatterProfile/1, RealTimeAssistance/1 and EmbodimentInterfaces/1, whose subsystems S22/S23/S24 are PRIVATE (subsystems.sexp:26-28) and whose types are PRIVATE where they exist (interfaces-and-types.sexp:41,44,24); PrivateMemoryEvent/1 is not a model type at all (orchestrator-notes.md N9). :V6I-15-memory-scope-isolation (:301) and :V6I-MEM-public-base-clean (:305) likewise name private scopes. The 21 forms are governance prose ABOUT the boundary and carry no private payload, so importing them does not create a public->private consumes edge under L5 (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:164-170) — but the classification of an invariant whose subject is private has no declared rule, which is the open point."
  :dependencies ("DECISION: the shared invariant family + id rendering (ADJ-MX4-INV-SEAT) [schema dependency]" "IMPORTED ISR define-interface — 16 symbol references (dag.json, the largest in-class reference count of any DDI-4 invariant class) [already satisfied: interfaces-and-types.sexp]" "DDI-2 V1.6-SCHEMAS define-record 9 refs, define-reference 9 refs, define-closed-enum 5 refs; V1.5-SCHEMAS define-record 1 ref; V1.8-SCHEMAS define-reference 7 refs [record/enum/reference targets]" "DDI-1 V1.8-SCHEMAS define-canonical-identity — 7 refs; V1.6 define-construction-order — 1 ref [class references]" "DDI-4 sibling SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-wp-purpose — 1 ref (:V6I-13 names WP-08) [intra-batch order]" "NOT AVAILABLE: PrivateMemoryEvent/1 (V1.6:312) is named by :V6I-16 and :V6I-MEM-public-base-clean but is NOT a model type (orchestrator-notes.md N9) [reference-target gap; its owner S19-extension vs S22 is itself undecided]")
  :consumers ("CANONICAL MODEL (live, partial): rationale RAT-V6I-17 (rationale-references.sexp:3) anchors :V6I-17 — but at SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp, not at the definition (V1.6:348); no `seat` fact references RAT-V6I-17 (seats.sexp uses RAT-WP-HONESTY, RAT-ONE-SEAT, RAT-PUBPRIV only), so this rationale fact is currently referenced by nothing" "SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:3 header cites :V6I-17 as the reason the human tables are generated" "MODEL-MIGRATION-CONFLICT-LEDGER.md:20-24 names ':V6I-17 + pipeline symbolic-only-path' as the governing invariant of the five recorded data-flow cycles" "legacy audits V6S1-V6S17 in V1.6-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, files-and-roles.sexp:440); kill witnesses V6KW-01..V6KW-11 in PUBLIC-OBSERVATORY-QUALIFICATION-TESTS.md, declared 'design-only · UNEXECUTED' (orchestrator-notes.md N7)" "V1.7/V1.8 successors that carry the same content under new ids: :RA-I-3 / :V7I-no-mandatory-model-v7 / :V8I-02 for :V6I-02; :RA-I-4 / :V7I-PUBPRIV-acyclic / :V8I-PUBPRIV-all-families for :V6I-07 and :V6I-16; :V7I-MEM-one-owner for :V6I-05; :V7I-MEM-user-private-no-auto-public for :V6I-MEM-public-base-clean; :V8I-03 for :V6I-17")
  :identity-version-rule "MIXED. ONLY-VERSION by id for all 21 (no V6I-* name recurs in another registry). At CONCEPT level: 6 forms are SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT — :V6I-02 (V1.6:17) is restated three more times with growing claims (V1.7:20, V1.7:301, V1.8:17, the last adding 'semantically-equivalent' which V1.8:459-464 then retracts); :V6I-07 (:38) by V1.7:23, V1.7:297, V1.8:277 with DIFFERENT edge-family definitions (V1.7:294-295 vs V1.8:264-274); :V6I-15 (:301) by V1.7:104-105 MemoryScopeV7, which declares itself a replacement for the '(:public :user :ephemeral)' scope model WITHOUT re-typing MemoryEvent/1 (ADJ-V17-ENUM-2); :V6I-16 (:334) by V1.7:297/V1.8:277; :V6I-17 (:348) by V1.8:20; :V6I-COG-symbolic-only (:265) by :V7I-COG-info-preserving (V1.7:95). And 1 form is in DIRECT CONTRADICTION with a later registry: :V6I-REF-single-source-of-truth (V1.6:158-162) says a type defined as BOTH record and reference is REJECTED, while V1.8:347-348 defines define-reference MemoryEvent/1 and CognitionResult/1 whose define-record seats are V1.6:100 and V1.6:204, and V1.8:420-422 states the opposite doctrine ('the reference is the identity seat, the define-record remains the structure seat'). That is not supersession by id; it is two live contradictory rules."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION — 19 of 21 forms are dossier-marked NEEDS_SCHEMA_EXTENSION and would be IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL once the family exists; :V6I-REF-single-source-of-truth cannot be imported as canonical while V1.8 states the opposite doctrine (it would be IMPORT-AS-HISTORICAL-VERSION or BLOCKED), and :V6I-17-one-source-of-truth cannot be imported as canonical while the model itself inverts its authority direction (see conflict column)."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "HIGH and of a kind unique to this class: :V6I-17-one-source-of-truth (V1.6:348-352) declares the two v1.6 registries the source of truth from which human tables are GENERATED. The model inverts this: it declares those registries CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT (files-and-roles.sexp:402,412,441 via classification-rules.sexp:48-52) and its own 14 modules canonical ('thereafter EDIT HERE', interfaces-and-types.sexp:2, subsystems.sexp:2, stores-and-authorities.sexp:2), generating its views from the modules (generation-order.sexp:44-59). Importing :V6I-17 verbatim therefore installs, inside the model, a fact asserting that the model is not the seat (A16 in the V1.6 dossier; A1 in the ISR dossier). Second risk: :V6I-REF vs V1.8:347-348/420-422 (A1 V1.6 dossier). Third: the RAT-V6I-17 anchor points at the wrong file."
  :requirement "NEW / UNKNOWN — the V1.6 invariants are traced by V6Q-01..V6Q-18 in PUBLIC-OBSERVATORY-QUALIFICATION-TESTS.md, of which only V6Q-01, V6Q-02, V6Q-09, V6Q-13 and V6Q-17 are model `test` facts (rtw:46-50) and all 18 are declared 'design-only · UNEXECUTED' (orchestrator-notes.md N7). The R-V6-* requirement ids that DO exist (rtw:21-28) belong to subsystems, not to invariants. No requirement is attached to any of the 21 forms."
  :invariant "L1 (string values legal, keyword ids not), L2 (one id per fact type), L3 (typed :about refs, unavailable for PrivateMemoryEvent/1), L5 (the class is ABOUT the public/private boundary the law enforces — MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:47,164-170 — and L5 today covers only the `consumes` family, while :V6I-16 and its V1.8 successor name eight families), L7 (module universe). Source: the 21 forms ARE the invariants."
  :qualification-test "NEW — QT-DDI4-INV-V16-COUNT plus QT-DDI4-INV-CONTRADICTION. Executable one-liner (count): `assert len([f for f in facts('invariant') if f.source_file=='V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp']) == 21`. Executable one-liner (contradiction): `for every pair of invariant facts whose :supersedes / concept-chain field names the other, assert exactly one carries :status ACTIVE` — i.e. two live invariants may not both claim the same concept, which is the mechanised form of the one-seat law the class itself states. Run over the source today this FAILS for :V6I-REF-single-source-of-truth vs V1.8:420-422, which is the intended signal."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact invariant V6I-17-one-source-of-truth :source-file \"V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp\" :source-line 348 :text \"…\" :status ACTIVE)` together with an ACTIVE :V8I-03-one-seat — must be REJECTED by the contradiction check, reason 'two ACTIVE invariants for one concept'. APPEND `(fact invariant V6I-16-extension-isolation :scope-subsystem S22 …)` where S22 is PRIVATE while the invariant module is read on the public path — must be REJECTED if the decision is that invariants inherit their subject's classification (L5), and must be ACCEPTED if the decision is that governance prose is always PUBLIC: the falsifier is written to force that decision to be declared rather than defaulted (cf. the L5 'undecidable kind fails closed' rule, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:48-50). REPLACE `:status ACTIVE` with `:status :ACTIVE` — must be REJECTED, checker-reason 'MALFORMED-FACT' (X27 vc:172-174)."
  :rollback "Delete the 21 facts and adjust UF-INVARIANT; remove the fact type and enums from MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp and move :version (:37 / ROOT.sexp:9); delete invariants.sexp and re-run build_root.py; build_deferred.py restores deferred-imports.sexp:33. If RAT-V6I-17 was repointed at V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp:348 in the same change, restore rationale-references.sexp:3 verbatim."
  :batch-reason "DDI-4 because build_deferred.py:101 maps `define-invariant` to DDI-4. AGREES — all 55 out-edges point at IMPORTED (16), DDI-1 (8), DDI-2 (30) and DDI-4 (1) classes and dag.json records no order violation naming this class as a target. Intra-batch: it must follow class 2 (define-wp-purpose) for the single WP-08 reference."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "Can :V6I-17-one-source-of-truth be imported at all, given it asserts that the v1.6 registries are the source of truth while the model declares itself canonical and them inputs — and if it is imported with a :status RETIRED, what retires it and where is that recorded? Which record/reference doctrine is canonical, :V6I-REF (V1.6:158-162, 'both is REJECTED') or V1.8:420-422 ('reference is the identity seat, record the structure seat')? Does an invariant whose subject is a PRIVATE type inherit PRIVATE classification under L5?"
  :adjudication-items ("A1 (V1.6 dossier): record-vs-reference doctrine — :V6I-REF (V1.6:158) vs V1.8:347-348 and :420-422" "A16 (V1.6 dossier) = A1 (ISR dossier): :V6I-17 authority direction — registries as source of truth vs model as canonical seat (files-and-roles.sexp:402,412,441; interfaces-and-types.sexp:2)" "A17 (V1.6 dossier): no invariant fact family; the 21 forms cite audits and kill witnesses that are HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE or predeclared-UNEXECUTED" "ADJ-V17-ENUM-2 (V1.7 dossier): :V6I-15's scope model vs MemoryScopeV7 (V1.7:104-105) which replaces it without re-typing MemoryEvent/1" "ADJ-MX4-INV-SEAT (new, shared): one module + one policy for the 92 invariant forms" "ADJ-MX4-RATV6I17-ANCHOR (new): rationale RAT-V6I-17 (rationale-references.sexp:3) names :doc \"SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp\" while :V6I-17 is defined at V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp:348 — the anchor resolves textually against a header comment (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:3) and points away from the definition; no check would notice" "ADJ-MX4-INV-CLASSIFICATION (new): the classification of an invariant whose subject is a PRIVATE type is undeclared, and L5's fail-closed rule for undecidable kinds (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:48-50) would apply to a new family")
