(ddi-class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum
  :batch DDI-2 :source-file "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp" :fact-class "define-closed-enum" :source-count 8 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms (("SafetyMode" :line 20 :sha16 "f2de0430b4f48766") ("ProposerKind" :line 51 :sha16 "de073b79bbd459a4") ("CognitionCapability" :line 168 :sha16 "a45b5d9e0ec11005") ("CognitionError" :line 177 :sha16 "136db7ad2972ed5b") ("PublicMemoryType" :line 278 :sha16 "d5a95cdb6f4a4d25") ("PublicMemoryScope" :line 282 :sha16 "04051e3c55a07b8a") ("MemoryType" :line 284 :sha16 "d85e02df672c06fb") ("MemoryScope" :line 288 :sha16 "a818d2b17c9ffb13"))
  :source-file "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp"
  :source-forms 8
  :current-authority-seat "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp — section '0. NON-NEGOTIABLE GLOBAL INVARIANTS' (header L14): SafetyMode L20-24; section '1. MODEL-AGNOSTIC SEMANTIC PROPOSER' (header L48): ProposerKind L51-56; section '3. PUBLIC LEGAL LANGUAGE COGNITION LAYER (§4)' (header L164): CognitionCapability L168-176, CognitionError L177-181; section '4. COMPLETE MEMORY ARCHITECTURE (§5)' (header L274): PublicMemoryType L278-281, PublicMemoryScope L282, MemoryType L284-287, MemoryScope L288. Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:31 (DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE, :batch DDI-2, :source-count 8)."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "UNDECIDED — interfaces-and-types.sexp (existing; header :1 'one fact per canonical type/interface') per the V1.5/V1.6 dossiers, OR a NEW module 'enums.sexp' per the V1.7/V1.8 dossiers. Whichever is chosen must hold ALL 41 DDI-2 enums (V1.5+V1.6+V1.7+V1.8), because two enum modules would be two seats for one concept; a NEW module also costs a ROOT.sexp composition change (ROOT.sexp:12-27 :module-count 14) and a universe-floor review (verification-corpus.sexp:60-70). No one-seat reason forces NEW on its own — see ADJ-DDI2-ENUM-SEAT."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "NEW fact types `enum` (:id-space TOKEN-SPACE :required (classification) :optional (owner-subsystem) :enum ((classification classification)) :ref ((owner-subsystem subsystem))) and `enum-value` (:required (enum value) :optional (ordinal) :types ((enum SYMBOL) (value SYMBOL) (ordinal INTEGER)) :ref ((enum enum))). flattening rule: one `enum` fact per define-closed-enum (id = enum name, TOKEN) + one `enum-value` fact per member (id = <enum>__<VALUE>, :enum <enum> :value <VALUE> :ordinal <n>); keyword members rendered as bare symbols by colon-strip (orchestrator-notes.md N12); per-member attributes (:label/:obligation/:binding/:sa) become STRING/SYMBOL fields of the enum-value fact. Cardinality by my own reader: 8 `enum` + 71 `enum-value` facts (SafetyMode 4, ProposerKind 5, CognitionCapability 15, CognitionError 14, PublicMemoryType 12, PublicMemoryScope 3, MemoryType 13, MemoryScope 5). Values are keywords in the source and become bare TOKEN symbols by colon-strip (orchestrator-notes.md N12); '+' inside CognitionCapability members (e.g. :UNICODE_NORMALIZATION+SEGMENTATION, V1.6:169) is TOKEN-legal (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:17). no `enum`/`enum-value`/`field`/`primitive`/`cardinality`/`ref-class`/`adapter`/`canonical-identity` fact type exists among the 34 fact types (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:84-288); `define-enum` there is schema syntax for the model's own closed domains only (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:18,47-76); L1 forbids keywords, nested lists and NIL as values (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6) and the closed field set forbids adding keys to `type` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:9-13,148-152)"
  :owner "MIXED — declared for 3 of 8, UNKNOWN for 5. S21 for SafetyMode: SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:104-105 (S21 :interface 'SafetyState/1 + SafetyMode enum'), subsystem S21 subsystems.sexp:25 owner-seat SEAT-WRITE-AUTHORITY (seats.sexp:60-61 BUILT). S19 for PublicMemoryType / PublicMemoryScope / MemoryType / MemoryScope: SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:96-97 (S19 'Memory Kernel (v1.6 §5 complete taxonomy)'), subsystems.sexp:23 SEAT-MEMORY (seats.sexp:56-57 BUILT). UNKNOWN for ProposerKind, CognitionCapability, CognitionError — no registry row names an owner; S03 (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:41-44) and S04 (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:45-48) are section-prose inferences only (V1.6:48-50, :164-166), not facts (V1.6 dossier U2)."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — a closed value domain is declared, never written at runtime; `writer` is a field of `store` only (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:155-158) and the only declared no-writer seat is SEAT-NO-WRITER (seats.sexp:99-100), which is bound to stores. The writer of INSTANCES carrying these values is the writer of the owning store where one exists (memory store writer SEAT-WRITE-AUTHORITY, stores-and-authorities.sexp:10). No registry names a writer for an enum."
  :classification "MIXED — private members named: MemoryType member :PRIVATE_CLIENT_MATTER (V1.6:287, comment 'last = deferred private type') and MemoryScope members :client and :matter (V1.6:288); V1.6:283 declares both enums 'declared for the PRIVATE extension + declassification only; NOT used by the public base'. The other 6 enums carry no private member. The model has NO classification for enums today: L5 ranges over `consumes` edges and `type` classification only (KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:243-254; MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:148-152), so a private-bearing enum is invisible to L5 — this is the leak surface named by :V7I-PUBPRIV-acyclic 'ZERO private-bearing enum' (V1.7:297-299)."
  :dependencies ("SCHEMA FIRST: MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp declaration of `enum` + `enum-value` and a schema-version bump 4 -> 5 (ROOT.sexp:9; falsifiers X74/X75 verification-corpus.sexp:354-364, positive control X76 :365-370) — reference kind: fact-type declaration" "EXISTING model facts: subsystem S19 (subsystems.sexp:23) and S21 (:25) — :owner-subsystem refs for the 5 owned enums" "SAME BATCH: V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-record — 11 of the 22 records bind these enums as field types (dag.json 'V1.6 define-record -> V1.6 define-closed-enum' 11 refs); the `field :domain` ref cannot close until both exist" "DECISION FIRST: the one enum module (ADJ-DDI2-ENUM-SEAT) and the classification treatment of private-bearing enums (ADJ-DDI2-PRIVATE-ENUM)")
  :consumers ("V1.6 define-record field types: ToolInvocation/1.mode (V1.6:120), SafetyState/1.mode (:141), CognitionResult/1.safety_mode + .errors (:207-208), LanguageCognitionLayer/1.capabilities (:211), MemoryEvent/1.memory_type+.scope (:103), MemoryProjection/1.scope (:295), MemoryPolicy/1.scope_isolation (:293), PrivateMemoryEvent/1.memory_type+.scope (:315) — 11 refs (dag.json)" "V1.6 define-invariant (5 refs, DDI-4): :V6I-03-symbolic-only-complete (:25), :V6I-15 (:301), :V6I-MEM-public-base-clean (:305-308), :V6I-COG-one-to-one (:270), :V6I-13 (:261)" "V1.6 define-mapping cognition->existing-lisp-seat (V1.6:231-246) — all 15 CognitionCapability members mapped exactly once (same batch, DDI-2)" "V1.6 define-protocol SemanticProposer (V1.6:57-65, DDI-4) — 1 ref" "SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-subsystem S21 (:104) and S03 (:41) name SafetyMode in :interface / :rollback — 2 refs; this is an IMPORTED class referencing a DDI-2 class (dag.json order violation, rank 0 -> rank 2)" "V1.7 define-invariant :V7I-no-mandatory-model-v7 (V1.7:301-303) names :SYMBOLIC_ONLY — 1 ref" "no tracked source/ or systems/ file names any record/enum id of the six registries (git grep at RO = 0); the only mechanical readers are the legacy audits/harness classified HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:436,440,444,450,453)")
  :identity-version-rule "MIXED by form. SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT (2): CognitionError (V1.6:177-181, 14 members) vs CognitionErrorV7 (V1.7:40-43, 15 members — 7 members dropped, 8 added; the V1.6 enum is still the declared field type of CognitionResult/1.errors at V1.6:207 and V1.8:348/428 confirm V1.6 §3 as CognitionResult/1's structure seat); PublicMemoryScope (V1.6:282) vs MemoryScopeV7 (V1.7:105, comment V1.7:104 'Replaces the vague (:public :user :ephemeral)') while MemoryEvent/1.scope (V1.6:103) and MemoryProjection/1.scope (:295) are NOT re-typed. MemoryScope (V1.6:288) is likewise divergent with MemoryScopeV7. ONLY-VERSION (5): SafetyMode, ProposerKind, CognitionCapability, PublicMemoryType, MemoryType — no same-name define in any other registry (version-chains.md; my own grep). No form declares a supersession key; the divergence is stated only in a V1.7 comment."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION. It becomes IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL for the 5 ONLY-VERSION enums (8 enum + 71 enum-value facts) once (a) the enum fact family exists, (b) the one enum module is fixed, and (c) the private-bearing-enum classification is decided. For CognitionError / PublicMemoryScope / MemoryScope the choice between IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL and IMPORT-AS-HISTORICAL-VERSION is exactly ADJ-V17-ENUM-1 / ADJ-V17-ENUM-2 and cannot be made here."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "HIGH. (1) Two enum modules for one concept if V1.5/V1.6 land in interfaces-and-types.sexp and V1.7/V1.8 in a NEW module (ADJ-DDI2-ENUM-SEAT). (2) Two live taxonomies per concept: cognition-error (V1.6:177 vs V1.7:40) and memory-scope (V1.6:282/288 vs V1.7:105) — importing both as canonical `enum` facts creates two seats for one domain, which is what :V6I-REF-single-source-of-truth (V1.6:158-162) and :V8I-03-one-seat (V1.8:20) forbid. (3) MemoryType duplicates all 12 PublicMemoryType members plus one (V1.6:278-287): two enums, one value space, deliberately (V1.6:276-277) — an importer that de-duplicates them would destroy the public/private split. (4) No id collision with existing model facts: none of the 8 names is an id in the 14 modules (my own grep)."
  :requirement "Partial. R-V6-SAFE (requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:27) covers SafetyMode via S21's req-map S21__WP-07/S21__WP-08 (:89-90); R-V6-MEM (:23) covers the memory enums via S19__FUTURE_BOOK_REVISION (:85). NO model requirement covers ProposerKind / CognitionCapability / CognitionError (their owner is UNKNOWN, so no req-map row can name them). L6 closure is over `subsystem`, not over enums (KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:256-258), so importing enums does not by itself break L6 — but it also gives them no traceability."
  :invariant "L1 (no keywords, no nested lists — MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6 — is exactly why the nested value lists cannot be imported verbatim) + L2 (unique enum id; one id under one fact type, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:106-107, KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:125-127) + L3 (:enum ref of every enum-value closes on a declared `enum`). Source invariants: :V6I-MEM-public-base-clean (V1.6:305-308, audit V6S12) and :V7I-PUBPRIV-acyclic 'ZERO private-bearing enum' in the public closure (V1.7:297-299) — neither has a model law today, because L5 does not see enums."
  :qualification-test "Existing: V6Q-01 (`test` fact requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:46, bound to S21 via req-map :89) and V6Q-02 (:47, S19 via :85) are the nearest model tests, both declared 'design-only, UNEXECUTED' (PUBLIC-OBSERVATORY-QUALIFICATION-TESTS.md:1150; orchestrator-notes.md N7). NEW executable one-liner: every `enum-value` fact's :enum resolves to a declared `enum` fact AND every `field :domain` naming an enum resolves to a declared `enum` — i.e. `python3 CHECKER/independent_check.py` reports 0 L3 violations after the import, with the family cardinality pinned by a NEW property-family PF-L3-DANGLING-ENUM-VALUE :cardinality 71 (shape of verification-corpus.sexp:42-56)."
  :falsifier "APPEND to the chosen enum module `(fact enum-value NoSuchEnum__X :enum NoSuchEnum :value X)` — both paths must reject, kernel-reason 'resolves to no declared enum', checker-reason 'L3' (mirrors K14-UNKNOWN-CONSUMER verification-corpus.sexp:152-154). REPLACE in the same module `:value SYMBOLIC_ONLY` with `:value :SYMBOLIC_ONLY` — must be rejected as an L1 value kind (keyword), mirroring K13-PRIVATE-TYPO (:148-151). CHECK-class falsifier for the private split: APPEND `(fact enum-value PublicMemoryType__PRIVATE_CLIENT_MATTER :enum PublicMemoryType :value PRIVATE_CLIENT_MATTER)` — must be rejected by whatever law the private-enum decision installs; TODAY nothing rejects it, and that absence is the finding."
  :rollback "delete the imported facts of this class and the fact-type/enum declarations added to MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp for it, re-run build_root.py so ROOT.sexp re-pins the 14 modules (ROOT.sexp:12-27; L7), and restore the ledger row to DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT / AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE (deferred-imports.sexp) so the source file is authoritative again; the source registry is never edited by the import (V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp:256 'v1.5 files are NOT edited' is the precedent)"
  :batch-reason "DDI-2 because build_deferred.py maps the head define-closed-enum to DDI-2 ('type / record / enum / reference schema detail'), materialised at deferred-imports.sexp:31; no per-form reason is recorded. DISAGREES in ONE direction only: two IMPORTED / DDI-1 classes already reference it — SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-subsystem (rank 0, 2 refs: SR:104 S21 -> V1.6:20 SafetyMode, SR:41 S03 -> V1.6:20) — so the model already carries subsystem facts whose declared interface names an enum that does not exist as a fact. Its own out-edges are empty (dag.json: this class references nothing), so DDI-2 is not too early for its dependencies; it is too LATE for the IMPORTED subsystem rows that name it."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "(a) Which single module seats all 41 DDI-2 enums (interfaces-and-types.sexp vs NEW enums.sexp)? (b) Does `enum` carry :classification, and what law makes a PUBLIC record's field unable to name a private-bearing enum (today L5 sees only `consumes`, KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:243-254, while V1.7:297-299 demands 'ZERO private-bearing enum')? (c) Which cognition-error enum binds CognitionResult/1 (V1.6:177 vs V1.7:40) and which scope enum binds MemoryEvent/1 / MemoryProjection/1 / MemoryPolicy/1 (V1.6:282/288 vs V1.7:105)? (d) Do the 3 owner-less enums (ProposerKind, CognitionCapability, CognitionError) get an owner-subsystem — required if `enum` mirrors `type` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:148-152) — or is :owner-subsystem optional on `enum`?"
  :adjudication-items ("ADJ-DDI2-ENUM-SEAT: the four DDI-2 enum classes (V1.5 16 enums/83 values, V1.6 8/71, V1.7 8/61, V1.8 9/37 — my own reader over the six registries) must share ONE module (one seat per concept); the dossiers disagree — V1.5/V1.6 propose interfaces-and-types.sexp, V1.7/V1.8 propose a NEW 'enums' module. No winner is picked here." "ADJ-DDI2-PRIVATE-ENUM: MemoryType :PRIVATE_CLIENT_MATTER (V1.6:287) and MemoryScope :client/:matter (V1.6:288) are private-bearing values inside enums that a PUBLIC model type binds (MemoryPolicy/1.scope_isolation V1.6:293; MemoryPolicy/1 is PUBLIC at interfaces-and-types.sexp:35). V1.6:305-308 and V1.7:297-299 forbid exactly this; the model has no law that sees it. Repair at the record, exempt, or grow L5?" "A9 (V1.6 dossier) / ADJ-V17-ENUM-1: CognitionError (V1.6:177, bound by CognitionResult/1.errors V1.6:207) vs CognitionErrorV7 (V1.7:40, bound by nothing) — no supersession is declared in either registry." "A10 (V1.6 dossier) / ADJ-V17-ENUM-2: PublicMemoryScope/MemoryScope (V1.6:282,288) vs MemoryScopeV7 (V1.7:105, declared a replacement at V1.7:104) while the records are not re-typed." "A19 (V1.6 dossier): no enum/enum-value family exists and owners are stated for only 5 of 8 — the family shape (is :owner-subsystem required?) must be decided before DDI-2." "UNKNOWN/count divergence: the V1.6 dossier states 73 member values for this class; my own reader counts 71 (SafetyMode 4 + ProposerKind 5 + CognitionCapability 15 + CognitionError 14 + PublicMemoryType 12 + PublicMemoryScope 3 + MemoryType 13 + MemoryScope 5). The import cardinality must be re-counted by the importer, not taken from either report.")
  :topological-position 7 :atomic-groups (4 8)
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "NOT-APPLICABLE" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE (value domains -> deftype member types, source/version-graph.lisp:148-149 deftype legal-date / legal-instant; CognitionError is the NAME set of a condition taxonomy, see condition_restart)" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE (SafetyMode is consumed by the safe-mode controller declared as EXTEND of write-authority.lisp, SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:104-107; today source/write-authority.lisp:4-8 exports emit-graph/with-write-authority only; :16-49 emit-graph requires :authority in (:canonical :provenance) admits only (:canonical :provenance) by member check — the closed-set idiom, not dispatch)" :condition-restart "CognitionError members (V1.6:177-181 'every stage fails to a typed error, never a guess') are the closed NAMES of typed conditions in the cognition seat (pattern: source/greek-nlp-core.lisp:111-121 nlp-error subclasses; source/legal-ast.lisp:1573-1595); :CLARIFICATION_REQUIRED is the branch that a restart may take INSIDE one invocation (V1.6:227 ':seat legal-dialectic.lisp + condition/restart'; existing restart-case seats source/legal-ast.lisp:1598-1604 with-ast-restarts (restart-case); source/trace-core.lisp:264; source/greek-tokenizer-advanced.lisp:434 handle-unknown-char) | invariant: every stage error is a typed condition, never a guess (V6I-06 V1.6:35-37; deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:24) | fallback: return typed error value (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:24)" :macro-dsl "as class 1 (one enum macro or hand-written deftype per enum; registry form stays data) | invariant: compile-time expansion only (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:25) | fallback: hand-written deftype + constant list (source/capability-registry.lisp:59 +param-types+ closed list + :169 %type-ok-p ecase (unknown type errors structurally, no fail-open))" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE as owner; CognitionCapability values KEY the analyzer registry (source/greek-nlp-core.lisp:387-407 analyzer class + analyze defgeneric + *analyzer-registry*/register-analyzer/get-analyzer (analyzer-not-found typed condition); :573 define-analyzer macro) and SafetyMode values gate the write path — values are protocol arguments" :package-asdf-boundary "private-bearing MemoryType/MemoryScope (V1.6:284-288 :PRIVATE_CLIENT_MATTER/:client/:matter) may NOT live in the public memory package: CL-native form = PublicMemoryType/PublicMemoryScope deftypes in orchestrator.memory (source/memory.lisp:24) and the private extension defined in the DEFERRED_PRIVATE package as a UNION type over the public one (private consumes public, never the reverse — V6I-16 V1.6:334-338); SafetyMode -> S21 (EXTEND write-authority.lisp); ProposerKind/CognitionCapability/CognitionError -> S03/S04 packages (owners unstated, dossier A19) | invariant: V6I-MEM-public-base-clean (V1.6:305-308) + L5 (AM/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:1-3 (*read-eval* nil, standard readtable, no eval), :23 *enums*, :24 *conds*, :56-60 reader, :243-257 law5-isolation :243-257) | fallback: monolith package (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:31) — which would VIOLATE V6I-MEM-public-base-clean, so the real fallback is 'private enums not imported into the public build'" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE" :compile-time-validation "as class 1 (member list == enum-value facts) plus a build-time proof that no PUBLIC record field's :domain names a private-bearing enum (the type-level twin of L5; today PUBLIC MemoryPolicy/1 :scope_isolation (list MemoryScope) V1.6:293 would FAIL it — dossier A10) | invariant: V6I-MEM-public-base-clean (V1.6:305-308) | fallback: runtime check (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL