  :source-forms 1
  :current-authority-seat "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp §1 (section header V1.6:48), form define-protocol SemanticProposer at :57-66 — :generic-functions (propose-candidates negotiate-capability declare-limitations), :input PerceptionEnvelope/1, :output \"(list CandidateInterpretation/1)\", 5 :constraints strings, :absent-behavior. Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:35 (:source-count 1, DDI-4, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE). COMPETING/PRIOR SEAT: ISR:39-40 define-interface SemanticProposer (:owner S03 :kind :protocol :consumers (S03)) — that class is IMPORTED and CANONICAL_IN_MODEL (deferred-imports.sexp:6), so the identity is already in the model as `type SemanticProposer :classification PUBLIC :consumer-role PROPOSER :owner-subsystem S03` (interfaces-and-types.sexp:57)."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "interfaces-and-types.sexp (EXISTING) — the identity already lives there (interfaces-and-types.sexp:57) and its consumes edges live in dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:30,122; putting the protocol payload anywhere else would split one identity across two modules. CONDITIONAL on the L2 ruling below: if the payload becomes a NEW fact family with a DISTINCT id, that family may still live in interfaces-and-types.sexp; if it becomes optional fields on `type`, no new module is involved at all."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "BLOCKED BY L2 — a NEW `protocol` fact with id SemanticProposer is FORBIDDEN: 'one id may be owned by one fact type only' (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:106-107) and SemanticProposer is already owned by `type` (interfaces-and-types.sexp:57). Three representable shapes, none free of consequence: (a) EXTEND `type` with :optional (input output absent-behavior) — a schema change to the model's most-referenced fact type (60 instances); (b) NEW `protocol-function` (:type ref type, :name SYMBOL) x3 and `protocol-constraint` (:type ref type, :ordinal INTEGER, :text STRING) x5 keyed BY the existing type id, which is L2-clean because the ids are synthesised (SemanticProposer__propose-candidates …); (c) a NEW `protocol` family with a renamed id (e.g. SemanticProposerProtocol), which creates a second identity for one concept and contradicts one-seat. Flattening rule for (b): :generic-functions is a nested list (V1.6:58) and :constraints a nested list of 5 strings (:61-65) — neither is an L1-legal value (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6), so 3 + 5 flat facts; :output is already a STRING (:60); :input PerceptionEnvelope/1 is a plain symbol that resolves to a model type (interfaces-and-types.sexp:39)."
  :owner "S03 — DECLARED, not inferred: ISR:39 :owner S03 and interfaces-and-types.sexp:57 :owner-subsystem S03; SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:41-44 S03 :interface 'SemanticProposer + CandidateInterpretation/1 …'. This is one of only two DDI-4 classes with a declared owner."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — and the form says so substantively: constraint 2 is 'holds NO keys; writes NO journal/canonical state; never self-certifies' (V1.6:62). The model's write seat for the affected stores is SEAT-WRITE-AUTHORITY (stores-and-authorities.sexp:8,9,10), which is a different seat; the protocol is explicitly excluded from it."
  :classification "PUBLIC — declared: interfaces-and-types.sexp:57 :classification PUBLIC :consumer-role PROPOSER. No private member."
  :dependencies ("FIRST: the L2 ruling (type vs protocol vs type-with-protocol-fields) — nothing can be written until the id question is answered [L2 / one-seat dependency]" "EXISTING model facts: type SemanticProposer (interfaces-and-types.sexp:57), type PerceptionEnvelope/1 (:39), type CandidateInterpretation/1 (:9), consumes SemanticProposer__PerceptionEnvelope/1 (dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:122) and S03__SemanticProposer (:30) [all satisfied]" "DDI-2 V1.6-SCHEMAS define-closed-enum SafetyMode :SYMBOLIC_ONLY (V1.6:20-21) — the :absent-behavior value [enum-value reference, not yet a model fact]" "DDI-2 V1.6 define-record (1 ref) and define-reference (1 ref); DDI-2 V1.7 define-reference (1 ref) [dag.json]" "NOT AVAILABLE: the three generic functions propose-candidates / negotiate-capability / declare-limitations are NOT FOUND in any tracked Lisp (git grep over source/ systems/); the CL contract admits generic functions only at cognition.lisp:107 for triage/plan/execute-step/synthesize (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:21) [seat gap: the protocol names three functions with no seat]" "NOT AVAILABLE: the 'non-evaluating ingress decoder' named in constraint 4 (V1.6:64) — source/ingress-decoder.lisp is NOT FOUND (git ls-files); only safe-read.lisp exists (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:35) [seat gap, A21 in the V1.6 dossier]")
  :consumers ("DDI-2 V1.6-SCHEMAS define-adapter-contract — 2 references: ONNXProposerAdapter (V1.6:67-68) and OCRPerceptionAdapter (:71-72), both :implements SemanticProposer — dag.json order violation from_rank 2 -> to_rank 4" "IMPORTED ISR define-interface — 1 reference (ISR:11 PerceptionEnvelope/1 -> V1.6:57) — dag.json order violation from_rank 0 -> to_rank 4" "IMPORTED SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-subsystem — 1 reference (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:41 S03 -> V1.6:57) — dag.json order violation from_rank 0 -> to_rank 4" "CANONICAL MODEL (live): the identity is a `type` fact consumed by two `consumes` facts (dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:30,122); the PROTOCOL PAYLOAD (generic functions, constraints, absent-behavior) is in no model fact" "the class is a member of the single class-level cycle recorded by dag.json (class_level_cycles: V1.6 define-protocol -> V1.8 define-canonical-identity -> V1.8 define-reference -> SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-subsystem -> ISR define-interface -> back)")
  :identity-version-rule "LIVE-REFERENCE-TARGET — the id SemanticProposer is already a canonical model fact (interfaces-and-types.sexp:57) and a reference target of two `consumes` facts; this DDI-4 class supplies the payload for an identity that has already been imported by a DIFFERENT class (ISR define-interface, IMPORTED). Also ONLY-VERSION for the head define-protocol (1 form in the corpus, classes.md row 28) with no V1.7/V1.8 successor. The migration's own field loss is visible here: build_model.py dropped :kind :protocol from ISR:39 and DERIVED :consumer-role PROPOSER at migration time (build_model.py:141-146 'a type that appears as a consumer is a PROPOSER class'; ISR dossier A3), so the model's SemanticProposer already differs from both source forms."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION — mechanically blocked by L2, not merely undecided: no fact can be written under this id. After the ruling it becomes MERGE-INTO-EXISTING-FACT (shape a: fields on the existing `type`) or IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL of 8 synthesised-id facts (shape b)."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "CERTAIN and already realised: three statements of one identity exist — ISR:39 define-interface (:kind :protocol), V1.6:57 define-protocol, and the model's `type` fact (interfaces-and-types.sexp:57) whose :consumer-role PROPOSER appears in neither source form. A11/A3 in the ISR dossier and A6 in the V1.6 dossier name it. Importing the payload under a renamed id would make it four."
  :requirement "R-V6-ADP — inferred via S20 (rtw:86-88, req-map S20__WP-07/WP-11/WP-14 :requirement R-V6-ADP) is the ADAPTER requirement, not the protocol's; S03's model requirement is R-25 (rtw:69). Neither is stated by the form. Reported UNKNOWN for the protocol payload specifically."
  :invariant "L2 (one id owned by one fact type, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:34-36,106-107) — the binding constraint; L1 (the nested :generic-functions and :constraints lists are illegal values); L3 (:input/:output must resolve to declared types — both do today); L5 (consumer-role PROPOSER is what makes SemanticProposer a legal consumer at all, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:48-50). Source invariants: :V6I-10-proposer-never-authority (V1.6:75-78), :V6I-04-adapter-no-canonical-authority (:29-31), :V6I-COG-symbolic-only (:265). CL-contract obligation: a generic-function mechanism is admitted only with reason/seat/requirement/invariant/test/fallback/migration/rollback (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:6,21) — this protocol's three functions have NO seat, so importing it as-is imports an unadmitted mechanism."
  :qualification-test "NEW — QT-DDI4-PROTOCOL-NO-WRITE. Executable one-liner: `assert no store fact has :writer or :owner resolving to a seat owned by a type carrying :consumer-role PROPOSER, and every protocol-function fact names a symbol that occurs in a tracked .lisp file` — the first half mechanises constraint 2 (V1.6:62), the second half mechanises the CL-contract seat obligation and FAILS today for all three functions, which is the intended signal. Existing model test coverage: V6Q-01 is a model `test` fact (rtw:46) and is mapped to S21's write authority (rtw:89), not to this protocol."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact protocol SemanticProposer :input PerceptionEnvelope/1 :output \"(list CandidateInterpretation/1)\")` — must be REJECTED on both paths: the id is already owned by fact type `type` (L2; MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:106-107). This falsifier is the class's whole finding in one line. APPEND `(fact protocol-function SemanticProposer__ghost :type SemanticProposer :name ghost-fn)` where ghost-fn occurs in no tracked .lisp — must be REJECTED by QT-DDI4-PROTOCOL-NO-WRITE's seat half. APPEND `(fact consumes SemanticProposer__LegalIR/1 :consumer SemanticProposer :provides LegalIR/1)` — must be REJECTED or ACCEPTED strictly per :consumer-role (X28-CONSUMER-WITHOUT-ROLE vc:175-177 is the existing falsifier of the same shape)."
  :rollback "Delete the protocol payload facts (or the added `type` fields) and revert MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp (:148-152 for shape a, or the new fact types for shape b) with a schema :version move (:37 / ROOT.sexp:9); re-run build_root.py; build_deferred.py restores deferred-imports.sexp:35. interfaces-and-types.sexp:57 and dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:30,122 must be left exactly as they are — they belong to the IMPORTED class, not to this one."
  :batch-reason "DDI-4 because build_deferred.py:101 maps `define-protocol` to DDI-4. DISAGREES — three earlier classes reference it and dag.json records all three as order violations: ISR define-interface (IMPORTED, from_rank 0 -> to_rank 4), SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-subsystem (IMPORTED, from_rank 0 -> to_rank 4) and V1.6 define-adapter-contract (DDI-2, from_rank 2 -> to_rank 4, 2 refs). Worse, the identity is ALREADY in the model via the IMPORTED class, so 'deferred to last' describes a payload whose head has already been imported out of order. The class is also the DDI-4 member of the corpus's single class-level cycle (dag.json class_level_cycles), so no batch order can be derived for it mechanically — the cycle must be cut by a decision."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "Is SemanticProposer a `type`, a `protocol`, or a type carrying protocol fields — given L2 forbids one id under two fact types and the id is already owned by `type` (interfaces-and-types.sexp:57)? Where is the Lisp seat of propose-candidates / negotiate-capability / declare-limitations, which the CL contract requires before the mechanism is admitted (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:6,21) and which git grep does not find? And where is the non-evaluating ingress decoder that constraint 4 requires (source/ingress-decoder.lisp NOT FOUND)?"
  :adjudication-items ("A6 (V1.6 dossier) = A3 (ISR dossier): SemanticProposer type-vs-protocol; the model's :consumer-role PROPOSER appears in neither source form" "A21 (V1.6 dossier): the non-evaluating ingress decoder has no seat (source/ingress-decoder.lisp NOT FOUND) while three DDI-4 forms require it (V1.6:31, :64, :268)" "ADJ-MX4-PROTOCOL-L2 (new): the import is mechanically blocked by L2 — this is the only DDI-4 class that cannot be written in any form until an identity ruling is made" "ADJ-MX4-PROTOCOL-CYCLE (new): the class sits in the corpus's only class-level cycle (dag.json class_level_cycles), so its batch cannot be derived from the reference graph at all" "ADJ-MX4-CL-ADMISSION (new, shared with class 11): importing a CLOS-protocol declaration whose generic functions have no seat imports a mechanism the CL contract has not admitted (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:6)")
  :topological-position 22 :atomic-groups (8)
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "protocol identity = the EXISTING `type` fact (interfaces-and-types.sexp:57) + NEW `protocol-function` facts (:protocol ref type, :name SYMBOL, :in ref type, :out ref type) and `protocol-constraint` facts (closed enum of obligations) — hash-pinned; the protocol's OUTPUT records are hash-bearing (CandidateInterpretation/1 = lawmax/neural-candidate/1, V1.6:92-95) | invariant: L2 — the id SemanticProposer is owned by `type`; a second `protocol` id for the same concept is forbidden (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:34-36; V1.6 dossier A6/A21) | fallback: a NEW `protocol` family with a DISTINCT id (second seat — needs adjudication)" :clos-class "abstract protocol class `semantic-proposer` with concrete adapter subclasses (ONNXProposerAdapter / OCRPerceptionAdapter — V1.6:67-74, DDI-2) — pattern greek-nlp-core.lisp:163-168 (abstract `lexicon`) → hash-table-lexicon :195 / file-lexicon :229 / composite-lexicon :306; LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:20 'one class per concept' | invariant: :V6I-04 adapter has NO canonical write authority / NO keys / NO self-certification (V1.6:29-31) + :V6I-10 | fallback: plain structs (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:20)" :generic-function "defgeneric propose-candidates (proposer envelope) → list of CandidateInterpretation/1; negotiate-capability; declare-limitations — the three NAMES are fixed by V1.6:58; dispatch on the adapter class; an ABSENT proposer is 'no applicable method → symbolic path', never a blocking error (V1.6:66) — pattern cognition.lisp:78-80 build-frame-from-advice with a default method returning nil, and cognition.lisp:92-113 stage generics; LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:21 'dispatch is total or errors typed' | invariant: :V6I-10 'A proposer produces PerceptionEnvelope-derived CandidateInterpretation only' (V1.6:75-78) + :absent-behavior (V1.6:66) | fallback: single dispatch function (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:21)" :condition-restart "adapter failure ⇒ a TYPED condition caught at the wall, degrading SafetyMode to :DEGRADED/:SYMBOLIC_ONLY (V1.6:23 'fail-closed to SYMBOLIC_ONLY semantics'); today cognition.lisp:62-63 `advise` wraps the advisor in ignore-errors — the future form must be a typed condition per LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:24 'every error is a typed condition' | invariant: :V6I-03 'Removing every proposer yields SafetyMode :SYMBOLIC_ONLY, never a broken state' (V1.6:25-28) | fallback: return typed error value" :macro-dsl "NOT a macro — the constraint 'passes EXCLUSIVELY through the non-evaluating ingress decoder (no cl:read/eval/macro/compile)' (V1.6:64): safe-read.lisp:152-165; the `ingress-decoder.lisp` named by LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:35 is NOT FOUND in source/ | invariant: SIK §14 no read/eval over external bytes (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:35) | fallback: reject input" :protocol "THE class of this form: a CLOS protocol = abstract class + 3 defgenerics + documented contract (the 5 constraints as `protocol-constraint` facts); exemplars greek-nlp-core.lisp:170-189 ('Generic functions - THE PROTOCOL'), :387-394 analyzer/analyze, protocols.lisp:51-60 | invariant: :V6I-10 + :V6I-04 | fallback: a single function-typed slot registered through the capability registry (capability-registry.lisp:48 :fn; :46 trust :trusted|:advisor; define-capability :140-147) with :trust :advisor" :package-asdf-boundary "the protocol package lives in the public system; each adapter in its OWN ASDF system that :depends-on the protocol package, never the reverse; no trusted-path system :depends-on an adapter system | invariant: 'removable with NO loss of memory or canonical data' (V1.6:65) + :V8I-02 (V1.8:17-19) | fallback: adapter registered at runtime through the capability registry (SEAT-CAPABILITY-REGISTRY seats.sexp:58; capability-seat-collision capability-registry.lisp:72-81 keeps one owner per capability)" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE (the proposer 'writes NO journal/canonical state' V1.6:62 — the ABSENCE is the invariant, enforced by write-authority.lisp:16-51)" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE (candidates are not beliefs until symbolically promoted — :V6I-10; that is C9/C5's JTMS concern)" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE" :compile-time-validation "gate-time: protocol-function names are plain symbols (L1 TOKEN); :in/:out are L3 refs to declared `type` facts (PerceptionEnvelope/1, CandidateInterpretation/1 are imported types per deferred-imports.sexp:6); every DDI-2 adapter-contract :implements resolves to this protocol (L3) with :mandatory NO (yes-no) | invariant: :V7I-no-mandatory-model-v7 'No define-adapter-contract … is :mandatory t' (V1.7:301-303) | fallback: prose" :runtime-validation "'score is NEVER converted to legal truth' (V1.6:63) is enforced at the wall: verify-proposal / verdict (legal-extraction-verify.lisp:30-31,340) is the ONLY path from candidate to IR | invariant: :V6I-10 (V1.6:75-78) | fallback: reject candidate" :python-in-cl-risk "YES — :generic-functions as a JSON list of strings and :constraints as 5 free strings; the naive import loses that these are CLOS generic-function NAMES with typed signatures. CL-native alternative: `protocol-function` facts (name SYMBOL, :in ref type, :out ref type) so the future defgeneric lambda-lists are DERIVABLE from data, and the constraints as a closed enum of obligations (e.g. NO_KEYS, NO_CANONICAL_WRITE, NO_SELF_CERT, INGRESS_ONLY, REMOVABLE) checkable per adapter-contract fact." :future-freedom "CONSTRAINS S20 adapter API to three generic-function names (V1.6:58) — a stable contract that PRESERVES V8I-02 (absent ⇒ SYMBOLIC_ONLY, V1.6:66); S04 consumes only typed candidates; S19 untouched ('removable with NO loss of memory', V1.6:65). No JTMS constraint. Batch-order note: DDI-2 adapter contracts reference this DDI-4 protocol (dossier: dag.json order violation). UNKNOWN: the ingress-decoder seat named by the contract does not exist in source/.")
  )

(ddi-class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-adapter-contract
  :batch DDI-2 :source-file "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp" :fact-class "define-adapter-contract" :source-count 2 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms (("ONNXProposerAdapter" :line 67 :sha16 "35197ad7e34f71fb") ("OCRPerceptionAdapter" :line 71 :sha16 "b998bc4e834da73f"))
  :source-file "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp"
  :source-forms 2
  :current-authority-seat "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp section '1. MODEL-AGNOSTIC SEMANTIC PROPOSER' (header L48): ONNXProposerAdapter L67-70, OCRPerceptionAdapter L71-74; ledger deferred-imports.sexp:30 (DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE, DDI-2, :source-count 2)."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "interfaces-and-types.sexp (existing) — the adapter's only typed reference target, `type SemanticProposer :consumer-role PROPOSER`, already lives there (interfaces-and-types.sexp:57), and the model's one 'component' family for non-type artifacts is in the same module (:66-67). A NEW 'adapters.sexp' is not justified for 2 facts and would put an adapter in a different seat from the interface it implements."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "NEW fact type `adapter` (:id-space TOKEN-SPACE :required (implements kind mandatory replaceable canonical-write-authority owner-subsystem) :optional (note) :types ((implements SYMBOL) (kind SYMBOL) (mandatory SYMBOL) (replaceable SYMBOL) (canonical-write-authority SYMBOL) (owner-subsystem SYMBOL) (note STRING)) :enum ((mandatory yes-no) (replaceable yes-no) (canonical-write-authority yes-no)) :ref ((implements type) (owner-subsystem subsystem))). Flattening rule: the source values `nil` and `t` are FORBIDDEN L1 values (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:6 'no NIL'); they render as the existing yes-no enum (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:71) — :mandatory nil -> NO, :replaceable t -> YES, :canonical-write-authority nil -> NO. `:kind :EXTERNAL_MODEL` / `:OCR_PERCEPTION` are ProposerKind members (V1.6:54-55) and become a ref to the DDI-2 `enum-value` family. 2 `adapter` facts. no `enum`/`enum-value`/`field`/`primitive`/`cardinality`/`ref-class`/`adapter`/`canonical-identity` fact type exists among the 34 fact types (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:84-288); `define-enum` there is schema syntax for the model's own closed domains only (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:18,47-76); L1 forbids keywords, nested lists and NIL as values (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6) and the closed field set forbids adding keys to `type` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:9-13,148-152)"
  :owner "S20 — DECLARED in a registry row: SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:100-101 (S20 'Adapter replaceability plane (v1.6 §8)', :interface 'CapabilityManifest/1 + ToolInvocation/1 + adapter contracts'), subsystems.sexp:24 owner-seat SEAT-CAPABILITY-REGISTRY (seats.sexp:58-59 BUILT source/capability-registry.lisp). S03 by implementation: both adapters :implement SemanticProposer, whose owner is S03 (interfaces-and-types.sexp:57; ISR:39), and SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:22 assigns the ONNX pin to WP-07, S03's packet (req-map S03__WP-07, requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:69). S20 is the only value written as a registry field; S03 is an inference from the implemented protocol, not a declaration. Both are recorded; the choice is adjudication A18 and is NOT made here."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — the source states it: `:canonical-write-authority nil` on both forms (V1.6:70,74). This is the one class in DDI-2 whose non-writer status is DECLARED rather than inferred; it must be rendered as an explicit NO (yes-no, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:71), not as an absent key, because absence is indistinguishable from omission under the closed field set (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:9-13)."
  :classification "PUBLIC — no private member; the adapters are optional enrichment on the public path. Constitutional check V8I-02 / :V6I-02-no-mandatory-model (V1.6:17-19 'No model, ONNX runtime, Python runtime, cloud or provider is mandatory anywhere in the public build') is SATISFIED at source by :mandatory nil (V1.6:68,72) — orchestrator-notes.md N13. Note the tension the note records: WP-07.md:25 pins 'neural = Python + ONNX Runtime' while SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:22 says that pin 'MUST become optional adapter'."
  :dependencies ("SCHEMA FIRST: `adapter` fact type + schema-version bump (X74-X76 verification-corpus.sexp:354-370) — fact-type declaration" "EXISTING model fact: type SemanticProposer (interfaces-and-types.sexp:57) — :implements ref target" "SAME BATCH: V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum ProposerKind (V1.6:51-56) — :kind ref target (dag.json records this class's out-edges as define-interface (2) and define-protocol (2); the ProposerKind binding is by value, not by symbol reference)" "DDI-4: V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-protocol SemanticProposer (V1.6:57-65) is the contract both adapters implement and is a LATER batch — dag.json order violation 'V1.6 define-adapter-contract (rank 2) -> V1.6 define-protocol (rank 4), 2 refs'" "DECISION FIRST: owner S20 vs S03 (A18); a `type` or `adapter` fact cannot be written without one (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:145-147,148-152 make owner-subsystem required on every owned family)")
  :consumers ("V1.6 define-invariant :V6I-04-adapter-no-canonical-authority (V1.6:29-31) and :V6I-09-future-tech-is-adapter (:43-46) — DDI-4" "V1.7 define-invariant :V7I-no-mandatory-model-v7 (V1.7:301-303) — polices :mandatory across all adapters; DDI-4" "legacy audit V6S15 (V1.6-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh:253-255) — HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:440)" "prose: IMPLEMENTATION-BOOK-MIGRATION-IMPACT-v1.6.md:25,67-70; SUPERSEDED-REGISTER.md:247-251" "dag.json: NO class references this one (in-edges empty) — nothing in the six registries depends on it" "no tracked source/ or systems/ file names any record/enum id of the six registries (git grep at RO = 0); the only mechanical readers are the legacy audits/harness classified HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:436,440,444,450,453)")
  :identity-version-rule "ONLY-VERSION — define-adapter-contract occurs only in V1.6 (classes.md row 29; my own grep over the six registries); neither name recurs in V1.7/V1.8. No id collision: ONNXProposerAdapter and OCRPerceptionAdapter are not ids of any fact in the 14 modules."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION on the owner (A18); mechanically it is the closest thing in DDI-2 to a PURE_DATA_MIGRATION once the `adapter` family exists — 2 flat facts, every value renderable, one typed ref target that already exists. It cannot be SKIP-WITH-PROOF: the facts carry the only machine-readable statement that no model/vendor is mandatory, which is the V8I-02 / :V6I-02 constitutional criterion."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "MEDIUM. The model already carries `component proposers :owner-subsystem S03` (interfaces-and-types.sexp:67) and `consumes proposers__MemoryProjection/1` (dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:124) for an artifact that resolves to no tracked file (V1.6 dossier U7) — importing adapters as a second non-type artifact family beside `component` risks two seats for 'a thing that is not a type but implements one'. S20's seat SEAT-CAPABILITY-REGISTRY (seats.sexp:58-59, source/capability-registry.lisp) is where both dossier candidates place the artifact, so there is no seat-path conflict."
  :requirement "R-V6-ADP (requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:21) via S20's three req-map rows S20__WP-07 / S20__WP-11 / S20__WP-14 (:86-88) if the owner is S20; R-25 via S03__WP-07 (:69) if the owner is S03. The requirement therefore FOLLOWS the owner decision — a second reason A18 must be settled first."
  :invariant "L3 (:implements closes on `type`, :owner-subsystem on `subsystem`) + L1 (yes-no rendering of nil/t). Source invariants: :V6I-02-no-mandatory-model (V1.6:17-19), :V6I-04-adapter-no-canonical-authority (:29-31), :V6I-10-proposer-never-authority (:75-79), :V7I-no-mandatory-model-v7 (V1.7:301-303). None of these has a model law: nothing in KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp or gate_checks.py reads a mandatory/optional flag, so importing the facts without a check turns a policed property into inert data (cf. ADJ-V18-EXEC-1)."
  :qualification-test "Existing: V6Q-17 (`test` fact requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:50, bound to S20 by req-map :86-88) — declared design-only/UNEXECUTED (orchestrator-notes.md N7). NEW executable one-liner: `grep -c ':mandatory YES' <module>` must be 0 for every `adapter` fact, and every `adapter :implements` must resolve to a declared `type` — i.e. no adapter may be mandatory and no adapter may implement an undeclared interface."
  :falsifier "APPEND to the target module `(fact adapter HeldOutAdapter :implements NoSuchInterface :kind EXTERNAL_MODEL :mandatory NO :replaceable YES :canonical-write-authority NO :owner-subsystem S20)` — both paths must reject: kernel-reason 'resolves to no declared type', checker-reason 'L3' (shape of K15-WRONG-TYPE-PROVIDES, verification-corpus.sexp:155-157). REPLACE `:mandatory NO` with `:mandatory YES` on ONNXProposerAdapter — must be rejected by the NEW no-mandatory check; today NOTHING rejects it (no such check exists in gate_checks.py — my own grep), and that is the honest finding. REPLACE `:canonical-write-authority NO` with `:canonical-write-authority YES` — must be rejected as an adapter claiming write authority (:V6I-04)."
  :rollback "delete the imported facts of this class and the fact-type/enum declarations added to MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp for it, re-run build_root.py so ROOT.sexp re-pins the 14 modules (ROOT.sexp:12-27; L7), and restore the ledger row to DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT / AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE (deferred-imports.sexp) so the source file is authoritative again; the source registry is never edited by the import (V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp:256 'v1.5 files are NOT edited' is the precedent)"
  :batch-reason "DDI-2 because build_deferred.py maps the head to DDI-2, materialised at deferred-imports.sexp:30. DISAGREES: the class's own out-edges point at a LATER batch — dag.json 'V1.6 define-adapter-contract (rank 2) -> V1.6 define-protocol (rank 4), 2 refs' (V1.6:67 and :71 both -> V1.6:57 SemanticProposer). define-protocol is DDI-4 (deferred-imports.sexp:35). The dependency is satisfiable anyway ONLY because SemanticProposer is already a model `type` fact from the IMPORTED ISR class (interfaces-and-types.sexp:57 via ISR:39) — i.e. the reference closes on the IMPORTED projection of the protocol, not on the protocol form itself; that substitution is exactly adjudication A6."
  :decision-kind "SCHEMA_EXTENSION"
  :decision-question "(a) Owner: S20 (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:101 names 'adapter contracts' as the S20 interface) or S03 (the adapters implement S03's protocol; WP-07 is S03's packet per SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:22)? (b) Is `adapter` a new fact family, or are adapters `component` facts with extra fields — noting that `component` has a closed field set of exactly (owner-subsystem) (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:144-147)? (c) Does the model grow a check that reads :mandatory, or is the no-mandatory-model guarantee imported as inert data (ADJ-V18-EXEC-1)?"
  :adjudication-items ("A18 (V1.6 dossier): adapter owner S20 (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:101) vs S03 (implements the S03 protocol; WP-07 per SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:22 and IMPLEMENTATION-BOOK-MIGRATION-IMPACT-v1.6.md:25) — two registry-grounded answers, no tie-breaker in the sources." "ADJ-DDI2-NIL-RENDERING (shared with every DDI-2 class carrying nil/t): MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:6 forbids NIL as a value; the yes-no enum (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:71) exists but no rendering rule for source `nil`/`t` is declared anywhere (V1.6 dossier U3). The convention must be fixed once, for all batches." "A6 (V1.6 dossier), inherited: SemanticProposer is a `type` fact with :consumer-role PROPOSER (interfaces-and-types.sexp:57) while V1.6:57-65 defines it as a CLOS protocol; the adapter's :implements ref therefore closes on a projection whose shape is itself unadjudicated." "ADJ-V18-EXEC-1 (shared): no model harness executes a 'no mandatory adapter' contract; verification-corpus.sexp:122-125 declares two harnesses, both run_corpus.py, both for model laws L1-L7.")
  :topological-position 43 :atomic-groups (8)
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "the adapter's CapabilityManifest/1 (V1.6:108-114: runtime_build_digest, conformance_suite_ref, expiration, fail_closed, signature) is the immutable, signed identity of a concrete adapter build; the contract row itself is a registration record | invariant: adapter-specific data lives ONLY in CapabilityManifest/PerceptionEnvelope (V6I-12 V1.6:155-157) | fallback: copy-on-write (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:27)" :clos-class "a class per adapter KIND only if the SemanticProposer generic functions (V1.6:58 propose-candidates/negotiate-capability/declare-limitations) must specialize on it; otherwise the adapter is a registered capability struct (source/capability-registry.lisp:40-47 defstruct capability (:read-only t slots, immutable after registration)) with :trust :advisor | invariant: one class per concept (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:20); adapter has NO canonical write authority (V6I-04 V1.6:29-31) — expressed structurally as trust :advisor (source/capability-registry.lisp:46, :80 %valid-trust-p) | fallback: plain structs (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:20)" :generic-function "methods on the SemanticProposer protocol generics (DDI-4 define-protocol V1.6:57-66) specialized per adapter kind; absence of every method => SafetyMode :SYMBOLIC_ONLY (V1.6:66 :absent-behavior) | invariant: dispatch total or typed error (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:21); removing all proposers leaves a working system (V6I-03) | fallback: single dispatch fn (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:21)" :condition-restart "adapter unavailable/expired/downgraded => typed condition handled by falling to SYMBOLIC_ONLY (V1.6:23 :DEGRADED 'fail-closed to SYMBOLIC_ONLY semantics'); duplicate registration => source/capability-registry.lisp:72 capability-seat-collision (one capability, one owner file) | invariant: V6I-03 + V7I-no-mandatory-model-v7 (V1.7:301-303) | fallback: return typed error value (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:24)" :macro-dsl "registration through the existing source/capability-registry.lisp:140 define-capability (the ONE declarative capability definition) with :trust :advisor (no new DSL) | invariant: one declarative capability definition; HTTP/MCP/CLI are projections (source/capability-registry.lisp:140-143) | fallback: register-capability function call (source/capability-registry.lisp:144-147 shows the macro is a thin form over it)" :protocol "implements SemanticProposer (V1.6:57-66; ISR:39 SemanticProposer :consumer-role PROPOSER, AM/interfaces-and-types.sexp:57) — the CLOS protocol is the seat, the adapter is a conforming implementation with declared limitations | invariant: 'emits ONLY typed, anchored candidates; holds NO keys; passes EXCLUSIVELY through the non-evaluating ingress decoder' (V1.6:61-65) | fallback: single dispatch fn (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:21)" :package-asdf-boundary "adapters are OUT-OF-PROCESS / outside every trusted ASDF system (WP-07 'external neural runtime', WORK/orchestrator-notes.md N13); no trusted system :depends-on an adapter system (16 ASDF systems, 53 edges, cycle NONE (deployment/collab/dialogue/0146-claude.md:18); 17 .asd paths at HEAD of which systems/orchestrator-omega.asd is a symlink to ../orchestrator-omega.asd; source/safe-read.lisp:38-39 loaded FIRST in orchestrator-infrastructure) | invariant: no mandatory model/ONNX/Python/runtime in the public build (V8I-02 V1.8:17-19; V7I-no-mandatory-model-v7) | fallback: NOT the contract's 'monolith package' — the invariant's own fallback is SafetyMode :SYMBOLIC_ONLY (V1.6:21), i.e. the build without the adapter system" :persistent-event "adapter adoption / shadow->canary->rollback (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:101 S20 :rollback) as journaled events via source/journal.lisp:507 chained-append (atomic compare-and-append under lock; stale-chain-link :495); today registration is an in-memory hash table only (source/capability-registry.lisp:63) | invariant: no self-improvement canonical without test+authorization+journaled adoption+rollback (V6I-08 V1.6:41-42) | fallback: in-memory registry (current)" :truth-maintenance-dependency "adapter output NEVER enters the JTMS as an authoritative premise: it passes the epistemic wall (source/legal-extraction-verify.lisp:17-23 V1-V4 deterministic checks (V4 consistency in the JTMS); :340 verdict; verify-and-register) and enters, if at all, as a candidate whose score is never truth (V1.6:63) | invariant: V6I-10 proposer-never-authority (V1.6:75-78) | fallback: reject (fail-closed)" :temporal-index-projection "manifest validity window: :expiration + :fail_closed (V1.6:114) evaluated with the typed instant seat (source/version-graph.lisp:148-149 deftype legal-date / legal-instant); expired manifest => adapter refused (THREAT-MODEL Θ20 'adapter downgrade/expired manifest', deployment/LAWMAX-THREAT-MODEL.md:48) | invariant: CapabilityManifest fail-closed on downgrade/expiry | fallback: reject adapter" :compile-time-validation "build-time proof that NO adapter contract is :mandatory YES (V7I-no-mandatory-model-v7 V1.7:301-303; V8I-SYM mutation 'mandatory-model-node' V1.8:334-335) — best made STRUCTURAL: a define-conditional (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:26-30) forbidding :mandatory YES when :kind in {LOCAL_MODEL, EXTERNAL_MODEL, OCR_PERCEPTION} (see CL2-A6); registration-time validation of params/trust (source/capability-registry.lisp:80-102) | invariant: V8I-02 | fallback: runtime check (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:32)" :runtime-validation "adapter output validated by the NON-EVALUATING ingress decoder (V1.6:64) — seat NOT BUILT (source/ingress-decoder.lisp NOT FOUND (git ls-files); deployment/LAWMAX-SECURE-SEMANTIC-INGRESS-CONTRACT.md:12 'External non-evaluating JSON/CBOR decoder = NEW, MISSING'; deployment/LAWMAX-THREAT-MODEL.md:46 Θ18, :48 Θ20); safe-read.lisp is explicitly NOT that boundary (source/safe-read.lisp:68 safe-read-error; :28-30 INTERNAL-ONLY (forbids Internet/HTML/PDF/OCR/LLM raw input); :203 read-data-form) => runtime validation of adapter outputs is UNKNOWN/design-target today; capability params are runtime-checked by %type-ok-p (source/capability-registry.lisp:59 +param-types+ closed list + :169 %type-ok-p ecase (unknown type errors structurally, no fail-open)) | invariant: no cl:read/eval/macroexpand over external bytes (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:35; V1.6:259) | fallback: reject input (fail-closed)" :python-in-cl-risk "MEDIUM. Naive import: a config dict {mandatory: false, replaceable: true, write_authority: null} — NIL/nil is not a legal model value (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:6 'no NIL'; dossier A18) and booleans become strings. CL-native: adapter facts with yes-no enum fields (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:71) and :implements an L3 ref to the SemanticProposer type; in production the adapter is a capability struct with :trust :advisor (source/capability-registry.lisp:40-47 defstruct capability (:read-only t slots, immutable after registration)), never a dict of flags; the write-authority prohibition is structural (advisor capabilities cannot obtain write authority; source/write-authority.lisp:4-8 exports emit-graph/with-write-authority only; :16-49 emit-graph requires :authority in (:canonical :provenance))." :future-freedom "YES — flagged. The two ids name TECHNOLOGIES (ONNX, OCR) as canonical registry entities; V6I-01 'lock meanings, NEVER tools' (V1.6:15-16) and V6I-12 (V1.6:155-157) tolerate this only because both are :mandatory nil :replaceable t. Importing them as `type` facts would make a tool a canonical interface; importing them as adapter-instance facts with :mandatory NO keeps S20 free. Recommendation to adjudicate (CL2-A6): make :mandatory YES structurally impossible for model kinds via a schema conditional, turning V8I-02 from prose into a kernel law (CLAUDE.md law: make the error structurally impossible). No S04/S19/JTMS constraint.")
  )

