  :source-forms 22
  :current-authority-seat "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp — section '2. UNIVERSAL STABLE CONTRACTS (§6)' header L80-84 ('13 universal contracts. EXISTING canonical types are `define-reference` ... Contracts genuinely introduced by v1.6 are `define-record`'): PerceptionEnvelope/1 L85, MemoryEvent/1 L100, CapabilityManifest/1 L108, ToolInvocation/1 L115, Plan/1 L122, ExecutionReceipt/1 L135, SafetyState/1 L139; section '3. PUBLIC LEGAL LANGUAGE COGNITION LAYER' header L164 (comment L182 'typed cognition I/O records'): MorphLattice/1 L183, PackedParseForest/1 L186, CoreferenceRecord/1 L189, DiscourseState/1 L192, LegalSemanticAlternative/1 L195, ClarificationState/1 L198, PromotionEvidence/1 L201, CognitionResult/1 L204, LanguageCognitionLayer/1 L209; section '4. COMPLETE MEMORY ARCHITECTURE' header L274-277: MemoryPolicy/1 L289, MemoryProjection/1 L294; section '5. FUTURE EXTENSION CONTRACTS (§7)' header L310-311: PrivateMemoryEvent/1 L312, PrivateMatterProfile/1 L317, RealTimeAssistance/1 L323, EmbodimentInterfaces/1 L328. Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:36 (DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE, DDI-2, :source-count 22). For the 14 that are ISR contracts, ISR also declares a :seat string (INTERFACE-AND-SCHEMA-REGISTRY.sexp:11-56)."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "SPLIT, and the split is the decision: type IDENTITY already lives in interfaces-and-types.sexp (14 of the 22 are `type` facts there); the FIELD structure has no seat. UNDECIDED between extending interfaces-and-types.sexp (V1.5/V1.6 dossiers) and a NEW module 'record-fields.sexp' (V1.7/V1.8 dossiers) — the same module must take all four DDI-2 record classes (84 records / 777 fields by my own count) or 'one seat per concept' is lost (ADJ-DDI2-FIELD-SEAT). The 8 records that are NOT model types (7 cognition + PrivateMemoryEvent/1) additionally need an ISR row before a `type` fact can be written at all (see dependencies)."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "EXISTING `type` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:148-152) for identity — 14 already exist (interfaces-and-types.sexp:39,34,12,60,40,26,55,19,30,35,36,41,44,24), 8 would be new — PLUS a NEW `field` fact type. flattening rule: keep the existing `type` fact as the record identity; one `field` fact per (:name :type T) entry (id = <record>__<field>, :record <type-id> :name <field> :ordinal <n> :type-token <T> :list YES/NO :nullable YES/NO :domain <enum-id or type-id or primitive-id>); (list X) -> :list YES, (or X null) -> :nullable YES, (member ...) -> an anonymous enum id <record>__<field>__MEMBERS with enum-value facts; primitive tokens (id semver ref sha256 sig instant text ...) need a `primitive` fact family or an explicit exemption from L3 (V5-A8 / A20 / ADJ-V17-REC-5) Cardinality by my own reader: 190 `field` facts over 22 records, including 19 `(list X)` fields, 2 `(or X null)` fields and 9 inline `(member ...)` sets (which need either 9 anonymous `enum` ids or a STRING encoding — a decision, not a mechanical step). primitive type tokens are defined in NONE of the six registries (V1.5-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh:227 and V1.6-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh:151-152 hard-code them as `prim`). no `enum`/`enum-value`/`field`/`primitive`/`cardinality`/`ref-class`/`adapter`/`canonical-identity` fact type exists among the 34 fact types (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:84-288); `define-enum` there is schema syntax for the model's own closed domains only (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:18,47-76); L1 forbids keywords, nested lists and NIL as values (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6) and the closed field set forbids adding keys to `type` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:9-13,148-152)"
  :owner "MIXED — 14 declared, 8 UNKNOWN or disputed. DECLARED (ISR + model agree): S02 PerceptionEnvelope/1 (ISR:11; interfaces-and-types.sexp:39), S19 MemoryEvent/1 (ISR:17; :34), S20 CapabilityManifest/1 (ISR:19; :12) and ToolInvocation/1 (ISR:21; :60), S12 Plan/1 (ISR:23; :40) and ExecutionReceipt/1 (ISR:29; :26), S21 SafetyState/1 (ISR:31; :55), S04 CognitionResult/1 (ISR:43; :19) and LanguageCognitionLayer/1 (ISR:41; :30), S19 MemoryPolicy/1 (ISR:47; :35) and MemoryProjection/1 (ISR:45; :36), S22 PrivateMatterProfile/1 (ISR:51; :41), S23 RealTimeAssistance/1 (ISR:53; :44), S24 EmbodimentInterfaces/1 (ISR:55; :24). UNKNOWN (6 cognition records absent from ISR and from every registry's owner field): MorphLattice/1, PackedParseForest/1, CoreferenceRecord/1, DiscourseState/1, LegalSemanticAlternative/1, ClarificationState/1 — S04 is a prose inference from V1.6:164-166 and SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:45-48 only. DISPUTED: PromotionEvidence/1 — its producing stage names S03's and S04's seats together (V1.6:228 'legal-extraction-verify.lisp + legal-ast.lisp + legal-reasoning-bridge.lisp'; seats.sexp:30,32). DISPUTED: PrivateMemoryEvent/1 — S19 by section ('the private extension lives in §5', V1.6:276-277) vs S22 Private Matter Profile (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:108-110); orchestrator-notes.md N9. No winner is picked here."
  :writer "NO_WRITER for the schema facts themselves. For the record INSTANCES the model already declares writers where a store exists: memory store writer SEAT-WRITE-AUTHORITY (stores-and-authorities.sexp:10) for MemoryEvent/1, legal-ir writer SEAT-WRITE-AUTHORITY (:9), trust-bundle writer SEAT-MLTP-THRESHOLD-CUSTODY (:14). For the 8 unseated records there is no store and therefore no writer — and NO registry names one; UNKNOWN, not NO_WRITER, because the cognition records are stage outputs whose producing seat is named only in the DDI-1 construction order (V1.6:217-229)."
  :classification "MIXED — private members named: PrivateMemoryEvent/1 (V1.6:312 ':status :DEFERRED_PRIVATE :public-dependency nil'), PrivateMatterProfile/1 (:317), RealTimeAssistance/1 (:323), EmbodimentInterfaces/1 (:328). Three of those four are already PRIVATE `type` facts (interfaces-and-types.sexp:41,44,24) and are counted in property-family PF-L5-PRIVATE-TYPE-LEAK :cardinality 6 (verification-corpus.sexp:45-47); PrivateMemoryEvent/1 is NOT a model fact at all (orchestrator-notes.md N9), so importing it would move that cardinality to 7 and require the family declaration to move with it. The other 18 are PUBLIC. NOTE the leak the sources themselves flag: PUBLIC MemoryPolicy/1 (interfaces-and-types.sexp:35) has field :scope_isolation :type (list MemoryScope) (V1.6:293), and MemoryScope carries :client/:matter (V1.6:288) — against :V6I-MEM-public-base-clean (V1.6:305-308) and :V7I-PUBPRIV-acyclic (V1.7:297-299)."
  :dependencies ("SCHEMA FIRST: NEW `field` fact type (+ a primitive-type family or an explicit L3 exemption for the 11 primitive tokens) and a schema-version bump (X74-X76 verification-corpus.sexp:354-370) — fact-type declaration" "SAME BATCH, STRICTLY FIRST: V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum — 11 field :domain refs (dag.json 'V1.6 define-record -> V1.6 define-closed-enum', 11 refs); a `field :domain` naming an enum cannot be L3-closed before the enum facts exist" "EXISTING model facts: the 14 `type` facts and their 26 `consumes` edges (dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:23-124) — identity ref targets" "ISR EXTENSION (an IMPORTED class, deferred-imports.sexp:6): 8 records have no ISR row although :ISR-V6-closure (ISR:177-180) states 'Every contract referenced by any subsystem or schema is DEFINED here exactly once with an owner and a definition seat ... Referenced-but-undefined => architecture-gate FAIL' — reference kind: closure obligation on an already-imported class" "DECISION FIRST: owner for 8 records; the one `field` module (ADJ-DDI2-FIELD-SEAT); the inline-(member ...) encoding; the record/reference doctrine (A1) for MemoryEvent/1 and CognitionResult/1")
  :consumers ("SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-subsystem (IMPORTED, rank 0) — 12 refs (dag.json), e.g. SR:100 S20 -> V1.6:108 CapabilityManifest/1, SR:100 S20 -> V1.6:115 ToolInvocation/1" "V1.6 define-construction-order cognition-stage-dag (V1.6:217, DDI-1) — 9 refs; V1.7 define-construction-order cognition-stage-dag-v7 (V1.7:80, DDI-1) — 6 refs" "V1.7 define-ra-closure-roots (V1.7:290, DDI-1) — 7 refs; V1.8 define-ra-closure-roots (V1.8:259, DDI-1) — 6 refs" "V1.8 define-cognition-node-types (V1.8:363, DDI-3) — 6 refs; V1.8 define-canonical-identity (V1.8:428-429, DDI-1) — 2 refs; V1.8 define-reference (V1.8:348, DDI-2) — 1 ref" "V1.6 define-invariant — 9 refs (DDI-4); V1.6 define-ref-classification-v6 (V1.6:344, DDI-2) — 3 refs; V1.6 define-protocol (V1.6:57) — 1 ref; V1.7 define-pipeline (V1.7:308, DDI-1) — 2 refs" "no tracked source/ or systems/ file names any record/enum id of the six registries (git grep at RO = 0); the only mechanical readers are the legacy audits/harness classified HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:436,440,444,450,453)")
  :identity-version-rule "MIXED. LIVE-REFERENCE-TARGET (2): MemoryEvent/1 and CognitionResult/1 — V1.8:347 and V1.8:348 are define-reference blocks whose :canonical-file/:locator point INTO this file at these very forms (V1.8:420-422 'the reference is the identity seat, the define-record remains the structure seat'), and V1.8:429/:428 repeat the identity in define-canonical-identity (DDI-1). Importing the records moves the pointer target out of V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp and the reference becomes stale (ADJ-V18-REF-2). SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT (3): CoreferenceRecord/1 -> ReferenceGraph/1 (V1.7:54 comment 'supersedes v1.6 CoreferenceRecord/1 singular'); LegalSemanticAlternative/1 -> LegalSemanticAlternativeSet/1 (V1.7:62-65); ClarificationState/1 -> ClarificationDecision/1 (V1.7:70) and again -> ClarificationRequest/Response/LifecycleState (V1.8:28-39). None of the three carries a supersession key; the statement is a comment. ONLY-VERSION (17): no other registry defines these names (my own grep; version-chains.md)."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION for the class as a whole. Per-form target once the blockers clear: MERGE-INTO-EXISTING-FACT for the 14 whose `type` fact exists (add `field` facts beside the existing identity — never a second `type` id, which L2 forbids, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:106-107); IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL for the 8 unseated records only after ISR is extended and an owner is decided; IMPORT-AS-HISTORICAL-VERSION or SKIP-WITH-PROOF for the 3 superseded cognition records is an open question (A8) — SUPERSEDED-REGISTER.md:254-258 says v1.6 is superseded at the candidate layer without falsifying anything, which is not a migration rule."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "HIGH. (1) Record-vs-reference duality: :V6I-REF-single-source-of-truth (V1.6:158-162) REJECTS a type defined as both a record and a reference, yet V1.8:347-348 defines exactly that for MemoryEvent/1 and CognitionResult/1 and V1.8:420-422 legitimises it — importing both classes without settling A1 creates two identity seats per type. (2) Two field modules across the four DDI-2 record classes (ADJ-DDI2-FIELD-SEAT). (3) ClarifiedInterpretation/1-style same-name divergence does not arise inside V1.6, but MemoryPolicy/1 (V1.6:289) vs MemoryScopePolicy/1 (V1.7:106) is a second memory-policy seat (ADJ-V17-REC-4). (4) 8 records outside ISR are a live violation of ISR's own closure invariant (ISR:177-180) — importing them silently would make the model the first place they are 'defined exactly once', bypassing the registry that claims that role."
  :requirement "Partial and owner-dependent. The 14 seated records inherit their owner subsystem's req-map row (e.g. S20 -> R-V6-ADP/V6Q-17/WP-07+11+14, requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:86-88; S19 -> R-V6-MEM/V6Q-02/FUTURE_BOOK_REVISION, :85; S04 -> R-129/Q08/WP-08, :70). The 8 unseated records have NO requirement, NO test and NO WP — and cannot get a req-map row until they have an owner subsystem, because req-map's :subsystem is a closed ref (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:178-181). L6 is over subsystems, so this is silent today."
  :invariant "L1 (nested field lists and keywords cannot be values — MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6 — hence the flattening), L2 (one `type` id, one owner family — MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:106-107), L3 (:record and :domain refs closed), L5 (public/private isolation — the four private records and the MemoryPolicy/1 (list MemoryScope) field). Source invariants: :V6I-REF-single-source-of-truth (V1.6:158-162), :V6I-MEM-public-base-clean (V1.6:305-308), :V6I-16-extension-isolation (V1.6:334-338), :ISR-V6-closure (ISR:177-180)."
  :qualification-test "Existing model `test` facts reachable through the owners: Q08 (requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:32, S04), V6Q-02 (:47, S19), V6Q-17 (:50, S20), V6Q-01 (:46, S21), V6Q-09 (:48, S22), V6Q-13 (:49, S23/S24) — all design-only/UNEXECUTED (orchestrator-notes.md N7). NEW executable one-liner: for every `field` fact, its :record resolves to a declared `type` and its :domain resolves to a declared `type`, `enum` or `primitive`; and the count of `field` facts whose :record is a PRIVATE type equals the count declared by a NEW property-family, so that dropping a private record's fields is a named failure rather than a smaller number."
  :falsifier "APPEND to the field module `(fact field MemoryEvent/1__no_such :record MemoryEvent/1 :name no_such :ordinal 99 :domain NoSuchDomain)` — both paths must reject: kernel-reason 'resolves to no declared type or enum', checker-reason 'L3' (shape of K15, verification-corpus.sexp:155-157). APPEND `(fact type MemoryEvent/1 :classification PUBLIC :owner-subsystem S19)` a second time — must be rejected as 'duplicate seat TYPE MemoryEvent/1' (L2; the exact wording is KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:124). REPLACE on the imported PrivateMemoryEvent/1 `:classification PRIVATE` with `:classification PUBLIC` — must be rejected as a public/private leak once a consumes edge exists (FX-L5-PUBLIC-PRIVATE-LEAK verification-corpus.sexp:34-35); note that with NO consumes edge nothing today rejects it, which is the finding."
  :rollback "delete the imported facts of this class and the fact-type/enum declarations added to MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp for it, re-run build_root.py so ROOT.sexp re-pins the 14 modules (ROOT.sexp:12-27; L7), and restore the ledger row to DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT / AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE (deferred-imports.sexp) so the source file is authoritative again; the source registry is never edited by the import (V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp:256 'v1.5 files are NOT edited' is the precedent)"
  :batch-reason "DDI-2 because build_deferred.py maps the head define-record to DDI-2, materialised at deferred-imports.sexp:36. DISAGREES in BOTH directions. Too late: five rank-0/rank-1 classes already reference it — SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-subsystem (IMPORTED, 12 refs), V1.6/V1.7 define-construction-order (DDI-1, 9+6 refs), V1.7/V1.8 define-ra-closure-roots (DDI-1, 7+6 refs), V1.8 define-canonical-identity (DDI-1, 2 refs), V1.7 define-pipeline (DDI-1, 2 refs) — dag.json lists all six as order violations. Too early: nothing. Its only out-edge is to V1.6 define-closed-enum, same batch. The mechanical evidence therefore says the RECORD IDENTITIES belong in DDI-1 (they are the ref targets of the DDI-1 topology) while their FIELDS belong in DDI-2."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "(a) A1 — record-vs-reference doctrine: does the model admit one identity seat per type (:V6I-REF, V1.6:158-162) or the V1.8 identity-seat/structure-seat split (V1.8:420-422)? (b) Who owns MorphLattice/1, PackedParseForest/1, CoreferenceRecord/1, DiscourseState/1, LegalSemanticAlternative/1, ClarificationState/1, PromotionEvidence/1 and PrivateMemoryEvent/1, and is INTERFACE-AND-SCHEMA-REGISTRY.sexp (an IMPORTED class) extended first so :ISR-V6-closure holds? (c) Do the 3 superseded cognition records import as historical versions or are they skipped with proof? (d) How is an inline `(member ...)` set encoded — anonymous enum id `<record>__<field>__MEMBERS`, or a STRING? (e) Is `primitive` a fact family, or are the 11 primitive tokens exempt from L3?"
  :adjudication-items ("ADJ-DDI2-FIELD-SEAT: the four DDI-2 record classes (V1.5 18/181 fields, V1.6 22/190, V1.7 25/227, V1.8 19/179 — my own count) must share ONE `field` seat; the dossiers propose interfaces-and-types.sexp (V1.5/V1.6) vs a NEW module 'record-fields'/'schemas' (V1.7/V1.8). No winner is picked here." "A1 (V1.6 dossier): record-vs-reference doctrine — :V6I-REF (V1.6:158-162) rejects it, V1.8:347-348 + V1.8:420-422 institutionalise it, for MemoryEvent/1 and CognitionResult/1." "A7 (V1.6 dossier): 8 records outside ISR while :ISR-V6-closure (ISR:177-180) demands definition there exactly once with an owner; `type` requires :owner-subsystem (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:148-152)." "A8 (V1.6 dossier): cognition lineage triple (V1.6:217 -> V1.7:80 -> V1.8:53/363) — do the 3 superseded records import as lineage?" "N9 (orchestrator): PrivateMemoryEvent/1 owner S19 (V1.6:276-277) vs S22 (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:108-110); it is PRIVATE and not a model type today, so PF-L5-PRIVATE-TYPE-LEAK :cardinality 6 (verification-corpus.sexp:45-47) must move with it." "A10 / ADJ-DDI2-PRIVATE-ENUM: PUBLIC MemoryPolicy/1 binds (list MemoryScope) with :client/:matter (V1.6:293 vs :288) against V1.6:305-308 and V1.7:297-299." "A20 (V1.6 dossier): primitives + field grammar — id/semver/mime/sha256/span/instant/ref/sig/text/duration/uncertainty are defined in no registry; (list X)/(or X null)/(member ...) have no model counterpart (orchestrator-notes.md N4)." "A5 (V1.6 dossier): the :extends bases of ToolInvocation/1 ('source/*.lisp lawmax/neural-task/1') and Plan/1 ('cockpit_intent + decisions.lisp') resolve to no tracked Lisp identifier — the :extends key has no import target." "PromotionEvidence/1 owner: its producing stage seat spans S03 (seats.sexp:30) and S04 (:32) — V1.6:228 names both; no registry assigns one.")
  :topological-position 8 :atomic-groups (4)
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "every universal contract is content-addressed (V1.6:86 envelope_id = hex(sha256(id_domain || 0x1F || canonical(BODY))); V6I-11 V1.6:151-154) through source/journal.lisp:61 canon-sexp (ONE canonical value serialization; admissible domain NIL/keyword/string/integer/list, :65-66) + source/journal.lisp:88 sha256-hex; MemoryEvent/1 is 'a projection over the memory.lisp substrate' (V1.6:101) whose substrate hash ALREADY is canon-sexp (source/memory.lisp:96-110 record-episode (chained-append + body hash via journal:canon-sexp, :hv 2)) | invariant: type-closed, non-circular, identity = content-address, lifecycle detached (V6I-11) | fallback: copy-on-write (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:27)" :clos-class "cognition I/O records (MorphLattice ... CognitionResult) as typed classes in the S04 seat (pattern source/legal-ast.lisp:291-338 ast-node; source/greek-nlp-core.lisp:127 token, :549 document) so stage generics can specialize on them; MemoryEvent/1 must NOT become a second memory object: the seat is the plist journal line with accessors (source/memory.lisp:53-61) — a CLOS view would be a duplicate seat unless it is a typed decoder VIEW over that line | invariant: one class per concept; one memory seat (V7I-MEM-one-owner V1.7:115-118) | fallback: plain structs (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:20)" :generic-function "cognition stage records are the specializers/results of the existing stage generics (source/cognition.lisp:92 plan / :96 execute-step / :101 synthesize / :107 triage / :113 critique (defgeneric, open dispatch per frame); source/greek-nlp-core.lisp:387-407 analyzer class + analyze defgeneric + *analyzer-registry*/register-analyzer/get-analyzer (analyzer-not-found typed condition); :573 define-analyzer macro analyze); each stage of cognition-stage-dag (V1.6:217-229) is a METHOD, not a new function family | invariant: out-type of a stage == in-type of the next (V7I-COG-info-preserving V1.7:95-101; typed edges V8I-COG-typed-edges V1.8:386-391) | fallback: single dispatch fn (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:21)" :condition-restart "typed decoder conditions per record (source/legal-ast.lisp:1704-1717 form-to-ast (typed decoder: closed+mandatory key-set, no duplicate keys, deep type check, class allowlist, no eval); :1071 ast-decode-error); ClarificationState/1 :status (:OPEN :ANSWERED :ABANDONED, V1.6:200) and CognitionResult/1 :errors (V1.6:207) are the visible results of typed conditions; a restart (source/legal-ast.lisp:1598-1604 with-ast-restarts (restart-case); source/trace-core.lisp:264; source/greek-tokenizer-advanced.lisp:434 handle-unknown-char) covers ONLY the dynamic extent of one cognition invocation — suspension across invocations must be a persisted record (CL2-A7) | invariant: never a guess; ambiguity => UNKNOWN/CONFLICTING/clarification (V6I-06 V1.6:35-37) | fallback: return typed error value (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:24)" :macro-dsl "as class 2 (record macro admissible only with golden expansion vs `field` facts; registry forms stay data) | invariant: compile-time only (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:25); single field-list seat (V6I-REF V1.6:158-162; CL2-A1) | fallback: hand-written defstruct/defclass + decoder" :protocol "cognition records are the typed I/O of the Language Cognition Layer inside the Public Legal Discernment Engine (V1.6:164-166 'NOT a second reasoning engine'); LanguageCognitionLayer/1 :analyzer_registry_ref (V1.6:212 'incremental/hot-swappable analyzers via capability registry') binds to the analyzer protocol registry (source/greek-nlp-core.lisp:387-407 analyzer class + analyze defgeneric + *analyzer-registry*/register-analyzer/get-analyzer (analyzer-not-found typed condition); :573 define-analyzer macro) | invariant: V6I-13 one cognition seat (V1.6:261-264); V6I-COG-one-to-one | fallback: explicit per-stage function calls" :package-asdf-boundary "18 PUBLIC records -> S02/S03/S04/S12/S19/S20/S21 seat packages (AM/seats.sexp:28-61); 4 :DEFERRED_PRIVATE records (V1.6:312-333) -> a private system that NO public system :depends-on (AM/seats.sexp:91-96 have no path => no package exists) | invariant: public->private/embodiment edges FORBIDDEN, boundary acyclic (V6I-16 V1.6:334-338; L5 AM/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:1-3 (*read-eval* nil, standard readtable, no eval), :23 *enums*, :24 *conds*, :56-60 reader, :243-257 law5-isolation :243-257; ASDF acyclic 16 ASDF systems, 53 edges, cycle NONE (deployment/collab/dialogue/0146-claude.md:18); 17 .asd paths at HEAD of which systems/orchestrator-omega.asd is a symlink to ../orchestrator-omega.asd; source/safe-read.lisp:38-39 loaded FIRST in orchestrator-infrastructure) | fallback: monolith package (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:31) — inadmissible for the 4 private records; their real fallback is non-import into the public build" :persistent-event "MemoryEvent/1 (bitemporal valid_time/known_time, :supersedes, write_authority_id V1.6:102-107), ExecutionReceipt/1, PromotionEvidence/1, SafetyState/1 as-of are journaled through source/journal.lisp:507 chained-append (atomic compare-and-append under lock; stale-chain-link :495); NOTE the model names SEAT-WRITE-AUTHORITY as writer of the memory store (AM/stores-and-authorities.sexp:10) while source/memory.lisp:96 calls journal:chained-append directly and source/write-authority.lisp:4-8 exports emit-graph/with-write-authority only; :16-49 emit-graph requires :authority in (:canonical :provenance) has no memory/journal API (CL2-A11) | invariant: canonical memory writes ONLY by the authorized write authority (V6I-05 V1.6:32-34; V6I-14) | fallback: write-file-atomic (source/journal.lisp:25)" :truth-maintenance-dependency "LegalSemanticAlternative :score is uncertainty, never truth; PromotionEvidence :outcome (:PROMOTED :REJECTED :UNKNOWN V1.6:203) = the epistemic wall verdict (source/legal-extraction-verify.lisp:17-23 V1-V4 deterministic checks (V4 consistency in the JTMS); :340 verdict) that admits a candidate as a JTMS premise; CognitionResult/1 :coverage :OUTSIDE => UNKNOWN (V1.6:207,213) | invariant: symbolic-only judgement; proposer never authority (V6I-10; V6I-COG-symbolic-only V1.6:265-269) | fallback: full recompute (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:28)" :temporal-index-projection "MemoryEvent/1 valid_time x known_time 'bitemporal (reuse L2)' (V1.6:105) => the ONE bitemporal seat source/version-graph.lisp:1030 version-at (valid-at legal-date x known-at legal-instant; both typed and mandatory) with typed legal-instant (source/version-graph.lisp:148-149 deftype legal-date / legal-instant); MemoryProjection/1 :as_of is a point-in-time projection; CapabilityManifest :expiration | invariant: one bitemporal seat (source/legal-temporal.lisp:6-16); memory continuity byte-verifiable across model replacement (V6I-14 V1.6:297-300) | fallback: explicit fold recompute" :compile-time-validation "slot :type declarations + build-time set equality slots == `field` facts (as class 2); build-time transitive closure over the 5 public roots (V1.6:340-347, superseded by V1.7/V1.8 ra-closure-roots DDI-1) must contain no :DEFERRED_PRIVATE record (audit V6S12) — the model's L5 already does this at type level (AM/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:1-3 (*read-eval* nil, standard readtable, no eval), :23 *enums*, :24 *conds*, :56-60 reader, :243-257 law5-isolation :243-257) | invariant: V6I-MEM-public-base-clean; V6I-16 | fallback: runtime check (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:32)" :runtime-validation "typed decoder per record over safe-read (internal) or the non-evaluating ingress decoder (external, NOT BUILT: source/ingress-decoder.lisp NOT FOUND (git ls-files); deployment/LAWMAX-SECURE-SEMANTIC-INGRESS-CONTRACT.md:12 'External non-evaluating JSON/CBOR decoder = NEW, MISSING'; deployment/LAWMAX-THREAT-MODEL.md:46 Θ18, :48 Θ20); PerceptionEnvelope/1 is the adapter-fed boundary record and must ONLY be produced by that decoder (V1.6:85, :64) | invariant: no cl:read/eval over external bytes (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:35; V1.6:259) | fallback: reject input" :python-in-cl-risk "HIGH. Naive import: (a) :extends STRING pointers ('source/*.lisp lawmax/neural-task/1', 'cockpit_intent + decisions.lisp' V1.6:116,123 — NOT FOUND in source, dossier A5) become opaque strings; (b) :status :DEFERRED_PRIVATE / :public-dependency nil (V1.6:312) become keyword/NIL values (illegal, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:6); (c) field type expressions as strings parsed by regex (as class 2); (d) MemoryEvent/1 as a hash-table record duplicating the memory.lisp plist substrate. CL-native: :extends as an L3 ref to a `type`/seat fact or dropped by adjudication; :status via the seat-status enum (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:62) and classification PRIVATE (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:47); decomposed typed fields; MemoryEvent/1 as a typed decoder VIEW over the journal plist (accessors source/memory.lisp:53-61), hashed by the same canon-sexp." :future-freedom "YES — flagged. (a) S04: CognitionResult/1.errors binds V1.6 CognitionError (V1.6:207) while V1.7 declares CognitionErrorV7 — duplicate taxonomy (ADJ-V17-ENUM-1); intermediate records (MorphLattice, PackedParseForest, ...) freeze the INTERNAL representations of language cognition as canonical hash-bearing I/O — by design (V6I-COG-symbolic-only) and versioned (/1), so a future technique must emit these records or a /2 — acceptable if the version rule is explicit. (b) S19: MemoryEvent/1 :scope PublicMemoryScope vs MemoryScopeV7 (ADJ-V17-ENUM-2); MemoryPolicy/1 carries private-bearing MemoryScope (V1.6:293) — leak to repair (A10). (c) S20/V8I-02: freedom-preserving — MemoryProjection/1 is 'the ONLY thing a model receives' (V1.6:294-296), CapabilityManifest/1 makes every adapter replaceable (V1.6:108). (d) Reasoning: no second engine (V1.6:164-166).")
  )

(ddi-class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-reference
  :batch DDI-2 :source-file "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp" :fact-class "define-reference" :source-count 6 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms (("CandidateInterpretation/1" :line 92 :sha16 "dbab024931378a6b") ("LegalIR/1" :line 96 :sha16 "7ff3107628071d41") ("ActionIntent/1" :line 127 :sha16 "a3d4c332d18b6149") ("Approval/1" :line 131 :sha16 "fd50298c13b17025") ("TrustBundle/1" :line 143 :sha16 "625c55482fd1d530") ("DeclassificationReceipt/1" :line 147 :sha16 "ab262b94a5ccd16f"))
  :source-file "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp"
  :source-forms 6
  :current-authority-seat "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp section '2. UNIVERSAL STABLE CONTRACTS (§6)' header L80-84 (the rule itself: 'EXISTING canonical types are `define-reference` (identity + version + canonical seat; NO redefined fields — one source of truth, V6I-REF)'): CandidateInterpretation/1 L92-95, LegalIR/1 L96-99, ActionIntent/1 L127-130, Approval/1 L131-134, TrustBundle/1 L143-146, DeclassificationReceipt/1 L147-150. Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:38 (DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE, DDI-2, :source-count 6). ISR carries a competing :seat string for all six (ISR:13,15,25,27,33,35)."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "interfaces-and-types.sexp (existing) IF the payload becomes optional fields of `type`; a NEW module only if a separate `canonical-identity` family is chosen. Either way the module MUST be the same one that takes V1.7 define-reference (8 forms), V1.8 define-reference (9 forms) and V1.8 define-canonical-identity (8 forms, DDI-1) — four classes, one concept 'the canonical identity of a type' (ADJ-DDI2-IDENTITY-FAMILY). Because define-canonical-identity is DDI-1, the family shape is decided BEFORE this class is reached; this row inherits that decision rather than making it."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "TWO candidate shapes, both requiring MODEL-SCHEMA change. (i) EXTEND `type` with :optional (identity version canonical-file locator owner-wp) — cheapest, keeps one fact per type, but the closed field set (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:9-13,148-152) makes this a schema edit and a schema-version bump. (ii) NEW `canonical-identity` (:required (type identity version) :optional (canonical-file locator owner-wp) :ref ((type type) (owner-wp wp))) — matches the V1.8 define-canonical-identity shape and keeps `type` untouched. Flattening rule: values are already flat strings; :owner-wp becomes a closed ref to the existing `wp` facts (WP-07 requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:59, WP-03 :56, WP-12 :63, WP-06 :58 — all exist). 6 facts. no `enum`/`enum-value`/`field`/`primitive`/`cardinality`/`ref-class`/`adapter`/`canonical-identity` fact type exists among the 34 fact types (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:84-288); `define-enum` there is schema syntax for the model's own closed domains only (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:18,47-76); L1 forbids keywords, nested lists and NIL as values (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6) and the closed field set forbids adding keys to `type` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:9-13,148-152)"
  :owner "All six declared and agreeing across ISR and the model: S03 CandidateInterpretation/1 (ISR:13; interfaces-and-types.sexp:9), S04 LegalIR/1 (ISR:15; :32), S12 ActionIntent/1 (ISR:25; :5), S12 Approval/1 (ISR:27; :8), S10 TrustBundle/1 (ISR:33; :61), S18 DeclassificationReceipt/1 (ISR:35; :23). The form itself declares :owner-wp, not an owner subsystem — WP-07, WP-03, WP-12, WP-12, WP-06, WP-12 respectively (V1.6:95,99,130,134,146,150)."
  :writer "NO_WRITER for the identity facts. Where the referenced type has a store the model already names the writer: legal-ir writer SEAT-WRITE-AUTHORITY (stores-and-authorities.sexp:9) for LegalIR/1; trust-bundle writer SEAT-MLTP-THRESHOLD-CUSTODY (:14) for TrustBundle/1. CandidateInterpretation/1, ActionIntent/1, Approval/1 and DeclassificationReceipt/1 have no store and no declared writer anywhere — NO_WRITER by absence of a store, not by declaration."
  :classification "PUBLIC (all six) — every one is a PUBLIC `type` fact in the model (interfaces-and-types.sexp:9,32,5,8,61,23); none appears in the private-forbidden lists (V1.7:296; V1.8:262-263). DeclassificationReceipt/1 is the PUBLIC side of the one private->public gate (V1.6:147-150) and is consumed by PRIVATE S22 (dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:110) — a PRIVATE consumer of a PUBLIC type, which L5 permits (KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:252-254 fails only PUBLIC-consumes-PRIVATE)."
  :dependencies ("DDI-1 FIRST: V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-canonical-identity (deferred-imports.sexp:59, DDI-1) fixes the identity fact family; this class must reuse it (ADJ-DDI2-IDENTITY-FAMILY) — reference kind: shared fact family" "SCHEMA FIRST: whichever shape wins, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp changes and the schema version moves (X74-X76 verification-corpus.sexp:354-370)" "EXISTING model facts: the 6 `type` facts (interfaces-and-types.sexp:9,32,5,8,61,23) and the 4 `wp` facts WP-03/WP-06/WP-07/WP-12 (requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:56,58,59,63) — :type and :owner-wp ref targets, all present" "DECISION FIRST: A2/A3/A4 — three of the six :canonical pointers do not resolve to a tracked artifact that defines the thing (see conflict field)")
  :consumers ("V1.6 define-invariant — 9 refs (DDI-4), including :V6I-REF-single-source-of-truth (V1.6:158-162) which names all six by name" "SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-subsystem (IMPORTED, rank 0) — 7 refs (dag.json), e.g. SR:41 S03 -> V1.6:92, SR:45 S04 -> V1.6:96" "V1.8 define-canonical-identity (DDI-1) — 3 refs (V1.8:425 -> V1.6:96 LegalIR/1; V1.8:426 -> V1.6:143 TrustBundle/1; V1.8:427 -> V1.6:147 DeclassificationReceipt/1)" "V1.7 define-ra-closure-roots (DDI-1) — 2 refs; V1.8 define-ra-closure-roots (DDI-1) — 2 refs; V1.7 define-pipeline (DDI-1) — 1 ref; V1.6 define-ref-classification-v6 (DDI-2) — 2 refs; V1.6 define-protocol (DDI-4) — 1 ref; ISR define-interface (IMPORTED) — 1 ref (ISR:117)" "V1.8 define-reference LegalIR/1 (V1.8:345), TrustBundle/1 (:346), DeclassificationReceipt/1 (:349) — competing reference blocks for three of the same identities" "no tracked source/ or systems/ file names any record/enum id of the six registries (git grep at RO = 0); the only mechanical readers are the legacy audits/harness classified HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:436,440,444,450,453)")
  :identity-version-rule "SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT for 3, ONLY-VERSION for 3. DIVERGENT: LegalIR/1 — V1.6:97 :canonical names TWO artifacts ('legal-ast.lisp + LAWMAX-LEGAL-IR-SEMANTIC-CONTRACT.md', matching ISR:15-16) while V1.8:345 names only the .md with :locator 'Counterproof'; same :identity 'lawmax/legal-ir/1' and same :version. TrustBundle/1 — V1.6:143 :canonical is a prose description ('MLTP LocalTrustState + trust_bundle_ref (bnd1:)') while V1.8:346 is file+locator; same identity. DeclassificationReceipt/1 — V1.6:147 :canonical 'boundary schemas (§1.3/§1.4)' while V1.8:349 points BACK at V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp with :locator 'DeclassificationReceipt/1', i.e. a reference to a reference. ONLY-VERSION: CandidateInterpretation/1, ActionIntent/1, Approval/1 — no V1.7/V1.8 reference or identity form (my own grep). All six are also LIVE-REFERENCE-TARGET in the weaker sense that ISR (IMPORTED) and the DDI-1 closure roots name them."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION. Once the identity family is fixed in DDI-1 it is MERGE-INTO-EXISTING-FACT for all six (the `type` fact exists; only the identity payload is added) — never IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL as a second fact keyed by the same id, which L2 forbids (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:106-107). For LegalIR/1, TrustBundle/1 and DeclassificationReceipt/1 the choice between the V1.6 and the V1.8 pointer is an adjudication, not a merge."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "HIGH — this class is the clearest duplicate-seat surface in DDI-2. Three identities have TWO reference blocks each (V1.6 vs V1.8) with different key vocabularies and different targets; a fourth (CognitionResult/1) has V1.7 vs V1.8. Three :canonical pointers do not resolve: 'source/*.lisp neural-candidate/1' (V1.6:93) and 'cockpit_intent' (V1.6:128) exist in no tracked Lisp (V1.6 dossier A4, verified by that dossier's git grep; only CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.4.md prose), and 'boundary schemas (§1.3/§1.4)' (V1.6:147) contains no DeclassificationReceipt definition (V1.6 dossier A3). Approval/1's :canonical carries the locator '(L12)' whose meaning is UNKNOWN (V1.6 dossier U1). Model-side there is no id collision: adding identity payload to the existing `type` facts creates no new id."
  :requirement "Inherited from the owner subsystems' req-map rows: S03__WP-07 (R-25/Q22, requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:69), S04__WP-08 (R-129/Q08, :70), S12__WP-12 (R-118/Q19, :78), S10__WP-06 (R-130/Q28, :76), S18__WP-12 (R-111/Q20, :84). The forms' own :owner-wp values (WP-07/WP-03/WP-12/WP-12/WP-06/WP-12) DISAGREE with three of those req-map WPs (S04's row is WP-08, not WP-03; S10's row is WP-06, which agrees) — the :owner-wp of a type and the :wp of its owner's req-map row are two different bindings and nothing reconciles them."
  :invariant "L2 (one id under one fact type — the identity payload must not become a second fact with the same id), L3 (:type closes on `type`, :owner-wp on `wp`). Source invariants: :V6I-REF-single-source-of-truth (V1.6:158-162, audit V6S13) and :V8I-XREF-real (V1.8:353-357) — the latter demands that a reference's canonical-file exist and contain the locator, a check that exists in NO model gate (my own grep of gate_checks.py finds no locator resolver; cf. orchestrator-notes.md N17 for the same defect in `rationale`)."
  :qualification-test "NEW. Executable one-liner: for every canonical-identity fact, (a) :type resolves to a declared `type`, (b) the file named by :canonical-file exists in the candidate tree, and (c) `grep -F -- '<locator>' <canonical-file>` returns at least one line — the V8I-XREF-real mechanism (V1.8:353-357), which today has no implementation on either verification path. This same check would catch the live RAT-PUBPRIV defect in `rationale` (rationale-references.sexp:7; orchestrator-notes.md N17), so one check closes two holes."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact canonical-identity NoSuchType :type NoSuchType :identity lawmax/x/1 :version 1)` — both paths must reject: kernel-reason 'resolves to no declared type', checker-reason 'L3'. REPLACE on the imported LegalIR/1 identity `:canonical-file \"deployment/LAWMAX-LEGAL-IR-SEMANTIC-CONTRACT.md\"` with `\"deployment/no-such-file.md\"` — must be rejected by the NEW anchor check; TODAY nothing rejects it. REPLACE `:locator \"Counterproof\"` with `:locator \"NoSuchLocator\"` — must be rejected for the same reason; this is the mutation V1.8:440-441 names ('locator-absent-from-canonical-file') and which no model check performs."
  :rollback "delete the imported facts of this class and the fact-type/enum declarations added to MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp for it, re-run build_root.py so ROOT.sexp re-pins the 14 modules (ROOT.sexp:12-27; L7), and restore the ledger row to DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT / AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE (deferred-imports.sexp) so the source file is authoritative again; the source registry is never edited by the import (V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp:256 'v1.5 files are NOT edited' is the precedent)"
  :batch-reason "DDI-2 because build_deferred.py maps define-reference to DDI-2, materialised at deferred-imports.sexp:38. DISAGREES: this class is a dependency of DDI-1, not a dependent of it — V1.8 define-canonical-identity (DDI-1) references it 3 times, V1.7/V1.8 define-ra-closure-roots (DDI-1) 2+2 times, V1.7 define-pipeline (DDI-1) once, and the IMPORTED SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY 7 times (dag.json order violations). Simultaneously its own out-edge is to SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-wp-purpose (DDI-4, 6 refs, e.g. V1.6:127 -> SR:27 WP-12) — so the class sits between an EARLIER batch that needs it and a LATER batch it needs. That is a genuine ordering contradiction, not a placement preference; it resolves only if the identity family is created in DDI-1 and this class merges into it."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "(a) ONE identity family for all four classes — extend `type` with optional identity fields, or a separate `canonical-identity` fact type (decided in DDI-1, inherited here)? (b) For LegalIR/1, TrustBundle/1 and DeclassificationReceipt/1: which :canonical pointer is the seat — V1.6's (two artifacts / prose) or V1.8's (single file + locator)? (c) What is the seat of CandidateInterpretation/1 and ActionIntent/1 whose canonical identifiers exist only in v1.4 prose — DOCUMENT_SEAT on CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.4.md, DESIGN_TARGET, or must a Lisp seat be built first? (d) Where is DeclassificationReceipt/1's STRUCTURE seat, given that no registry defines its fields (they appear only in the :note at V1.6:150) and V1.8:274 derives declassification edges from those note-only fields?"
  :adjudication-items ("ADJ-DDI2-IDENTITY-FAMILY: four classes carry the SAME payload (identity + version + canonical pointer) under three key vocabularies — V1.6 define-reference :canonical/:identity/:version/:owner-wp (V1.6:92-150), V1.7 define-reference :canonical/:identity/:version (V1.7:34-39,257-258), V1.8 define-reference :canonical-file/:identity/:version/:locator (V1.8:107,345-352) and V1.8 define-canonical-identity (V1.8:425-432, batch DDI-1, deferred-imports.sexp:59). ONE fact family must be decided in DDI-1 before any of the three DDI-2 reference classes can be imported." "A2 (V1.6 dossier): LegalIR/1 canonical pointer — V1.6:97 + ISR:15 name legal-ast.lisp AND the contract .md; V1.8:345 names the .md alone." "A3 (V1.6 dossier): DeclassificationReceipt/1 has no structure seat anywhere; V1.8:349 references the V1.6 reference block (reference-to-a-reference) and V1.8:274 derives edges from fields that exist only in a :note string." "A4 (V1.6 dossier): CandidateInterpretation/1 and ActionIntent/1 point at identifiers (neural-candidate/1, cockpit_intent) absent from all tracked Lisp." "U1 (V1.6 dossier): the '(L12)' locator in Approval/1 :canonical (V1.6:132; ISR:27) is unresolved — release-authority.lisp line 12 is header prose." "ADJ-DDI2-OWNER-WP-VS-REQMAP: a type's :owner-wp (V1.6:95,99,130,134,146,150) and its owner subsystem's req-map :wp (requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:67-95) are two independent WP bindings with no reconciliation rule.")
  :topological-position 9 :atomic-groups ()
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "NOT-APPLICABLE (a reference carries no body; the identity string 'lawmax/legal-ir/1' is a stable name, not a content address — V6I-09 stable contracts V1.6:43-46)" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart "unresolvable identity/seat at build => typed violation (L3 closed reference, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:24-25; kernel AM/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:1-3 (*read-eval* nil, standard readtable, no eval), :23 *enums*, :24 *conds*, :56-60 reader, :243-257 law5-isolation) | invariant: referenced-but-undefined contract => gate FAIL (:ISR-V6-closure INTERFACE-AND-SCHEMA-REGISTRY.sexp:177-180; V6I-17 V1.6:348-355) | fallback: return typed error value (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:24)" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE (data: identity, version, seat anchor)" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE" :package-asdf-boundary "a :CODE-anchored reference resolves to an exported symbol of the owning package: LegalIR/1 -> orchestrator.legal-ast (source/legal-ast.lisp:57; SEAT-LEGAL-AST AM/seats.sexp:32); Approval/1 -> systems/orchestrator-cli/approval-policy.lisp (SEAT-APPROVAL-POLICY AM/seats.sexp:46); CandidateInterpretation/1 'source/*.lisp neural-candidate/1' and ActionIntent/1 'cockpit_intent' resolve to NO tracked Lisp (0 hits for neural-candidate in source/*.lisp; dossier A4) => DOCUMENT_SEAT on v1.4 prose or UNKNOWN | invariant: one seat per concept, seat path unique (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:305-308 define-unique SEAT-PATH-UNIQUE) | fallback: document anchor (rationale doc+anchor, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:182-184)" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE (:version is a contract version, not time)" :compile-time-validation "build-time resolution of :canonical to a `seat` fact (L3) and, for code seats, existence of the exported symbol (find-symbol/fboundp in the named package — structural, unlike a grep); the V1.8 §15 format (:canonical-file + :locator, V1.8:345-352) is the audited successor (V8I-XREF-real V1.8:353-356) | invariant: V8I-XREF-identity two-part non-circular resolution (V1.8:433-441) | fallback: grep of the canonical file (the current V8I-XREF-real mechanism)" :runtime-validation "NOT-APPLICABLE (identity resolution is a build-time property; at runtime the identity string travels inside records, e.g. TrustBundle bnd1: refs V1.6:144)" :python-in-cl-risk "MEDIUM. Naive import: the prose :canonical strings ('legal-ast.lisp + LAWMAX-LEGAL-IR-SEMANTIC-CONTRACT.md (v1.5 C1 records)') stored verbatim as STRING values that nothing resolves — the same dangling-anchor class as WORK/orchestrator-notes.md N17. CL-native: a canonical-identity fact (:type L3 ref, :identity STRING, :version STRING, :seat L3 ref to `seat`, :locator STRING) shared with V1.8 define-canonical-identity (DDI-1) so one family, one resolver; prose-only targets declared DOCUMENT_SEAT facts rather than free text." :future-freedom "NO constraint on S04/S19/JTMS/S20. The identity 'lawmax/neural-candidate/1' keeps the word 'neural' although V1.6 §1 retires the neural-plane framing (V1.6:49-50) — a naming residue in a stable contract name, not a technique lock (the proposer is model-agnostic, V1.6:95). Competing identity seats for LegalIR/1, TrustBundle/1, DeclassificationReceipt/1 (V1.6:96,143,147 vs V1.8:345-349 vs V1.8:425-427; ADJ-V18-REF-1) are a one-seat adjudication.")
  )

(ddi-class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-construction-order
  :batch DDI-1 :source-file "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp" :fact-class "define-construction-order" :source-count 1 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms (("cognition-stage-dag" :line 217 :sha16 "7ccec82074bc8392"))
  :source-file "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp"
  :source-forms 1
  :current-authority-seat "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp section '3. PUBLIC LEGAL LANGUAGE COGNITION LAYER (§4)' (header L164), comment L216 ('---- ordered stage DAG (construction contract): each stage has typed in/out and a symbolic-only guarantee ----'), form cognition-stage-dag L217-229; ledger deferred-imports.sexp:32 (DDI-1)."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp (existing) if cognition stages are admitted as a second ordered family beside the pipeline; otherwise NEW:cognition-graph — reason: the model's `stage` fact type has zero fields (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:159) and holds the pipeline ACQUIRE..PUBLISH (dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:5-12); cognition stages carry typed :in/:out/:seat/:symbolic-only and would either overload one L4 relation with two unrelated graphs or need their own seat. Conditional on A8 / ADJ-V17-CO-1 (which of the three cognition seats is canonical)."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "NEW `cog-stage` (:graph SYMBOL :order INTEGER :in ref type :out ref type :seat ref seat :symbolic-only yes-no) + NEW `cog-edge` (:from :to ref cog-stage). Flattening: 12 plists (V1.6:218-229) → 12 cog-stage facts (ids cognition-stage-dag__COG-1-SEGMENT …) + 11 consecutive cog-edge facts; `:symbolic-only t` → YES (enum yes-no, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:71); composite :seat strings ('greek-lemmatizer.lisp + legal-casegrammar.lisp[general]' :220, 'InterpretiveProfile/1 (v1.5 C1)' :226, 'legal-qa.lisp + citation/1' :229) are not seat ids and cannot be flattened without NEW seat facts (ADJ-V17-CO-2)."
  :owner "S04 by declaration — :V6I-13-cognition-one-seat (V1.6:261-264: 'ONE seat (inside the Public Legal Discernment Engine, WP-08)'); SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:45-48 S04 'Symbolic Common Lisp core + Public Language Cognition Layer'; the consumer field LanguageCognitionLayer/1.stage_dag_ref (V1.6:215) belongs to an S04 type (interfaces-and-types.sexp:30). But the stage :seat strings span S03 (legal-extraction-verify.lisp :228 = seats.sexp:30), S04 (legal-ast.lisp :228 = seats.sexp:32), S07 (legal-event-calculus.lisp :225 = seats.sexp:38) and S09 (citation/1 :229, interfaces-and-types.sexp:63) — owner of the DAG fact: S04; owners of its seats: plural."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — the form declares no store; `writer` is a field of `store` only (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:155-158). Imported facts are authored in the target module under its 'thereafter EDIT HERE' header (e.g. interfaces-and-types.sexp:2)."
  :classification "PUBLIC — all 12 stages :symbolic-only t; :in/:out records are the public cognition records of V1.6 §3; no private member. 7 of the 9 :in/:out records (MorphLattice/1, PackedParseForest/1, CoreferenceRecord/1, DiscourseState/1, LegalSemanticAlternative/1, ClarificationState/1, PromotionEvidence/1) are NOT model types (dossier V1.6 A7), so their classification is not yet a fact."
  :dependencies ("DDI-2 V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-record: PerceptionEnvelope/1 (:85), MorphLattice/1 (:183), PackedParseForest/1 (:186), CoreferenceRecord/1 (:189), DiscourseState/1 (:192), LegalSemanticAlternative/1 (:195), ClarificationState/1 (:198), PromotionEvidence/1 (:201), CognitionResult/1 (:204) — :in/:out field-type refs (9 refs, dag.json)" "DDI-2 V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-reference (:34-39, 6 refs), V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-reference CognitionResult/1 (:348), V1.5 define-record InterpretiveProfile/1 (:476) — same names (dag.json)" "EXISTING types: PerceptionEnvelope/1 (:39), CognitionResult/1 (:19), InterpretiveProfile/1 (:28), citation/1 (:63) in interfaces-and-types.sexp" "NEW seat facts for 8 tracked files that have no `seat` (greek-nlp-core, greek-tokenizer-advanced, greek-lemmatizer, legal-casegrammar, greek-legislation-ontology, legal-deontic, legal-dialectic, legal-reasoning-bridge, legal-qa — all TRACKED per dossier V1.6) — seats.sexp:33 says greek-nlp-core.lisp is 'a further artifact of S04, not a further seat' (ADJ-V17-CO-2)" "DDI-4 SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY__define-file-disposition legal-casegrammar.lisp SPLIT (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:130) for the '[general]' partition (dag.json 1 ref)")
  :consumers ("LanguageCognitionLayer/1.stage_dag_ref (V1.6:215) — the type is a model fact (interfaces-and-types.sexp:30) but the field is DDI-2" ":V6I-COG-symbolic-only (V1.6:265-269, DDI-4); :V6I-COG-one-to-one (V1.6:270)" "audit V6S17 (V1.6-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh:262-269 — HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE)" "WP-08 via define-wp-reconciliation COGNITION_DAG (V1.7:380; V1.8:304 — DDI-4)")
  :identity-version-rule "SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT — V1.6:217 cognition-stage-dag (12 stages COG-1..COG-12) → V1.7:80 cognition-stage-dag-v7 (14 stages, new intermediate records, :preserves; V1.7:33 'Reused v1.6 records are REFERENCED; new intermediate types defined here') → V1.8:53 cognition-graph-v8 + V1.8:363 cognition-graph-v8-types (typed graph; CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:33-37 DFT-07: 'NOT a linear list with a :branch annotation'); SUPERSEDED-REGISTER.md:254-258 ('Nothing is falsified: all valid v1.6 seats … carried forward'). Three different names; no V1.8 form carries this name. Ids: cognition-stage-dag__COG-n-<NAME>."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION — canonical cognition seat (V1.6 / V1.7 / V1.8) undecided (A8, ADJ-V17-CO-1). If V1.8 is chosen: IMPORT-AS-HISTORICAL-VERSION (lineage only) or SKIP-WITH-PROOF — proof would be a COG-1..12 → V1.8 node mapping, which no registry states (V1.6 has 12 stages, V1.8 14 flow nodes + 6 lifecycle nodes)."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "Three seats for one concept (cognition order): V1.6:217, V1.7:80, V1.8:53+363 — importing any two violates one-seat (:V8I-03-one-seat V1.8:20-22; :SR-V6-one-seat; :V6I-13 'ONE seat'). Would collide with the pipeline `stage` family if reused (dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:5-21). Also overlaps V1.6 define-mapping cognition->existing-lisp-seat (V1.6:231-246, DDI-2), which maps the same seats by capability (A13)."
  :requirement "R-129 (S04 req-map S04__WP-08 requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:70; SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:46 :interface LanguageCognitionLayer/1) is the nearest existing model requirement; RA-C2 'type-correct information-preserving cognition DAG' (TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:358) is NOT a model fact. Whether R-129 covers the stage DAG is stated nowhere → R-129 or NEW (adjudicate)."
  :invariant "L4 (acyclic cog-edge) + L3 (in/out types and seats resolve); source :V6I-COG-symbolic-only (V1.6:265), :V6I-COG-one-to-one (V1.6:270), :V6I-13-cognition-one-seat (V1.6:261)."
  :qualification-test "Q08 (model test fact requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:32, S04's req-map test) exists as an id only (prose, N7); V6Q-14 'language cognition coverage' (PUBLIC-OBSERVATORY-QUALIFICATION-TESTS.md:1153-1156) is predeclared UNEXECUTED and NOT a model test fact. NEW executable statement: for consecutive stages k, k+1: out-type(k) = in-type(k+1) (the V1.6:218-229 chain); the cog-edge graph is acyclic; every :seat resolves to a `seat` fact."
  :falsifier "REPLACE `:out MorphLattice/1` of COG-1-SEGMENT with `:out PackedParseForest/1` (incompatible with COG-2 :in MorphLattice/1) — must be rejected 'stage out-type does not equal next stage in-type'; APPEND `(fact cog-edge cognition-stage-dag__COG-12-NLG__COG-1-SEGMENT :from cognition-stage-dag__COG-12-NLG :to cognition-stage-dag__COG-1-SEGMENT)` — kernel-reason 'cycle in the cog-edge graph over cog-stage', checker-reason 'L4'."
  :rollback "Delete the imported facts and any new fact-type/field declaration from MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp (schema-version must move, X74-X76 verification-corpus.sexp:354-372); re-run build_root.py so ROOT.sexp pins the restored modules (L7); build_deferred.py regenerates the ledger row as DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT :batch DDI-1. The source registry is never edited (authority stays AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE until the batch is independently reviewed, deferred-imports.sexp:73-76)."
  :batch-reason "DDI-1 by build_deferred.py:90 (head). DISAGREES twice: (1) all :in/:out targets are DDI-2 records/references (dag.json: 9 V1.6 define-record + 6 V1.7 define-reference + 1 V1.5 define-record + 1 V1.8 define-reference); (2) its declared successor cognition-graph-v8 / node-types is DDI-3 (build_deferred.py:97) — the canonical-seat decision cannot be taken inside DDI-1 without DDI-3 content."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "Which cognition order is canonical — V1.6:217 (12 stages, DDI-1), V1.7:80 (14 stages, DDI-1) or V1.8:53+363 (typed graph, DDI-3)? If V1.8: does the V1.6 form import as lineage, or is it skipped with a stage→node mapping proof? Do cognition stages share the pipeline `stage` family (one L4 relation, two graphs) or get their own fact types? How are composite / unseated :seat strings bound to the typed seat universe (new BUILT seats vs 'further artifact' notes, seats.sexp:33)?"
  :adjudication-items ("A8 (dossier V1.6) = ADJ-V17-CO-1: cognition lineage triple, canonical seat and batch split DDI-1/DDI-3" "A13 (dossier V1.6) / ADJ-V17-CO-2: seat strings resolve to no `seat` fact; 8 cognition files unseated" "A11 (dossier V1.6): LanguageCognitionLayer/1.stage_dag_ref binds the V1.6 DAG or the V1.8 graph" "ADJ-MX1-CO6-1 (new): batch placement DISAGREES (targets DDI-2; successor DDI-3)")
  :topological-position 20 :atomic-groups (3)
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "Stage :in/:out records (PerceptionEnvelope/1 … CognitionResult/1, V1.6:85-204, DDI-2) are typed immutable values handed between stages; the stage table itself is constant data (12 stage facts + 11 edge facts), not a mutable pipeline object | invariant: :V6I-COG-symbolic-only (V1.6:265-269); :V6I-COG-one-to-one (V1.6:270) | fallback: copy-on-write records" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "One stage = one method of an `execute-step`-shaped generic (cognition.lisp:96 defgeneric execute-step (step frame cog)) specialised on the stage designator (eql COG-n), with the stage's :in record as typed argument and :out record as typed result; stage designators are data (facts), methods are the built seats — REUSING the existing generics (cognition.lisp:92-107 plan/execute-step/synthesize/triage), never a forked pipeline | invariant: contract L21 'dispatch is total or errors typed'; :V6I-13-cognition-one-seat (V1.6:261-264) 'reuses the existing Lisp seats and never forks a second implementation' | fallback: single dispatch function over a stage table" :condition-restart "The CLARIFY stage's seat string literally names 'condition/restart' (V1.6:227 COG-10-CLARIFY; V1.7:91 COG7-11-CLARIFY): clarification = a typed condition `clarification-required` with restarts (passthrough | provide-clarification), invoked PROGRAMMATICALLY only (pattern legal-ast.lisp:1604-1615 / trace-core.lisp:264-277 ':interactive (eval (read)) REMOVED'); no restart may pick a winner. legal-dialectic.lisp has NO condition/restart today (only defpackage :14) → [design-target] | invariant: no silent forced winner (V1.7:99 (e) :no-forced-winner); contract L24 'controlled ambiguity/recovery, no silent failure' seat 'cognition clarification (COG7-11)' | fallback: return typed error value (ClarificationState / ClarificationDecision record)" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE" :protocol "The stage protocol is the existing generic-function protocol (triage/plan/execute-step/synthesize, cognition.lisp:92-107) with typed in/out; the SemanticProposer PROPOSER protocol (interfaces-and-types.sexp:57 :consumer-role PROPOSER; V1.6 define-protocol V1.6:57, DDI-4) is a SEPARATE optional protocol stages may consult, never require | invariant: :V6I-10-proposer-never-authority (V1.6:75); :V6I-COG-symbolic-only | fallback: explicit function table" :package-asdf-boundary "Stage seats span packages of several subsystems: :orchestrator.legal-ast (legal-ast.lisp:57, S04 seats.sexp:32), legal-event-calculus (S07 seats.sexp:38), legal-extraction-verify (S03 seats.sexp:30), :orchestrator.dialectic (legal-dialectic.lisp:14), plus 8 files with NO seat fact (greek-nlp-core, greek-tokenizer-advanced, greek-lemmatizer, legal-casegrammar, greek-legislation-ontology, legal-deontic, legal-dialectic, legal-qa — dossier ADJ-V17-CO-2). ':symbolic-only t' is a PACKAGE property: no ASDF system implementing a stage may :depends-on a proposer/adapter system (V1.6:67-73 adapters :mandatory nil) — the leak becomes a build failure, not an audit; legal-casegrammar.lisp[general] SPLIT (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:130-134 :no-copy) is exactly a package split public/private | invariant: :V6I-COG-symbolic-only (V1.6:265-269); contract L31 'package boundary = capability boundary; declared forbidden dependencies' ([0146]:18 16 systems/53 edges acyclic) | fallback: monolith package + runtime SafetyMode check" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE" :compile-time-validation "Typed connectivity at kernel-law time once stages are flat facts: stage_i :out = stage_{i+1} :in over closed `type` refs (L3); every :seat is a SEAT-SPACE id (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:44,132-136) not a string; :symbolic-only rendered as yes-no enum (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:71) | invariant: :V7I-COG-info-preserving (a) 'each stage :out type equals the next stage :in type (typed, connected)' (V1.7:96); L3 | fallback: runtime check-type at method boundaries" :runtime-validation "check-type of the :in record at method entry and of the :out record at exit, signalling a typed condition on mismatch — no coercion, no proposer-derived default | invariant: contract L21 'dispatch is total or errors typed'; :V6I-COG-symbolic-only | fallback: fail-closed → SafetyMode :DEGRADED ⇒ SYMBOLIC_ONLY semantics (V1.6:23)" :python-in-cl-risk "HIGH. Naive import yields a list of dicts [{'stage':'COG-1-SEGMENT','in':…,'out':…,'seat':'greek-nlp-core.lisp','symbolic_only':True}] and a for-loop runner; seat strings stay strings ('greek-nlp-core.lisp (EXTEND)', 'legal-casegrammar.lisp[general]', 'InterpretiveProfile/1 (v1.5 C1)' — a TYPE used as a seat; 'legal-qa.lisp + citation/1' — two seats in one string), and `t` becomes a Python bool. Every one of these is an L1 violation (nested plists, boolean, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6) or an L3 violation (seat not in SEAT-SPACE). CL-native alternative: flat `cog-node` facts (:in/:out -> type, :seat -> seat, :symbolic-only yes-no) + `cog-edge` facts under L4, stages as methods of the existing generics, symbolic-only as an ASDF forbidden-dependency property. 'An arbitrary string is not a seat' (V1.7:354)." :future-freedom "CONSTRAINS S04 (language cognition) if imported as canonical: (i) it is the FIRST of three divergent cognition DAG seats (V1.6:217 12 stages → V1.7:80 14 stages → V1.8:53/363 typed graph, DDI-3) and V1.8:24-27 declares the linear list with :branch annotation REPLACED (DFT-07) — importing V1.6 as facts would freeze a superseded shape into the model (ADJ-V17-CO-1; V1.6 dossier A8); (ii) binding each stage to a file name freezes today's file layout (8 unseated files) into the canonical model, so a future re-partition of greek-nlp-core.lisp becomes a model change. No S19/S20/LLM constraint: all stages :symbolic-only t, proposers optional (V6I-02). Recommended reading: lineage-only / zero facts unless adjudicated.")
  )

(ddi-class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-mapping
  :batch DDI-2 :source-file "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp" :fact-class "define-mapping" :source-count 1 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms (("cognition->existing-lisp-seat" :line 231 :sha16 "0e941294436c348c"))
  :source-file "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp"
  :source-forms 1
  :current-authority-seat "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp section '3. PUBLIC LEGAL LANGUAGE COGNITION LAYER (§4)' (header L164), comment L230 ('capability -> seat map: EVERY CognitionCapability mapped EXACTLY once (existing seat OR declared extension)'), form L231-246 (15 rows). Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:34 (DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE, DDI-2, :source-count 1). V1.7:343-345 declares this map the CLOSURE of cognition capabilities, so V1.7 treats V1.6 as the authority."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "SAME module as the DDI-1 capability-seat class (V1.7 define-capability-seat V1.7:346-352, V1.8 define-capability-seat V1.8:243-249, both deferred-imports.sexp:41,55 DDI-1) — the concept 'a capability resolves to exactly one seat' must have ONE seat, and DDI-1 creates it first. The V1.6 dossier proposes NEW capability-seats.sexp; the DDI-1 matrix row for V1.8 define-capability-seat is where that module is decided. This class inherits it and must not open a second one."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "The DDI-1 `capability-seat` family, EXTENDED — or an adjudicated refusal. Shape needed here: (:capability <enum-value of CognitionCapability> :seat <seat|type|field|invariant> :disposition REUSE|EXTEND|SPLIT|DECLARED :subsystem <subsystem>). Flattening rule: 15 facts, one per row; the id must be synthesised because the form's own name `cognition->existing-lisp-seat` contains '>' which is OUTSIDE the TOKEN charset [A-Za-z0-9_.+/-] (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5,17,41) — the ONLY charset violation among real atoms in all six registries (orchestrator-notes.md N12); the rename must be recorded by the identity rule. The :seat VALUES are composite English strings ('greek-lemmatizer.lisp + legal-casegrammar.lisp[general] (SPLIT->public)', V1.6:234) that carry file + disposition + partition in one string; they cannot become a typed ref without being parsed, and parsing prose is not a migration. no `enum`/`enum-value`/`field`/`primitive`/`cardinality`/`ref-class`/`adapter`/`canonical-identity` fact type exists among the 34 fact types (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:84-288); `define-enum` there is schema syntax for the model's own closed domains only (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:18,47-76); L1 forbids keywords, nested lists and NIL as values (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6) and the closed field set forbids adding keys to `type` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:9-13,148-152)"
  :owner "UNKNOWN as a fact. S04 is the section inference (V1.6:164-166 'INSIDE the existing Public Legal Discernment Engine (WP-08 core)'; SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:45-48), but no registry row assigns this form an owner, and the mapped seats themselves span at least four subsystems: S04 (legal-ast.lisp, seats.sexp:32), S03 (legal-extraction-verify.lisp, :30), S07 (legal-event-calculus.lisp, :38) and S09 (citation/1, interfaces-and-types.sexp:63). V1.6 dossier U2 records the same absence."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — a capability->seat map is a declaration, not a store. No registry names a writer. Note that three of the 15 rows name a NON-ARTIFACT as the seat (see conflict field), so 'writer' is not even meaningful for them."
  :classification "PUBLIC — the whole cognition capability set is the public discernment path; no private member. But the map is exactly the artifact :V6I-COG-symbolic-only (V1.6:265-269) and :V6I-COG-one-to-one (:270-273) use to prove the public path is complete without a proposer, so its classification is load-bearing, not incidental."
  :dependencies ("DDI-1 FIRST: V1.7/V1.8 define-capability-seat (deferred-imports.sexp:41,55) create the capability-seat family — reference kind: shared fact family" "SAME BATCH: V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum CognitionCapability (V1.6:168-176) — all 15 :capability keys are its members; a typed :capability ref cannot close before the enum-value facts exist" "SAME BATCH (2 of the 15 rows): V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-record LanguageCognitionLayer/1 fields controlling_text_declaration and coverage_declaration_ref (V1.6:213-214) are used AS SEATS at V1.6:244-245 — a `field` fact must exist before those rows can be typed" "LATER BATCH (1 row): V1.6 define-invariant :V6I-13 (V1.6:261) is used as the seat of :NO_PERFECT_UNDERSTANDING_CLAIM (V1.6:246) — define-invariant is DDI-4 (deferred-imports.sexp:33), and no `invariant` fact type exists at all" "LATER BATCH (1 row): SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-file-disposition legal-casegrammar.lisp (SR:130-134) is DDI-4 (deferred-imports.sexp:9) and is what makes 'legal-casegrammar.lisp[general]' meaningful — dag.json order violation, 1 ref" "SEAT FACTS: 9 of the mapped source files have NO `seat` fact (greek-nlp-core.lisp, greek-tokenizer-advanced.lisp, greek-lemmatizer.lisp, legal-casegrammar.lisp, greek-legislation-ontology.lisp, legal-deontic.lisp, legal-dialectic.lisp, legal-reasoning-bridge.lisp, legal-qa.lisp) and seats.sexp:33 explicitly says greek-nlp-core.lisp is 'a further artifact of the same subsystem, not a further seat'")
  :consumers (":V6I-COG-one-to-one (V1.6:270-273, DDI-4) — the invariant this map exists to satisfy" "V1.7:343-345 comment 'Cognition capabilities are closed by the v1.6 cognition->existing-lisp-seat map (audit V6S14)' — V1.7 define-capability-seat (DDI-1) defers to it" "legacy audit V6S14 (V1.6-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh:243-251) — HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:440)" "dag.json: NO class references this one (in-edges empty)" "no tracked source/ or systems/ file names any record/enum id of the six registries (git grep at RO = 0); the only mechanical readers are the legacy audits/harness classified HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:436,440,444,450,453)")
  :identity-version-rule "ONLY-VERSION, with a MANDATORY RENAME. define-mapping occurs only in V1.6 (classes.md row 33) and no other registry maps cognition capabilities — V1.7:343-345 and V1.8:240-249 cover only the seven RA capabilities, not these fifteen. The id `cognition->existing-lisp-seat` (V1.6:231) is not importable as-is: '>' is outside TOKEN (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:17), so the identity rule must record the rename (e.g. cognition-to-existing-lisp-seat) as part of the import, and the rename convention must be the same one used for the 7 anonymous forms (orchestrator-notes.md N11)."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION. The obstruction is not shape but CONTENT: V1.8:250-254 (:V8I-CAP-real) requires a capability seat to name either :CODE file+package+symbol or :DOCUMENT file+section, and V1.7:343-344 forbids an invariant from being a capability seat — yet three of these 15 rows name a record FIELD (V1.6:244, :245) or an INVARIANT (:246) as the seat. Importing them verbatim would import a violation of the successor's own law; refusing them silently would drop 3 of 15 capabilities from a map whose whole claim is 'EXACTLY once'."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "HIGH. (1) Two capability-seat families if this class does not reuse the DDI-1 one. (2) Three rows use non-artifacts as seats: 'controlling_text_declaration' (V1.6:244) and 'coverage_declaration_ref' (:245) are FIELDS of LanguageCognitionLayer/1 (V1.6:213-214); 'invariant :V6I-13' (:246) is an INVARIANT — V1.7:343-344 and V1.8:250-254 both say a capability seat must be a real code or document location. (3) One row uses a TYPE as a seat: 'InterpretiveProfile/1 (v1.5 C1)' (V1.6:238), which is a model `type` fact (interfaces-and-types.sexp:28) — a type used as the seat of a capability is a category error under L2. (4) 'legal-casegrammar.lisp[general]' names a PARTITION of a file that the file itself does not mark (V1.6 dossier U4: no [general] marker found by grep) and that is declared twice, by V1.6:247 define-rule casegrammar-split and by SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:130-134 define-file-disposition (both DDI-4) — adjudication A14. (5) `seat` ids are SEAT-SPACE with prefix 'SEAT-' (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:44) and every seat path is unique (define-unique SEAT-PATH-UNIQUE, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:308); creating 9 new seats for the mapped files would collide with seats.sexp:33's explicit statement that those files are not further seats."
  :requirement "NONE in the model. The capabilities have no `requirement` fact; S04's req-map row is S04__WP-08 :requirement R-129 :test Q08 (requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:70), which is about the Legal AST seat, not about capability closure. V1.6's own binding is the invariant :V6I-COG-one-to-one plus audit V6S14, neither of which is a model requirement or test (orchestrator-notes.md N7, N8)."
  :invariant "L1 (id charset — the TOKEN violation is an L1 id-space failure, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:15-17,41; the kernel emits 'L1 <type> <id>: the id ...' at KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:122-123), L2 (one id per fact type), L3 (:capability and :seat closed refs). Source invariants: :V6I-COG-one-to-one (V1.6:270-273), :V6I-13-cognition-one-seat (:261-264), :V7I-CAP-seat-closure (V1.7:353-357), :V8I-CAP-real (V1.8:250-254)."
  :qualification-test "NEW. Executable one-liner: the number of `capability-seat` facts whose :capability is a CognitionCapability member equals 15 AND each of the 15 enum-value facts of CognitionCapability appears exactly once as a :capability — a bijection check, which is precisely what :V6I-COG-one-to-one asserts and what no model check performs today (my own grep of gate_checks.py: no capability check). Pin the cardinality with a NEW property-family (shape of verification-corpus.sexp:42-56) so that losing a row is a named failure."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact capability-seat COGNITION__NO_SUCH :capability NO_SUCH_CAPABILITY :seat SEAT-LEGAL-AST :disposition REUSE :subsystem S04)` — both paths must reject: kernel-reason 'resolves to no declared enum-value', checker-reason 'L3'. APPEND a SECOND fact for an already-mapped capability (e.g. a duplicate :MORPHOLOGICAL_LATTICE row) — must be rejected by the NEW bijection check as 'capability mapped twice'; today nothing rejects it. CHECK-class: keep the id `cognition->existing-lisp-seat` unrenamed and require the kernel to reject it for the id-space reason ('the id ... charset'), proving the charset rule is enforced on the CANONICAL RENDERING (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:16)."
  :rollback "delete the imported facts of this class and the fact-type/enum declarations added to MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp for it, re-run build_root.py so ROOT.sexp re-pins the 14 modules (ROOT.sexp:12-27; L7), and restore the ledger row to DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT / AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE (deferred-imports.sexp) so the source file is authoritative again; the source registry is never edited by the import (V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp:256 'v1.5 files are NOT edited' is the precedent)"
  :batch-reason "DDI-2 because build_deferred.py maps define-mapping to DDI-2, materialised at deferred-imports.sexp:34. DISAGREES: the class is a capability-seat statement, and every other capability-seat class in the six registries is DDI-1 (V1.7 define-capability-seat deferred-imports.sexp:41; V1.8 define-capability-seat :55) — the same concept is split across two batches. Its out-edges also point at LATER batches: dag.json 'V1.6 define-mapping (rank 2) -> SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-file-disposition (rank 4), 1 ref' plus the untracked reference to :V6I-13 (DDI-4). It has no in-edges. Dependency evidence places it with DDI-1 for the family and after DDI-4 for two of its rows — it cannot be satisfied inside DDI-2 alone."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "(a) Does this class join the DDI-1 capability-seat family, or is the cognition-capability map a separate concept with its own family? (b) What is the recorded rename of `cognition->existing-lisp-seat` (charset), and is the rename convention the same one used for the 7 anonymous forms (orchestrator-notes.md N11)? (c) Three rows name a field / a field+file / an invariant as the seat (V1.6:244-246), which V1.7:343-344 and V1.8:250-254 forbid — are those rows re-seated, imported with a declared exemption, or dropped with proof? (d) Do the 9 mapped source files become `seat` facts, contradicting seats.sexp:33 ('not a further seat'), or does the map point at the SUBSYSTEM's seat instead?"
  :adjudication-items ("A13 (V1.6 dossier): id charset violation, composite string seats, field/invariant used as seats, and 9 mapped files with no seat fact — one adjudication with four limbs, all cited above." "ADJ-DDI2-CAPABILITY-SPLIT: cognition capabilities (V1.6, DDI-2) and RA capabilities (V1.7/V1.8, DDI-1) are the same concept in two batches; one family, one batch, or an explicit reason for two." "A14 (V1.6 dossier): the casegrammar split is declared twice — V1.6:247 define-rule and SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:130-134 define-file-disposition (both DDI-4); the map depends on whichever wins." "U4 (V1.6 dossier): source/legal-casegrammar.lisp carries no [general]/[private] marker, so 'legal-casegrammar.lisp[general]' is a seat that cannot be located in the artifact it names.")
  :topological-position 21 :atomic-groups ()
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "NOT-APPLICABLE" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart "unmapped or multiply-mapped capability => typed build violation (V6I-COG-one-to-one V1.6:270-272, audit V6S14); at runtime get-analyzer signals analyzer-not-found (source/greek-nlp-core.lisp:387-407 analyzer class + analyze defgeneric + *analyzer-registry*/register-analyzer/get-analyzer (analyzer-not-found typed condition); :573 define-analyzer macro) | invariant: EVERY capability mapped EXACTLY once | fallback: return typed error value (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:24)" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE (data rows capability -> seat)" :protocol "capability -> analyzer binding through the analyzer protocol registry keyed by capability name (source/greek-nlp-core.lisp:387-407 analyzer class + analyze defgeneric + *analyzer-registry*/register-analyzer/get-analyzer (analyzer-not-found typed condition); :573 define-analyzer macro *analyzer-registry*/register-analyzer; LanguageCognitionLayer/1 :analyzer_registry_ref V1.6:212) — the CL-native mapping is a registry entry, not a filename | invariant: V6I-COG-one-to-one; hot-swappable analyzers (V1.6:258 :hot-swap) | fallback: static alist capability -> function" :package-asdf-boundary "each mapped seat is a package: the map must reference `seat` facts (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:132-136; AM/seats.sexp:32-33 SEAT-LEGAL-AST notes greek-nlp-core.lisp and legal-inference-engine.lisp as artifacts of S04) — 8 of the 11 named files have no seat fact today (ADJ-V17-CO-2) | invariant: package boundary = capability boundary (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:31) | fallback: monolith package (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:31)" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE" :compile-time-validation "build-time set equality: CognitionCapability members == mapping keys, each key exactly once (define-unique shape, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:34-36; V6I-COG-one-to-one); :seat refs L3-closed | invariant: V6I-COG-one-to-one (V1.6:270-272) | fallback: runtime check (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:32)" :runtime-validation "registry lookup by capability; miss => analyzer-not-found (source/greek-nlp-core.lisp:387-407 analyzer class + analyze defgeneric + *analyzer-registry*/register-analyzer/get-analyzer (analyzer-not-found typed condition); :573 define-analyzer macro) | invariant: outside declared coverage => UNKNOWN (V6I-13 V1.6:261-264) | fallback: reject" :python-in-cl-risk "HIGH. Naive import: dict capability -> composite STRING ('greek-nlp-core.lisp (EXTEND)') — a filename plus a disposition plus a comment in one string; two rows name record FIELDS as seats and one names an INVARIANT (V1.6:244-246, dossier A13). CL-native: typed rows (capability -> enum-value ref, seat -> `seat` ref, disposition -> enum REUSE/EXTEND/SPLIT/DECLARED), i.e. the V1.8 define-capability-seat shape (:kind :CODE/:DOCUMENT, :package, :symbol V1.8:243-249, DDI-1); the field/invariant 'seats' become explicit DECLARED-EXTENSION rows with no seat and a rationale." :future-freedom "YES — flagged. The map binds MEANINGS (capabilities) to TOOLS (file names) — the very thing V6I-01 forbids to lock (V1.6:15-16) — while V1.7:344-345 makes it the only closure of cognition capabilities. Importing filenames as the binding constrains S04: replacing greek-nlp-core.lisp changes canonical facts. CL-native re-expression through `seat` ids (the seat fact owns the path, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:129-136) keeps the capability closure while leaving the artifact replaceable behind the seat. Adjudicate with dossier A13 (CL2-A5).")
