(ddi-class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-rule
  :batch DDI-4 :source-file "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp" :fact-class "define-rule" :source-count 2 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms (("casegrammar-split" :line 247 :sha16 "d4f85455718c33f2") ("common-lisp-cognition-usage" :line 251 :sha16 "db61c3ef045cedc6"))
  :source-file "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp"
  :source-forms 2
  :current-authority-seat "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp §3 (section header V1.6:164), forms casegrammar-split at :247-250 (3 clauses) and common-lisp-cognition-usage at :251-260 (9 clauses). Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:39 (:source-count 2, DDI-4, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE). COMPETING SEATS: casegrammar-split duplicates SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:130-134 define-file-disposition (class 3, same batch, deferred-imports.sexp:9) and is restated a third time in the V1.6 section comment at :167; common-lisp-cognition-usage overlaps LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:6,18-35 (AUTHORED_NORMATIVE_PROSE, files-and-roles.sexp:403), which is the later and richer statement of the same mechanism list."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "For casegrammar-split: whichever module class 3 resolves to (file-dispositions.sexp or interfaces-and-types.sexp components) — the two forms must NOT land in two modules. For common-lisp-cognition-usage: rationale-references.sexp (EXISTING) as a pointer at LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md, because that document is the declared mechanism-admission seat (its §2 table carries the eight-field discipline reason->seat->requirement->invariant->test->fallback->migration->rollback, :6,18-35) and importing the 9 clauses as facts would create a second, poorer mechanism registry inside the model. Recorded as a proposal contingent on the seat ruling, not a resolution."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "NEW `rule` + `rule-clause` (as class 6) — 2 `rule` facts + 12 `rule-clause` facts (3 + 9). Flattening rule is MANDATORY: both forms are lists of nested (key \"prose\") pairs (V1.6:248-250, :252-260), not L1-legal values (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6). Clause keys colon-strip to plain symbols (public, private, no-copy, clos, conditions, macros, compile-time, packages, immutable, hot-swap, no-external-eval, no-python-in-lisp) — all TOKEN-legal. Clause ids synthesised <rule>__<key>. ALTERNATIVE for casegrammar-split: it is not a rule at all but the same datum as class 3's `file-disposition`, in which case importing it as a `rule` fact manufactures the duplicate seat the model exists to prevent."
  :owner "SPLIT / UNKNOWN. casegrammar-split: S04 (public half) and S22 (private half) per SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:132-133 — the V1.6 form itself names NEITHER, so its owner is only knowable from the competing seat. common-lisp-cognition-usage: the dossier records 'S04 (cognition layer) — not stated'; the clauses in fact span S20 (:hot-swap -> capability registry, SEAT-CAPABILITY-REGISTRY seats.sexp:58), S03/S04 (:clos), and a repository-wide package policy with no subsystem. UNKNOWN, not guessed."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — neither form declares a store (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:155-158). The :hot-swap clause names source/capability-registry.lisp:140 (define-capability macro) and the :no-external-eval clause names source/safe-read.lisp, both tracked, but neither is a write authority."
  :classification "MIXED — private member named: casegrammar-split's :private clause routes 'client-fact schemas and matter-solving' to DEFER_PRIVATE (V1.6:249), i.e. S22 PrivateMatterProfile (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:133; subsystems.sexp:26 PRIVATE). common-lisp-cognition-usage is PUBLIC (repository-wide construction policy, no private subject)."
  :dependencies ("FIRST: the class-3 duplicate-seat ruling for casegrammar-split [one-seat dependency, intra-batch]" "FIRST: the mechanism-admission ruling for common-lisp-cognition-usage against LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:6,18-35 [one-seat dependency, against AUTHORED_NORMATIVE_PROSE which the migration cannot retire]" "EXISTING model facts: subsystem S04 (subsystems.sexp:8), S22 (:26), seat SEAT-CAPABILITY-REGISTRY (seats.sexp:58) [reference targets available]" "NOT AVAILABLE: two clauses have no located counterpart anywhere — :packages 'declared forbidden dependencies' (no registry of forbidden package dependencies exists in the six registries: NOT FOUND) and :no-python-in-lisp (no counterpart clause in the CL contract: grep NOT FOUND) [content with no seat and no successor]" "dag.json records 0 out-edges and 0 in-edges for this class — no mechanical dependency evidence in either direction")
  :consumers ("V1.6-SCHEMAS internal: cognition-stage-dag (V1.6:220-221) and cognition->existing-lisp-seat (:234-235) consume the 'legal-casegrammar.lisp[general]' partition that casegrammar-split defines; the V1.6 section comment at :167 restates it" "SemanticProposer :generic-functions (V1.6:58) instantiates the :clos clause of common-lisp-cognition-usage (class 10, same batch)" "CANONICAL MODEL: none — `file` facts classify source/ by bulk dir-rule DR-0060 (files-and-roles.sexp:1077) as PRODUCTION_CODE only; no split, disposition or mechanism fact exists; 0 hits for either rule name in the 14 modules")
  :identity-version-rule "SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT for both, in opposite directions. casegrammar-split (V1.6:247-250) and SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:130-134 hold the same three clauses with divergent key sets, both DDI-4, both AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE, neither declaring the other superseded — a horizontal duplicate. common-lisp-cognition-usage (V1.6:251-260) is superseded IN SUBSTANCE by LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md (a v1.7 CANDIDATE, :1) whose §2 table covers the same mechanisms with the eight-field admission discipline — but that document is AUTHORED_NORMATIVE_PROSE (files-and-roles.sexp:403), not a migration source, so the supersession crosses an authority class and is recorded nowhere. Neither rule name recurs in another registry (ONLY-VERSION by id)."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION for both forms. casegrammar-split is additionally a candidate for SKIP-WITH-PROOF (proof: the identical rule is imported from SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:130-134 as class 3), and that is the only migration_rule value in DDI-4 for which a real proof is available — but it requires the class-3 ruling first. common-lisp-cognition-usage is a candidate for SKIP-WITH-PROOF (proof: superseded by the CL contract) EXCEPT for the two clauses with no counterpart (:packages, :no-python-in-lisp), which would be silently lost — so the proof is incomplete today."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "CERTAIN for casegrammar-split (three statements: V1.6:247, SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:130, V1.6:167 comment — A14 V1.6 dossier / A11-SR SR dossier). HIGH for common-lisp-cognition-usage: importing 9 mechanism clauses as facts beside the CL contract's 16-row admission table creates a second mechanism registry, and the model would then hold a mechanism list that does NOT carry the eight-field discipline the contract requires (A15 V1.6 dossier)."
  :requirement "UNKNOWN — neither form carries a requirement id and no model `requirement` fact (rtw:5-28) covers file disposition or language-mechanism policy. The CL contract's own rows name requirements in prose ('typed Legal objects', 'pluggable cognition stages', LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:20-21) that are not ids at all."
  :invariant "L1 (nested clause lists are illegal values — flattening mandatory), L2 (clause id synthesis; and the duplicate-seat risk is an L2 question at concept level), L5 (casegrammar-split straddles the public/private boundary — same L5 question as class 3). Source invariants: :SR-V6-one-seat (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:136) governs the duplicate; :V6I-COG-symbolic-only (V1.6:265) and LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:6 govern the mechanism clauses."
  :qualification-test "NEW — QT-DDI4-RULE-NO-DUPLICATE-CONCEPT. Executable one-liner: `assert no two rule/file-disposition facts carry the same :path or the same clause triple` — i.e. the casegrammar duplicate becomes a detectable state rather than a reading of two files. Second: QT-DDI4-MECHANISM-ADMISSION — `for every rule-clause of common-lisp-cognition-usage, assert a matching row exists in LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md §2 with all eight fields` — run today it FAILS for :packages and :no-python-in-lisp, which is the intended signal. No existing model `test` fact covers either (rtw:30-50)."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact rule casegrammar-split :source-file \"V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp\" :source-line 247)` while a `file-disposition` fact for source/legal-casegrammar.lisp already exists — must be REJECTED by QT-DDI4-RULE-NO-DUPLICATE-CONCEPT, reason 'two seats for one file disposition'. Today no check would notice, which is the defect. APPEND `(fact rule-clause common-lisp-cognition-usage__mop :rule common-lisp-cognition-usage :key mop :text \"use the metaobject protocol\")` — must be REJECTED by QT-DDI4-MECHANISM-ADMISSION: the CL contract declares MOP 'NOT USED in the trusted path … forbidden without a specific proven invariant' (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:23). APPEND a `rule-clause` whose :rule names no `rule` fact — must be REJECTED, checker-reason 'L3'."
  :rollback "Delete the 2 rule + 12 rule-clause facts; remove the fact types from MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp and move :version (:37 / ROOT.sexp:9); re-run build_root.py; build_deferred.py restores deferred-imports.sexp:39. If casegrammar-split was skipped in favour of class 3, the rollback of class 3 must restore this class's deferred status too — the two rollbacks are coupled and must be planned as one."
  :batch-reason "DDI-4 because build_deferred.py:101 maps `define-rule` to DDI-4. AGREES — but with no evidence either way: dag.json records 0 in-edges and 0 out-edges for this class (its content references file paths and prose, not registry symbols). Intra-batch it is coupled to class 3 (same rule) and class 10 (the :clos clause), so its position inside DDI-4 is constrained even though its batch is not."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "Which form is the seat of the casegrammar split — V1.6:247 define-rule or SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:130 define-file-disposition (the same question as class 3, from the other side)? Is common-lisp-cognition-usage retired into a rationale pointer at LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md, imported as 9 rule-clause facts, or kept authoritative at source — and what happens to :packages and :no-python-in-lisp, which have no counterpart in that contract?"
  :adjudication-items ("A14 (V1.6 dossier) = A11-SR-CASEGRAMMAR-SPLIT-SEAT (SR dossier): two seats, one rule" "A15 (V1.6 dossier): common-lisp-cognition-usage overlaps the CL contract's mechanism table; two clauses have no located counterpart" "ADJ-MX4-CL-ADMISSION (new, shared with class 10): a mechanism list imported without the eight-field admission discipline (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:6) is a weaker second registry of the same concept" "ADJ-MX4-SKIP-PROOF (new): casegrammar-split is the ONLY DDI-4 form for which SKIP-WITH-PROOF has a real proof available (its twin is imported by class 3) — and it is unavailable until class 3 is decided")
  :topological-position 46 :atomic-groups ()
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "casegrammar-split: the SAME fact as C3 (one seat — adjudicate A11-SR-CASEGRAMMAR-SPLIT-SEAT); common-lisp-cognition-usage: its 9 clauses are the mechanism admissions of LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:18-35 (AUTHORED_NORMATIVE_PROSE files-and-roles.sexp:403) — a `rationale` pointer to the contract, not a text copy | invariant: :V6I-17 one source of truth (V1.6:348-355) | fallback: `rule-clause` facts (rule, key, text)" :clos-class "meta-rule :clos 'CLOS protocols + generic functions for adapters/analyzers' (V1.6:252) = contract rows LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:20-21 — seats cognition.lisp:35 frame / :42 working-memory; greek-nlp-core.lisp:163 lexicon / :387 analyzer | invariant: 'one class per concept' (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:20) | fallback: plain structs" :generic-function ":clos clause → cognition.lisp:92-113 defgeneric plan / execute-step / synthesize / triage / critique; greek-nlp-core.lisp:394 analyze | invariant: 'dispatch is total or errors typed' (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:21) | fallback: single dispatch function" :condition-restart ":conditions 'condition/restart system for controlled ambiguity and recovery' (V1.6:253) → LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:24: safe-read.lisp:68 safe-read-error; legal-ast.lisp:1597 with-ast-restarts; version-graph.lisp:184-205 typed uncertainty conditions | invariant: 'every error is a typed condition' (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:24) | fallback: typed error value" :macro-dsl ":macros 'macros/DSLs for grammar, morphology, Legal IR and rules' (V1.6:254) + :no-external-eval (:259) → LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:25,35: greek-legislation-ontology.lisp:57 defconcept; legal-inference-engine.lisp:491 defrule; legal-ast.lisp:1548 defastnode; capability-registry.lisp:140 define-capability; mcp-server.lisp:80 define-mcp-tool; safe-read.lisp:156 *read