(ddi-class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-ref-classification-v6
  :batch DDI-2 :source-file "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp" :fact-class "define-ref-classification-v6" :source-count 1 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms (("(public-build :hash-bearing (LegalIR/1 MemoryEvent/1 TrustBundle/1 LanguageCognitionLayer/1 CognitionResult/1))" :line 344 :sha16 "419c0424a4357a33"))
  :source-file "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp"
  :source-forms 1
  :current-authority-seat "V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp section '6. PUBLIC/PRIVATE/EMBODIMENT BOUNDARY (acyclic)' (header L340), comment L341-343 ('the real check is the TRANSITIVE type closure over these roots (audit V6S12) ... the manual list is only the seed, not the proof (defect 5)'), form L344-347. Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:37 (DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE, DDI-2, :source-count 1)."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp (existing) — it is the module that already holds the model's only boundary data (stage/stage-edge/consumes, dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:1-124) and the module PF-L4-STAGE-CYCLE enumerates (verification-corpus.sexp:54-56). It MUST be the same module that takes V1.7/V1.8 define-ra-closure-roots (DDI-1, deferred-imports.sexp:47,64), which are the successors of this form; those DDI-1 rows fix the module first."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "The DDI-1 closure-root family (created by V1.7/V1.8 define-ra-closure-roots), EXTENDED or REFUSED — not a new one. Shape needed: NEW `closure-root` (:required (family root) :types ((family SYMBOL) (root SYMBOL)) :ref ((root type))) plus NEW `private-forbidden` (:required (type) :ref ((type type))). Flattening rule: 3 nested class rows become 11 facts — 5 public-build hash-bearing roots, 2 private-profile consumables, 3 embodiment adapter-only names, plus 1 fact per class kind if the kind is not folded into :family. Id must be SYNTHESISED: the form has no atomic name (its second element is a nested list) and its identity is the (file, head) pair only (orchestrator-notes.md N11) — the same convention needed for V1.7:290, V1.8:259, V1.5:569, V1.7:379, V1.8:303, V1.8:444. no `enum`/`enum-value`/`field`/`primitive`/`cardinality`/`ref-class`/`adapter`/`canonical-identity` fact type exists among the 34 fact types (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:84-288); `define-enum` there is schema syntax for the model's own closed domains only (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:18,47-76); L1 forbids keywords, nested lists and NIL as values (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6) and the closed field set forbids adding keys to `type` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:9-13,148-152)"
  :owner "UNKNOWN. The form declares no owner. The boundary concept belongs to S18 by SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:91-93 ('Public->private boundary schemas'; subsystems.sexp:22 owner-seat SEAT-BOUNDARY-SHAPES, seats.sexp:73-74 DOCUMENT_SEAT deployment/shapes/legal-shapes.ttl), but no registry states that S18 owns the closure-root declaration, and the successors V1.7:290 / V1.8:259 are equally ownerless."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — a boundary declaration, not a store. No registry names a writer."
  :classification "MIXED by construction: the form's whole purpose is to separate PUBLIC roots from PRIVATE consumers. Private members named: the private-profile class (V1.6:346, SignedPublicRelease / ProofCarryingInterface) and the embodiment class (:347, SensorAdapter / EmbodimentAdapter / ActuatorCapability). Of the 5 public roots, all 5 are PUBLIC `type` facts (interfaces-and-types.sexp:32,34,61,30,19). Of the 5 private/embodiment names, NONE is defined in any of the six registries (the V1.6 dossier's grep finds them only at V1.6:346-347); the three embodiment names correspond to FIELD NAMES of EmbodimentInterfaces/1 (V1.6:329), not to types."
  :dependencies ("DDI-1 FIRST: V1.7 define-ra-closure-roots (V1.7:290-296) and V1.8 define-ra-closure-roots (V1.8:259-265) create the family — reference kind: shared fact family. Both are DDI-1 (deferred-imports.sexp:47,64) while this predecessor is DDI-2: the successors import BEFORE it" "EXISTING model facts: the 5 PUBLIC `type` facts (interfaces-and-types.sexp:19,30,32,34,61) — :root ref targets, all present" "UNSATISFIABLE: SignedPublicRelease, ProofCarryingInterface, SensorAdapter, EmbodimentAdapter, ActuatorCapability are declared nowhere — L3 cannot close on them at all (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:24-25 'a closed reference universe')" "Id-synthesis convention for anonymous forms (orchestrator-notes.md N11) — a schema-level decision shared with 6 other forms")
  :consumers ("V1.6:341-343 comment (the seed/proof distinction) and audit V6S12 (V1.6-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh:204-236) — HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:440)" ":V6I-MEM-public-base-clean (V1.6:305-308) and :V6I-16-extension-isolation (:334-338) — DDI-4" "dag.json: NO class references this one (in-edges empty). Its own out-edges: ISR define-interface (5), V1.8 define-canonical-identity (4), V1.8 define-reference (4), V1.6 define-record (3), V1.6 define-reference (2), V1.7 define-reference (1)" "no tracked source/ or systems/ file names any record/enum id of the six registries (git grep at RO = 0); the only mechanical readers are the legacy audits/harness classified HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:436,440,444,450,453)")
  :identity-version-rule "SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT. V1.7:290-296 define-ra-closure-roots carries 11 public roots + an edge-kinds list + a private-forbidden list of 5 named types; V1.8:259-265 carries 10 roots (dropping LanguageCognitionLayer/1), an edge-families list and a private-forbidden list of 7. The V1.6 form's 5 roots are a strict subset of V1.7's 11; its private-profile and embodiment classes have NO counterpart in either successor (the successors list private-forbidden TYPES, not consumable interfaces). No form declares supersession; the divergence is visible only by comparing V1.6:344-347, V1.7:290-296 and V1.8:259-265. The form is anonymous, so any identity is synthesised (N11)."
  :migration-rule "SKIP-WITH-PROOF is the only rule that can be executed as stated, and it still needs a decision. The reasons are on the record: (i) both successors are in an EARLIER batch, so by the time DDI-2 runs the concept already has a seat; (ii) 5 of the 10 names it references are undefined everywhere, so an IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL or IMPORT-AS-HISTORICAL-VERSION cannot be L3-closed; (iii) V1.6:341-343 says the list is 'only the seed, not the proof'. The proof a SKIP requires is that no fact in the successors' import loses information present here — which is FALSE for the private-profile and embodiment rows, since neither successor carries them. That residue must be either re-seated or declared dead."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "HIGH. Three classes state 'the public closure roots' — V1.6:344 (DDI-2), V1.7:290 (DDI-1), V1.8:259 (DDI-1) — with different memberships. Importing more than one as canonical creates two or three seats for one boundary. The model's own boundary law is per-edge (L5 over `consumes`, KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:243-254), not root-based, so a `closure-root` family would be a NEW kind of boundary statement sitting beside an existing one — a second seat for 'what the public boundary is' unless the relationship is declared."
  :requirement "NONE. No `requirement` fact covers the boundary declaration; the model's public/private guarantee is carried by property-family PF-L5-PRIVATE-TYPE-LEAK (verification-corpus.sexp:45-47, :cardinality 6) and by the rationale RAT-PUBPRIV (rationale-references.sexp:7) — and orchestrator-notes.md N17 records that RAT-PUBPRIV's anchor string does not occur in the document it names, so the stated justification of the boundary points at text that does not exist."
  :invariant "L3 (every :root closes on a declared `type` — impossible for the 5 undefined names), L5 (public/private isolation, the law this form is the source-level statement of), L4 (acyclicity of the closure, which V1.7:297-299 :V7I-PUBPRIV-acyclic asserts and the model enforces only over stage-edges). Source invariants: :V6I-07-public-independent-of-private (V1.6:38-40), :V6I-16-extension-isolation (:334-338), :V7I-PUBPRIV-acyclic (V1.7:297-303), :V8I-PUBPRIV-all-families (V1.8:277-284)."
  :qualification-test "Existing: none (no model test names the closure roots). PF-L5-PRIVATE-TYPE-LEAK (verification-corpus.sexp:45-47) is the closest live mechanism and it enumerates PRIVATE `type` facts, not roots. NEW executable one-liner: the transitive closure over `consumes` from every declared public root contains no `type` whose :classification is PRIVATE and no field whose :domain is a private-bearing enum — the V6S12 check, expressed over model facts. Today the model can only decide the first half, and only per edge."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact closure-root PUBLIC_BUILD__SignedPublicRelease :family public-build :root SignedPublicRelease)` — both paths must reject: kernel-reason 'resolves to no declared type', checker-reason 'L3'. This is the falsifier that PROVES the 5 undefined names cannot be imported. APPEND `(fact consumes S13__PrivateMatterProfile/1 :consumer S13 :provides PrivateMatterProfile/1)` — must be rejected as 'public/private leak: PUBLIC S13 consumes PRIVATE type PrivateMatterProfile/1' (FX-L5-PUBLIC-PRIVATE-LEAK verification-corpus.sexp:34-35; KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:252-254). REPLACE a root's :family public-build with :family private-profile — must be rejected by the NEW closure check if the root is a public hash-bearing type."
  :rollback "No model change to roll back if the class is SKIPPED — rollback is the null action, and the ledger row stays DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT at deferred-imports.sexp:37. If it is imported: delete the imported facts of this class and the fact-type/enum declarations added to MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp for it, re-run build_root.py so ROOT.sexp re-pins the 14 modules (ROOT.sexp:12-27; L7), and restore the ledger row to DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT / AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE (deferred-imports.sexp) so the source file is authoritative again; the source registry is never edited by the import (V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp:256 'v1.5 files are NOT edited' is the precedent)"
  :batch-reason "DDI-2 because build_deferred.py maps define-ref-classification-v6 to DDI-2, materialised at deferred-imports.sexp:37. DISAGREES, and this is the sharpest batch contradiction in DDI-2: BOTH successors of this form are DDI-1 (deferred-imports.sexp:47 V1.7 define-ra-closure-roots, :64 V1.8 define-ra-closure-roots). A predecessor scheduled AFTER its own successors cannot be imported as canonical without unseating them, and cannot be imported as history without a historical-version family. dag.json confirms it has zero in-edges (nothing depends on it) and out-edges only to classes in DDI-1/DDI-2/IMPORTED — so nothing forces it to be in DDI-2 at all."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "(a) Does the V1.6 boundary seed import at all, given that V1.7:290 and V1.8:259 supersede it in an EARLIER batch — SKIP-WITH-PROOF, or IMPORT-AS-HISTORICAL-VERSION with a synthesised id? (b) What happens to the private-profile and embodiment rows (V1.6:346-347), whose 5 names are defined in no registry and whose content has NO counterpart in either successor — re-seat, declare dead, or leave as an undischarged residue? (c) Is a root-based closure family admitted beside the model's per-edge L5, and if so which one is authoritative when they disagree?"
  :adjudication-items ("A12 (V1.6 dossier): the form names SignedPublicRelease, ProofCarryingInterface, SensorAdapter, EmbodimentAdapter and ActuatorCapability, which are defined in NO registry; and it is superseded by two DDI-1 classes — successors import before the predecessor." "N11 (orchestrator): anonymous form — its identity is the (file, head) pair only; the id-synthesis convention is a schema-level decision shared with 6 other anonymous forms." "ADJ-DDI2-ROOTS-VS-L5: the model's public/private law is per-`consumes`-edge (KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:243-254); a `closure-root` family would be a second, root-based statement of the same boundary. Which is authoritative?" "N17 (orchestrator), inherited: RAT-PUBPRIV (rationale-references.sexp:7) is the declared rationale of every private seat and its :anchor string does not occur in deployment/LAWMAX-THREAT-MODEL.md — the boundary's stated justification is a dangling anchor no counted check opens.")
  :topological-position 45 :atomic-groups ()
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "NOT-APPLICABLE" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart "a private/embodiment name reachable from a public root => typed L5 violation (AM/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:1-3 (*read-eval* nil, standard readtable, no eval), :23 *enums*, :24 *conds*, :56-60 reader, :243-257 law5-isolation :243-257) | invariant: transitive public closure contains NO :DEFERRED_PRIVATE record (V1.6:340-343 'the manual list is only the seed, not the proof') | fallback: return typed error value (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:24)" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE (seed data)" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE" :package-asdf-boundary "the three families ARE the package/ASDF partition (public build systems / private profile system consuming signed releases only / embodiment adapters out of process) — the source-level twin of L5 (16 ASDF systems, 53 edges, cycle NONE (deployment/collab/dialogue/0146-claude.md:18); 17 .asd paths at HEAD of which systems/orchestrator-omega.asd is a symlink to ../orchestrator-omega.asd; source/safe-read.lisp:38-39 loaded FIRST in orchestrator-infrastructure) | invariant: V6I-07 public never depends on private (V1.6:38-40); V6I-16 acyclic | fallback: monolith package (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:31) — inadmissible under V6I-07; real fallback is non-import of private/embodiment names" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE" :compile-time-validation "build-time transitive closure from the roots over declared edge families (V1.8:264-276 derived from REAL sources), a mechanism the kernel implements as L5 over `consumes`/`type` facts (AM/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:1-3 (*read-eval* nil, standard readtable, no eval), :23 *enums*, :24 *conds*, :56-60 reader, :243-257 law5-isolation :243-257) | invariant: V8I-PUBPRIV-all-families (V1.8:277-283) | fallback: runtime check (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:32)" :runtime-validation "NOT-APPLICABLE (closure is a build property)" :python-in-cl-risk "MEDIUM. Naive import: three lists of STRING names, five of which (SignedPublicRelease, ProofCarryingInterface, SensorAdapter, EmbodimentAdapter, ActuatorCapability) are defined nowhere (dossier A12) => dangling strings that pass any dict check. CL-native: closure-root facts with L3-closed :root refs to `type` (shared family with V1.7/V1.8 ra-closure-roots, DDI-1) and no undefined names; undefined targets become DESIGN_TARGET/INTERFACE_ONLY seats or are not imported." :future-freedom "NO constraint if superseded by V1.7/V1.8 ra-closure-roots (DDI-1); importing the V1.6 seed as a second closure-root family would add a duplicate seat (constitution :no-duplicate). Embodiment marked :adapter-only preserves S20 replaceability.")
  )

