  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "NEW `invariant` (as class 1), with an additional :optional (audit successor supersedes) field set if the chains are to be represented: :audit STRING (the V7S-* ids the texts cite), :successor SYMBOL :ref ((successor invariant)) for the 13 forms with a V1.8 successor. Flattening rule: all 23 are docstring-only prose STRINGs, L1-legal; ids colon-stripped (keyword ids (`:V5I-01`, `:SR-V6-one-seat`, …) are not TOKEN-SPACE ids — TOKEN excludes ':' (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:41,17) — so a colon-stripping id-rendering convention must be declared once for all 92 define-invariant forms (orchestrator-notes.md N12)) to RA-I-1-root-authority-certifies-not-replaces … V7I-WP-honest, all TOKEN-legal. WARNING on :audit — the V7S-* ids (V7S-PUBPRIV, V7S-COGDAG, V7S-INFO, V7S-COV, V7S-SYM, V7S-OWN, V7S-CAP, V7S-SRC, V7S-WP) live ONLY inside V1.7-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh, which is HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:444) and 'never a blocking or sufficient acceptance gate' (LEGACY-AUDIT-DISPOSITION.md:10); typing :audit as a :ref into `test` would create 9 dangling references, and typing it as a free STRING imports test names the model cannot resolve (ADJ-V17-INV-3)."
  :owner "UNKNOWN for all 23 — define-invariant carries no :owner in V1.7 and the dossier records 'UNKNOWN as a fact (invariants carry no :owner); section context only' for every form. Section context suggests S25 for the resolver invariants (:166,:180), S15 for the citation invariant (:199), S14 for RA-T (:212), S26 for RA-INST (:234), S19 for the memory invariants (:111,:115), S04 for the cognition invariant (:95), S21 for SYM (:318) — all inferences from section placement, none declared. Not asserted here."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — no store (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:155-158). Note :V7I-OWN-single-writer (V1.7:337-340) is ABOUT writers; that does not give the invariant a writer."
  :classification "PUBLIC by content for 22; MIXED for :V7I-RA-INST-no-authority (V1.7:234-237), whose subject is the tenant profile — TenantProfile/1 is PRIVATE (interfaces-and-types.sexp:59), S26 is PRIVATE (subsystems.sexp:30) and SEAT-TENANT-PROFILE is INTERFACE_ONLY (seats.sexp:97). :V7I-PUBPRIV-acyclic (:297) likewise names the private families. As in class 9 the texts carry no private payload, but the classification rule for governance prose about private subjects is undeclared (ADJ-MX4-INV-CLASSIFICATION)."
  :dependencies ("DECISION: the shared invariant family + id rendering + one-seat policy (ADJ-MX4-INV-SEAT, ADJ-V17-INV-1) [schema dependency]" "DDI-1 V1.7-SCHEMAS define-pipeline (1 ref), define-construction-order (1 ref); DDI-1 V1.8-SCHEMAS define-pipeline (1 ref) [class references, dag.json]" "DDI-2 V1.6-SCHEMAS define-closed-enum (1 ref); DDI-2 V1.7 define-record (1 ref) [enum/record references]" "DDI-3 V1.7-SCHEMAS define-decision-function (1 ref) [class reference]" "DDI-4 sibling SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-wp-purpose (1 ref) [intra-batch order]" "IMPORTED ISR define-interface (1 ref) [satisfied]" "NOT AVAILABLE: the 9 V7S-* audit ids cited by the texts exist only in a HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE shell script (files-and-roles.sexp:444) [dangling test vocabulary]")
  :consumers ("CANONICAL MODEL: none — 0 hits for any V7I-*/RA-I-* id in the 14 modules; only the ledger row deferred-imports.sexp:45" "V1.8-SCHEMAS explicitly carries or supersedes 13 of them: :V8I-01 carries :RA-I-1 (V1.8:14); :V8I-02 restates :RA-I-3 and :V7I-no-mandatory-model-v7 (V1.8:17); :V8I-03 restates :RA-I-5 (V1.8:20); :V8I-PUBPRIV-all-families supersedes :RA-I-4 and :V7I-PUBPRIV-acyclic (V1.8:277); :V8I-OWN-universal supersedes :V7I-OWN-single-writer (V1.8:296); :V8I-WP-real supersedes :V7I-WP-honest (V1.8:320); :V8I-CAP-real supersedes :V7I-CAP-seat-closure (V1.8:250); :V8I-SYM-exact supersedes :V7I-SYM-reachable (V1.8:336); :V8I-RA-K-tiered supersedes :V7I-RA-K-metrics-not-truth (V1.8:184); :V8I-RASTATUS-product supersedes :V7I-RA-qual-revocable (V1.8:97); :V8I-MARK-separated carries :V7I-RA-L-no-unlicensed (V1.8:212); :V8I-COG-typed-edges / :V8I-COGGRAPH-acyclic-except-resume supersede :V7I-COG-info-preserving (V1.8:386, :66)" "V1.5 predecessor: :V7I-COV-availability-live (V1.7:280) restates :V5I-04 (V1.5:246) for the superseding decision function" "legacy: V1.7-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, files-and-roles.sexp:444)")
  :identity-version-rule "SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT for 13 of 23 (the chains listed in consumers, each with a V1.8 successor that changes the claim, not just the id) and ONLY-VERSION for the remaining 10 (:RA-I-2 :17, :V7I-MEM-user-private-no-auto-public :111, :V7I-MEM-one-owner :115, :V7I-RA-I-deterministic :166, :V7I-RA-R-proof-carrying-pages :180, :V7I-RA-T-lawmax-canonical-home :212, :V7I-RA-INST-no-authority :234, :V7I-COV-availability-live :280, :V7I-SRC-open-fail-closed :372, plus :V7I-no-mandatory-model-v7 :301 which duplicates :RA-I-3 INSIDE THE SAME FILE). One chain is a CONTRADICTION rather than a refinement: :V7I-SYM-reachable states 5 mutations (V1.7:318-321) while :V8I-SYM-exact fixes exactly 4 and declares 'the prior 5/3/2 ambiguity is retired' (V1.8:336-341) — importing both as history puts two incompatible mutation counts in the model (ADJ-V17-INV-2). No supersession is recorded in any machine-readable form: V1.7 is not edited (V1.7:255-256 'v1.5 files are NOT edited' is the analogous statement) and both classes remain AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE (deferred-imports.sexp:45, :62)."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION. Per-form after the policy ruling: 10 ONLY-VERSION forms would be IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL; 13 would be IMPORT-AS-HISTORICAL-VERSION under a latest-only policy, IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL under an all-as-history policy, or SKIP-WITH-PROOF under a pointer-only policy (the proof being the V1.8 successor id). The 13 cannot be silently dropped: the model would then carry V1.8's claims with no record that V1.7 claimed something different."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "HIGHEST of the invariant classes together with class 14. 13 of 23 forms have a live successor in a registry that is itself AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE; one form (:V7I-no-mandatory-model-v7 :301) duplicates another form in the SAME FILE (:RA-I-3 :20); and three forms restate laws the model already mechanises (:V7I-OWN-single-writer vs define-unique STORE-OWNER-IS-ONE-SEAT MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:319 + PF-L2-DUPLICATE-STORE vc:48-50; :RA-I-5 vs L2; :V7I-PUBPRIV-acyclic vs L5). Importing them creates prose seats beside mechanised laws with no declared precedence."
  :requirement "UNKNOWN / NEW — no requirement id is attached to any form. The V1.7 RA-layer requirement ids (RA-E RA-I RA-J RA-K RA-L RA-R RA-T) appear in define-capability-seat (V1.7:346-352, DDI-1) and in TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md, and NONE is a model `requirement` fact (rtw:5-28) — orchestrator-notes.md N1. L6 closure for this class is therefore unavailable until the requirement universe question is settled."
  :invariant "L1 (prose strings legal, keyword ids not), L2 (one id per fact type; and the concept-level duplicates are an L2 question), L3 (:successor and :audit references — the latter would be dangling), L5 (the class is ABOUT the boundary; L5 today covers only `consumes`), L6 (no requirement/test ids resolve), L7 (module universe). Source: the 23 forms ARE the invariants."
  :qualification-test "NEW — QT-DDI4-INV-SUCCESSION. Executable one-liner: `for every invariant fact carrying :successor S, assert S is a declared invariant fact AND exactly one of the pair carries :status ACTIVE` — i.e. a superseded invariant may exist in the model only as history, never as a second live claim. Companion: `assert every :audit value resolves to a declared test fact OR the fact carries :audit-unresolved YES` — turning the 9 dangling V7S-* ids into a declared state instead of prose. No existing model `test` fact covers either (rtw:30-50); the V6Q-* ids that do exist are declared UNEXECUTED (orchestrator-notes.md N7)."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact invariant V7I-SYM-reachable :source-file \"V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp\" :source-line 318 :text \"…\" :status ACTIVE :successor V8I-SYM-exact)` while V8I-SYM-exact also carries :status ACTIVE — must be REJECTED by QT-DDI4-INV-SUCCESSION, reason 'two ACTIVE invariants in one succession chain'. APPEND `(fact invariant V7I-WP-honest :audit V7S-WP …)` with :audit typed as a :ref into `test` — must be REJECTED: kernel-reason 'resolves to no declared test', checker-reason 'L3' (precedent FX-L3-DANGLING-WP vc:30-31). REPLACE `:source-file \"V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp\"` with a path that is not a tracked file — must be REJECTED by a source-file existence check (there is none today; the RAT-PUBPRIV precedent shows why one is needed, orchestrator-notes.md N17)."
  :rollback "Delete the 23 facts and adjust UF-INVARIANT; remove the fact type/enums from MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp and move :version (:37 / ROOT.sexp:9); delete invariants.sexp and re-run build_root.py; build_deferred.py restores deferred-imports.sexp:45. If a latest-only policy was applied, rolling back means the model loses the V1.8 texts as well — the two invariant classes (12 and 14) must be rolled back together."
  :batch-reason "DDI-4 because build_deferred.py:101 maps `define-invariant` to DDI-4. AGREES — all 7 recorded out-edges point at IMPORTED (1), DDI-1 (3), DDI-2 (2), DDI-3 (1) and DDI-4 (1) classes; dag.json records no order violation naming this class as a target. Intra-batch it must follow class 2 (WP reference) and is coupled to class 14 by 13 succession chains — a coupling the batch label does not express."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "What is the import policy for a superseded prose invariant — latest-only, all-as-history, or pointer-only — given 13 of these 23 forms have a V1.8 successor and both registries remain AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE? Which mutation count is canonical for the symbolic-only path, V1.7's 5 (:318-321) or V1.8's 4 (:336-341)? And what happens to :V7I-no-mandatory-model-v7 (:301), which duplicates :RA-I-3 (:20) inside one file?"
  :adjudication-items ("ADJ-V17-INV-1 (V1.7 dossier): duplicate invariant seats across V1.6/V1.7/V1.8 — 11 named chains" "ADJ-V17-INV-2 (V1.7 dossier): 5 mutations (V1.7:321) vs exactly 4 (V1.8:339-341) — a contradiction between registries, not a refinement" "ADJ-V17-INV-3 (V1.7 dossier): the V7S-* audit ids live only in a HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE script; importing the text imports dangling test references" "ADJ-MX4-INV-SEAT (new, shared): one module + one policy for the 92 invariant forms" "ADJ-MX4-PROSE-VS-LAW (new, shared with class 14): :V7I-OWN-single-writer, :RA-I-5 and :V7I-PUBPRIV-acyclic restate laws the model already mechanises (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:319, :34-36, :164-170) — is the mechanised law the seat, with the prose retired to a rationale pointer, or do both stand?" "ADJ-MX4-INV-CLASSIFICATION (new, shared with class 9): governance prose whose subject is PRIVATE has no declared classification rule")
  :topological-position 31 :atomic-groups ()
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "hash-pinned anchor facts with a supersession chain (:supersedes / :superseded-by as L3 refs invariant→invariant, L4-acyclic) so the one-seat question (ADJ-V17-INV-1) is DATA; :V7I-RA-T 'snapshots/deltas are signed, content-addressed' (V1.7:214) → canon-sexp/sha256 seat journal.lisp:61-90 | invariant: :RA-I-5 one seat per concept (V1.7:26-28) | fallback: latest-only import (V1.8 ids live) with V1.7 as rationale pointers" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart ":V7I-RA-I-deterministic: non-unique input ⇒ typed AmbiguityResult/1 VALUE (V1.7:166-169), never a guess; :V7I-COG-info-preserving (d): COG7-11 is an EXPLICIT branch whose seat is 'legal-dialectic.lisp + condition/restart' (V1.7:91) — the only mandated restart; CognitionErrorV7 values otherwise (V1.7:40-43) | invariant: :V7I-COG-info-preserving (e) 'no silent forced winner' (V1.7:95-101) | fallback: typed error value (see ADJ-CL4-03: the named restart seat is not built)" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE (registry forms are DATA read under *read-eval* nil (deferred-imports.sexp:4; ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:56; safe-read.lisp:152-165) — never a macro expanded over the registry file)" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE" :package-asdf-boundary ":RA-I-4 / :V7I-PUBPRIV-acyclic / :V7I-RA-INST: the public closure contains zero INTERFACE_ONLY/DEFERRED_PRIVATE record — model L5 over consumes (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:243) + ASDF/package boundary for TenantProfile (SEAT-TENANT-PROFILE INTERFACE_ONLY seats.sexp:97) | invariant: :V7I-PUBPRIV-acyclic 'public → private/real-time/embodiment edges are FORBIDDEN and structurally absent' (V1.7:297-300) | fallback: L5 over the consumes family only (today's single family — cf. ADJ-V18-INV-5)" :persistent-event ":V7I-OWN-single-writer: ONE canonical write seat write-authority.lisp for journal/memory/IR (V1.7:337-340; the define-write-authority rows :327-336 are DDI-1 in V1.7 / IMPORTED from V1.8) — seat write-authority.lisp:16-51,53; :V7I-RA-qual-revocable: expiring/downgrading state transitions are journaled | invariant: :V7I-OWN-single-writer | fallback: replay" :truth-maintenance-dependency ":V7I-COG-info-preserving (c)(e): alternatives + uncertainty preserved, no forced winner — the alternative SET (LegalSemanticAlternativeSet/1 V1.7:62-65) maps to competing JTMS nodes left :undefined under WFS (legal-inference-engine.lisp:233-236) rather than to a selected winner; :V7I-RA-K 'metrics are NEVER evidence of legal correctness' (V1.7:199-202) keeps metrics OUT of the belief graph | invariant: :V7I-COG-info-preserving | fallback: full recompute" :temporal-index-projection ":V7I-COV-availability-live: availability is a LIVE input of the census decision (V1.7:280-284) = an as-of projection over coverage state; :V7I-MEM-user-private scopes with retention/deletion (V1.7:106-110) = scope × time policy | invariant: :V7I-COV-availability-live 'mutation removing the guard flips' (V1.7:284) | fallback: recompute the decision table (define-decision-function is DDI-3)" :compile-time-validation "mechanizable subset at gate time: :V7I-OWN-single-writer → L2 define-unique STORE-OWNER-IS-ONE-SEAT (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:319) + PF-L2-DUPLICATE-STORE (verification-corpus.sexp:48-50) — ALREADY enforced; :V7I-SYM-reachable → L4 + reachability over stage/stage-edge (dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:5-21); :V7I-CAP-seat-closure → L3 refs from DDI-1 capability-seat facts to real file/package/symbol — the kernel reads only model modules (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:170-184), so a 'real symbol' check is a gate_checks.py-class check with git access (pattern gate_checks.py:786 check_seats) declared as a check fact; :V7I-WP-honest → C13 | invariant: each clause's 'Audit … with N mutations' sentence | fallback: V1.7-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh — HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:444); the V7S-* ids exist nowhere else (dossier ADJ-V17-INV-3)" :runtime-validation ":V7I-RA-I-deterministic (resolver, SEAT-CANONICAL-URIS seats.sexp:62), :V7I-RA-L (RIGHTS_UNKNOWN ⇒ no redistribution), :V7I-SRC-open-fail-closed (unknown source type fails closed), :V7I-RA-INST (a tenant never gains write authority — write-authority.lisp:35-38 closed authority set) | invariant: the fail-closed clauses (V1.7:140-142, 167-169, 235-238, 373-375) | fallback: reject" :python-in-cl-risk "YES — 23 blobs with dangling audit ids (V7S-*), 13 duplicates of V1.6/V1.8 ids imported as separate 'facts' (violating :RA-I-5 by the act of import), and :V7I-SYM-reachable's '5 mutations' (V1.7:321) frozen next to :V8I-SYM-exact's 'EXACTLY 4' (V1.8:339-341) as two live strings. CL-native alternative: supersession-chain facts (L3 refs invariant→invariant, L4 acyclic) with only the LATEST id live; mechanized clauses as data laws (define-unique / edge relations); audit ids as `test` facts ONLY if a tracked, authoritative harness exists (none: files-and-roles.sexp:444 is HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE)." :future-freedom "CONSTRAINS: :V7I-MEM-one-owner fixes S19 = memory.lisp EXTEND with owner FUTURE_IMPLEMENTATION_BOOK_PACKET_REQUIRED (V1.7:115-118) — a schedule block on S19 construction, not a mechanism constraint; :V7I-COG-info-preserving fixes the 14-stage DAG and :no-forced-winner for S04 (carried by DDI-1/DDI-3 classes) — compatible with JTMS :undefined; :V7I-RA-K binds S15 to citation-authority.lisp (seats.sexp:52). PROTECTS: :RA-I-3/:V7I-no-mandatory-model-v7 (V8I-02). CONTRADICTION with V1.8 (5 vs 4 mutations; :V8I-SYM-structural retracts 'semantic') constrains the future test corpus — must be adjudicated before either is a live fact (ADJ-CL4-05).")
  )

(ddi-class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-reference
  :batch DDI-2 :source-file "V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp" :fact-class "define-reference" :source-count 8 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms (("PerceptionEnvelope/1" :line 34 :sha16 "6fbc92ac4cbdd688") ("MorphLattice/1" :line 35 :sha16 "7fb367acbe9e5114") ("PackedParseForest/1" :line 36 :sha16 "9cc44374e4ae5931") ("DiscourseState/1" :line 37 :sha16 "1518f2b21ba58af2") ("PromotionEvidence/1" :line 38 :sha16 "bba94e53316e4a3d") ("CognitionResult/1" :line 39 :sha16 "d04f120dfadb82d4") ("availability_state" :line 257 :sha16 "9b6bf259151d4101") ("census_coverage_state" :line 258 :sha16 "d650dbb0336e8680"))
  :source-file "V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp"
  :source-forms 8
  :current-authority-seat "V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp section '1. TYPE-CORRECT COGNITION DAG (C-2)' (header L30): PerceptionEnvelope/1 L34, MorphLattice/1 L35, PackedParseForest/1 L36, DiscourseState/1 L37, PromotionEvidence/1 L38, CognitionResult/1 L39; section '10. C-11 CORRECTED COVERAGE DECISION (availability LIVE)' (header L254): availability_state L257, census_coverage_state L258. Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:49 (DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE, DDI-2, :source-count 8)."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "The SAME module and the SAME family as V1.6 define-reference, V1.8 define-reference and the DDI-1 V1.8 define-canonical-identity (ADJ-DDI2-IDENTITY-FAMILY) — decided in DDI-1, inherited here. interfaces-and-types.sexp if the payload becomes optional fields of `type`; a NEW module only if a separate identity family is chosen. Two of the eight (availability_state, census_coverage_state) reference ENUMS, not types, so the family must be able to name an `enum` as its subject — which the V1.8 shape (:type -> type) cannot do as written."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "The DDI-1 identity family, with a widened subject. Shape needed: (:subject <type|enum> :identity STRING :version STRING :canonical-file STRING :locator STRING) where :subject is a ref into `type` OR `enum` (a two-target closed ref, as `consumes :consumer` already is — MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:167-170). Flattening rule: values are already flat strings; 8 facts. The V1.7 key is :canonical (a prose seat string such as 'V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp §3' or 'V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp:188'), NOT the V1.8 :canonical-file + :locator pair — a prose section reference cannot be machine-resolved, so importing it verbatim would create an unresolvable anchor of exactly the kind orchestrator-notes.md N17 documents for RAT-PUBPRIV. no `enum`/`enum-value`/`field`/`primitive`/`cardinality`/`ref-class`/`adapter`/`canonical-identity` fact type exists among the 34 fact types (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:84-288); `define-enum` there is schema syntax for the model's own closed domains only (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:18,47-76); L1 forbids keywords, nested lists and NIL as values (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6) and the closed field set forbids adding keys to `type` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:9-13,148-152)"
  :owner "MIXED — 2 declared, 6 UNKNOWN. DECLARED: S02 PerceptionEnvelope/1 (ISR:11; interfaces-and-types.sexp:39; SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:38), S04 CognitionResult/1 (ISR:43; interfaces-and-types.sexp:19; SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:45). UNKNOWN (4 records): MorphLattice/1, PackedParseForest/1, DiscourseState/1, PromotionEvidence/1 — absent from ISR (V1.7 dossier: ISR grep 0) and from every owner field; S04 is a prose inference (V1.6:164-166). UNKNOWN (2 enums): availability_state and census_coverage_state carry no owner; SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:85-86 names census_coverage_state inside S16's :interface string and SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:36 names census-coverage-decision inside S01's — two subsystems mention it, neither declares ownership."
  :writer "NO_WRITER for the identity facts themselves. For the referenced subjects: no store exists for any of the 6 records or 2 enums (stores-and-authorities.sexp:5-14 lists 10 stores, none of them a cognition or coverage-state store), and no registry names a writer — so the writer of the subject is UNKNOWN, not NO_WRITER."
  :classification "MIXED — 2 PUBLIC by model fact (PerceptionEnvelope/1 interfaces-and-types.sexp:39, CognitionResult/1 :19), 6 UNCLASSIFIED. No private member. The 4 unseated records carry no classification anywhere (V1.7 dossier: 'UNKNOWN (no classification anywhere; not a model type)') and the 2 enums are PUBLIC only 'by content' — the model has no classification for enums at all. Under MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:48-49 an undecidable kind is a typed failure, so UNCLASSIFIED is a blocker, not a default."
  :dependencies ("DDI-1 FIRST: V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-canonical-identity (deferred-imports.sexp:59, DDI-1) fixes the identity family — reference kind: shared fact family" "SAME BATCH: V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-record (the 5 record subjects' structure seats: V1.6:85,183,186,192,201,204) and V1.5-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum / define-frozen-enum-reference (the 2 enum subjects: V1.5:188 and V1.5:182) — the :subject ref cannot close before those exist as facts" "ISR EXTENSION (IMPORTED class): 4 of the 6 record subjects have no ISR row (:ISR-V6-closure ISR:177-180)" "DECISION FIRST: owner + classification for 6 subjects; whether the identity family admits `enum` subjects; whether V1.7:39 is retired in favour of V1.8:348 (ADJ-V17-REF-2)")
  :consumers ("V1.6 define-construction-order (DDI-1) — 6 refs; V1.7 define-construction-order (DDI-1) — 6 refs; V1.8 define-cognition-node-types (DDI-3) — 6 refs" "V1.7 define-pipeline (DDI-1) — 3 refs; V1.7 define-ra-closure-roots (DDI-1) — 1 ref; V1.8 define-ra-closure-roots (DDI-1) — 1 ref; V1.8 define-canonical-identity (DDI-1) — 1 ref" "SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-subsystem (IMPORTED) — 2 refs (SR:38 S02 -> V1.7:34; SR:85 S16 -> V1.7:258)" "V1.5 define-invariant (DDI-4) — 2 refs; V1.5 define-decision-function (DDI-3) — 1 ref; V1.7 define-decision-function (DDI-3) — 1 ref; V1.6 define-protocol (DDI-4) — 1 ref; V1.6 define-ref-classification-v6 (DDI-2) — 1 ref" "legacy readers: V1.7-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh and V1.8-VERIFY.py:1373-1375 — both HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:444,453)" "no tracked source/ or systems/ file names any record/enum id of the six registries (git grep at RO = 0); the only mechanical readers are the legacy audits/harness classified HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:436,440,444,450,453)")
  :identity-version-rule "MIXED. SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT (1): CognitionResult/1 — V1.7:39 :canonical 'V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp §3' (prose) vs V1.8:348 :canonical-file + :locator (machine-openable) vs V1.8:428 define-canonical-identity; identical :identity 'lawmax/cognition-result/1' and :version, divergent reference FORMAT. V1.8:353-357 (:V8I-XREF-real) makes the V1.8 format the audited one, but no form declares V1.7:39 retired (ADJ-V17-REF-2). ONLY-VERSION but POINTING AT A DDI-2 TARGET (5): PerceptionEnvelope/1, MorphLattice/1, PackedParseForest/1, DiscourseState/1, PromotionEvidence/1 — their :canonical strings all name V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp sections, i.e. a file this very batch imports; after DDI-2 the pointer is stale. ONLY-VERSION with a LINE LOCATOR (2): availability_state :canonical 'V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp:188' and census_coverage_state :canonical 'V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp:184 (frozen v1.4 enum)' — a LINE NUMBER inside another migration source, and for census_coverage_state the cited line 184 is inside the form whose head is at V1.5:182, not the head itself. A line-number anchor cannot survive any edit of the target file."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION. Once the identity family exists it is MERGE-INTO-EXISTING-FACT for the 2 subjects that are model types and IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL for the rest — but only after the 6 unclassified/unowned subjects are seated, and only after the pointer question is answered, because every one of the 8 :canonical values points INTO a file that DDI-2 itself imports (V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp x6, V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp x2). Importing the pointers unchanged would install 8 anchors that are correct today and wrong the moment the target class is imported (ADJ-V18-REF-2 in the V1.8 dossier states the same problem for 5 V1.8 references)."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "HIGH. (1) Three reference blocks compete for CognitionResult/1's identity: V1.7:39, V1.8:348 and V1.8:428 — the last two are in different batches (DDI-2 and DDI-1). (2) The V1.7 :canonical key and the V1.8 :canonical-file/:locator pair are two vocabularies for one payload (ADJ-DDI2-IDENTITY-FAMILY). (3) The 4 unseated records would acquire their FIRST registry-level identity here while their structure lives in V1.6 and their ISR row does not exist — three places, no seat. (4) No model id collision: no `type` or other fact carries these ids except PerceptionEnvelope/1 and CognitionResult/1, where the payload merges into the existing fact."
  :requirement "Partial. R-16/Q16 via req-map S02__WP-02 (requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:68) for PerceptionEnvelope/1; R-129/Q08 via S04__WP-08 (:70) for CognitionResult/1. NONE for the 4 unseated records and the 2 enums — and none is obtainable until they have an owner subsystem. R-132/Q29 via S16__WP-01 (:82) is the nearest for census_coverage_state, on the strength of a mention inside an :interface string (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:85-86), which is not an ownership declaration."
  :invariant "L2 (one id per fact type — the identity payload must merge into the existing `type` fact, not create a second one), L3 (:subject closed over type|enum). Source invariants: :V6I-REF-single-source-of-truth (V1.6:158-162), :V8I-XREF-real (V1.8:353-357, 'real file+locator'), :V8I-XREF-identity (V1.8:433-441 with its five named mutations including 'locator-absent-from-canonical-file'). Neither verification path implements an anchor resolver today (my own grep of gate_checks.py and KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp: none) — the same structural hole as the live RAT-PUBPRIV defect (orchestrator-notes.md N17)."
  :qualification-test "NEW. Executable one-liner: for every identity fact, :subject resolves to a declared `type` or `enum`, the file named by :canonical-file exists in the candidate tree, and `grep -F -- '<locator>' <canonical-file>` matches at least once — and, additionally, the :canonical-file is NOT one of the six migration sources once that source's class has been imported (otherwise the model points at a file it has superseded). The second clause is what makes the pointer-staleness failure detectable rather than latent."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact canonical-identity MorphLattice/1 :subject MorphLattice/1 :identity lawmax/morph-lattice/1 :version 1)` while MorphLattice/1 is not a declared `type` — both paths must reject: kernel-reason 'resolves to no declared type', checker-reason 'L3'. This falsifier IS the proof that the 4 unseated records block the class. REPLACE `:canonical-file \"deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp\"` with a path that does not exist — must be rejected by the NEW anchor check. CHECK-class: after importing V1.6 define-record, require the gate to fail if any identity fact still names V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp as its canonical file — the staleness check."
  :rollback "delete the imported facts of this class and the fact-type/enum declarations added to MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp for it, re-run build_root.py so ROOT.sexp re-pins the 14 modules (ROOT.sexp:12-27; L7), and restore the ledger row to DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT / AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE (deferred-imports.sexp) so the source file is authoritative again; the source registry is never edited by the import (V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp:256 'v1.5 files are NOT edited' is the precedent)"
  :batch-reason "DDI-2 because build_deferred.py maps define-reference to DDI-2, materialised at deferred-imports.sexp:49. DISAGREES in the 'too late' direction: seven earlier-rank classes reference it — V1.6/V1.7 define-construction-order (DDI-1, 6+6 refs), V1.7 define-pipeline (DDI-1, 3), V1.7/V1.8 define-ra-closure-roots (DDI-1, 1+1), V1.8 define-canonical-identity (DDI-1, 1), SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-subsystem (IMPORTED, 2) — all listed as order violations in dag.json. It has ZERO out-edges in dag.json, i.e. nothing in the registries is a prerequisite of it — the placement is late, never early."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "(a) Does the DDI-1 identity family admit an `enum` subject, so that availability_state and census_coverage_state can be imported at all? (b) Is V1.7:39 (CognitionResult/1) retired in favour of the audited V1.8:348 format, or do both import? (c) What do the 8 :canonical pointers point at AFTER DDI-2 imports their targets — the model module, or is the pointer dropped? (d) Are the prose section locators ('V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp §3') and the line-number locator ('V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp:188') converted to machine-resolvable anchors, or imported as unresolvable strings?"
  :adjudication-items ("ADJ-DDI2-IDENTITY-FAMILY: four classes carry the SAME payload (identity + version + canonical pointer) under three key vocabularies — V1.6 define-reference :canonical/:identity/:version/:owner-wp (V1.6:92-150), V1.7 define-reference :canonical/:identity/:version (V1.7:34-39,257-258), V1.8 define-reference :canonical-file/:identity/:version/:locator (V1.8:107,345-352) and V1.8 define-canonical-identity (V1.8:425-432, batch DDI-1, deferred-imports.sexp:59). ONE fact family must be decided in DDI-1 before any of the three DDI-2 reference classes can be imported." "ADJ-V17-REF-1 (V1.7 dossier): MorphLattice/1, PackedParseForest/1, DiscourseState/1 and PromotionEvidence/1 are referenced by V1.7 and V1.8 cognition graphs but absent from ISR (violating :ISR-V6-closure ISR:177-180) and from the model; `type` requires :owner-subsystem (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:148-152)." "ADJ-V17-REF-2 (V1.7 dossier): CognitionResult/1 is referenced at V1.7:39 (prose canonical) and V1.8:348 (canonical-file + locator, audit-opened by :V8I-XREF-real) — is V1.7:39 retired?" "ADJ-DDI2-ENUM-SUBJECT: two of the eight references have an ENUM as subject (V1.7:257,258); the V1.8 identity shape names a type. Widen the family or refuse the two forms." "ADJ-DDI2-STALE-ANCHOR (shared with V1.8 define-reference ADJ-V18-REF-2): all 8 :canonical values point into V1.5/V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp, which files-and-roles.sexp:441,447 classify CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT and which DDI-2 imports — the anchors become stale by construction." "UNKNOWN: census_coverage_state's locator 'V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp:184' names a line INSIDE the form (the :members line) rather than the form head at V1.5:182 — a line-number anchor with no stability guarantee.")
  :topological-position 4 :atomic-groups ()
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "NOT-APPLICABLE" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart "as class 9 (unresolvable seat => typed L3 violation) | invariant: :ISR-V6-closure (4 of 6 record references have NO ISR entry and no owner — ADJ-V17-REF-1) | fallback: return typed error value (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:24)" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE" :package-asdf-boundary "the 6 record identities resolve to the S04 cognition package(s) once ISR/owner are decided (ADJ-V17-REF-1); the 2 enum identities resolve to the enum family's seat (class 1/4) | invariant: one seat per concept | fallback: document anchor (V1.6/V1.5 section pointers)" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE" :compile-time-validation "build-time: :canonical 'V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp §3' is a SECTION pointer into a migration source; after DDI-2 imports the V1.6 records the pointer must move to the model `type` fact (or become stale — the same problem as ADJ-V18-REF-2); the identity strings are the audited property (V8I-XREF-identity part A, V1.8:433-441) | invariant: identity+version bound to exactly one define-reference block (V1.8:416-424) | fallback: grep of the section string" :runtime-validation "NOT-APPLICABLE" :python-in-cl-risk "MEDIUM. Naive import: :canonical 'V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp §3' as a STRING pointer to a section of a file that DDI-2 itself retires from authority; identity strings duplicated across V1.7:39 / V1.8:348 / V1.8:428 (three seats for CognitionResult/1's identity). CL-native: ONE canonical-identity fact per type (shared with V1.8 define-canonical-identity, DDI-1) whose :seat is an L3 ref to the model module that owns the structure — never a file+section string into a migration source." :future-freedom "NO constraint on S04/S19/JTMS/S20. The four unseated cognition records (MorphLattice/1, PackedParseForest/1, DiscourseState/1, PromotionEvidence/1) need an owner (S04?) and ISR rows before any `type` fact can exist (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:148-152 requires owner-subsystem) — an ownership adjudication, not a freedom loss.")
  )

(ddi-class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum
  :batch DDI-2 :source-file "V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp" :fact-class "define-closed-enum" :source-count 8 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms (("CognitionErrorV7" :line 40 :sha16 "a894015def0dbc5a") ("MemoryScopeV7" :line 105 :sha16 "e07875ed400dd01e") ("ArtifactRightsClass" :line 121 :sha16 "a5206bf6f9112716") ("RightsDisposition" :line 124 :sha16 "f4ee69b71c58de34") ("LegalReviewState" :line 125 :sha16 "7180d34d169c2ce7") ("ResolverInputKind" :line 147 :sha16 "16e87a267e851a1e") ("RetrievalFormat" :line 172 :sha16 "25d1d4c1e7ad82da") ("RootAuthorityState" :line 241 :sha16 "81586043cdc1d6d6"))
  :source-file "V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp"
  :source-forms 8
  :current-authority-seat "V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp — section '1. TYPE-CORRECT COGNITION DAG (C-2)' (header L30): CognitionErrorV7 L40-43; section '2. PUBLIC-SYSTEM MEMORY PRIVACY SCOPES (C-9)' (header L103, comment L104 'Replaces the vague (:public :user :ephemeral) with typed scopes carrying per-scope policy'): MemoryScopeV7 L105; section '3. RA-L RIGHTS / LICENSE' (header L120): ArtifactRightsClass L121-123, RightsDisposition L124, LegalReviewState L125; section '4. RA-I UNIVERSAL LEGAL RESOLVER' (header L144): ResolverInputKind L147-149; section '5. RA-R PUBLIC RETRIEVAL' (header L171): RetrievalFormat L172; section '9. RA ROOT-AUTHORITY QUALIFICATION STATE' (header L240): RootAuthorityState L241. Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:42 (DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE, DDI-2, :source-count 8)."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "UNDECIDED, and it MUST be the same module as the V1.5/V1.6/V1.8 enums — the V1.7 dossier proposes a NEW module 'enums' while the V1.5/V1.6 dossiers propose interfaces-and-types.sexp (ADJ-DDI2-ENUM-SEAT). Nothing in this class forces NEW: 8 enums / 61 values is small beside the existing 60 `type` facts, and a NEW module costs a ROOT.sexp composition change (ROOT.sexp:12-27, :module-count 14) plus an L7 re-pin."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "The same NEW `enum` + `enum-value` family as the other three DDI-2 enum classes. flattening rule: one `enum` fact per define-closed-enum (id = enum name, TOKEN) + one `enum-value` fact per member (id = <enum>__<VALUE>, :enum <enum> :value <VALUE> :ordinal <n>); keyword members rendered as bare symbols by colon-strip (orchestrator-notes.md N12); per-member attributes (:label/:obligation/:binding/:sa) become STRING/SYMBOL fields of the enum-value fact. Cardinality by my own reader: 8 `enum` + 61 `enum-value` facts (CognitionErrorV7 15, MemoryScopeV7 4, ArtifactRightsClass 8, RightsDisposition 4, LegalReviewState 5, ResolverInputKind 12, RetrievalFormat 7, RootAuthorityState 6). no `enum`/`enum-value`/`field`/`primitive`/`cardinality`/`ref-class`/`adapter`/`canonical-identity` fact type exists among the 34 fact types (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:84-288); `define-enum` there is schema syntax for the model's own closed domains only (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:18,47-76); L1 forbids keywords, nested lists and NIL as values (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6) and the closed field set forbids adding keys to `type` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:9-13,148-152)"
  :owner "UNKNOWN for all 8 as facts — no define-closed-enum form in V1.7 carries an owner key, and no registry row assigns one. Section context only: S25 for ResolverInputKind (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:119-121 S25 'canonical-uris.lisp (EXTEND: ECLI/CELEX/ADA/FEK)'), S13 for RetrievalFormat (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:75), S25 for the rights enums (RightsMatrix/1 owner S25, ISR:87), S19 for MemoryScopeV7 (memory section), S14 for RootAuthorityState (RootAuthorityQualification/1 owner S14, ISR:101), S04 for CognitionErrorV7. Every one of these is an inference from the CONSUMING record's owner or from a section header, not a declaration (V1.7 dossier unknown #1). If `enum` requires :owner-subsystem (as `type` does, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:148-152) this class cannot be imported until the field is decided optional or the owners are declared."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — closed value domains are declared, not written. Instances carrying these values are written by the owning store's writer where one exists: resolver-dataset writer SEAT-NO-WRITER (stores-and-authorities.sexp:11), static-site writer SEAT-NO-WRITER (:12), dataset-distribution writer SEAT-RA-T-SIGNER (:7). No registry names a writer for an enum."
  :classification "PUBLIC by content for all 8 — no form carries a private marker and none appears in the private-forbidden lists (V1.7:296; V1.8:262-263). ONE caveat that must not be lost: MemoryScopeV7 (V1.7:105) contains the members :USER_PRIVATE and :SERVICE_INTERNAL, i.e. private-BEARING values inside an enum V1.7 itself declares PUBLIC — exactly the shape V1.6:283 treats as private-bearing for MemoryScope and that :V7I-PUBPRIV-acyclic (V1.7:297-299) forbids in the public closure ('ZERO ... private-bearing enum'). The classification of an enum is not decidable from the model today because L5 sees only `consumes` edges (KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:243-254)."
  :dependencies ("SCHEMA FIRST: `enum` + `enum-value` fact types and the schema-version bump (X74-X76 verification-corpus.sexp:354-370) — fact-type declaration" "DECISION FIRST: the one enum module (ADJ-DDI2-ENUM-SEAT) and whether `enum` requires :owner-subsystem" "NO SOURCE DEPENDENCY: dag.json records ZERO out-edges for this class — it references nothing in the six registries. Its only in-edge is V1.7 define-record (8 refs), same batch" "DECISION FIRST (3 of 8): the supersession questions ADJ-V17-ENUM-1/2/3 — importing CognitionErrorV7, MemoryScopeV7 and RootAuthorityState as canonical creates a second seat for a domain that another registry already seats")
  :consumers ("V1.7 define-record field types (8 refs, dag.json): RightsMatrix/1.artifact_class (V1.7:127), RightsMatrix/1 dispositions (:130-131), RightsMatrix/1.legal_review_state (:134), NonAuthoritativeTranslation/1.reviewer_state (:225), ResolverQuery/1.input_kind (:151), CanonicalRetrievalView/1.available_formats (:177), RootAuthorityQualification/1.state (:243), MemoryScopePolicy/1.scope (:107)" "V1.7 define-invariant :V7I-RA-L-no-unlicensed (V1.7:139), :V7I-RA-R-proof-carrying-pages (:180), :V7I-RA-qual-revocable (:249) — DDI-4" "documents: LAWMAX-LICENSE-POLICY.md:6,11-15,30 (ArtifactRightsClass, RightsDisposition RA-L-1, LegalReviewState RA-L-2); V1.7-ROOT-AUTHORITY-ACCEPTANCE-MATRIX.md:3-4 (RootAuthorityState)" "CognitionErrorV7 is consumed by NOTHING: no field in any of the six registries has type CognitionErrorV7 (the cognition result still binds V1.6 CognitionError at V1.6:207) — an enum with zero consumers" "no tracked source/ or systems/ file names any record/enum id of the six registries (git grep at RO = 0); the only mechanical readers are the legacy audits/harness classified HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:436,440,444,450,453)")
  :identity-version-rule "MIXED. SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT in the FORWARD direction for 1: RootAuthorityState (V1.7:241, scalar, 6 members) is replaced by the V1.8 orthogonal product DimensionState x RelianceClass (V1.8:75,83; DFT-10, CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:43) — but RootAuthorityQualification/1, its only consumer, remains a live model `type` (interfaces-and-types.sexp:53). SUPERSEDING-BUT-UNADOPTED for 2: CognitionErrorV7 (V1.7:40) is declared as the typed failure taxonomy while the record it would type still binds V1.6 CognitionError (V1.6:207); MemoryScopeV7 (V1.7:105) is declared a replacement in a COMMENT (V1.7:104) while MemoryEvent/1 (V1.6:103) and MemoryProjection/1 (V1.6:295) are not re-typed. ONLY-VERSION for 5: ArtifactRightsClass, RightsDisposition, LegalReviewState, ResolverInputKind, RetrievalFormat — no same-name form elsewhere (my own grep; version-chains.md)."
  :migration-rule "MIXED and partly blocked. IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL for the 5 ONLY-VERSION enums (5 `enum` + 36 `enum-value` facts) once the family and module exist — they have exactly one seat, declared consumers and a document anchor each. BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION for CognitionErrorV7, MemoryScopeV7 and RootAuthorityState: each would be either IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL (retiring the other registry's enum) or IMPORT-AS-HISTORICAL-VERSION, and no source declares which."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "HIGH for 3 of 8. Cognition-error: V1.6:177 CognitionError (14 members, bound) vs V1.7:40 CognitionErrorV7 (15 members, unbound) — importing both gives two closed domains for one concept, which :V8I-03-one-seat (V1.8:20) forbids. Memory scope: V1.6:282 PublicMemoryScope + V1.6:288 MemoryScope vs V1.7:105 MemoryScopeV7 — three enums, one concept, two registries. Root-authority state: V1.7:241 RootAuthorityState vs V1.8:75/:83 DimensionState+RelianceClass — a scalar and a product for one state space. LOW for the other 5. No id collision with model facts: none of the 8 names is an id in the 14 modules (my own grep)."
  :requirement "NONE directly. The nearest model requirements are those of the consuming records' owners: R-V6-RESOLVE via req-map S25__FUTURE_BOOK_REVISION (requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:94, test RA-Q-RESOLVE), R-124 via S13__WP-12 (:79) and S15__WP-13 (:81), R-102 via S14__WP-11 (:80). The V1.7 RA-layer requirement ids (RA-L, RA-I, RA-R, RA-K, RA-T) are NOT model `requirement` facts (requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:5-28; orchestrator-notes.md N1/N8), so an enum imported under an RA requirement could not be L6-closed even if `enum` participated in L6."
  :invariant "L1 (nested value lists and keyword values cannot be imported verbatim, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6), L2 (one enum id), L3 (:enum ref closed). Source invariants: :V7I-RA-L-no-unlicensed (V1.7:139-143), :V7I-RA-qual-revocable (:249-253), :V7I-PUBPRIV-acyclic 'ZERO private-bearing enum' (:297-299) — the last one is the only law that would see MemoryScopeV7's private-bearing members, and it has no model implementation."
  :qualification-test "Existing: RA-Q-RESOLVE (`test` fact requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:44, bound by req-map S25__FUTURE_BOOK_REVISION :94) is the only model test in this area; the RA-layer tests RA-Q-CITE / RA-Q-DATASET / RA-Q-JURIS / RA-Q-LICENSE / RA-Q-RETRIEVE / RA-Q-TRANSLATE are NOT model `test` facts (orchestrator-notes.md N1/N7). NEW executable one-liner: every `field :domain` naming an enum resolves to a declared `enum`, AND every declared `enum` has at least one `field` that names it — the second half fails today for CognitionErrorV7 (zero consumers), which is the honest signal that importing it would add an orphan domain."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact enum-value RetrievalFormat__NOT_A_FORMAT :enum RetrievalFormatV9 :value NOT_A_FORMAT)` — both paths must reject: kernel-reason 'resolves to no declared enum', checker-reason 'L3'. REPLACE in the imported RightsMatrix/1 field `:domain RightsDisposition` with `:domain LegalReviewState` — must be rejected only if the model records which enum a field binds; if nothing rejects it, the field/domain binding is decorative and the finding must be reported. APPEND a second `(fact enum CognitionError ...)` beside CognitionErrorV7 with overlapping members — must be rejected by whatever one-seat rule the ADJ-V17-ENUM-1 decision installs; today L2 permits it (different ids), which is exactly why the decision cannot be deferred."
  :rollback "delete the imported facts of this class and the fact-type/enum declarations added to MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp for it, re-run build_root.py so ROOT.sexp re-pins the 14 modules (ROOT.sexp:12-27; L7), and restore the ledger row to DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT / AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE (deferred-imports.sexp) so the source file is authoritative again; the source registry is never edited by the import (V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp:256 'v1.5 files are NOT edited' is the precedent)"
  :batch-reason "DDI-2 because build_deferred.py maps define-closed-enum to DDI-2, materialised at deferred-imports.sexp:42. AGREES on the mechanical evidence: dag.json shows zero out-edges and a single in-edge from V1.7 define-record (8 refs) in the SAME batch, so nothing earlier depends on it and it depends on nothing. This is the cleanest batch placement in DDI-2 — the only tension is that 3 of its 8 forms carry cross-registry supersession questions that DDI-2 alone cannot settle."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "(a) Which single module seats all 41 DDI-2 enums (ADJ-DDI2-ENUM-SEAT)? (b) Does `enum` require :owner-subsystem — noting that NO V1.7 enum has a declared owner, so a required field would block the whole class? (c) Which cognition-error enum is canonical (V1.6:177 vs V1.7:40) and which memory-scope enum (V1.6:282/288 vs V1.7:105)? (d) Is RootAuthorityState retired by DFT-10 (V1.8:75,83) or kept as the domain of the still-live RootAuthorityQualification/1 (interfaces-and-types.sexp:53)?"
  :adjudication-items ("ADJ-DDI2-ENUM-SEAT: the four DDI-2 enum classes (V1.5 16 enums/83 values, V1.6 8/71, V1.7 8/61, V1.8 9/37 — my own reader over the six registries) must share ONE module (one seat per concept); the dossiers disagree — V1.5/V1.6 propose interfaces-and-types.sexp, V1.7/V1.8 propose a NEW 'enums' module. No winner is picked here." "ADJ-V17-ENUM-1 (V1.7 dossier): CognitionError (V1.6:177, bound by CognitionResult/1.errors V1.6:207) vs CognitionErrorV7 (V1.7:40, bound by nothing)." "ADJ-V17-ENUM-2 (V1.7 dossier): PublicMemoryScope/MemoryScope (V1.6:282,288) vs MemoryScopeV7 (V1.7:105, replacement declared only in the comment at V1.7:104) while MemoryEvent/1 and MemoryProjection/1 are not re-typed." "ADJ-V17-ENUM-3 (V1.7 dossier): RootAuthorityState (scalar, V1.7:241) vs DimensionState x RelianceClass (V1.8:75,83, DFT-10) — retire or keep as a projection domain?" "ADJ-DDI2-ENUM-OWNER: no V1.7 enum declares an owner; if `enum` mirrors `type` (:owner-subsystem required, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:148-152) the class is unimportable as-is." "ADJ-DDI2-PRIVATE-ENUM (shared): MemoryScopeV7's :USER_PRIVATE/:SERVICE_INTERNAL members sit inside an enum used by a public memory policy, against :V7I-PUBPRIV-acyclic (V1.7:297-299), and the model has no law that can see it.")
  :topological-position 23 :atomic-groups (4)
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "NOT-APPLICABLE" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE (deftype member types, source/version-graph.lisp:148-149 deftype legal-date / legal-instant; CognitionErrorV7 = names of a condition taxonomy)" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE (RetrievalFormat content negotiation is dispatch on the REPRESENTATION protocol already built: source/corpus-service.lisp:44-70 representation-class + define-representation, :serialize generic — the enum names its media types, the protocol dispatches)" :condition-restart "CognitionErrorV7 members (V1.7:40-43 'typed failure — never a guess, never a silent forced winner') as typed conditions in the S04 seat; ResolverInputKind ambiguity => typed AmbiguityResult/1, never a guess (V7I-RA-I-deterministic V1.7:166-169) | invariant: every error a typed condition (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:24) | fallback: return typed error value (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:24)" :macro-dsl "as class 1 | invariant: compile-time expansion only (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:25) | fallback: hand-written deftype + constant list" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE as owner (RetrievalFormat values are keys of the representation protocol, source/corpus-service.lisp:55-70)" :package-asdf-boundary "MemoryScopeV7 -> orchestrator.memory (source/memory.lisp:24) if canonical for S19 (vs class 6); rights enums -> S25 (SEAT-CANONICAL-URIS AM/seats.sexp:62) or the RIGHTS_LICENSE DOCUMENT seat (V1.8:248); ResolverInputKind -> orchestrator.uris (source/canonical-uris.lisp:12); RootAuthorityState -> S14 | invariant: package boundary = capability boundary (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:31) | fallback: monolith package (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:31)" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE (RootAuthorityState is a scalar superseded by the V1.8 DimensionState x RelianceClass product whose projection is dependency-directed — class 16)" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE" :compile-time-validation "as class 1; plus a build-time proof that no PUBLIC record binds BOTH a V1.6 and a V1.7 taxonomy for one field (CognitionResult/1.errors V1.6:207 vs CognitionErrorV7; MemoryEvent/1.scope V1.6:103 vs MemoryScopeV7) — a one-seat check the constitution demands (:no-duplicate) | invariant: one seat per concept (RA-I-5 V1.7:26-28) | fallback: runtime check (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:32)" :runtime-validation "`typep` at decode (as class 1); RightsDisposition :RIGHTS_UNKNOWN and LegalReviewState gate redistribution fail-closed (V7I-RA-L-no-unlicensed V1.7:139-142) | invariant: absent proof => RIGHTS_UNKNOWN, no redistribution | fallback: reject" :python-in-cl-risk "LOW. Flat symbol lists; the only naive hazards are keyword rendering (N12) and treating CognitionErrorV7 as a string list instead of a condition class hierarchy. CL-native: deftype per enum + typed conditions for the error taxonomy; enum-value facts with ordinal." :future-freedom "YES — flagged (duplicates). CognitionErrorV7 (S04) and MemoryScopeV7 (S19) each compete with a V1.6 enum bound by canonical records (ADJ-V17-ENUM-1/2); importing both fixes two seats for one concept in the cognition and memory subsystems until adjudicated. RetrievalFormat names FORMATS (HTML/JSON-LD/RDF_ELI/AKOMA_NTOSO/PROOF_BUNDLE, V1.7:172) — formats are contract meanings, replaceable behind the representation protocol (source/corpus-service.lisp:44-70), so no tool lock. ResolverInputKind closes S25's input grammar by design (deterministic grammar, V7I-RA-I). No V8I-02 effect.")
  )

(ddi-class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-record
  :batch DDI-2 :source-file "V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp" :fact-class "define-record" :source-count 25 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms (("NormalizedDocument/1" :line 45 :sha16 "53d1c035e54df271") ("SegmentSequence/1" :line 48 :sha16 "5c340b38b5dbe85c") ("TokenStream/1" :line 51 :sha16 "eef26abb85469a5a") ("ReferenceGraph/1" :line 54 :sha16 "6a6081a5638b56fa") ("LegalEntityGraph/1" :line 58 :sha16 "7a6fe67070fde33a") ("LegalSemanticAlternativeSet/1" :line 62 :sha16 "fe36dc2931cf1356") ("InterpretiveProfileEvaluation/1" :line 66 :sha16 "2d6ef45eb8eb7913") ("ClarificationDecision/1" :line 70 :sha16 "917313b79dc4fe1c") ("ClarifiedInterpretation/1" :line 75 :sha16 "5dcd35b01276208f") ("MemoryScopePolicy/1" :line 106 :sha16 "cf36597b43489f5b") ("RightsMatrix/1" :line 126 :sha16 "19b6c2ce5e368c43") ("LicensePolicy/1" :line 135 :sha16 "6105268b5fd5fb35") ("ResolverQuery/1" :line 150 :sha16 "e0d07ab93e3ca2df") ("AmbiguityResult/1" :line 153 :sha16 "0772c200e04c6431") ("ResolverResult/1" :line 155 :sha16 "6c03d4ba169d040f") ("ResolverReceipt/1" :line 163 :sha16 "5972f6ab35e1f6a2") ("CanonicalRetrievalView/1" :line 173 :sha16 "abe84e25194005a5") ("CitationPanel/1" :line 188 :sha16 "2d4fc993ccb51d00") ("CitationSupremacyMetric/1" :line 191 :sha16 "54601bda9d262b35") ("DatasetSnapshot/1" :line 205 :sha16 "11f101b79edf5ef5") ("DatasetDelta/1" :line 209 :sha16 "41573efed064cc5d") ("AnonymizationReceipt/1" :line 218 :sha16 "27c7152d6141de60") ("NonAuthoritativeTranslation/1" :line 222 :sha16 "19beb942f65207de") ("TenantProfile/1" :line 227 :sha16 "c96b903a3abb1590") ("RootAuthorityQualification/1" :line 242 :sha16 "49ca27b2fa9cb9af"))
  :source-file "V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp"
  :source-forms 25
  :current-authority-seat "V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp sections 1-9: §1 'TYPE-CORRECT COGNITION DAG (C-2)' (header L30) NormalizedDocument/1 L45, SegmentSequence/1 L48, TokenStream/1 L51, ReferenceGraph/1 L54, LegalEntityGraph/1 L58, LegalSemanticAlternativeSet/1 L62, InterpretiveProfileEvaluation/1 L66, ClarificationDecision/1 L70, ClarifiedInterpretation/1 L75; §2 (L103) MemoryScopePolicy/1 L106; §3 (L120) RightsMatrix/1 L126, LicensePolicy/1 L135; §4 (L144) ResolverQuery/1 L150, AmbiguityResult/1 L153, ResolverResult/1 L155, ResolverReceipt/1 L163; §5 (L171) CanonicalRetrievalView/1 L173; §6 (L187) CitationPanel/1 L188, CitationSupremacyMetric/1 L191; §7 (L204) DatasetSnapshot/1 L205, DatasetDelta/1 L209; §8 (L217) AnonymizationReceipt/1 L218, NonAuthoritativeTranslation/1 L222, TenantProfile/1 L227; §9 (L240) RootAuthorityQualification/1 L242. ISR declares a competing :seat string for 13 of them ('V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp §n', ISR:76-102). Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:48 (DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE, DDI-2, :source-count 25)."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "SPLIT as for every record class: identity is already in interfaces-and-types.sexp for 14 of the 25; the FIELD structure has no seat and must land in the ONE module chosen for all four DDI-2 record classes (ADJ-DDI2-FIELD-SEAT; the V1.7 dossier proposes NEW 'record-fields', the V1.5/V1.6 dossiers propose interfaces-and-types.sexp). The 11 records with no ISR row cannot get a `type` fact in ANY module until an owner exists (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:148-152)."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "EXISTING `type` for identity (14 present: interfaces-and-types.sexp:18,52,33,48,6,50,49,11,15,22,7,38,59,53) + 11 new `type` facts + a NEW `field` fact type. flattening rule: keep the existing `type` fact as the record identity; one `field` fact per (:name :type T) entry (id = <record>__<field>, :record <type-id> :name <field> :ordinal <n> :type-token <T> :list YES/NO :nullable YES/NO :domain <enum-id or type-id or primitive-id>); (list X) -> :list YES, (or X null) -> :nullable YES, (member ...) -> an anonymous enum id <record>__<field>__MEMBERS with enum-value facts; primitive tokens (id semver ref sha256 sig instant text ...) need a `primitive` fact family or an explicit exemption from L3 (V5-A8 / A20 / ADJ-V17-REC-5) Cardinality by my own reader: 227 `field` facts over 25 records — the largest single flattening in DDI-2 — including 33 `(list X)` fields, 21 `(or X null)` fields and 18 inline `(member ...)` sets. TenantProfile/1 alone carries 7 inline member sets (V1.7:227-239), most of them constant `:false` guarantees; encoding a one-member domain as an enum or as a literal is a decision that changes what a falsifier can mutate. primitive type tokens are defined in NONE of the six registries (V1.5-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh:227 and V1.6-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh:151-152 hard-code them as `prim`). no `enum`/`enum-value`/`field`/`primitive`/`cardinality`/`ref-class`/`adapter`/`canonical-identity` fact type exists among the 34 fact types (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:84-288); `define-enum` there is schema syntax for the model's own closed domains only (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:18,47-76); L1 forbids keywords, nested lists and NIL as values (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6) and the closed field set forbids adding keys to `type` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:9-13,148-152)"
  :owner "MIXED — 14 declared, 11 UNKNOWN. DECLARED (ISR and model agree): S04 ClarifiedInterpretation/1 (ISR:117; interfaces-and-types.sexp:18), S25 RightsMatrix/1 (ISR:87; :52), S25 LicensePolicy/1 (ISR:89; :33), S25 ResolverQuery/1 (ISR:77; :48), S25 AmbiguityResult/1 (ISR:81; :6), S25 ResolverResult/1 (ISR:79; :50), S25 ResolverReceipt/1 (ISR:83; :49), S13 CanonicalRetrievalView/1 (ISR:85; :11), S15 CitationSupremacyMetric/1 (ISR:91; :15), S14 DatasetSnapshot/1 (ISR:93; :22), S07 AnonymizationReceipt/1 (ISR:95; :7), S16 NonAuthoritativeTranslation/1 (ISR:97; :38), S26 TenantProfile/1 (ISR:99; :59), S14 RootAuthorityQualification/1 (ISR:101; :53). UNKNOWN (11): NormalizedDocument/1, SegmentSequence/1, TokenStream/1, ReferenceGraph/1, LegalEntityGraph/1, LegalSemanticAlternativeSet/1, InterpretiveProfileEvaluation/1, ClarificationDecision/1 (8 cognition intermediates), MemoryScopePolicy/1, CitationPanel/1, DatasetDelta/1 — no ISR row and no owner field anywhere. For DatasetDelta/1 the only named owner is TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:353 (S14), a document that is NOT one of the six migration sources; for CitationPanel/1 the section implies S15 (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:81) and nothing states it. UNKNOWN is the honest value."
  :writer "MIXED. Declared through stores for 4: DatasetSnapshot/1 -> dataset-distribution writer SEAT-RA-T-SIGNER (stores-and-authorities.sexp:7), ResolverResult/1 + ResolverQuery/1 + ResolverReceipt/1 -> resolver-dataset writer SEAT-NO-WRITER (:11), CanonicalRetrievalView/1 -> static-site writer SEAT-NO-WRITER (:12), TenantProfile/1 -> tenant-profile writer SEAT-NO-WRITER (:13). UNKNOWN for the rest: no store, and no registry names a writer. NOT 'NO_WRITER' — an absent store is not a declared absence of a writer, and the model distinguishes the two (SEAT-NO-WRITER seats.sexp:99-100 exists precisely so that 'none' is declared rather than assumed)."
  :classification "MIXED — private member named: TenantProfile/1 (V1.7:227 ':status :INTERFACE_ONLY :public-dependency nil'; ISR:99-100; model `type` :classification PRIVATE interfaces-and-types.sexp:59; owner S26 PRIVATE/DEFER_PRIVATE subsystems.sexp:30; seat SEAT-TENANT-PROFILE INTERFACE_ONLY seats.sexp:97-98) — it is one of the 6 members of PF-L5-PRIVATE-TYPE-LEAK (verification-corpus.sexp:45-47) and correctly has zero `consumes` edges. 13 are PUBLIC model types. 11 are UNCLASSIFIED — not PUBLIC by default: MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:48-49 and the L5 kernel (KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:239-247) treat an undecidable kind as a TYPED FAILURE, never as 'non-public by default', so importing an unclassified record is structurally impossible, not merely untidy."
  :dependencies ("SCHEMA FIRST: NEW `field` fact type (+ primitive family or L3 exemption) and a schema-version bump (X74-X76 verification-corpus.sexp:354-370)" "SAME BATCH, STRICTLY FIRST: V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum — 8 field :domain refs (dag.json 'V1.7 define-record -> V1.7 define-closed-enum', 8 refs)" "ISR EXTENSION (IMPORTED class): 11 records have no ISR row against :ISR-V6-closure (ISR:177-180) — reference kind: closure obligation on an already-imported class" "EXISTING model facts: the 14 `type` facts and their `consumes` edges (dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:23-124) — identity ref targets" "DECISION FIRST: owner for 11 records; ClarifiedInterpretation/1's divergent twin (V1.8:40); the coexisting predecessor/successor pairs (CitationSupremacyMetric/1 vs CitationMetricV8/1; RootAuthorityQualification/1 vs RootAuthorityStatus/1)")
  :consumers ("V1.7 define-construction-order cognition-stage-dag-v7 (V1.7:80, DDI-1) — 9 refs; V1.8 define-cognition-node-types (V1.8:363, DDI-3) — 9 refs" "V1.7 define-ra-closure-roots (V1.7:290, DDI-1) — 7 refs; V1.8 define-ra-closure-roots (V1.8:259, DDI-1) — 5 refs" "SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-subsystem (IMPORTED) — 5 refs; ISR define-interface (IMPORTED) — 3 refs (ISR:110 RootAuthorityStatus/1 -> V1.7:242; ISR:136 ResolutionRecord/1 -> V1.7:155)" "V1.8 define-canonical-identity (DDI-1) — 3 refs (V1.8:430 -> V1.7:155; :431 -> V1.7:205; :432 -> V1.7:126); V1.8 define-reference (DDI-2) — 3 refs (V1.8:350,351,352)" "V1.7 define-capability-seat (DDI-1) — 1 ref (V1.7:352 :RIGHTS_LICENSE -> V1.7:126 RightsMatrix/1); V1.8 define-capability-seat (DDI-1) — 1 ref (V1.8:248); V1.7 define-pipeline (DDI-1) — 1 ref; V1.7 define-invariant (DDI-4) — 1 ref" "no tracked source/ or systems/ file names any record/enum id of the six registries (git grep at RO = 0); the only mechanical readers are the legacy audits/harness classified HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:436,440,444,450,453)")
  :identity-version-rule "MIXED, four ways. SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT (1, same name same version): ClarifiedInterpretation/1 — V1.7:75-79 (9 fields, selected_alternative_ref mandatory) vs V1.8:40-46 (11 fields, selected_alternative_ref nullable, merged_result_ref and input_provenance_refs added, merge_semantics typed by MergeSemanticsV8); ISR:117 names 'V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp §1' as the seat; both classes are DDI-2 AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE (deferred-imports.sexp:48 and :66). SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT under a NEW NAME (2): CitationSupremacyMetric/1 (V1.7:191) -> CitationMetricV8/1 (V1.8:179, comment 'supersedes'); RootAuthorityQualification/1 (V1.7:242) -> RootAuthorityStatus/1 (V1.8:76). In BOTH pairs the model keeps the predecessor AND the successor as live `type` facts (interfaces-and-types.sexp:15 and :14; :53 and :54) and ISR keeps both rows (ISR:91,154; ISR:101,110) while ISR:112 calls the v1.7 record the ROLLBACK of the v1.8 one. LIVE-REFERENCE-TARGET (3): ResolverResult/1 (V1.7:155), DatasetSnapshot/1 (V1.7:205), RightsMatrix/1 (V1.7:126) are the :canonical-file+:locator targets of V1.8:350, :351, :352 — importing their structure moves the pointer target out of V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp. ONLY-VERSION (19): the rest."
  :migration-rule "MIXED. MERGE-INTO-EXISTING-FACT for the 13 PUBLIC records whose `type` fact exists and whose identity is uncontested — add `field` facts to the existing identity. BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION for ClarifiedInterpretation/1 (which field set?), CitationSupremacyMetric/1 and RootAuthorityQualification/1 (retire, keep as rollback, or merge?), and for all 11 unseated records (owner + ISR). For TenantProfile/1 the fields may be importable only under the private-field policy question raised by V1.8:280 ('closure contains ZERO :DEFERRED_PRIVATE record') — see ADJ-V18-REC-3, which applies here too because TenantProfile/1 is INTERFACE_ONLY/PRIVATE."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "HIGHEST in DDI-2. (1) ClarifiedInterpretation/1 has TWO define-record seats with the same name and the same :version '1' and different field sets (V1.7:75 vs V1.8:40) — importing either without retiring the other is a duplicate source of truth under :V6I-REF-single-source-of-truth (V1.6:158-162) and :V8I-03-one-seat (V1.8:20); importing both is impossible under L2 (one id, one fact — MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:106-107, KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:124). (2) The model ALREADY carries both members of two predecessor/successor pairs as live types; adding fields to both would make the duplication structural rather than nominal. (3) MemoryScopePolicy/1 (V1.7:106) is a second memory-policy seat beside MemoryPolicy/1 (V1.6:289, ISR:47, interfaces-and-types.sexp:35). (4) CitationPanel/1 is referenced by BOTH metric records (V1.7:193 and V1.8:180) but defined only here and registered nowhere — a referenced-but-undefined contract, which ISR:177-180 declares an architecture-gate FAIL."
  :requirement "Partial, via owners: R-V6-RESOLVE/RA-Q-RESOLVE via S25__FUTURE_BOOK_REVISION (requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:94), R-124/Q16 via S13__WP-12 (:79), R-124/Q42 via S15__WP-13 (:81), R-102/Q27 via S14__WP-11 (:80), R-51/Q06 via S07__WP-09 (:73), R-132/Q29 via S16__WP-01 (:82), R-V6-TENANT/RA-Q-TENANT via S26__DEFERRED (:95), R-129/Q08 via S04__WP-08 (:70). The 11 unseated records have NO requirement path at all and cannot acquire one until they have an owner (req-map :subsystem is a closed ref, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:178-181). The RA-layer requirement ids named by V1.7 (RA-I, RA-L, RA-R, RA-K, RA-T, RA-J, RA-E) are not model `requirement` facts (orchestrator-notes.md N1/N8)."
  :invariant "L1 (nested field lists, keywords, `(or X null)` cannot be values — MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6), L2 (ClarifiedInterpretation/1 cannot be two facts), L3 (:record and :domain refs closed; the 11 unseated records make the DDI-1 cognition-order refs dangle today), L5 (TenantProfile/1 PRIVATE; the 11 unclassified records fail CLOSED by design, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:48-49), L6 (no requirement path for 11 records). Source invariants: :ISR-V6-closure (ISR:177-180), :V6I-REF-single-source-of-truth (V1.6:158-162), :V7I-OWN-single-writer (V1.7:337-341), :V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality (V1.8:47-51 — which contradicts V1.7:77)."
  :qualification-test "Existing model `test` facts reachable via owners: Q16 (:33), Q42 (:39), Q27 (:37), Q06 (:31), Q29 (:38), Q08 (:32), RA-Q-RESOLVE (:44), RA-Q-TENANT (:45). All design-only/UNEXECUTED (orchestrator-notes.md N7). NEW executable one-liner: no two `field` facts share (:record, :name) AND every `type` that any DDI-1 construction-order or closure-root fact names resolves to a declared `type` — the second half is the check that would have caught the 11 unseated records before DDI-1 imported the orders that reference them."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact type ClarifiedInterpretation/1 :classification PUBLIC :owner-subsystem S04)` a second time — must be rejected as 'duplicate seat TYPE ClarifiedInterpretation/1' (L2, KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:124); this is the falsifier that makes the V1.7/V1.8 twin structurally undecidable rather than silently last-write-wins. APPEND `(fact field NormalizedDocument/1__doc_id :record NormalizedDocument/1 :name doc_id :ordinal 1 :domain id)` while NormalizedDocument/1 is not a declared `type` — both paths must reject: kernel-reason 'resolves to no declared type', checker-reason 'L3'. APPEND `(fact consumes S13__TenantProfile/1 :consumer S13 :provides TenantProfile/1)` — must be rejected as 'public/private leak: PUBLIC S13 consumes PRIVATE type TenantProfile/1' (FX-L5-PUBLIC-PRIVATE-LEAK verification-corpus.sexp:34-35)."
  :rollback "delete the imported facts of this class and the fact-type/enum declarations added to MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp for it, re-run build_root.py so ROOT.sexp re-pins the 14 modules (ROOT.sexp:12-27; L7), and restore the ledger row to DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT / AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE (deferred-imports.sexp) so the source file is authoritative again; the source registry is never edited by the import (V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp:256 'v1.5 files are NOT edited' is the precedent)"
  :batch-reason "DDI-2 because build_deferred.py maps define-record to DDI-2, materialised at deferred-imports.sexp:48. DISAGREES, decisively, in the 'too late' direction: SEVEN classes of EARLIER rank reference it — ISR define-interface (IMPORTED, 3 refs), SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-subsystem (IMPORTED, 5), V1.7 define-construction-order (DDI-1, 9), V1.7 define-ra-closure-roots (DDI-1, 7), V1.8 define-ra-closure-roots (DDI-1, 5), V1.8 define-canonical-identity (DDI-1, 3), V1.7/V1.8 define-capability-seat (DDI-1, 1+1), V1.7 define-pipeline (DDI-1, 1) — every one is listed as an order violation in dag.json. The model already contains DDI-1-bound facts whose ref targets are these records' identities; DDI-1 cannot be L3-closed for the 11 unseated ones no matter what DDI-2 does. Its own out-edge is a single same-batch edge to V1.7 define-closed-enum. The evidence says: record IDENTITIES belong in DDI-1, record FIELDS in DDI-2."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "(a) ClarifiedInterpretation/1: which of the two same-name, same-version field sets is canonical (V1.7:75-79 vs V1.8:40-46), given ISR:117 points at V1.8 and both ledger rows say AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE? (b) CitationSupremacyMetric/1 vs CitationMetricV8/1 and RootAuthorityQualification/1 vs RootAuthorityStatus/1: retire the predecessor, keep it as the declared rollback (ISR:112), or merge? (c) Who owns the 11 records with no ISR row, and is ISR extended before DDI-1's construction orders and closure roots are allowed to reference them? (d) MemoryScopePolicy/1 vs MemoryPolicy/1 — one memory-policy seat or two? (e) Are the fields of the PRIVATE TenantProfile/1 imported into the public model at all?"
  :adjudication-items ("ADJ-DDI2-FIELD-SEAT: the four DDI-2 record classes (V1.5 18/181 fields, V1.6 22/190, V1.7 25/227, V1.8 19/179 — my own count) must share ONE `field` seat; the dossiers propose interfaces-and-types.sexp (V1.5/V1.6) vs a NEW module 'record-fields'/'schemas' (V1.7/V1.8). No winner is picked here." "ADJ-V17-REC-1 (V1.7 dossier): 11 V1.7 records are absent from ISR although :ISR-V6-closure (ISR:177-180) demands definition there exactly once with an owner, and V1.8 binds 8 of them as cognition node types." "ADJ-V17-REC-2 / ADJ-V18-REC-1: ClarifiedInterpretation/1 defined twice with the same version and different fields (V1.7:75 vs V1.8:40)." "ADJ-V17-REC-3 / ADJ-V18-REC-2: CitationSupremacyMetric/1 vs CitationMetricV8/1 and RootAuthorityQualification/1 vs RootAuthorityStatus/1 — both members of each pair are live model types and live ISR rows." "ADJ-V17-REC-4: MemoryScopePolicy/1 (V1.7:106) overlaps MemoryPolicy/1 (V1.6:289, ISR:47, interfaces-and-types.sexp:35)." "ADJ-V17-REC-5 / A20: the field-type vocabulary (id semver ref sha256 sig instant uncertainty keyword url text mime span usc-id anchor scope duration) has NO definition seat in any registry — a `field :domain` cannot be L3-closed until a primitive seat exists." "ADJ-DDI2-CITATIONPANEL: CitationPanel/1 is referenced by V1.7:193 and V1.8:180 but defined only at V1.7:188 and registered in no registry — referenced-but-undefined, which ISR:177-180 calls an architecture-gate FAIL." "ADJ-DDI2-INLINE-MEMBER: 18 inline (member ...) sets in this class alone (7 of them in TenantProfile/1, V1.7:227-239) need a single encoding rule — anonymous enum ids or STRING literals — decided once for all four record classes.")
