  :source-file "V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp"
  :source-forms 1
  :current-authority-seat "V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp §16, form define-wp-reconciliation at :379-399 — 20 (:concept :wp :evidence) rows, 14 mapped to WP-02..WP-14 and 6 to FUTURE_IMPLEMENTATION_BOOK_PACKET_REQUIRED. Asserted by :V7I-WP-honest at :400-403. Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:51 (:source-count 1, DDI-4, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE). The form is ANONYMOUS — its second element is a row list, not a name (orchestrator-notes.md N11), so an id must be synthesised."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp (EXISTING) — the `wp` facts it references live there (rtw:52-65) and the competing subsystem-keyed view (`req-map`, rtw:67-95) is in the same module; a concept->WP family belongs beside them or the WP concept acquires a third home. CONDITIONAL on the seat ruling shared with classes 2 and 15."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "NEW `concept-wp` :id-space TOKEN-SPACE :required (concept wp) :optional (file evidence source-file source-line) :types ((concept SYMBOL) (wp SYMBOL) (file STRING) (evidence STRING) (source-file STRING) (source-line INTEGER)) :ref ((wp wp)). Flattening rule MANDATORY: the form is a nested list of 20 plists (V1.7:379-399), not an L1-legal value (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6) — 20 flat facts, ids synthesised <concept>__<wp> or define-wp-reconciliation__V1.7-SCHEMAS (orchestrator-notes.md N11 requires the convention be declared once for all 7 anonymous forms in the corpus). BLOCKER: 6 of 20 rows carry :wp FUTURE_IMPLEMENTATION_BOOK_PACKET_REQUIRED (V1.7:394-399), which is NOT a `wp` fact (0 hits in the 14 modules) — the :ref would dangle for 6 of 20 rows. The concept ids (COGNITION_DAG, NEURAL_PROPOSER, …) are facts of no type at all, so :concept must stay an untyped SYMBOL or a `concept` family must be minted."
  :owner "UNKNOWN — the form carries no owner; the dossier records 'none (cross-cutting WP map)' and TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:382 records the subsystem as 'cross'. The 20 rows span S02..S26. Not guessed."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — no store (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:155-158)."
  :classification "PUBLIC by content — a design map with no private payload. One row names a private concept (TENANT_PROFILES -> FUTURE, V1.7:397; S26 is PRIVATE, subsystems.sexp:30) but carries no private datum. No private member to isolate under L5."
  :dependencies ("DDI-4 sibling class 2 (define-wp-purpose) — 10 symbol references (dag.json 'V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp define-wp-reconciliation -> SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp define-wp-purpose': 10); an INTRA-BATCH ordering constraint the batch label does not express [wp reference]" "FIRST: the sentinel-token decision (FUTURE_IMPLEMENTATION_BOOK_PACKET_REQUIRED vs FUTURE_BOOK_REVISION vs DEFERRED vs FUTURE_BOOK) — 6 of 20 rows are unrepresentable until one token wins [enum/id dependency, shared with classes 2 and 15]" "FIRST: the anonymous-form id convention (orchestrator-notes.md N11) [id-space dependency]" "FIRST: the row-set ruling against V1.8:303-319 (16 rows) [one-seat dependency]" "EXISTING model facts: 10 of the 14 real WP tokens are `wp` facts (rtw:55-65) [reference targets available for 14 of 20 rows]")
  :consumers (":V7I-WP-honest (V1.7:400-403) — DDI-4 class 12, same batch" "legacy: V1.7-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, files-and-roles.sexp:444) reads the form; V1.8-VERIFY.py:29,404-409 loads V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp but per :1373-1375 only for record/reference forms" "CANONICAL MODEL: none — no concept-wp fact type; 0 hits for any concept id or for FUTURE_IMPLEMENTATION_BOOK_PACKET_REQUIRED in the 14 modules")
  :identity-version-rule "SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT — V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp:303-319 holds the successor with 16 rows, adding a :file key and rewriting every :evidence string to be literally grep-able (V1.8:302 'Each :evidence is a string the audit greps INSIDE the named WP-NN.md (real file open)'). FOUR concepts are DROPPED without a superseding note: BITEMPORAL_TWIN, RESOLVER_URIS, PUBLIC_RETRIEVAL_SITE, CONTENT_NEGOTIATION_SITEMAPS. Both classes remain AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE (deferred-imports.sexp:51 and :69), so nothing in the repository declares the V1.7 rows retired. Evidence quality also diverges: the dossier's per-row check finds 9 of the 14 V1.7 WP evidence strings are NOT literal in the named WP file (e.g. 'WP-08.md:19 Public Legal Discernment core' — the phrase occurs at WP-08.md:1, not :19; 'typed Legal IR' occurs 0 times in WP-03.md), while V1.8's 11 evidence strings all occur."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION — cannot be IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL while a divergent successor is equally authoritative; cannot be IMPORT-AS-HISTORICAL-VERSION until the row-set and token decisions are made; cannot be SKIP-WITH-PROOF because 4 concepts exist ONLY here and would be silently lost."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "CERTAIN — three seats for WP assignment (this concept-keyed map, define-wp-purpose's requirement-keyed :owns, and req-map's subsystem-keyed rows) plus a divergent successor of this very form. The three already disagree: LEGAL_IR -> WP-03 here and at V1.8:307, while the model maps LegalIR/1's owner S04 to WP-08 (rtw:70)."
  :requirement "UNKNOWN — no requirement id at source. TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:362 registers RA-C6 for the V1.7 WP reconciliation and :382 registers DFT-02/T8-WP for the V1.8 one; neither is a model `requirement` or `test` fact (rtw:5-50)."
  :invariant "L1 (the 20-row nested list is not a value — flattening mandatory), L3 (:wp must resolve to a declared wp; 6 of 20 rows cannot), L2 (synthesised ids), L6 (the WP end of the requirement->seat->test->WP chain). Source invariant: :V7I-WP-honest (V1.7:400-403), superseded by :V8I-WP-real (V1.8:320-323)."
  :qualification-test "NEW — QT-DDI4-WP-EVIDENCE-RESOLVES. Executable one-liner: `for every concept-wp fact with a :file and :evidence, open :file and require :evidence to occur in it (grep -F -q)` — exactly the check :V8I-WP-real (V1.8:320-323) describes and that no model check performs today. Run against the V1.7 rows it FAILS for 9 of 14; against the V1.8 rows it passes for all 11. That difference is the mechanical statement of which row set is grounded. No existing model `test` fact covers it (rtw:30-50)."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact concept-wp MEMORY_KERNEL__FUTURE :concept MEMORY_KERNEL :wp FUTURE_IMPLEMENTATION_BOOK_PACKET_REQUIRED)` — must be REJECTED: kernel-reason 'resolves to no declared wp', checker-reason 'L3' (precedent FX-L3-DANGLING-WP vc:30-31). This is the 6-of-20-rows blocker in one line. APPEND `(fact concept-wp MEMORY_KERNEL__WP-11 :concept MEMORY_KERNEL :wp WP-11)` — must be REJECTED by QT-DDI4-WP-EVIDENCE-RESOLVES and by the explicit clause 'MEMORY_KERNEL stays FUTURE… (never WP-11)' (V1.8:321-322). REPLACE a :evidence string with one absent from its :file — must be REJECTED by the same test; today no check would notice."
  :rollback "Delete the 20 concept-wp facts; remove the fact type from MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp and move :version (:37 / ROOT.sexp:9); re-run build_root.py; build_deferred.py restores deferred-imports.sexp:51. Coupled rollback: if class 15 (V1.8 rows) was imported in the same change, both must be rolled back together or the model keeps one half of a divergent pair."
  :batch-reason "DDI-4 because build_deferred.py:102 maps `define-wp-reconciliation` to DDI-4. AGREES on batch — its 10 out-edges point at a DDI-4 sibling (define-wp-purpose), so no earlier batch waits on it and dag.json records no order violation naming it as a target. But the batch label hides the real constraint: the class is unimportable until class 2 (same batch) and class 15 (same batch) are decided, i.e. DDI-4 contains an internal dependency chain 2 -> 13 -> 15 that no ledger field records."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "Which row set is canonical — V1.7's 20 rows (:379-399, line-referenced and 9-of-14 non-literal evidence) or V1.8's 16 rows (:303-319, literal grep-able evidence) — and what becomes of the 4 concepts that exist only in V1.7? Which of concept-wp / wp-purpose :owns / req-map is the seat of WP assignment? And which single token means 'no WP owns this'?"
  :adjudication-items ("ADJ-V17-WP-1 (V1.7 dossier): V1.7 20 rows vs V1.8 16 rows; V1.7 evidence locators are line-numbered and mostly non-literal" "ADJ-V17-WP-2 (V1.7 dossier) = A14-SR-FUTURE-TOKEN-NAMING = ADJ-V18-WP-1: four tokens for one disposition" "ADJ-MX4-ANON-ID (new, shared with class 15): 7 anonymous forms in the corpus (orchestrator-notes.md N11) need one declared id-synthesis convention before any of them can be imported" "ADJ-MX4-DDI4-INTERNAL-ORDER (new): DDI-4 has an internal dependency chain (class 2 -> classes 13/15 -> class 12/14) that the ledger's single :batch field cannot express")
  :topological-position 48 :atomic-groups ()
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "NEW `concept-wp` facts (:concept SYMBOL, :wp ref wp, :evidence STRING) hash-pinned — but this row set differs from V1.8 (20 vs 16 rows; BITEMPORAL_TWIN, RESOLVER_URIS, PUBLIC_RETRIEVAL_SITE, CONTENT_NEGOTIATION_SITEMAPS dropped without note — dossier ADJ-V18-WP-2) | invariant: :V7I-WP-honest (V1.7:400-403) | fallback: import V1.8 rows only (C15) and keep V1.7 as a rationale pointer" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart "NOT-APPLICABLE" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE" :package-asdf-boundary "NOT-APPLICABLE" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE" :compile-time-validation "L3: :wp must resolve to a declared `wp` fact — FUTURE_IMPLEMENTATION_BOOK_PACKET_REQUIRED is NOT one (model wp facts: DEFERRED, FUTURE_BOOK_REVISION, requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:52-53; SR:118 equates the tokens only in a comment); the V1.7 :evidence strings are line-referenced but 9 of 14 are not literal in the WP files (dossier ADJ-V17-WP-1) — they cannot be a grep obligation | invariant: :V7I-WP-honest 'a concept mapping to a WP whose evidence does not name it … flips the check' (V1.7:402-403) | fallback: none honest — the V1.7 rows are unverifiable as written" :runtime-validation "NOT-APPLICABLE" :python-in-cl-risk "YES — 20 rows as a JSON array of dicts, 'WP-08.md:19'-style locators parsed by regex, and a Python grep over WP-NN.md at build time (no such check exists today: grep 'WP-' over gate_checks.py finds none). CL-native alternative: `concept-wp` facts with L3 refs and the evidence obligation declared as a harness-bound check fact (pattern verification-corpus.sexp:122-137: harness + falsifier with :reason) executed by the ONE runner — never an inline loop in the generator." :future-freedom "SCHEDULE ONLY — MEMORY_KERNEL (V1.7:394), UNIFIED_RESOLVER, LICENSE_RIGHTS_MATRIX, CONTENT_NEGOTIATION_SITEMAPS, TENANT_PROFILES, ROOT_AUTHORITY_FLYWHEEL → FUTURE packet; COGNITION_DAG → WP-08 agrees with SR:47 and req-map S04__WP-08 (requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:70). LEGAL_IR → WP-03 (V1.7:383) vs LegalIR/1 owner S04 → WP-08 (req-map :70) is the keyed-by-concept vs keyed-by-subsystem disagreement (ADJ-V18-WP-3). No mechanism constraint on S04/S19/JTMS/S20.")
  )

(ddi-class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-invariant
  :batch DDI-4 :source-file "V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp" :fact-class "define-invariant" :source-count 23 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms ((":V8I-01-certifies-not-replaces" :line 14 :sha16 "aa3e7c03b7d8e73f") (":V8I-02-no-mandatory-model" :line 17 :sha16 "3a8dedd47a4fe98c") (":V8I-03-one-seat" :line 20 :sha16 "ce0c53b4c56fdf3a") (":V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality" :line 47 :sha16 "dba0f816daa79248") (":V8I-COGGRAPH-acyclic-except-resume" :line 66 :sha16 "48855a783534adb1") (":V8I-RASTATUS-product" :line 97 :sha16 "affef9a944cd46d4") (":V8I-EPOCH-one-expression" :line 128 :sha16 "8b9ef85ed1980d7c") (":V8I-CONT-separated" :line 149 :sha16 "05e3e522537189e2") (":V8I-CORR-privacy" :line 168 :sha16 "0f133b2167b2a20f") (":V8I-RA-K-tiered" :line 184 :sha16 "ed059e89fc71457b") (":V8I-SIDE-gdpr-honest" :line 200 :sha16 "7e6048e367de6026") (":V8I-MARK-separated" :line 212 :sha16 "81f2e0dd8f25469e") (":V8I-FROST-precise" :line 231 :sha16 "ab965078f976510a") (":V8I-CAP-real" :line 250 :sha16 "763534c8d8c9dc79") (":V8I-PUBPRIV-all-families" :line 277 :sha16 "407a8df54db4e90b") (":V8I-OWN-universal" :line 296 :sha16 "266efa1f30e9cc20") (":V8I-WP-real" :line 320 :sha16 "ecd1b36c6b864e0f") (":V8I-SYM-exact" :line 336 :sha16 "481f7627596db21f") (":V8I-XREF-real" :line 353 :sha16 "91b5846adca7fc5b") (":V8I-COG-typed-edges" :line 386 :sha16 "300a63df8a936099") (":V8I-XREF-identity" :line 433 :sha16 "11a82e28a0be0bf4") (":V8I-RA-DELTA-seats" :line 455 :sha16 "aad63e39c1b456da") (":V8I-SYM-structural" :line 459 :sha16 "9267530969beb559"))
  :source-file "V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp"
  :source-forms 23
  :current-authority-seat "V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp, one invariant closing each of sections 0-17: 3 root invariants :V8I-01/:V8I-02/:V8I-03 at :14,17,20 and 20 section invariants at :47,66,97,128,149,168,184,200,212,231,250,277,296,320,336,353,386,433,455,459 (full list classes.md row 50). Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:62 (:source-count 23, DDI-4, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE). No model fact carries any of these ids (grep of the 14 modules = 0). Note V1.8 is the CURRENT registry — two of its sibling classes are already IMPORTED (define-write-authority deferred-imports.sexp:70, define-pipeline :63) — so this class is deferred prose inside a file the model already treats as canonical for other classes."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "NEW:invariants.sexp — shared seat with classes 1/4/5/9/12. rationale-references.sexp is the pointer alternative; note the model already anchors RAT-PIPELINE at V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp (rationale-references.sexp:6, :anchor \"define-pipeline symbolic-only-path\"), so a V1.8 pointer style is already in use for a different class. Cost of a new module: a NEW *.sexp under ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/ is auto-classified CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT by classification-rule R-008 (classification-rules.sexp:39-41) and auto-pinned by build_root.py:57 (directory listing), so ROOT.sexp :module-count 14 (ROOT.sexp:12) becomes 15 and every module SHA is re-derived (law L7)."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "NEW `invariant` (as class 1) with :optional (audit supersedes status). Flattening rule: all 23 are docstring-only prose STRINGs, L1-legal; ids colon-stripped (keyword ids (`:V5I-01`, `:SR-V6-one-seat`, …) are not TOKEN-SPACE ids — TOKEN excludes ':' (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:41,17) — so a colon-stripping id-rendering convention must be declared once for all 92 define-invariant forms (orchestrator-notes.md N12)) to V8I-01-certifies-not-replaces … V8I-SYM-structural, all TOKEN-legal. WARNING on :audit — the V8-* audit ids (V8-SYM, V8-OWN, V8-XREF, V8-CLARIFY, V8-COGLIFE, V8-WP, V8-CAP, V8-RASTATUS, V8-RA-DELTAS) are implemented only in V1.8-VERIFY.py, HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:453) and NON_AUTHORITATIVE (LEGACY-AUDIT-DISPOSITION.md:1-6), so the same dangling-reference problem as class 12. A :supersedes field would be usable for 16 of 23 forms if — and only if — the predecessor invariants are imported too, which couples this class to classes 4, 9 and 12."
  :owner "UNKNOWN for all 23 — define-invariant carries no :owner in V1.8 and the dossier records 'UNKNOWN as a fact (define-invariant carries no :owner); section context only' for every form. Section context suggests S04 (:47 clarification, :66/:386 cognition), S14 (:97 RootAuthorityStatus), S25 (:128 citation URI, :212 mark), S11 (:149 continuity, :231 crypto), S18 (:168 correction), S15 (:184 metrics), S26 (:200 sidecar), S10 (:296 ownership) — inferences from section placement, none declared. Not asserted here."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — no store (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:155-158). :V8I-OWN-universal (V1.8:296-299) is ABOUT store writers; that does not give the invariant a writer."
  :classification "MIXED — private members named: :V8I-CORR-privacy (V1.8:168-172) is about RestrictedForensicRecord/1, a PRIVATE type (interfaces-and-types.sexp:51) owned by the PUBLIC S18 (subsystems.sexp:22 — itself an open question, ISR dossier A6); :V8I-SIDE-gdpr-honest (:200-204) is about SidecarSourceProfile/1, PRIVATE (interfaces-and-types.sexp:58); :V8I-PUBPRIV-all-families (:277-283) names the DEFERRED_PRIVATE / INTERFACE_ONLY / SPECIFICATION_ONLY families. The texts carry no private payload; the classification rule for governance prose about private subjects remains undeclared (ADJ-MX4-INV-CLASSIFICATION)."
  :dependencies ("DECISION: the shared invariant family + id rendering + one-seat policy (ADJ-MX4-INV-SEAT, ADJ-V18-INV-1) [schema dependency]" "DDI-3 V1.8-SCHEMAS define-cognition-graph — 1 ref; DDI-2 V1.8 define-record — 3 refs, define-closed-enum — 1 ref [class references, dag.json]" "IMPORTED ISR define-interface — 3 refs [satisfied]" "DDI-4 sibling SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-wp-purpose — 1 ref [intra-batch order]" "COUPLED: 16 of 23 forms restate an invariant seated in V1.6 / V1.7 / SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY (classes 9, 12, 4) — a :supersedes reference is only closable if those classes are imported too [intra-batch coupling]" "NOT AVAILABLE: the V8-* audit ids exist only in V1.8-VERIFY.py (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, files-and-roles.sexp:453) [dangling test vocabulary]")
  :consumers ("CANONICAL MODEL: none — 0 hits for any V8I-* id in the 14 modules; only the ledger row deferred-imports.sexp:62. The model DOES anchor a different V1.8 form: rationale RAT-PIPELINE (rationale-references.sexp:6) :anchor \"define-pipeline symbolic-only-path\", and that pipeline is exactly what :V8I-SYM-exact and :V8I-SYM-structural disagree about" "V1.8-SCHEMAS internal: :V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality (:47) asserts define-cardinality-table (:394, DDI-2) and the fixtures (:398, DDI-4 class 16); :V8I-WP-real (:320) asserts define-wp-reconciliation (:303, class 15); :V8I-RA-DELTA-seats (:455) asserts define-ra-delta-seats (:444, DDI-1); :V8I-SYM-exact/:V8I-SYM-structural assert define-pipeline (:326, IMPORTED)" "CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:33-38,43-44,66,83-85 restates several of them in prose (AUTHORED_NORMATIVE_PROSE)" "TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:382-398 registers DFT-* / T8-* rows for them; none is a model requirement/test fact (orchestrator-notes.md N1)" "legacy: V1.8-VERIFY.py (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, files-and-roles.sexp:453; NON_AUTHORITATIVE, LEGACY-AUDIT-DISPOSITION.md:1-6)")
  :identity-version-rule "SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT is the wrong label for 3 of these and the right one for 16. 16 forms RESTATE an invariant seated in V1.6 / V1.7 / SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY with a changed claim (chains listed in ADJ-V18-INV-1); 7 are ONLY-VERSION (:V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality :47, :V8I-EPOCH-one-expression :128, :V8I-CONT-separated :149, :V8I-CORR-privacy :168, :V8I-SIDE-gdpr-honest :200, :V8I-XREF-real :353, :V8I-XREF-identity :433). And TWO are in INTERNAL CONTRADICTION with a sibling in the SAME FILE: :V8I-SYM-exact (:336-341, 'SEMANTICALLY EQUIVALENT', 4th mutation named proposer-removal-inequivalence, also at define-pipeline :335) versus :V8I-SYM-structural (:459-464, 'does NOT claim behavioral SEMANTIC equivalence', mutation proposer-removal-structural-inequivalence) — and V1.8:19 plus CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:36-38 still say semantic. A second internal contradiction: :V8I-COGGRAPH-acyclic-except-resume (:66-71) says audit V8-COGLIFE has 3 witnesses while :V8I-COG-typed-edges (:386-391) says the same audit runs 7. Neither contradiction is between versions; both are inside one registry, so no supersession rule resolves them."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION — and, uniquely in DDI-4, blocked by contradictions INSIDE the source file rather than only across files. No import policy (latest-only, all-as-history, pointer-only) resolves :V8I-SYM-exact vs :V8I-SYM-structural or the 3-vs-7 witness count, because both members of each pair are 'latest'. After the rulings: 7 ONLY-VERSION forms would be IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL; 16 would be IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL with their predecessors becoming IMPORT-AS-HISTORICAL-VERSION under a latest-only policy."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "HIGHEST in DDI-4, four-fold. (i) 16 forms restate an invariant seated elsewhere and the model already anchors two of those chains at SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp (rationale-references.sexp:4-5), i.e. the model has de facto chosen SR, not V1.8. (ii) Two internal contradictions (SYM semantic-vs-structural; COGLIFE 3-vs-7 witnesses). (iii) :V8I-RA-DELTA-seats says exactly SEVEN RA deltas and that FROST is NOT one (:455-458), while TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:391-398 registers EIGHT RA8-* rows including RA8-FROST (:398) and its own balance line (:400) says seven; TRACEABILITY:394 additionally cites an invariant :V8I-JURNS-namespace that does not exist in V1.8 (grep NOT FOUND). (iv) :V8I-FROST-precise (:231) describes a suite registry and policy epochs that MACHINE-LEGAL-TRUST-PROTOCOL.md:1349,1360-1368 already seats — so CryptoSuiteRegistry/1 and RecoveryEpoch/1 (both already model types, interfaces-and-types.sexp:21,45) may be second seats of an MLTP concept."
  :requirement "UNKNOWN / NEW — no requirement id is attached to any form. The V1.8 RA-layer requirement ids (RA8-CONT RA8-CORR RA8-EPOCH RA8-JURNS RA8-K RA8-MARK RA8-SIDE, plus RA8-FROST in TRACEABILITY only) appear in define-ra-delta-seats (V1.8:444-451, DDI-1) and in TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:391-398; NONE is a model `requirement` fact (rtw:5-28) — orchestrator-notes.md N1. L6 closure is unavailable for this class until the requirement universe question is settled."
  :invariant "L1 (prose strings legal, keyword ids not), L2 (one id per fact type; the 16 restatements are an L2 question at concept level), L3 (:supersedes and :audit references), L5 (:V8I-PUBPRIV-all-families names EIGHT edge families while the model's L5 covers only `consumes` — MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:164-170), L6 (no requirement/test ids resolve), L7 (module universe). Source: the 23 forms ARE the invariants."
  :qualification-test "NEW — QT-DDI4-INV-NO-INTERNAL-CONTRADICTION. Executable one-liner: `for every pair of invariant facts with the same :source-file that name the same :audit id, assert their claims are not mutually exclusive — concretely, assert a single declared mutation-count and witness-count per audit id across all invariants citing it`. Run over V1.8 today it FAILS twice: V8-COGLIFE witnesses 3 (:70-71) vs 7 (:389-391), and V8-SYM equivalence semantic (:339) vs structural (:462). That is the intended signal; no existing model `test` fact covers it (rtw:30-50) and the only executor of V8-* audits is NON_AUTHORITATIVE (LEGACY-AUDIT-DISPOSITION.md:1-6)."
  :falsifier "APPEND both `(fact invariant V8I-SYM-exact :audit V8-SYM :mutation-count 4 :equivalence SEMANTIC …)` and `(fact invariant V8I-SYM-structural :audit V8-SYM :mutation-count 4 :equivalence STRUCTURAL …)` — must be REJECTED by QT-DDI4-INV-NO-INTERNAL-CONTRADICTION, reason 'two invariants give audit V8-SYM incompatible equivalence claims'. APPEND `(fact invariant V8I-RA-DELTA-seats :delta-count 7 …)` while eight RA8-* requirement facts exist — must be REJECTED by a count-agreement check against the requirement universe. APPEND `(fact invariant V8I-COG-typed-edges :audit V8-COGLIFE :witnesses 7 …)` alongside `:V8I-COGGRAPH-acyclic-except-resume :witnesses 3` — must be REJECTED for the same reason. REPLACE `:status ACTIVE` with `:status :ACTIVE` — must be REJECTED, checker-reason 'MALFORMED-FACT' (X27 vc:172-174)."
  :rollback "Delete the 23 facts and adjust UF-INVARIANT; remove the fact type/enums from MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp and move :version (:37 / ROOT.sexp:9); delete invariants.sexp and re-run build_root.py; build_deferred.py restores deferred-imports.sexp:62. Coupled: if a latest-only policy retired the V1.6/V1.7/SR predecessors, rolling this class back restores 16 chains to a state where no member is canonical — classes 4, 9, 12 and 14 must be rolled back as one unit."
  :batch-reason "DDI-4 because build_deferred.py:101 maps `define-invariant` to DDI-4. AGREES — its 9 recorded out-edges point at IMPORTED (3), DDI-2 (4), DDI-3 (1) and DDI-4 (1) classes and dag.json records no order violation naming this class as a target. Two caveats that the batch label hides: (a) two sibling classes of the SAME FILE are already IMPORTED (define-pipeline deferred-imports.sexp:63, define-write-authority :70) and one of them, define-pipeline, is the subject of the two contradictory SYM invariants — so the model already carries the artefact whose governing prose is deferred; (b) the class is coupled to classes 4, 9 and 12 by 16 restatement chains."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "Which of the two symbolic-only claims is canonical — SEMANTIC equivalence (:V8I-SYM-exact V1.8:336-341, V1.8:19, CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:36-38) or STRUCTURAL only (:V8I-SYM-structural V1.8:459-464) — given the model already anchors RAT-PIPELINE at that pipeline (rationale-references.sexp:6)? Does audit V8-COGLIFE run 3 witnesses (:70-71) or 7 (:389-391)? Are there seven RA deltas (:455-458) or eight RA8 requirements (TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:391-398)? And for the 16 restatement chains, is the seat the latest form (V1.8) or the form the model already anchors (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp, rationale-references.sexp:4-5)?"
  :adjudication-items ("ADJ-V18-INV-1 (V1.8 dossier): 16 of 23 restate an invariant seated in V1.6/V1.7/SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY; the model anchors two chains at SR, not at V1.8" "ADJ-V18-INV-2 (V1.8 dossier): :V8I-SYM-exact (semantic) vs :V8I-SYM-structural (structural) — internal contradiction, with CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:36-38 and V1.8:19 on the semantic side" "ADJ-V18-INV-3 (V1.8 dossier): V8-COGLIFE witness count 3 vs 7" "ADJ-V18-INV-4 (V1.8 dossier): seven deltas vs eight RA8 requirements; TRACEABILITY:394 cites a non-existent invariant :V8I-JURNS-namespace" "ADJ-V18-INV-5 (V1.8 dossier): prose seat vs mechanised law for :V8I-OWN-universal / :V8I-PUBPRIV-all-families, and whether L5's single family (consumes) suffices for V1.8's eight (V1.8:264-274)" "ADJ-V18-INV-6 (V1.8 dossier): CryptoSuiteRegistry/1 and RecoveryEpoch/1 as EXTEND of MLTP §14.1/§14.2 (MACHINE-LEGAL-TRUST-PROTOCOL.md:1349,1360-1368) or as second seats" "ADJ-MX4-INV-SEAT (new, shared): one module + one policy for the 92 invariant forms" "ADJ-MX4-PROSE-VS-LAW (new, shared with class 12)" "ADJ-MX4-INV-CLASSIFICATION (new, shared with classes 9 and 12)")
  :topological-position 52 :atomic-groups ()
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "hash-pinned anchor facts with a supersession chain; :V8I-EPOCH: every MultiCommitment carries ≥2 DISTINCT hash families with domain separation from FIRST publication (V1.8:132-133) — canon-sexp is the ONE serialization (journal.lisp:61-68) but sha256-hex (:88) is a SINGLE family, so a second family + domain separation is a NEW seat (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:34 'pin encoder'); :V8I-CORR: the chain verifies with 'content unavailable/withdrawn' without retaining withdrawn content (V1.8:173-174) — the hash stays, the body goes | invariant: :V8I-EPOCH 'the same versioned citation URI NEVER resolves to a different Expression' (V1.8:134-135) | fallback: keep prior version (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:27)" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart ":V8I-COGGRAPH / :V8I-COG-typed-edges: SUSPEND→RESUME binds the EXACT suspended instance (resume_binding_ref V1.8:38, 384-385) — the CL-native form of a suspended cognition is a restart established at CLARIFY-DECIDE whose resume restart takes the ClarificationResponse (pattern legal-ast.lisp:1604-1613 restart-case with named restarts); the ClarificationLifecycleState values (V1.8:28-30) are enum VALUES | invariant: :V8I-COG-typed-edges 'the resume edge SUSPEND→RESUME is legal only because ClarificationResponse/1 carries resume_binding_ref binding the exact suspended instance' (V1.8:386-391) | fallback: typed error value + explicit state records (ClarificationRequest/Response facts, V1.8:32-39)" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE (registry forms are DATA read under *read-eval* nil (deferred-imports.sexp:4; ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:56; safe-read.lisp:152-165) — never a macro expanded over the registry file)" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE" :package-asdf-boundary ":V8I-PUBPRIV-all-families: 8 edge families DERIVED from real sources incl. source/mcp-server.lisp define-mcp-tool (:80-91) and static-site.lisp emit-* (V1.8:264-274) — the api-mcp-schema and publication families are PACKAGE-level facts (which exported symbols publish what); the model's L5 today covers only the consumes family (dossier ADJ-V18-INV-5) | invariant: :V8I-PUBPRIV-all-families 'no universal-closure claim is made for a family whose real source is not parsed' (V1.8:281-283) | fallback: consumes-only L5 with the honest one-family statement" :persistent-event ":V8I-CORR (PublicCorrectionEvent tombstone stays citation-resolvable), :V8I-EPOCH (RecoveryEpoch = NEW monotonic epoch N+1, never revert, V1.8:235-238), :V8I-CONT (EmergencyFreeze time-limited, journaled) → chained-append with a monotonic check (journal.lisp:369 %check-monotonic-at!; :507 chained-append) | invariant: :V8I-FROST 'The verifier NEVER silently reverts to an older epoch' (V1.8:238) | fallback: replay" :truth-maintenance-dependency ":V8I-RASTATUS-product: RelianceProjection is DERIVED, total, deterministic, preserves ALL simultaneous causes, and recovery of one dimension never silently recovers another (V1.8:100-102) — dependency-directed derivation (LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:29) over 8 typed dimensions; cause_refs play the role of justification in-lists; not a JTMS belief (no defeaters) but the same 'derived + replayable' discipline | invariant: :V8I-RASTATUS-product (V1.8:97-103) | fallback: full recompute (reliance-of is declared :total t :deterministic t, V1.8:411-414, DDI-3)" :temporal-index-projection ":V8I-EPOCH-one-expression: temporal_resolution must be :EXPRESSION_VERSION or :FULLY_DETERMINED_TEMPORAL_SLICE with timezone/calendar; 'A bare calendar as-of date is INSUFFICIENT when more than one change can occur the same day' (V1.8:129-132) — the existing temporal seat is DAY-granular: legal-temporal.lisp:41-46 (date<= = string<= over YYYY-MM-DD), version-graph.lisp:7 (bitemporal intervals) / :1030 version-at (valid-at/known-at) ⇒ the invariant requires a finer temporal index (expression-version ordering) than the seat provides today | invariant: :V8I-EPOCH (V1.8:128-136) | fallback: :CURRENT_VIEW_QUERY is never a canonical citation (V1.8:131-132) — i.e. refuse, do not approximate" :compile-time-validation "gate-time subset: :V8I-OWN-universal → L2 (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:319) ALREADY; :V8I-XREF-real/:V8I-XREF-identity → a check that OPENS :canonical-file and greps :locator (V1.8:354-356, 434-441) — the kernel reads only model modules (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:170-184), so this is a git-access check (gate_checks.py:786 pattern) declared as a check/falsifier fact; :V8I-CAP-real → same (opens source/*.lisp for defpackage + symbol, V1.8:251-254); :V8I-COGGRAPH → L4 over flow+branch+terminal edges with resume edges in their OWN relation (the kernel treats every from/to relation as an acyclicity duty, ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:211-228 — resume edges must not share the flow relation); :V8I-RA-DELTA-seats 'exactly SEVEN' → an exact-cardinality fact (property-family pattern verification-corpus.sexp:42-56) | invariant: each 'Audit … mutation' clause | fallback: V1.8-VERIFY.py — HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:453)" :runtime-validation ":V8I-02/:V8I-03 SYMBOLIC_ONLY path + one seat; :V8I-CONT (one person may invoke only a time-limited freeze; thaw requires quorum) and :V8I-FROST (no silent single-algorithm fallback) are production-time governance/crypto checks in the MLTP seats (SEAT-KERNEL-VERIFY seats.sexp:44; SEAT-MLTP-THRESHOLD-CUSTODY DESIGN_TARGET :87) | invariant: :V8I-FROST-precise (V1.8:231-238) | fallback: reject / hold" :python-in-cl-risk "YES — 23 blobs including two INTERNAL contradictions (:V8I-SYM-exact 'SEMANTICALLY EQUIVALENT' V1.8:338 vs :V8I-SYM-structural 'does NOT claim behavioral SEMANTIC equivalence' :462; V8-COGLIFE 3 witnesses :71 vs 7 :390) and 'exactly SEVEN' (:456) vs TRACEABILITY's eight (dossier ADJ-V18-INV-4) — as strings they coexist silently; the file-opening audits (XREF/CAP/WP) become Python grep loops. CL-native alternative: retraction as DATA (:retracts V8I-SYM-exact on V8I-SYM-structural, L4-acyclic), witness/mutation counts as exact-cardinality facts (universe-floor pattern verification-corpus.sexp:60-71) so 3-vs-7 is an L1/corpus violation, and file-opening obligations as declared checks in the harness universe." :future-freedom "CONSTRAINS: (1) :V8I-EPOCH forces sub-day temporal identity on S05/version-graph and the resolver — the day-granular date arithmetic (legal-temporal.lisp:41-46) cannot express it (ADJ-CL4-04); (2) :V8I-COGGRAPH/:V8I-COG-typed-edges fix S04's graph (19 nodes, resume semantics — DDI-3 classes); (3) :V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality constrains the ClarifiedInterpretation record (DDI-2) and the C16 fixtures; (4) :V8I-PUBPRIV-all-families makes mcp-server.lisp define-mcp-tool the derivation source of the api-mcp-schema family (V1.8:272) — binds S14's MCP surface as a public-edge source; (5) :V8I-SYM-structural explicitly DEFERS behavioral equivalence to a future WP (V1.8:462-463). PROTECTS: :V8I-02 (no mandatory model), :V8I-03 (no duplicate store — S19 stays one seat).")
