(ddi-class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum
  :batch DDI-2 :source-file "V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp" :fact-class "define-closed-enum" :source-count 9 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms (("ClarificationLifecycleState" :line 28 :sha16 "e42b407441408f13") ("MergeSemanticsV8" :line 31 :sha16 "0715d4ce29e4f984") ("DimensionState" :line 75 :sha16 "334cddef9e69b993") ("RelianceClass" :line 83 :sha16 "161f98f3cd0d41b0") ("CitationTemporalResolution" :line 109 :sha16 "bf7f32d45f2fd901") ("ContinuityRole" :line 139 :sha16 "66e403a32193c7c5") ("MetricAssuranceClass" :line 177 :sha16 "082460fb01fd1f6c") ("ReproTier" :line 178 :sha16 "612e7b6d283a6d49") ("CryptoMaturity" :line 219 :sha16 "6a3f80ead26ef58e"))
  :source-file "V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp"
  :source-forms 9
  :current-authority-seat "V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp — §1 'COGNITION LIFECYCLE (DFT-06 + DFT-07)' (header L24): ClarificationLifecycleState L28-30, MergeSemanticsV8 L31; §2 'ROOT-AUTHORITY PRODUCT STATE + PROJECTION (DFT-10 + §2)' (header L73): DimensionState L75, RelianceClass L83; §3 'RA-EPOCH' (header L105): CitationTemporalResolution L109; §4 'RA-CONT' (header L138): ContinuityRole L139; §6 'RA-K — tiered reproducibility' (header L176): MetricAssuranceClass L177, ReproTier L178; §9 'FROST / PQ' (header L218): CryptoMaturity L219. Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:57 (DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE, DDI-2, :source-count 9)."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "UNDECIDED and shared: the same single module as the other three DDI-2 enum classes (ADJ-DDI2-ENUM-SEAT). The V1.8 dossier proposes a NEW 'enums' module 'or interfaces-and-types extension' — the same fork the V1.7 dossier states and the opposite of what the V1.5/V1.6 dossiers propose. This is the CURRENT registry (V1.8 is the pre-freeze integration spec, V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp:7 'v1.8-final-pre-freeze-integration'), so whichever module wins, this class is the one whose enums are most likely to be canonical rather than historical."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "The shared NEW `enum` + `enum-value` family. flattening rule: one `enum` fact per define-closed-enum (id = enum name, TOKEN) + one `enum-value` fact per member (id = <enum>__<VALUE>, :enum <enum> :value <VALUE> :ordinal <n>); keyword members rendered as bare symbols by colon-strip (orchestrator-notes.md N12); per-member attributes (:label/:obligation/:binding/:sa) become STRING/SYMBOL fields of the enum-value fact. Cardinality by my own reader: 9 `enum` + 37 `enum-value` facts (ClarificationLifecycleState 10, MergeSemanticsV8 3, DimensionState 4, RelianceClass 4, CitationTemporalResolution 3, ContinuityRole 4, MetricAssuranceClass 4, ReproTier 3, CryptoMaturity 2). All 37 members are keywords rendered as bare TOKEN symbols by colon-strip (orchestrator-notes.md N12); none contains a character outside [A-Za-z0-9_.+/-] (my own check). no `enum`/`enum-value`/`field`/`primitive`/`cardinality`/`ref-class`/`adapter`/`canonical-identity` fact type exists among the 34 fact types (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:84-288); `define-enum` there is schema syntax for the model's own closed domains only (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:18,47-76); L1 forbids keywords, nested lists and NIL as values (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6) and the closed field set forbids adding keys to `type` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:9-13,148-152)"
  :owner "UNKNOWN for all 9 as facts — no V1.8 define-closed-enum form carries an owner key. Context owners, all inferred from the CONSUMING record's ISR row: S04 for ClarificationLifecycleState and MergeSemanticsV8 (ISR:117,120), S14 for DimensionState and RelianceClass (ISR:110,113), S25 for CitationTemporalResolution (ISR:127), S11 for ContinuityRole (ISR:140), S15 for MetricAssuranceClass and ReproTier (ISR:154), S10 for CryptoMaturity (ISR:166). Every one of these is an inference; the V1.8 dossier states it as 'UNKNOWN as a fact' for all nine."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — closed value domains are declared, not written. The instances that carry these values are written by their store's writer where one exists (citation-observatory writer SEAT-OBSERVATORY-COLLECTOR, stores-and-authorities.sexp:5; trust-bundle writer SEAT-MLTP-THRESHOLD-CUSTODY, :14); no registry names a writer for an enum."
  :classification "PUBLIC — all 9; no private member in any of the 37 values, and none of the enums appears in the V1.8 private-forbidden list (V1.8:262-263). This is the only one of the four DDI-2 enum classes with no private-bearing member (V1.5 and V1.6 have them; V1.7's MemoryScopeV7 has :USER_PRIVATE/:SERVICE_INTERNAL). Note the asymmetry it exposes: two of these PUBLIC enums (MetricAssuranceClass :INDEPENDENTLY_AUDITED_RESTRICTED, ReproTier :T3_SEALED_RESTRICTED) name RESTRICTED handling as a value while the model's `classification` enum has only PUBLIC and PRIVATE (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:47)."
  :dependencies ("SCHEMA FIRST: `enum` + `enum-value` fact types and the schema-version bump (X74-X76 verification-corpus.sexp:354-370)" "SAME BATCH: V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-record — 7 of the 9 enums are the :domain of a V1.8 record field (dag.json 'V1.8 define-record -> V1.8 define-closed-enum', 7 refs)" "SAME BATCH: V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-cardinality-table — its 3 rows are keyed by MergeSemanticsV8 values (V1.8:395-397 :when :ABSTAIN / :EXPLICIT_SELECTION / :EXPLICIT_MERGE); the table cannot be L3-closed before the enum-value facts exist" "DECISION FIRST: the one enum module; whether `enum` requires :owner-subsystem (no V1.8 enum declares one); what to do with the 2 orphan enums" "NO EARLIER dependency: dag.json records zero out-edges for this class")
  :consumers ("V1.8 define-record field domains (7 refs, dag.json): ClarifiedInterpretation/1.merge_semantics (V1.8:43), RootAuthorityStatus/1 x8 dimension fields (:78-80), RelianceProjection/1.reliance (:85), CanonicalCitationURI/1.temporal_resolution (V1.8 §3), ContinuityPolicy/1 (§4), CitationMetricV8/1.tier + .assurance (:180), CryptoSuiteRegistry/1 (§9)" "V1.8 define-cardinality-table clarified-interpretation-cardinality (V1.8:394-397, DDI-2) — keyed by MergeSemanticsV8" "V1.8 define-invariant (1 ref, DDI-4) — :V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality (V1.8:47-51) restates the MergeSemanticsV8 rules in prose" "V1.8 define-dimension-policy root-authority-dimensions (V1.8:88-103, DDI-3) — its :failure values are RelianceClass members" "ClarificationLifecycleState and ContinuityRole are consumed by NO record field in ANY of the six registries (V1.8 dossier ADJ-V18-ENUM-1; my own check of the field :type tokens agrees) — 2 orphan enums" "no tracked source/ or systems/ file names any record/enum id of the six registries (git grep at RO = 0); the only mechanical readers are the legacy audits/harness classified HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:436,440,444,450,453)")
  :identity-version-rule "MIXED. ONLY-VERSION (8): DimensionState, RelianceClass, CitationTemporalResolution, ContinuityRole, MetricAssuranceClass, ReproTier, CryptoMaturity and ClarificationLifecycleState — no same-name form in any other registry (my own grep; version-chains.md). PROMOTION OF AN INLINE SET (1): MergeSemanticsV8 (V1.8:31) carries exactly the three values that V1.7:78 held INLINE as `(member :EXPLICIT_SELECTION :EXPLICIT_MERGE :ABSTAIN)` inside ClarifiedInterpretation/1 — same value set, new named seat. This is the cleanest 'inline member set becomes a named enum' precedent in the six registries and should govern the inline-member encoding rule (ADJ-DDI2-INLINE-MEMBER). CONCEPT-LEVEL DIVERGENCE (1, no name collision): ClarificationLifecycleState (V1.8:28) is the third statement of 'clarification state' after V1.6:200 ClarificationState/1.status (:OPEN :ANSWERED :ABANDONED) and V1.7:40-43 CognitionErrorV7 (:CLARIFICATION_REQUIRED/:UNDERDETERMINED/:CONFLICTING); none declares supersession."
  :migration-rule "MIXED. IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL for the 7 enums that a V1.8 record field binds — V1.8 is the current registry, the values are flat, and each has exactly one seat. BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION for ClarificationLifecycleState and ContinuityRole: an enum with zero consumers is either (a) imported as an orphan closed domain, (b) bound to a field that does not yet exist, or (c) skipped — and importing an orphan enum installs a domain nothing can violate, which is inert data by construction."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "MEDIUM. (1) Three registries state 'clarification state' differently (V1.6:200 as a record field's inline set, V1.7:40-43 as error values, V1.8:28-30 as a named lifecycle enum) with no supersession declared — a concept with three seats and no collision, which no L2 check can see because the ids differ. (2) MergeSemanticsV8's values duplicate V1.7:78's inline set; if inline sets are encoded as anonymous enums, ClarifiedInterpretation/1 would carry BOTH an anonymous V1.7 domain and the named V1.8 one — two seats for one three-value domain. (3) No id collision with model facts: none of the 9 names is an id in the 14 modules (my own grep)."
  :requirement "NONE directly. Owner-side requirements exist only through the consuming records' subsystems: R-129/Q08 via req-map S04__WP-08 (requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:70), R-102/Q27 via S14__WP-11 (:80), R-134/Q28 via S11__WP-06 (:77), R-124/Q42 via S15__WP-13 (:81), R-130/Q28 via S10__WP-06 (:76). The V1.8 RA-layer requirement ids (RA8-EPOCH/CONT/CORR/JURNS/MARK/K/SIDE, V1.8:445-451) are NOT model `requirement` facts (orchestrator-notes.md N1) — so an enum imported under an RA8 requirement could not be L6-closed."
  :invariant "L1 (nested value lists and keywords, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6), L2 (one enum id), L3 (:enum ref closed; and the cardinality table's :when-value must close on a MergeSemanticsV8 enum-value). Source invariants: :V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality (V1.8:47-51), :V8I-RASTATUS-product (:97-103), :V8I-RA-K-tiered (:184-190), :V8I-FROST-precise (:231-238) — none of them has a model law; each is a statement ABOUT the values of these enums that nothing in KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp or gate_checks.py evaluates."
  :qualification-test "Existing: none names an enum. NEW executable one-liner: every `enum-value` :enum resolves to a declared `enum`, AND every declared `enum` is named by at least one `field :domain` OR is explicitly marked as an orphan by a declared reason — the second clause is what turns ClarificationLifecycleState and ContinuityRole from a silent oddity into a named, decided state. Pin the total with a NEW property-family (shape verification-corpus.sexp:42-56) so that losing a member is a failure rather than a smaller number (the exact defect verification-corpus.sexp:3-8 was written to stop)."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact enum-value MergeSemanticsV8__SILENT_WINNER :enum MergeSemanticsV8 :value SILENT_WINNER)` — must be rejected by the cardinality-pinned property family as a member outside the declared domain; and any `field :domain MergeSemanticsV8` fact whose instance uses it must fail L1 (out-of-domain value, the shape of K13-PRIVATE-TYPO verification-corpus.sexp:148-151). APPEND `(fact enum-value NoSuchEnum__X :enum NoSuchEnum :value X)` — both paths reject, kernel-reason 'resolves to no declared enum', checker-reason 'L3'. REPLACE the cardinality table's `:when-value ABSTAIN` with `:when-value ABSTAINED` — must be rejected as outside the MergeSemanticsV8 domain, proving the table's key is a typed reference and not a string."
  :rollback "delete the imported facts of this class and the fact-type/enum declarations added to MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp for it, re-run build_root.py so ROOT.sexp re-pins the 14 modules (ROOT.sexp:12-27; L7), and restore the ledger row to DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT / AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE (deferred-imports.sexp) so the source file is authoritative again; the source registry is never edited by the import (V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp:256 'v1.5 files are NOT edited' is the precedent)"
  :batch-reason "DDI-2 because build_deferred.py maps define-closed-enum to DDI-2, materialised at deferred-imports.sexp:57. AGREES. dag.json records zero out-edges and two in-edges, both from the SAME batch or later (V1.8 define-record 7 refs, DDI-2; V1.8 define-invariant 1 ref, DDI-4). No earlier-rank class references it — unlike every other DDI-2 class in this matrix. This is the one DDI-2 class whose declared batch is fully consistent with the mechanical reference graph."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "(a) Which single module seats all 41 DDI-2 enums (ADJ-DDI2-ENUM-SEAT)? (b) ClarificationLifecycleState (V1.8:28) and ContinuityRole (V1.8:139) are bound by no field anywhere — import as orphan domains, bind them to a field, or skip with proof? (c) Is 'clarification state' one concept with three seats (V1.6:200, V1.7:40-43, V1.8:28-30), and if so which is canonical? (d) Does `enum` require :owner-subsystem — no V1.8 enum declares one."
  :adjudication-items ("ADJ-DDI2-ENUM-SEAT: the four DDI-2 enum classes (V1.5 16 enums/83 values, V1.6 8/71, V1.7 8/61, V1.8 9/37 — my own reader over the six registries) must share ONE module (one seat per concept); the dossiers disagree — V1.5/V1.6 propose interfaces-and-types.sexp, V1.7/V1.8 propose a NEW 'enums' module. No winner is picked here." "ADJ-V18-ENUM-1 (V1.8 dossier): ClarificationLifecycleState (V1.8:28) and ContinuityRole (V1.8:139) are used by no record field in any registry — orphan enums." "ADJ-V18-ENUM-2 (V1.8 dossier): three seats for clarification state across registries (V1.6:200 ClarificationState/1.status, V1.7:40-43 CognitionErrorV7, V1.8:28 ClarificationLifecycleState) — none declares supersession." "ADJ-DDI2-INLINE-MEMBER (shared): MergeSemanticsV8 is the precedent that an inline (member ...) set becomes a named enum (V1.7:78 -> V1.8:31); the encoding rule for the other 53 inline sets across the four record classes must follow it or declare why not." "ADJ-DDI2-ENUM-OWNER (shared with V1.7): no V1.8 enum declares an owner; a required :owner-subsystem would block the class." "ADJ-DDI2-RESTRICTED-VALUE: MetricAssuranceClass :INDEPENDENTLY_AUDITED_RESTRICTED and ReproTier :T3_SEALED_RESTRICTED name a RESTRICTED handling class that the model's two-valued `classification` enum (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:47) cannot express; ISR uses :RESTRICTED as a classification (ISR:151,159) and build_model.py maps it to PRIVATE.")
  :topological-position 12 :atomic-groups (4 5 6)
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "NOT-APPLICABLE" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE (deftype member types, source/version-graph.lisp:148-149 deftype legal-date / legal-instant)" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart "ClarificationLifecycleState (:REQUESTED :SUSPENDED :RESPONDED :RESUMED :EXPIRED :CANCELLED + 4 TERMINAL_* V1.8:28-30) names the states of the clarification lifecycle; a CL restart can carry SUSPEND->RESUME only inside one dynamic extent — cross-invocation suspension/expiry (V1.8:35 :expiry) must be persisted (CL2-A7); terminals are typed outcomes, never exceptions swallowed | invariant: V8I-COGGRAPH-acyclic-except-resume (V1.8:66-71) | fallback: return typed error value (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:24)" :macro-dsl "as class 1 | invariant: compile-time only (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:25) | fallback: hand-written deftype + constant list" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE" :package-asdf-boundary "ClarificationLifecycleState/MergeSemanticsV8 -> S04 package; DimensionState/RelianceClass -> S14; CitationTemporalResolution -> S25 (orchestrator.uris); ContinuityRole/CryptoMaturity -> S11 (SEAT-SECURITY-CELLS DESIGN_TARGET AM/seats.sexp:79-80 — no package exists); MetricAssuranceClass/ReproTier -> S15 (orchestrator.citation-authority source/citation-authority.lisp:35) | invariant: package boundary = capability boundary (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:31) | fallback: monolith package (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:31)" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE (DimensionState x RelianceClass are the DOMAINS of the dependency-directed RelianceProjection — class 16 / DDI-3 reliance-of)" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE (CitationTemporalResolution labels the resolution KIND; the mechanism is class 16 CanonicalCitationURI/1)" :compile-time-validation "as class 1 (member list == enum-value facts); orphan enums ClarificationLifecycleState and ContinuityRole are bound by NO field (ADJ-V18-ENUM-1) — a build-time 'every enum has at least one binding field' check would name them | invariant: L1 closed domain | fallback: runtime check (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:32)" :runtime-validation "`typep` at decode (as class 1); MergeSemanticsV8 drives the conditional cardinality (class 18) | invariant: V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality (V1.8:47-51) | fallback: reject input" :python-in-cl-risk "LOW. Flat symbol lists; keyword rendering (N12); MergeSemanticsV8 is the model of how an inline (member ...) becomes a named enum (V1.8:31 promotes V1.7:78's inline list). CL-native: deftype per enum; enum-value facts with ordinal; the lifecycle enum backs a persisted state machine, not string comparisons." :future-freedom "NO problematic constraint. ClarificationLifecycleState constrains S04's control flow (suspend/resume/expiry) by design (DFT-07); CryptoMaturity (:FROZEN :PENDING_IMPLEMENTATION_REVIEW V1.8:219) is honest about FROST/DKG maturity and mandates no algorithm; MetricAssuranceClass/ReproTier constrain S15 reporting, not reasoning. No V8I-02 effect. Three clarification-state seats across registries (V1.6:200, V1.7:40-43, V1.8:28 — ADJ-V18-ENUM-2) are a one-seat adjudication for S04.")
  )

(ddi-class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-record
  :batch DDI-2 :source-file "V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp" :fact-class "define-record" :source-count 19 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms (("ClarificationRequest/1" :line 32 :sha16 "1f0344ab75354724") ("ClarificationResponse/1" :line 36 :sha16 "4b0b2caaf5372d17") ("ClarifiedInterpretation/1" :line 40 :sha16 "ecf44277925c137e") ("RootAuthorityStatus/1" :line 76 :sha16 "809ee3443b46f2fc") ("RelianceProjection/1" :line 84 :sha16 "8bd8eb17ccf1aa11") ("CanonicalCitationURI/1" :line 110 :sha16 "713ad3555fad3c99") ("ResolutionRecord/1" :line 116 :sha16 "4f846f515bf69841") ("MultiCommitment/1" :line 119 :sha16 "40f51cf0eee1f5c8") ("ReAnchoringManifest/1" :line 124 :sha16 "40d8b83fc5b82926") ("ContinuityPolicy/1" :line 140 :sha16 "60a1123c748d00fc") ("EmergencyFreeze/1" :line 145 :sha16 "27f89449d9bf85de") ("PublicCorrectionEvent/1" :line 160 :sha16 "f95ea27a3dcaa967") ("RestrictedForensicRecord/1" :line 165 :sha16 "e145018456a3be9f") ("CitationMetricV8/1" :line 179 :sha16 "6a3090b0a51cb3ca") ("SidecarSourceProfile/1" :line 193 :sha16 "11c577d370d5adb2") ("LawmaxStatusVsMark/1" :line 207 :sha16 "a53ee4a1345b00a7") ("CryptoSuiteRegistry/1" :line 220 :sha16 "39844155785aa635") ("RecoveryEpoch/1" :line 226 :sha16 "b966a38a93efeca8") ("JurisdictionNamespace/1" :line 452 :sha16 "2df203498672d407"))
  :source-file "V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp"
  :source-forms 19
  :current-authority-seat "V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp §1-§9 and §17: ClarificationRequest/1 L32, ClarificationResponse/1 L36, ClarifiedInterpretation/1 L40 (§1, header L24); RootAuthorityStatus/1 L76, RelianceProjection/1 L84 (§2, header L73); CanonicalCitationURI/1 L110, ResolutionRecord/1 L116, MultiCommitment/1 L119, ReAnchoringManifest/1 L124 (§3, header L105); ContinuityPolicy/1 L140, EmergencyFreeze/1 L145 (§4, header L138); PublicCorrectionEvent/1 L160, RestrictedForensicRecord/1 L165 (§5, header L159); CitationMetricV8/1 L179 (§6, header L176); SidecarSourceProfile/1 L193 (§7, header L192); LawmaxStatusVsMark/1 L207 (§8, header L206); CryptoSuiteRegistry/1 L220, RecoveryEpoch/1 L226 (§9, header L218); JurisdictionNamespace/1 L452 (§17, header L358, inside the VR-10 RA-delta block L443-451). ISR registers ALL 19 with :seat 'V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp §n' (INTERFACE-AND-SCHEMA-REGISTRY.sexp:105-175). Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:66 (DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE, DDI-2, :source-count 19)."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "SPLIT: identity is ALREADY complete in interfaces-and-types.sexp — all 19 are `type` facts (interfaces-and-types.sexp:16,17,18,54,46,10,47,37,43,20,25,42,51,14,58,31,21,45,29), which makes this the only DDI-2 record class with zero identity gap. The FIELD structure has no seat and must land in the ONE module chosen for all four record classes (ADJ-DDI2-FIELD-SEAT; the V1.8 dossier proposes NEW 'record-fields' or an interfaces-and-types extension)."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "EXISTING `type` (all 19 present) + the NEW `field` family. flattening rule: keep the existing `type` fact as the record identity; one `field` fact per (:name :type T) entry (id = <record>__<field>, :record <type-id> :name <field> :ordinal <n> :type-token <T> :list YES/NO :nullable YES/NO :domain <enum-id or type-id or primitive-id>); (list X) -> :list YES, (or X null) -> :nullable YES, (member ...) -> an anonymous enum id <record>__<field>__MEMBERS with enum-value facts; primitive tokens (id semver ref sha256 sig instant text ...) need a `primitive` fact family or an explicit exemption from L3 (V5-A8 / A20 / ADJ-V17-REC-5) Cardinality by my own reader: 179 `field` facts over 19 records, including 15 `(list X)` fields, 17 `(or X null)` fields and 17 inline `(member ...)` sets — many of the latter being CONSTANT one-member domains used as guarantees (EmergencyFreeze/1 has 3, PublicCorrectionEvent/1 has 4, RelianceProjection/1's `:derived :type (member :true)` at V1.8:86 is labelled 'VR-07: derived CONSTANT true'). A constant-true member set is a CLAIM, not a domain: encoding it as a one-value enum makes it falsifiable; encoding it as a string makes it decorative. primitive type tokens are defined in NONE of the six registries (V1.5-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh:227 and V1.6-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh:151-152 hard-code them as `prim`). no `enum`/`enum-value`/`field`/`primitive`/`cardinality`/`ref-class`/`adapter`/`canonical-identity` fact type exists among the 34 fact types (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:84-288); `define-enum` there is schema syntax for the model's own closed domains only (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:18,47-76); L1 forbids keywords, nested lists and NIL as values (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6) and the closed field set forbids adding keys to `type` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:9-13,148-152)"
  :owner "All 19 declared and agreeing across ISR, the model and (for 7 of them) the RA-delta table: S04 ClarificationRequest/1 (ISR:120; interfaces-and-types.sexp:16), S04 ClarificationResponse/1 (ISR:123; :17), S04 ClarifiedInterpretation/1 (ISR:117; :18), S14 RootAuthorityStatus/1 (ISR:110; :54), S14 RelianceProjection/1 (ISR:113; :46), S25 CanonicalCitationURI/1 (ISR:127; :10; V1.8:445 :owner S25), S25 ResolutionRecord/1 (ISR:136; :47), S25 MultiCommitment/1 (ISR:130; :37), S25 ReAnchoringManifest/1 (ISR:133; :43), S11 ContinuityPolicy/1 (ISR:140; :20; V1.8:446 :owner S11), S11 EmergencyFreeze/1 (ISR:143; :25), S18 PublicCorrectionEvent/1 (ISR:147; :42; V1.8:447 :owner S18), S18 RestrictedForensicRecord/1 (ISR:150; :51), S15 CitationMetricV8/1 (ISR:154; :14; V1.8:450 :owner S15), S26 SidecarSourceProfile/1 (ISR:158; :58; V1.8:451 :owner S26), S25 LawmaxStatusVsMark/1 (ISR:162; :31; V1.8:449 :owner S25), S10 CryptoSuiteRegistry/1 (ISR:166; :21), S11 RecoveryEpoch/1 (ISR:169; :45), S25 JurisdictionNamespace/1 (ISR:173; :29; V1.8:448 :owner S25). ONE ownership question survives: RecoveryEpoch/1's owner is S11 by ISR:169 while the MLTP epoch record it may duplicate is root-signed by S10's MLTP root (MACHINE-LEGAL-TRUST-PROTOCOL.md:1366) — a concept-ownership question, not a contradiction between registry rows (ADJ-V18-REC-5)."
  :writer "MIXED, and mostly UNKNOWN. Declared through stores: citation-observatory writer SEAT-OBSERVATORY-COLLECTOR (stores-and-authorities.sexp:5) for CitationMetricV8/1; trust-bundle writer SEAT-MLTP-THRESHOLD-CUSTODY (:14) for the crypto records if they are trust-bundle content; resolver-dataset writer SEAT-NO-WRITER (:11) for the resolver-side records; tenant-profile writer SEAT-NO-WRITER (:13) for SidecarSourceProfile/1's subsystem S26. For the majority no store exists and no registry names a writer — UNKNOWN, not NO_WRITER. Note S11 owns three records (ContinuityPolicy/1, EmergencyFreeze/1, RecoveryEpoch/1) and its seat SEAT-SECURITY-CELLS is a DESIGN_TARGET (seats.sexp:79-80, :packet WP-06) — an unbuilt seat cannot be a writer."
  :classification "MIXED — private members named: RestrictedForensicRecord/1 (V1.8:165 ':status :DEFERRED_PRIVATE :public-dependency nil'; ISR:151 :RESTRICTED; model PRIVATE interfaces-and-types.sexp:51) and SidecarSourceProfile/1 (V1.8:193 ':status :SPECIFICATION_ONLY :public-dependency nil'; ISR:159 :RESTRICTED; model PRIVATE :58). Both are members of the V1.8 private-forbidden list (V1.8:262-263) and both are counted in property-family PF-L5-PRIVATE-TYPE-LEAK :cardinality 6 (verification-corpus.sexp:45-47). The other 17 are PUBLIC. STRUCTURAL ANOMALY, cited: RestrictedForensicRecord/1 is a PRIVATE type owned by S18, a PUBLIC subsystem (subsystems.sexp:22), and seats.sexp declares DEFERRED_PRIVATE/INTERFACE_ONLY seats only for S22/S23/S24/S26 (seats.sexp:91-98) — there is no seat that can carry a private type owned by a public subsystem."
  :dependencies ("SCHEMA FIRST: NEW `field` fact type (+ primitive family or L3 exemption) and the schema-version bump (X74-X76 verification-corpus.sexp:354-370)" "SAME BATCH, STRICTLY FIRST: V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum — 7 field :domain refs (dag.json)" "EXISTING model facts: all 19 `type` facts and their `consumes` edges (dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:23-124) — nothing to create, only to extend" "DDI-1 CONSUMER ALREADY IMPORTED-ADJACENT: V1.8 define-ra-delta-seats (V1.8:444-451, DDI-1, deferred-imports.sexp:65) binds 7 of these records as the ONE canonical seat of each RA delta — dag.json 'V1.8 define-ra-delta-seats (rank 1) -> V1.8 define-record (rank 2), 7 refs'" "DECISION FIRST: ClarifiedInterpretation/1's twin (V1.7:75); the private-field policy for the 2 PRIVATE records; the status vocabulary (SPECIFICATION_ONLY / CANDIDATE_DEFINITION are not model seat-status values, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:62)")
  :consumers ("V1.8 define-ra-delta-seats (V1.8:444-451, DDI-1) — 7 refs; V1.8 define-ra-closure-roots (V1.8:259-265, DDI-1) — 4 refs" "V1.8 define-cognition-node-types (V1.8:363-383, DDI-3) — 3 refs; V1.8 define-invariant (DDI-4) — 3 refs; V1.7 define-construction-order (DDI-1) — 1 ref (V1.7:80 -> V1.8:40 ClarifiedInterpretation/1)" "V1.8 define-cardinality-table (V1.8:394-397, DDI-2) — binds ClarifiedInterpretation/1's three ref fields by NAME CONVENTION only (V1.8:43-45), not by typed reference" "V1.8 define-fixtures clarified-interpretation-fixtures (V1.8:398-405, DDI-4) — 7 test vectors over the same three fields" "ISR define-interface (IMPORTED, ISR:105-175) registers all 19 and is the source of the model's `type` facts (build_model.py) — the model's identity layer is already derived from here" "no tracked source/ or systems/ file names any record/enum id of the six registries (git grep at RO = 0); the only mechanical readers are the legacy audits/harness classified HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:436,440,444,450,453)")
  :identity-version-rule "MIXED. SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT (1, same name and version): ClarifiedInterpretation/1 — V1.8:40-46 (11 fields) vs V1.7:75-79 (9 fields); ISR:117 names 'V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp §1' as the seat, but BOTH source classes are DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT / AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE (deferred-imports.sexp:48 and :66) and neither declares the other retired. SUPERSEDING UNDER A NEW NAME, PREDECESSOR STILL LIVE (2): CitationMetricV8/1 (V1.8:179, comment 'supersedes CitationSupremacyMetric raw-publication invariant') while CitationSupremacyMetric/1 remains a model `type` (interfaces-and-types.sexp:15) and an ISR row (ISR:91); RootAuthorityStatus/1 (V1.8:76) while RootAuthorityQualification/1 remains a model `type` (:53) and an ISR row (ISR:101) which ISR:112 calls the ROLLBACK of the v1.8 one. LIVE-REFERENCE-TARGET (0 in this class: the V1.8 §15 references point at V1.6/V1.7 files, not at V1.8 records). ONLY-VERSION (16): the rest, all first defined here."
  :migration-rule "MERGE-INTO-EXISTING-FACT for 17 of the 19 (the `type` fact exists; only `field` facts are added) once the field family and module exist — this class is the closest thing in DDI-2 to a mechanical import, because its identity layer is already imported and its owners are uncontested. BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION for ClarifiedInterpretation/1 (which of two field sets) and for the two PRIVATE records (are private fields imported into the public model at all, given V1.8:280 'the closure contains ZERO :DEFERRED_PRIVATE record'?)."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "MEDIUM-HIGH. (1) ClarifiedInterpretation/1 same-name/same-version twin (see identity rule) — L2 makes importing both impossible, so one must be retired by decision, not by import order. (2) Two predecessor/successor pairs are both live in the model AND in ISR; adding fields to all four would make a nominal duplication structural. (3) CryptoSuiteRegistry/1 (V1.8:220) and RecoveryEpoch/1 (V1.8:226) may be the record form of MLTP §14.1/§14.2 (MACHINE-LEGAL-TRUST-PROTOCOL.md:1349, :1360-1368) — an EXTEND vs second-seat question with an ownership limb (S10/S11 vs the MLTP root). (4) JurisdictionNamespace/1 has its own seat per V1.8:448,452 and ISR:173, while CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:83-85 seats RA-JUR-NS inside CanonicalCitationURI/1 — a prose/registry divergence on where one delta lives. (5) No seat exists for a PRIVATE type owned by the PUBLIC subsystem S18 (seats.sexp:91-98)."
  :requirement "Partial and structurally blocked for the RA deltas. Model requirements reachable via owners: R-129/Q08 via S04__WP-08 (requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:70), R-102/Q27 via S14__WP-11 (:80), R-134/Q28 via S11__WP-06 (:77), R-111/Q20 via S18__WP-12 (:84), R-124/Q42 via S15__WP-13 (:81), R-V6-TENANT/RA-Q-TENANT via S26__DEFERRED (:95), R-130/Q28 via S10__WP-06 (:76), R-V6-RESOLVE/RA-Q-RESOLVE via S25__FUTURE_BOOK_REVISION (:94). BUT the requirement ids the source itself binds to 7 of these records — RA8-EPOCH, RA8-CONT, RA8-CORR, RA8-JURNS, RA8-MARK, RA8-K, RA8-SIDE (V1.8:445-451) — are NOT model `requirement` facts, and the tests T8-EPOCH/CONT/CORR/JURNS/MARK/K/SIDE are not model `test` facts (orchestrator-notes.md N1). Also blocking: ISR gives 9 of these types :future-wp FUTURE_IMPLEMENTATION_BOOK_PACKET_REQUIRED (ISR:112,115,129,138,142,145,160,164,175), a token that is not a model `wp` (requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:52-65 has DEFERRED and FUTURE_BOOK_REVISION only)."
  :invariant "L1 (nested field lists, keywords, `(or X null)`), L2 (ClarifiedInterpretation/1 cannot be two facts — KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:124), L3 (:record and :domain closed), L5 (2 PRIVATE records; PF-L5-PRIVATE-TYPE-LEAK :cardinality 6 verification-corpus.sexp:45-47), L6 (RA8 requirements/tests absent). Source invariants: :V8I-03-one-seat (V1.8:20-22), :V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality (:47-51), :V8I-PUBPRIV-all-families (:277-284), :V8I-OWN-universal (:296-299), :V8I-WP-real (:320-323), :V8I-RA-DELTA-seats (:455-458)."
  :qualification-test "Existing model `test` facts via owners: Q08 (:32), Q27 (:37), Q28 (:38), Q20 (:35), Q42 (:39), RA-Q-TENANT (:45), RA-Q-RESOLVE (:44) — all design-only/UNEXECUTED (orchestrator-notes.md N7). The source's own tests (T8-*) are not model facts. NEW executable one-liner: every `field` whose :record is one of the 7 RA-delta seats (V1.8:445-451) exists AND its record's requirement/test ids resolve to declared `requirement`/`test` facts — i.e. the RA-delta chain is L6-closed. Today it is not, and that is the entry criterion DDI-1 already inherits (orchestrator-notes.md N1)."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact field RestrictedForensicRecord/1__leak :record RestrictedForensicRecord/1 :name leak :ordinal 99 :domain ClarificationRequest/1)` — must be rejected by whatever rule the private-field decision installs; today L3 would ACCEPT it (both ids are declared types) and L5 would not see it, because L5 ranges over `consumes` only (KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:243-254). That acceptance is the finding. APPEND `(fact type ClarifiedInterpretation/1 :classification PUBLIC :owner-subsystem S04)` a second time — must be rejected as 'duplicate seat TYPE ClarifiedInterpretation/1' (L2). REPLACE `:classification PRIVATE` with `:classification PRIVAT` on SidecarSourceProfile/1 — must be rejected as outside the classification enum, the live K13-PRIVATE-TYPO falsifier (verification-corpus.sexp:148-151)."
  :rollback "delete the imported facts of this class and the fact-type/enum declarations added to MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp for it, re-run build_root.py so ROOT.sexp re-pins the 14 modules (ROOT.sexp:12-27; L7), and restore the ledger row to DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT / AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE (deferred-imports.sexp) so the source file is authoritative again; the source registry is never edited by the import (V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp:256 'v1.5 files are NOT edited' is the precedent)"
  :batch-reason "DDI-2 because build_deferred.py maps define-record to DDI-2, materialised at deferred-imports.sexp:66. DISAGREES, mildly and in the 'too late' direction: three DDI-1 classes reference it — V1.8 define-ra-delta-seats (7 refs; the ENTIRE VR-10 delta table names these records as its canonical seats), V1.8 define-ra-closure-roots (4 refs), V1.7 define-construction-order (1 ref) — all listed as order violations in dag.json. Unlike the V1.6/V1.7 record classes, the identities are ALREADY in the model (via the IMPORTED ISR class), so the DDI-1 refs do resolve; what DDI-2 adds is structure. On that reading the placement is defensible and the violation is nominal — the exception among the DDI-2 record classes."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "(a) ClarifiedInterpretation/1: V1.7:75-79 or V1.8:40-46, and does the version stay '1' if the field set changes? (b) Are the fields of the two PRIVATE records imported into the public model at all (V1.8:280 says the public closure contains ZERO :DEFERRED_PRIVATE record), and which seat carries a PRIVATE type owned by the PUBLIC subsystem S18 (seats.sexp:91-98 has none)? (c) Status vocabulary: :SPECIFICATION_ONLY (V1.8:193), :CANDIDATE_DEFINITION (V1.8:452; ISR:158) and INTERFACE_ONLY (TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:396) name one thing three ways and the model's seat-status enum (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:62) has none of the first two. (d) CryptoSuiteRegistry/1 and RecoveryEpoch/1 vs MLTP §14.1/§14.2 — EXTEND one seat or admit a second? (e) Does RA-JUR-NS have its own record (V1.8:452, ISR:173) or is it a dimension of CanonicalCitationURI/1 (CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:83-85)?"
  :adjudication-items ("ADJ-DDI2-FIELD-SEAT: the four DDI-2 record classes (V1.5 18/181 fields, V1.6 22/190, V1.7 25/227, V1.8 19/179 — my own count) must share ONE `field` seat; the dossiers propose interfaces-and-types.sexp (V1.5/V1.6) vs a NEW module 'record-fields'/'schemas' (V1.7/V1.8). No winner is picked here." "ADJ-V18-REC-1 (V1.8 dossier): ClarifiedInterpretation/1 defined twice with the same version and different fields (V1.7:75 vs V1.8:40); both DDI-2 AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE; ISR:117 points at V1.8." "ADJ-V18-REC-2 (V1.8 dossier): predecessor types stay canonical beside their v1.8 successors — RootAuthorityQualification/1 (interfaces-and-types.sexp:53) vs RootAuthorityStatus/1 (:54, ISR:112 names v1.7 as rollback); CitationSupremacyMetric/1 (:15) vs CitationMetricV8/1 (:14)." "ADJ-V18-REC-3 (V1.8 dossier): private-record field import policy under :V8I-PUBPRIV-all-families (V1.8:277-284) and the missing seat for S18's private type (seats.sexp:91-98)." "ADJ-V18-REC-4 (V1.8 dossier): status vocabulary — :DEFERRED_PRIVATE / :SPECIFICATION_ONLY / CANDIDATE_DEFINITION / :RESTRICTED / INTERFACE_ONLY across V1.8, ISR and TRACEABILITY-MATRIX; MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:62 knows six seat statuses and none of SPECIFICATION_ONLY/CANDIDATE_DEFINITION." "ADJ-V18-REC-5 (V1.8 dossier): CryptoSuiteRegistry/1 / RecoveryEpoch/1 vs MACHINE-LEGAL-TRUST-PROTOCOL.md §14.1/§14.2 (:1349, :1360-1368) — EXTEND or second seat; ownership S10 vs S11 vs the MLTP root." "ADJ-V18-REC-6 (V1.8 dossier): RA-JUR-NS seat — own record (V1.8:448,452; ISR:173) vs a dimension of CanonicalCitationURI/1 (CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:83-85)." "ADJ-V18-REC-7 (V1.8 dossier): ISR :future-wp FUTURE_IMPLEMENTATION_BOOK_PACKET_REQUIRED (ISR:112,115,129,138,142,145,160,164,175) is not a model `wp` — req-map rows for these types cannot be written until the WP token vocabulary is unified." "ADJ-DDI2-CONSTANT-MEMBER: 17 inline (member ...) sets in this class, several of them one-value constants used as guarantees (V1.8:86 ':derived :type (member :true)', EmergencyFreeze/1 x3, PublicCorrectionEvent/1 x4). A constant-true guarantee encoded as a string is unfalsifiable; encoded as a one-value domain it is checkable. The encoding rule decides which." "UNKNOWN/count divergence: the V1.8 dossier states 146 fields for this class; my own reader counts 179 over the same 19 records. The importer must re-count rather than trust either figure.")
  :topological-position 13 :atomic-groups (4 5 6 7)
