ort: (a) :status keywords :DEFERRED_PRIVATE / :SPECIFICATION_ONLY / CANDIDATE_DEFINITION (V1.8:165,193,452) as free strings although MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:62 seat-status lacks two of them (ADJ-V18-REC-4); (b) singleton (member :true)/(member :false) fields as booleans instead of structural constants; (c) type expressions as strings (as class 2); (d) RelianceProjection stored as a scalar 'reliance' value (the anti-pattern V1.8:74 forbids). CL-native: enum/seat-status vocabulary unified first; constants as constants; decomposed typed fields; the projection computed by a dependency-directed function over typed dimension states (source/legal-inference-engine.lisp:238 make-jtms; :385 fact-status (:in/:undefined/:out/:unknown); :395 tms-retract-premise), never stored." :future-freedom "YES — flagged. (a) S04: ClarifiedInterpretation/1 double definition (V1.7:75 vs V1.8:40; ADJ-V18-REC-1/ADJ-V17-REC-2) must resolve to ONE seat before any S04 class exists; the suspend/resume lifecycle constrains cognition control flow by design (DFT-07) and needs a persisted-state seat that no `store` fact provides today (10 stores, AM/stores-and-authorities.sexp:5-14 — CL2-A7). (b) S19: none. (c) S20/V8I-02: none — MultiCommitment mandates >=2 distinct hash FAMILIES without naming one (crypto agility, V1.8:121); CryptoSuiteRegistry is versioned (V1.8:220-225). (d) Reasoning: RelianceProjection is dependency-directed by design. Package split for the two PRIVATE records inside PUBLIC subsystems (ADJ-V18-REC-3) is an architecture decision.")
