  :proposed-canonical-target-module "NEW:cognition-graph.sexp — dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp cannot hold it without a second concept: its `stage` universe is the 8-node symbolic-only-path pipeline ACQUIRE..PUBLISH (AM/dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:5-21, from V1.8 define-pipeline, ledger :60 IMPORTED) and `stage-edge` has no edge family; adding 20 cognition nodes as `stage`s would merge two graphs into one L4 relation and make PERCEIVE..RESULT a peer of ACQUIRE..PUBLISH. Whether that merge is wanted is the decision below, not a default."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "NEW `cog-node` (id = node symbol, 20 facts; :graph SYMBOL cognition-graph-v8; :kind ENTRY|INTERIOR|TERMINAL from V1.8:64-65) + NEW `cog-edge` (id <FROM>__<TO>__<FAMILY> — the family MUST be in the id because (CLARIFY-DECIDE RESOLVE) is listed under both :flow-edges V1.8:59 and :branch-edges V1.8:60, so FROM__TO alone collides under L2 (ADJ-V18-COG-2); :from ref cog-node; :to ref cog-node; :family FLOW|BRANCH|RESUME|TERMINAL) — 21 facts (13+2+2+4). L4 consequence (verified): the kernel derives an acyclicity duty for EVERY fact type whose :from/:to refs target one node type (KERNEL:211-218), so `cog-edge` over `cog-node` is checked acyclic INCLUDING resume edges — the listed graph passes (SUSPEND→RESUME→RESOLVE never returns to CLARIFY-DECIDE, V1.8:61), so the 'acyclic except resume' wording of V1.8:66-67 is satisfiable by plain L4 with no exemption; a future resume edge back into CLARIFY-DECIDE would be rejected. Optional `cog-graph` (id cognition-graph-v8; :entry ref cog-node) — 1 fact."
  :owner "UNKNOWN as a registry fact (no :owner key V1.8:53-65). Evidence for S04: TM:387 (DFT-07 subsystem S04, owner seat 'legal-dialectic.lisp'); ISR owners of 4 of the 5 registered endpoint types are S04 (ISR:43,117,120,123; AM/interfaces-and-types.sexp:16-19) and PerceptionEnvelope/1 is S02 (ISR:11; :39); S04 'Public Language Cognition Layer' (SR:45-48; AM/subsystems.sexp:8, owner-seat SEAT-LEGAL-AST). source/legal-dialectic.lisp is tracked (git ls-files) but is NO model seat (AM/seats.sexp: none; :33 names greek-nlp-core.lisp 'a further artifact' of S04)."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — a graph definition is not a store; the runtime executor of the graph is the cognition layer (WP-08), whose only model store-writer is SEAT-WRITE-AUTHORITY for legal-ir (AM/stores-and-authorities.sexp:9) — not the writer of the graph."
  :classification "PUBLIC — all 5 model-typed endpoints PUBLIC (AM/interfaces-and-types.sexp:16-19,39); V1.7:81-94 marks every stage :symbolic-only t; no private node. The 12 untyped intermediate records have no classification fact (row 9)."
  :dependencies "(1) V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-cognition-node-types V1.8:363-383 — same batch; node set equality is required (V1.8-VERIFY.py:949-950 'nodes!=node-types'); the graph is untyped without it; (2) LINEAGE (DDI-1): V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-construction-order cognition-stage-dag V1.6:217-229 and V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-construction-order cognition-stage-dag-v7 V1.7:80-94 — same concept, different node sets (12 / 14 / 20), only they carry :seat bindings (V1.7:81-94) — neither declares supersession in the sexp (V1.8 dossier lineage); (3) DDI-2 V1.8 define-closed-enum ClarificationLifecycleState V1.8:28-30 (TERMINAL_* members mirror the TERM-* nodes V1.8:56 by name only); (4) IMPORTED `stage` universe (AM/dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:5-21) — decide same or separate node type; (5) L6: DFT-07 / T8-COGLIFE (TM:387) NOT model facts."
  :consumers ":V8I-COGGRAPH-acyclic-except-resume V1.8:66-71 (dag.json define-invariant -> define-cognition-graph = 1) and :V8I-COG-typed-edges V1.8:386-391 (DDI-4); TM:387 DFT-07; QT:1163 T8-COGLIFE (UNEXECUTED); CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:33 (DFT-07); V1.8-VERIFY.py:899 parses it (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, AM/files-and-roles.sexp:453; MUT table :1629-1645); LanguageCognitionLayer/1.stage_dag_ref (V1.6:215) binds 'the ordered construction DAG' — which version is unstated (V1.6 dossier A11). 0 canonical-model consumers."
  :identity-version-rule "id = `cognition-graph-v8` (TOKEN OK). Third seat of one concept: V1.6:217 cognition-stage-dag (12 stages COG-1..12, seats) → V1.7:80 cognition-stage-dag-v7 (14 stages COG7-01..14, seats, :preserves, :branch) → V1.8:53 cognition-graph-v8 (20 nodes, 4 edge families, NO seats). Node names differ across all three; the V1.6 and V1.7 forms are DDI-1 classes (AM/deferred-imports.sexp:32,43). Relation: SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT by lineage, but NOT declared (no :supersedes in V1.8:53-65; SUPERSEDED-REGISTER.md:257-258 names only the coverage decision). Interpretation 'V1.8 canonical' is a decision, not a fact."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION (canonical version; stage-vs-cog-node universe; where the V1.7 per-stage :seat bindings go)."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "Importing V1.6/V1.7 construction orders in DDI-1 seats a cognition DAG BEFORE this one (two or three graphs for one concept — ADJ-V17-CO-1/ADJ-V18-COG-1); reusing `stage` merges the cognition graph with the pipeline (one L4 relation, one id space — a cognition node named like a pipeline stage would collide; today no name collides: ACQUIRE..PUBLISH vs PERCEIVE..RESULT); the (CLARIFY-DECIDE RESOLVE) edge in two families collides under FROM__TO ids (ADJ-V18-COG-2)."
  :requirement "R-129 (S04 req-map AM/requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:70). Source DFT-07 (TM:387) NOT a model fact — NEW."
  :invariant "L4 (auto-derived for `cog-edge` over `cog-node`, KERNEL:211-218 — covers 'illegal-cycle'), L2 (edge ids with family), L3 (endpoints). Source guards: :V8I-COGGRAPH-acyclic-except-resume V1.8:66-71 (every terminal reachable, no outgoing flow edge from a terminal, entry declared) — reachability and terminal-has-no-outgoing are NOT model laws → NEW check COG-GRAPH (orphan terminal, unreachable node, terminal with outgoing edge, entry not a node)."
  :qualification-test "Existing: Q08 (S04 req-map test :70). Source: T8-COGLIFE (TM:387; QT:1163 UNEXECUTED); legacy V8-COGLIFE 5 named + 10 held-out mutations (V1.8-VERIFY.py:1629-1645) — witness count stated as 3 (V1.8:70-71) vs 7 (V1.8:389-391) (V1.8 dossier unknown). NEW executable statement: T-DDI3-COG-GRAPH — from `cog-edge` facts: every `cog-node` is reachable from :entry PERCEIVE; every node with :kind TERMINAL has out-degree 0 over FLOW/BRANCH/TERMINAL families; every node with out-degree 0 is a declared terminal; the node set equals the `cog-node-type` node set."
  :falsifier "(fact falsifier D3-07-COGNITION-CYCLE :harness COMPONENT :intent \"a flow edge closing the cognition graph into a cycle\" :mutation APPEND :module \"cognition-graph.sexp\" :form \"(fact cog-edge RESULT__PERCEIVE__FLOW :graph cognition-graph-v8 :from RESULT :to PERCEIVE :family FLOW)\" :kernel-reason \"cycle in the cog-edge graph over cog-node\" :checker-reason \"L4\") — enforceable by the EXISTING L4 kernel with no code (KERNEL:219-229); it is the legacy 'illegal-cycle' witness (V1.8-VERIFY.py:1633) rewritten as a corpus row. A second row for the orphan-terminal case needs the NEW COG-GRAPH check."
  :rollback "Drop the NEW module (cog-node/cog-edge/cog-graph facts) and rebuild ROOT.sexp (L7); flip AM/deferred-imports.sexp:58 back; if `stage` reuse was chosen instead, rollback edits dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp (an IMPORTED module) — a stronger reason to keep a separate module. Row 9 (node types) references cog-node ids — roll back together."
  :batch-reason "DDI-3 by BATCH map (AM/build_deferred.py:97 'define-cognition-graph':'DDI-3'; ledger :58 'current source'). DISAGREES: the same concept's earlier versions (V1.6:217, V1.7:80) are DDI-1 define-construction-order classes (AM/deferred-imports.sexp:32,43; ADJ-V17-CO-1) — DDI-1 would seat a cognition DAG two batches before the version choice is made; and the V1.7 :seat strings (V1.7:81-94) resolve to no model seat (ADJ-V17-CO-2). The batch order splits one lineage."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "Which cognition graph is the ONE canonical seat — V1.6:217-229 (12 stages, seats), V1.7:80-94 (14 stages, seats, :preserves flags) or V1.8:53-65 + 363-383 (20 nodes, typed edge families, no seats) — given that no form declares supersession and the first two are scheduled in DDI-1? Are cognition nodes `stage` facts (one L4 universe with the ACQUIRE..PUBLISH pipeline, AM/dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:5-21) or a separate `cog-node` family? Where do the V1.7 per-stage :seat bindings (greek-nlp-core.lisp, greek-tokenizer-advanced.lisp, greek-lemmatizer.lisp, legal-casegrammar.lisp[general], greek-legislation-ontology.lisp, legal-deontic.lisp, legal-dialectic.lisp, legal-qa.lisp — none a model `seat`, AM/seats.sexp:28-100) live once V1.8's seat-less graph is canonical? Does the edge id carry the family (ADJ-V18-COG-2)?"
  :adjudication-items ("ADJ-V18-COG-1 / A8 (V1.6 dossier) / ADJ-V17-CO-1 (three cognition DAG versions in two batches)" "ADJ-V18-COG-2 (edge (CLARIFY-DECIDE RESOLVE) in two families — id must carry the family)" "ADJ-V17-CO-2 / ADJ-V18-NT-4 / A13 (V1.6 dossier) (per-stage :seat files are not model seats)" "A11 (V1.6 dossier): LanguageCognitionLayer/1.stage_dag_ref (V1.6:215) binds which DAG" "ADJ-DDI3-STAGE-1: cognition nodes as `stage` (one L4 universe with the pipeline) vs NEW `cog-node` — the kernel's schema-derived L4 (KERNEL:211-218) makes either checkable; the id-space merge is the cost" "ADJ-DDI3-REQ-3: DFT-07 / T8-COGLIFE exist only in TM:387 / QT:1163 — requirement/test seat (orchestrator N1/N7)" "ADJ-DDI3-MOD-1: module NAME for the DDI-3 function layer is stated three ways by the dossiers — 'decisions-and-projections.sexp' (V1.5 dossier) vs 'decision-functions' (V1.7 and V1.8 dossiers) vs 'cognition-graph' (V1.8 dossier, for the graph) — one name per module must be fixed once; every NEW module is auto-classified CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT by AM/classification-rules.sexp:39-41 (R-008) and must be pinned in AM/ROOT.sexp:12-28 (:module-count 14 today) under L7." "ADJ-DDI3-EXEC-1 (= dossier ADJ-V18-EXEC-1, widened to every DDI-3 class): the only program that has ever executed a DDI-3 contract is V1.8-VERIFY.py / V1.5-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, AM/files-and-roles.sexp:436,453; AM/LEGACY-AUDIT-DISPOSITION.md:10 'never a blocking or sufficient acceptance gate'); the model's harness universe executes laws L1-L7 only (AM/verification-corpus.sexp:24-58,122-125; KERNEL:346). Which harness (existing COMPONENT harness with new schema-derived checks, or a NEW harness fact) executes imported decision/graph contracts, or are they imported as inert data with a declared reason?")
  :topological-position 33 :atomic-groups (2 3)
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "`cog-node` facts (graph, node, kind ENTRY/INTERIOR/TERMINAL) + `cog-edge` facts (graph, from, to, family FLOW/BRANCH/RESUME/TERMINAL) in a NEW module, not in the `stage`/`stage-edge` universe of the 8-node symbolic pipeline (dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:5-21) — the graph is a value the traversal interpreter reads, never a structure it mutates; the edge (CLARIFY-DECIDE RESOLVE) listed in two families (V1.8:59-60) needs family in the id or it is an L2 collision (ADJ-V18-COG-2) | invariant: :V8I-COGGRAPH-acyclic-except-resume (V1.8:66-71) — acyclicity is a property of an immutable edge set | fallback: adjacency list" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "one generic function per node kind with eql-specialized methods on the node designator — the admitted seat pattern source/cognition.lisp:101-118 (defgeneric synthesize / triage / critique; plan, execute-step exported :28) named by contract:21 ('open dispatch for analyzers/stages/adapters; dispatch is total or errors typed') — with the traversal ORDER driven by `cog-edge` facts instead of the hard-coded 5-stage sequence of cognition.lisp:123-135 (%run-stages 'Στάδια 2→5 (με 4.5)') which is a DIFFERENT, older pipeline than the 20-node v8 graph (CL-DDI3-A2) | invariant: contract:21 dispatch total or typed error; :V8I-COG-typed-edges (every node has exactly its declared in/out) | fallback: single dispatch function (contract:21 fallback)" :condition-restart "CLARIFY-SUSPEND / CLARIFY-RESUME (V1.8:56,60-61) is the condition/restart the registries themselves name (V1.6:227 ':seat legal-dialectic.lisp + condition/restart'; V1.7:91 same; contract:24 'cognition clarification (COG7-11)'): CLARIFY-DECIDE signals a typed condition carrying ClarificationRequest/1; RESUME is a restart taking a ClarificationResponse/1 whose resume_binding_ref (V1.8:38, 384-385) must bind the exact suspended instance — restarts invoked PROGRAMMATICALLY with a typed argument as in source/trace-core.lisp:264-277 (provide-trace: 'καμία read-then-eval οδός') and source/legal-ast.lisp:1600-1612 (use-empty-node / skip-node / provide-node); LIMIT: a restart lives in the dynamic extent of its restart-case, so a clarification answered in a later session cannot be a live restart — it must re-enter RESOLVE from a persisted request (see persistent_event; CL-DDI3-A3) | invariant: contract:24 'every error is a typed condition; no silent failure'; V1.8:67-69 resume binds the exact suspended instance; TERM-UNDERDETERMINED is the typed no-answer value (V1.8:62) | fallback: return a typed error value / terminal (contract:24 fallback)" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE" :protocol "the typed node protocol in-type -> out-type per node (define-cognition-node-types V1.8:363-383) with the mandatory path SYMBOLIC ONLY: every v1.7 stage is :symbolic-only t (V1.7:81-94) and the v8 node set has NO proposer node (V1.8:54-56) — proposers (S03, consumer-role PROPOSER MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:48-50) can attach only as optional adapters (V1.6 adapter contracts :mandatory nil :replaceable t, orchestrator note N13) | invariant: :V8I-02-no-mandatory-model (V1.8:17-19) 'Removing every proposer leaves a semantically-equivalent SYMBOLIC_ONLY mandatory path' | fallback: symbolic-only path" :package-asdf-boundary "node->package binding as facts — the :seat column of V1.7:81-94 (greek-nlp-core, greek-tokenizer-advanced, greek-lemmatizer, legal-casegrammar[general], greek-legislation-ontology, legal-deontic + legal-event-calculus, legal-dialectic, legal-extraction-verify + legal-ast, legal-qa) that V1.8 DROPPED (ADJ-V18-NT-4) — so that the edge set is also the allowed inter-package dependency set; existing packages: orchestrator.cognition (cognition.lisp:23), orchestrator.dialectic (legal-dialectic.lisp:14), orchestrator.deliberation (deliberation.lisp:27, used by cognition.lisp:126); none of cognition.lisp / deliberation.lisp / legal-dialectic.lisp is a model seat (seats.sexp: NOT FOUND); all are components of ONE ASDF system orchestrator-infrastructure.asd:5 (CL-DDI3-A6) | invariant: contract:31 'package boundary = capability boundary'; ASDF graph acyclic | fallback: monolith package (the present state)" :persistent-event "ClarificationRequest/1 and ClarificationResponse/1 as journaled events through the one journal idiom (source/journal.lisp:507 chained-append; canon-sexp :61-68 for the content hash) so RESUME can bind the exact instance after the suspending process has ended — resume_binding_ref = content-address of the persisted request; MemoryEvent/1 is a VERIFIED canonical identity (V1.8:429) | invariant: exact-instance binding (V1.8:67-69, 384-388); monotone transaction time (journal.lisp:252-262); canonical writes only via write-authority (contract:33; source/write-authority.lisp:16-30 emit-graph 'ONLY authorized write function') | fallback: in-process restart only (no cross-session resume)" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE" :compile-time-validation "model-build laws over the new facts, enforced generically by BOTH verification paths (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:1-2): acyclic over flow+branch+terminal families; the resume family declared EXEMPT as data rather than hard-coded in the checker (the legacy guard hard-codes it: V1.8-VERIFY.py:1629-1645); every terminal reachable with no outgoing flow edge; out(src)=in(tgt) per edge (with `cog-node-type`); L2 uniqueness catching the double-listed edge (V1.8:59-60) — the same fixture discipline as FX-L4-PIPELINE-CYCLE (verification-corpus.sexp:32-33) but over a SEPARATE relation, since the L4 fixture is defined over stage-edge | invariant: :V8I-COGGRAPH-acyclic-except-resume (V1.8:66-71); :V8I-COG-typed-edges (V1.8:386-391) | fallback: runtime check on graph load" :runtime-validation "at each node entry the value is checked against the node's declared :in type (check-type; frozen-set idiom capability-registry.lisp:54-59 fail-closed); a mismatch is a typed condition routed to TERM-ERROR (V1.8:63) | invariant: :V8I-COG-typed-edges | fallback: reject to TERM-ERROR" :python-in-cl-risk "HIGH. The naive import is a dict {nodes:[...], flow_edges:[[a,b],...]} plus a DFS validator with `if node == 'CLARIFY-RESUME': skip` — which is literally V1.8-VERIFY.py:897-902 cog_model and :1629-1645 (resume exemption hard-coded in the checker); in CL the equivalent is a hard-coded stage sequence, which cognition.lisp:123-135 already is. CL-native alternative: graph as facts; traversal = generic dispatch per node (cognition.lisp:107 pattern) reading `cog-edge`; suspension = typed condition + restart + journaled event; acyclicity/reachability/typing = generic build-time laws over a declared relation with the resume exemption as data." :future-freedom "S04 cognition: HIGH STAKES. (a) Three graph versions are simultaneously authoritative at source (V1.6:217 12 stages with seats; V1.7:80 13 stages with seats, :preserves, :no-forced-winner, :binds-exact-candidate; V1.8:53 20 nodes without seats — ADJ-V18-COG-1); importing V1.8 alone loses the seat binding and the information-preservation flags (:V7I-COG-info-preserving V1.7:95), reducing what the future can verify. (b) The existing cognition.lisp is a 5-stage design with an `*advisor*` hook (cognition.lisp:25-30) and is not a model seat — the v8 graph must not be bent to its stage order (CL-DDI3-A2). (c) Proposer attachment: no PROPOSE node exists — where S03 SemanticProposer plugs in is UNKNOWN. S19 memory: the graph has no memory node; cognition.lisp:42 working-memory vs SEAT-MEMORY source/memory.lisp (seats.sexp:56) is unbound by this import — UNKNOWN, not constrained. JTMS: RESOLVE/PROMOTE feed legal inference; the graph does not constrain it. S20 / V8I-02: preserved — the graph is symbolic-only and adapter-free (V1.7:81-94 :symbolic-only t on every stage).")
  )

(ddi-class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-dimension-policy
  :batch DDI-3 :source-file "V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp" :fact-class "define-dimension-policy" :source-count 1 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms (("root-authority-dimensions" :line 88 :sha16 "9dfbac8b2307366c"))
  :source-file "deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp"
  :source-forms 1
  :current-authority-seat "V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp, section ';; ==== 2. ROOT-AUTHORITY PRODUCT STATE + PROJECTION (DFT-10 + §2)' (V1.8:73-74: 'No scalar stored truth. Orthogonal product state; deterministic DERIVED projection preserving all causes'), form root-authority-dimensions V1.8:88-96 (8 rows: security, proof_integrity, freshness, rights, coverage, availability_ops, juris_access, qualification), following DimensionState V1.8:75, RootAuthorityStatus/1 V1.8:76-82, RelianceClass V1.8:83, RelianceProjection/1 V1.8:84-87; invariant :V8I-RASTATUS-product V1.8:97-103. Ledger: AM/deferred-imports.sexp:60 (DDI-3). TM:390 (DFT-10, S14, owner seat 'provider_registry', T8-RASTATUS, WP-14). CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:51-52 claims 'The Acceptance Matrix carries dimension | mandatory/advisory | failure value | recovery evidence | authority' — VERIFIED FALSE for V1.7-ROOT-AUTHORITY-ACCEPTANCE-MATRIX.md (grep proof_integrity|availability_ops|juris_access = 0)."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "NEW:decision-functions.sexp (the policy table is the input of reliance-of, row 10 — one module for the function and its parameters). Alternative stores-and-authorities.sexp only if :authority becomes a `seat` ref — but that module is one fact per STORE (:1) and a dimension is not a store; interfaces-and-types.sexp holds types, not policies. No existing module fits without a second concept."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "NEW `dimension-policy` (id <policy>__<dimension>, e.g. root-authority-dimensions__security; :policy SYMBOL; :dimension SYMBOL — one of the 8 DimensionState-typed fields of RootAuthorityStatus/1 V1.8:78-80 (exact 8=8 correspondence verified); :class MANDATORY|ADVISORY (NEW enum); :failure SYMBOL — a RelianceClass member V1.8:83 (WITHHELD / MACHINE_UNVERIFIED / ATTRIBUTED_RELIANCE; FULL_RELIANCE unused); :recovery-evidence STRING; :authority — UNRESOLVED: source values are free strings ('security cell', 'MLTP root', 'coverage owner', 'legal counsel', 'observatory', 'independent auditor', V1.8:89-96); either `:authority-seat ref seat` (4 of 6 loosely match SEAT-SECURITY-CELLS :79, SEAT-KERNEL-VERIFY :44, SEAT-COVERAGE-OWNER :83, SEAT-OBSERVATORY-COLLECTOR :81 of AM/seats.sexp; 'legal counsel' and 'independent auditor' match none) or `:authority-external STRING` — decision) — 8 facts. Plus optional `policy` (id root-authority-dimensions; :status-type ref type RootAuthorityStatus/1) — 1 fact."
  :owner "UNKNOWN as a registry fact (no :owner key). Evidence for S14: ISR:110-115 (RootAuthorityStatus/1 and RelianceProjection/1 :owner S14, signature-owner 'root-authority aggregator'); AM/interfaces-and-types.sexp:46,54 (S14 PUBLIC); TM:390 (DFT-10 subsystem S14, owner seat 'provider_registry' — NOT a tracked path: git ls-files 'provider_registry' = none; S14's model seat is SEAT-CAPABILITY-API source/capability-api.lisp, AM/seats.sexp:50-51)."
  :writer "NO_WRITER for the policy table (normative parameters). The per-dimension :authority strings name who may certify RECOVERY (V1.8:88-96) — these are not `seat` ids and two of them ('legal counsel', 'independent auditor') are external parties; a writer cannot be assigned without the ADJ-V18-DIM-1 decision."
  :classification "PUBLIC — S14 PUBLIC (AM/subsystems.sexp:18); RootAuthorityStatus/1 and RelianceProjection/1 PUBLIC (AM/interfaces-and-types.sexp:54,46); consumers S14/S15 PUBLIC (AM/dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:89,92,97,100). No private member; the 'juris_access' dimension's evidence 'lawful access + DPA review' (V1.8:95) is a string, not a private type."
  :dependencies "(1) DDI-2 V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum RelianceClass V1.8:83 (:failure values) and DimensionState V1.8:75 (states named in the rule of row 10); (2) DDI-2 V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-record RootAuthorityStatus/1 V1.8:76-82 (the 8 dimension fields; model `type` exists AM/interfaces-and-types.sexp:54) and RelianceProjection/1 V1.8:84-87 (:46); (3) IMPORTED seats if :authority is resolved to seat refs (AM/seats.sexp:44,79,81,83) — 2 authorities have no seat; (4) SCHEMA: enum family (ADJ-DDI3-ENUM-1) + NEW MANDATORY|ADVISORY enum; (5) L6: DFT-10 / T8-RASTATUS (TM:390) NOT model facts; (6) document seat: the table is claimed to live in the Acceptance Matrix (CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:51-52) — it does not (ADJ-V18-DIM-2)."
  :consumers "reliance-of V1.8:411-414 (:rule reads MANDATORY/ADVISORY class and failure-class(d), V1.8:408-410,413) — same batch; :V8I-RASTATUS-product V1.8:97-103 (DDI-4); TM:390 DFT-10; QT:1163 T8-RASTATUS; CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:49-52; V1.8-VERIFY.py:1120 parses it, MUT :1656-1673 (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE). 0 canonical-model consumers."
  :identity-version-rule "id = `root-authority-dimensions` (TOKEN OK); rows keyed by :dimension keyword (unique within the form — verified 8 distinct, V1.8:89-96). ONLY-VERSION (unique to V1.8; grep outside V1.8 = 0 per V1.8 dossier). Conceptual predecessor: scalar RootAuthorityState V1.7:241 + RootAuthorityQualification/1 V1.7:242 (still a model type AM/interfaces-and-types.sexp:53; ISR A10 'superseded pairs kept live')."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION (:authority shape; document seat of the table; MANDATORY/ADVISORY enum)."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "If :authority is imported as free text it creates 6 untyped authority names beside the 33 typed seats (AM/seats.sexp:1-100 doctrine: '\"none\" as a bare word is not an answer', :19) — an unconstrained-string regression of exactly the kind Review-2 N-10 removed (AM/seats.sexp:3-8). CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:51-52 names a second (document) seat for the table that does not exist. RootAuthorityQualification/1 (V1.7) remains a live model type beside RootAuthorityStatus/1 (ISR A10)."
  :requirement "R-102 (S14 req-map AM/requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:80). Source DFT-10 (TM:390) NOT a model fact — NEW."
  :invariant "L1 (enums MANDATORY|ADVISORY, RelianceClass), L2 (one row per dimension — id <policy>__<dimension> makes a duplicate dimension an L2 duplicate id), L3 (:authority-seat → seat, if chosen). Source guard: :V8I-RASTATUS-product V1.8:97-103 (proof_integrity SEPARATE and MANDATORY; never merged into security). NEW check: the dimension set equals the DimensionState-typed field set of RootAuthorityStatus/1 (8 = 8) — requires DDI-2 record fields as facts."
  :qualification-test "Existing: Q27 (S14 req-map test :80). Source: T8-RASTATUS (TM:390; QT:1163 UNEXECUTED); legacy V8-RASTATUS full 4^8 product (V1.8-VERIFY.py:1233-1240; SUPERSEDED-REGISTER.md:286-287). NEW executable statement: T-DDI3-DIM-POLICY — exactly 8 `dimension-policy` facts for root-authority-dimensions, dimensions pairwise distinct and equal to the 8 DimensionState fields of RootAuthorityStatus/1, every :failure a RelianceClass member other than FULL_RELIANCE, proof_integrity and security both MANDATORY."
  :falsifier "(fact falsifier D3-08-BOGUS-FAILURE-CLASS :harness COMPONENT :intent \"a dimension whose failure maps to a reliance class that does not exist\" :mutation REPLACE :module \"decision-functions.sexp\" :replace-from \":dimension security :class MANDATORY :failure WITHHELD\" :replace-to \":dimension security :class MANDATORY :failure BOGUS_CLASS\" :kernel-reason \"resolves to no declared enum-value\" :checker-reason \"L3\") — legacy 'held/bogus-failure-class' (V1.8-VERIFY.py:1662) as a corpus row; needs the enum-value family. NOTE: the legacy 'held/policy-weaken-security' (MANDATORY→ADVISORY, :1663) is a policy-content change that NO model law rejects — only the NEW T-DDI3-DIM-POLICY assertion 'security MANDATORY' would."
  :rollback "Drop the 8 `dimension-policy` (+1 `policy`) facts, rebuild ROOT.sexp (L7), flip AM/deferred-imports.sexp:60 back; row 10 (reliance-of) references the policy — roll back together."
  :batch-reason "DDI-3 by BATCH map (AM/build_deferred.py:97 'define-dimension-policy':'DDI-3'; ledger :60). AGREES: dependencies are DDI-2 enums/records (V1.8:75-87) and IMPORTED seats; consumer reliance-of is same-batch. The table is a 'decision' parameter set, matching the batch title."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "What is :authority (V1.8:89-96) in the model — a typed `seat` reference (then which seat for 'legal counsel' and 'independent auditor', which match none of the 33 seats, and is the loose mapping security cell→SEAT-SECURITY-CELLS / MLTP root→SEAT-KERNEL-VERIFY / coverage owner→SEAT-COVERAGE-OWNER / observatory→SEAT-OBSERVATORY-COLLECTOR authored by whom?) or an explicit EXTERNAL-party marker outside the seat universe? And where is the table's document seat, given CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:51-52 names the Acceptance Matrix and V1.7-ROOT-AUTHORITY-ACCEPTANCE-MATRIX.md does not contain it?"
  :adjudication-items ("ADJ-V18-DIM-1 (:authority strings are not seats)" "ADJ-V18-DIM-2 (Acceptance Matrix does not carry the table — VERIFIED, grep 0)" "A10 (ISR dossier): RootAuthorityQualification/1 (V1.7) vs RootAuthorityStatus/1 (V1.8) both live model types" "ADJ-DDI3-REQ-4: DFT-10 / T8-RASTATUS only in TM:390 / QT:1163; TM's owner seat 'provider_registry' is not a tracked path" "ADJ-DDI3-ENUM-1: no enum / enum-value fact family exists in AM/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:84-288 (34 fact types); every DDI-3 clause value, :output, :failure, :order and :result-when-insufficient is an enum member of a DDI-2 define-closed-enum / define-frozen-enum-reference form. Until DDI-2 seats enums as facts, DDI-3 values can only be bare SYMBOLs with no L3 closure (KERNEL:196-210 checks :ref targets only)." "ADJ-DDI3-MOD-1: module NAME for the DDI-3 function layer is stated three ways by the dossiers — 'decisions-and-projections.sexp' (V1.5 dossier) vs 'decision-functions' (V1.7 and V1.8 dossiers) vs 'cognition-graph' (V1.8 dossier, for the graph) — one name per module must be fixed once; every NEW module is auto-classified CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT by AM/classification-rules.sexp:39-41 (R-008) and must be pinned in AM/ROOT.sexp:12-28 (:module-count 14 today) under L7." "ADJ-DDI3-EXEC-1 (= dossier ADJ-V18-EXEC-1, widened to every DDI-3 class): the only program that has ever executed a DDI-3 contract is V1.8-VERIFY.py / V1.5-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, AM/files-and-roles.sexp:436,453; AM/LEGACY-AUDIT-DISPOSITION.md:10 'never a blocking or sufficient acceptance gate'); the model's harness universe executes laws L1-L7 only (AM/verification-corpus.sexp:24-58,122-125; KERNEL:346). Which harness (existing COMPONENT harness with new schema-derived checks, or a NEW harness fact) executes imported decision/graph contracts, or are they imported as inert data with a declared reason?")
  :topological-position 35 :atomic-groups (6)
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "8 `dimension-policy` facts (dimension, class MANDATORY|ADVISORY, failure RelianceClass-value, recovery-evidence STRING, authority -> typed ref or EXTERNAL_PARTY token) — a policy TABLE versioned by policy_epoch (RootAuthorityStatus/1.policy_epoch :semver V1.8:82), immutable per epoch | invariant: :V8I-RASTATUS-product (V1.8:97-103): exactly 8 typed dimensions, proof_integrity SEPARATE from security, 'never turns recovery of one dimension into silent recovery of another' | fallback: alist" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart "NOT-APPLICABLE" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE" :protocol "WHO may certify recovery: :authority as a typed reference into `seat` — 'MLTP root' ~ SEAT-KERNEL-VERIFY (seats.sexp:44), 'coverage owner' ~ SEAT-COVERAGE-OWNER (:83), 'observatory' ~ SEAT-OBSERVATORY-COLLECTOR (:81), 'security cell' ~ SEAT-SECURITY-CELLS (:79) — or an explicit EXTERNAL_PARTY token for 'legal counsel' / 'independent auditor'; no registry states the mapping (ADJ-V18-DIM-1) | invariant: L3 closed refs + 'forbids self-qualification' (V1.8:102) — self-qualification is structurally impossible only when the certifying authority is a typed seat distinct from the subject | fallback: free-text string (the present state)" :package-asdf-boundary "S14 package (ISR:110 owner of RootAuthorityStatus/1; subsystems.sexp:18 owner-seat SEAT-CAPABILITY-API source/capability-api.lisp seats.sexp:50; TRACEABILITY:390 names 'provider_registry' which is NOT FOUND in source — CL-DDI3-A8); producers of dimension states (S10 proof_integrity, S01 coverage, S11 security) write DimensionState values one-way and never read the policy | invariant: contract:31; one-way producer->aggregator dependency | fallback: monolith package" :persistent-event "the policy table is hash-pinned (L7 module hash) and every stored RootAuthorityStatus/1 names its policy_epoch + measured_at + signature (V1.8:82); per-dimension recovery is JOURNALED (V1.8:101-102) through journal.lisp:507 chained-append | invariant: a status without its policy epoch is not interpretable; monotone transaction time (journal.lisp:252) | fallback: embed a policy copy in each status" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE" :temporal-index-projection "evaluation is keyed by (measured_at, policy_epoch) (V1.8:82): the policy epoch is the invalidation key of contract:30 ('a cache entry names its validation epoch; epoch change invalidates') | invariant: policy change invalidates every derived projection | fallback: no cache" :compile-time-validation "build-time: exactly 8 rows = the 8 DimensionState fields of RootAuthorityStatus/1 (V1.8:78-80) as a `property-family` of EXACT cardinality (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:221-223); every :failure in RelianceClass (V1.8:83) and every :class in {MANDATORY, ADVISORY} by L1 closed enums; the row<->field correspondence needs DDI-2 record-field facts for L3 | invariant: :V8I-RASTATUS-product | fallback: runtime check" :runtime-validation "a RootAuthorityStatus/1 whose policy_epoch names an unknown policy version, or carries a dimension absent from the table, raises a typed condition (pattern capability-api.lisp:35 coercion-error under a typed hierarchy) — never reinterpreted under another epoch | invariant: no silent reinterpretation (V8I-RASTATUS 'never ... silent recovery') | fallback: reject" :python-in-cl-risk "MEDIUM. Naive import = 8 dicts with free-text authority and keyword failure values as strings; downstream, the aggregation loop of V1.8-VERIFY.py:1222-1232 reads them as (dn, cl, fl) tuples. CL-native alternative: 8 typed facts with :authority as a closed reference or an explicit external-party token, consumed by ONE fold (reliance-of) whose inputs are the facts themselves — so the policy is inspectable by both verification paths and by the runtime from one seat." :future-freedom "S04/S19/JTMS: NONE. S20 / V8I-02: NONE. Constraints on the import: (a) :authority strings naming humans ('legal counsel', 'independent auditor') cannot become seats — an EXTERNAL_PARTY token must be admitted; (b) the prose carrier claimed by CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:51-52 does not carry the table (ADJ-V18-DIM-2), so the model module would become the ONLY seat — acceptable but must be decided, not assumed.")
  )

