  :source-file "V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp"
  :source-forms 9
  :current-authority-seat "V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp §3 'RA-EPOCH — citation identity + crypto commitments' (header L105): USC-expression L107-108; §15 'CANONICAL REFERENCES (DFT-03, real file+locator)' (header L343, doctrine at L418-424 'the reference is the identity seat, the define-record remains the structure seat'): LegalIR/1 L345, TrustBundle/1 L346, MemoryEvent/1 L347, CognitionResult/1 L348, DeclassificationReceipt/1 L349, ResolverResult/1 L350, DatasetSnapshot/1 L351, RightsMatrix/1 L352. Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:67 (DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE, DDI-2, :source-count 9)."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "The module and family chosen in DDI-1 for V1.8 define-canonical-identity (deferred-imports.sexp:59) — these 9 forms and those 8 rows are the SAME payload for 8 of the same 8 identities (V1.8:425-432 point at these very blocks by :type-locator 'define-reference X'). Splitting them across two modules or two families would be the clearest possible duplicate seat. interfaces-and-types.sexp if identity becomes optional fields of `type`; a NEW module only if a separate family is chosen (ADJ-DDI2-IDENTITY-FAMILY)."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "The DDI-1 identity family, in the V1.8 shape: (:subject <type> :identity STRING :version STRING :canonical-file STRING :locator STRING). This is the most machine-checkable of the three reference vocabularies in the six registries — it is the only one whose anchor can be OPENED (:canonical-file is a real path, :locator a real string), which is what :V8I-XREF-real (V1.8:353-357) and :V8I-XREF-identity (V1.8:433-441) require. USC-expression is the ONE form whose subject is NOT a type: 'USC-expression' has no /1 suffix, is not an ISR interface and names the Expression LEVEL of the Universal Source Contract (V1.8:107-108, :identity 'lawmax/expression/1'). Either the family admits a non-type subject or that form needs its own home — the nearest existing shape is `rationale` (:doc :anchor, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:182-184; rationale-references.sexp:1-7). 9 facts, values already flat. no `enum`/`enum-value`/`field`/`primitive`/`cardinality`/`ref-class`/`adapter`/`canonical-identity` fact type exists among the 34 fact types (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:84-288); `define-enum` there is schema syntax for the model's own closed domains only (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:18,47-76); L1 forbids keywords, nested lists and NIL as values (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6) and the closed field set forbids adding keys to `type` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:9-13,148-152)"
  :owner "8 declared and agreeing (ISR + model): S04 LegalIR/1 (ISR:15; interfaces-and-types.sexp:32), S10 TrustBundle/1 (ISR:33; :61), S19 MemoryEvent/1 (ISR:17; :34), S04 CognitionResult/1 (ISR:43; :19), S18 DeclassificationReceipt/1 (ISR:35; :23), S25 ResolverResult/1 (ISR:79; :50), S14 DatasetSnapshot/1 (ISR:93; :22), S25 RightsMatrix/1 (ISR:87; :52). UNKNOWN for USC-expression: the Universal Source Contract is not a subsystem seat — seats.sexp has no USC seat, and S16's seat is the source-type authority registry document (seats.sexp:70-72). The document itself is AUTHORED_NORMATIVE_PROSE (files-and-roles.sexp:48)."
  :writer "NO_WRITER for the identity facts. Store-declared writers exist for 4 of the 8 subjects: legal-ir writer SEAT-WRITE-AUTHORITY (stores-and-authorities.sexp:9), trust-bundle writer SEAT-MLTP-THRESHOLD-CUSTODY (:14), memory writer SEAT-WRITE-AUTHORITY (:10), dataset-distribution writer SEAT-RA-T-SIGNER (:7); resolver-dataset writer is the declared SEAT-NO-WRITER (:11). CognitionResult/1, DeclassificationReceipt/1 and RightsMatrix/1 have no store — UNKNOWN."
  :classification "PUBLIC — all 8 type subjects are PUBLIC `type` facts (interfaces-and-types.sexp:32,61,34,19,23,50,22,52) and all 8 are members of the V1.8 public closure roots (V1.8:260-261). USC-expression references a PUBLIC normative document. No private member. DeclassificationReceipt/1 is again the boundary case: PUBLIC, and consumed by the PRIVATE S22 (dependencies-and-boundaries.sexp:110), which L5 permits (only PUBLIC-consumes-PRIVATE fails, KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:252-254)."
  :dependencies ("DDI-1 FIRST: V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-canonical-identity (deferred-imports.sexp:59) — 8 of its rows name these blocks; the family is created there — reference kind: shared fact family" "SAME BATCH: V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-record / define-reference and V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-record — 5 of the 9 :canonical-file values point INTO those migration sources (V1.8:347 -> source/memory.lisp is the exception; :348,:349 -> V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp; :350,:351,:352 -> V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp)" "EXISTING model facts: 8 `type` facts (all present) — :subject ref targets" "EXISTING repo artifacts: all 9 :canonical-file paths exist and all 9 :locator strings occur in them (verified by the V1.8 dossier's own grep) — deployment/LAWMAX-UNIVERSAL-SOURCE-CONTRACT.md (locator at USC:147,150), deployment/LAWMAX-LEGAL-IR-SEMANTIC-CONTRACT.md ('Counterproof' at :55,175,197), MACHINE-LEGAL-TRUST-PROTOCOL.md ('TrustBundle' at :21,88,153), source/memory.lisp ('record-episode' at :10,30,79)" "DECISION FIRST: the identity family; the competing V1.6/V1.7 reference blocks for 4 of these identities; what the pointers point at after DDI-2")
  :consumers ("V1.8 define-canonical-identity (V1.8:425-432, DDI-1) — 8 refs, each naming a §15 block by :type-locator; dag.json 'V1.8 define-canonical-identity (rank 1) -> V1.8 define-reference (rank 2), 8 refs'" "V1.7 define-ra-closure-roots (DDI-1) — 7 refs; V1.8 define-ra-closure-roots (DDI-1) — 7 refs; V1.7 define-pipeline (DDI-1) — 2 refs; V1.7/V1.8 define-capability-seat (DDI-1) — 1+1 refs; V1.6/V1.7 define-construction-order (DDI-1) — 1+1 refs" "SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY define-subsystem (IMPORTED) — 6 refs; ISR define-interface (IMPORTED) — 1 ref (ISR:136)" "V1.6 define-invariant (DDI-4) — 7 refs; V1.6 define-ref-classification-v6 (DDI-2) — 4 refs; V1.8 define-cognition-node-types (DDI-3) — 1 ref" "CanonicalCitationURI/1.expression_ref (V1.8:113) consumes USC-expression; :V8I-EPOCH-one-expression (V1.8:128-135) is its invariant" "legacy reader V1.8-VERIFY.py:410,727 — HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:453; LEGACY-AUDIT-DISPOSITION.md:1-6 'never a blocking or sufficient acceptance gate')" "no tracked source/ or systems/ file names any record/enum id of the six registries (git grep at RO = 0); the only mechanical readers are the legacy audits/harness classified HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:436,440,444,450,453)")
  :identity-version-rule "MIXED. SUPERSEDED-DIVERGENT / COMPETING (4): LegalIR/1 (V1.8:345 vs V1.6:96 — V1.6 names legal-ast.lisp AND the contract .md, matching ISR:15; V1.8 names the .md alone), TrustBundle/1 (V1.8:346 vs V1.6:143 — file+locator vs prose), CognitionResult/1 (V1.8:348 vs V1.7:39 — file+locator vs prose section), DeclassificationReceipt/1 (V1.8:349 vs V1.6:147 — and V1.8's locator resolves to the V1.6 REFERENCE block, so it is a reference to a reference). ONLY-VERSION AS A REFERENCE, FIRST OF ITS KIND (4): MemoryEvent/1, ResolverResult/1, DatasetSnapshot/1, RightsMatrix/1 — V1.8:420-421 calls these 'the four formerly UNRESOLVED types' now resolved at their §15 seats. ONLY-VERSION (1): USC-expression. ALSO DUPLICATED IN AN EARLIER BATCH (8): every type reference here is repeated by define-canonical-identity (V1.8:425-432, DDI-1) with the same identity and version — two forms, one payload, two batches."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION, and the block is inherited from DDI-1: whichever fact the DDI-1 define-canonical-identity import writes for these 8 identities, THIS class must MERGE-INTO-EXISTING-FACT rather than write a second one (L2). For LegalIR/1, TrustBundle/1, CognitionResult/1 and DeclassificationReceipt/1 the choice between the V1.6/V1.7 pointer and the V1.8 pointer is an adjudication. For USC-expression, either the family widens or the form is IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL into the `rationale` family (:doc/:anchor) — a different family for the same kind of statement, which is itself a seat question."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "HIGHEST in DDI-2 for identity. Eight identities are stated TWICE inside V1.8 alone (§15 define-reference and §17 define-canonical-identity) and four of them a THIRD time in V1.6/V1.7 — three statements, three key vocabularies, two batches. V1.8:420-422 legitimises the reference/record split but says nothing about the reference/canonical-identity split. Five :canonical-file values anchor INSIDE files that files-and-roles.sexp:441,447 classify CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT and that DDI-2 imports (V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp x2, V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp x3) — after the import the model would point at a superseded source, which is the stale-anchor class of defect orchestrator-notes.md N17 documents live in `rationale`. RightsMatrix/1 has TWO document anchors: V1.8:352 (V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp) and V1.8:248 + ISR:87 (LAWMAX-LICENSE-POLICY.md:44)."
  :requirement "Partial, via owners: R-129/Q08 via S04__WP-08 (requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:70), R-130/Q28 via S10__WP-06 (:76), R-V6-MEM/V6Q-02 via S19__FUTURE_BOOK_REVISION (:85), R-111/Q20 via S18__WP-12 (:84), R-V6-RESOLVE/RA-Q-RESOLVE via S25__FUTURE_BOOK_REVISION (:94), R-102/Q27 via S14__WP-11 (:80). NONE for USC-expression. The source's own binding for §15 is the invariant pair :V8I-XREF-real / :V8I-XREF-identity, neither of which is a model requirement or test."
  :invariant "L2 (one id per fact type — the identity payload merges into the existing `type`, never a second fact), L3 (:subject closed). Source invariants: :V8I-XREF-real (V1.8:353-357) and :V8I-XREF-identity (V1.8:433-441), whose five named mutations are 'wrong-file, wrong-identity, wrong-version, locator-absent-from-canonical-file, wrong-reference-target' (V1.8:440-441). NEITHER verification path implements an anchor resolver (my own grep of gate_checks.py and KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp finds none) — the model can check that a ref names a declared fact, never that a file contains a string. This is the same structural hole as the live RAT-PUBPRIV defect (rationale-references.sexp:7; orchestrator-notes.md N17): one anchor-resolving check would close both."
  :qualification-test "NEW, and it is the highest-value new check in DDI-2. Executable one-liner: for every identity fact, (1) :subject resolves to a declared `type`; (2) the path in :canonical-file exists in the candidate tree (git ls-files); (3) `grep -F -- '<locator>' <canonical-file>` matches at least once; (4) :canonical-file is not one of the six migration sources whose class has already been imported. Clause (3) is exactly the V8I-XREF-real mechanism the source demands and no gate performs; clause (4) is the staleness guard the import itself creates the need for. Applying (2)+(3) to the 5 existing `rationale` facts immediately reproduces the RAT-PUBPRIV finding."
  :falsifier "REPLACE `:locator \"Counterproof\"` with `:locator \"NoSuchLocator\"` on the imported LegalIR/1 identity — must be REJECTED with reason 'locator absent from canonical file' (the mutation V1.8:440-441 names); today NOTHING rejects it on either path. REPLACE `:canonical-file \"source/memory.lisp\"` with `\"source/no-such-file.lisp\"` on MemoryEvent/1 — must be rejected as a missing canonical file (compare `gate_checks.py seats`, which already resolves seat :path values against tracked paths — seats.sexp:12-13 states that obligation). APPEND `(fact canonical-identity USC-expression :subject USC-expression :identity \"lawmax/expression/1\" :version \"1\" :canonical-file \"deployment/LAWMAX-UNIVERSAL-SOURCE-CONTRACT.md\" :locator \"lawmax/expression/1\")` while USC-expression is not a declared `type` — both paths must reject with kernel-reason 'resolves to no declared type', checker-reason 'L3'; this falsifier IS the proof that the family must widen or the form must move."
  :rollback "delete the imported facts of this class and the fact-type/enum declarations added to MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp for it, re-run build_root.py so ROOT.sexp re-pins the 14 modules (ROOT.sexp:12-27; L7), and restore the ledger row to DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT / AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE (deferred-imports.sexp) so the source file is authoritative again; the source registry is never edited by the import (V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp:256 'v1.5 files are NOT edited' is the precedent)"
  :batch-reason "DDI-2 because build_deferred.py maps define-reference to DDI-2, materialised at deferred-imports.sexp:67. DISAGREES: its identity twin define-canonical-identity is DDI-1 (deferred-imports.sexp:59) and REFERENCES it 8 times (dag.json order violation, rank 1 -> rank 2) — the successor form imports before the form it cites. Six further DDI-1 classes reference it (V1.7/V1.8 define-ra-closure-roots 7+7, V1.7 define-pipeline 2, V1.7/V1.8 define-capability-seat 1+1, V1.6/V1.7 define-construction-order 1+1) and two IMPORTED classes reference it (SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY 6, ISR 1). In the other direction its own out-edges are all to earlier or same rank (ISR define-interface 5, V1.8 define-canonical-identity 5, V1.7 define-record 3, V1.6 define-record 1). The evidence says this class belongs WITH define-canonical-identity in DDI-1, as one identity import."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "(a) Are §15 define-reference (DDI-2) and §17 define-canonical-identity (DDI-1) ONE import or two — and if one, why are they in two batches? (b) For LegalIR/1, TrustBundle/1, CognitionResult/1 and DeclassificationReceipt/1: which canonical pointer is the seat (V1.6/V1.7 prose or V1.8 file+locator)? (c) What do the 5 pointers into V1.6/V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp point at after DDI-2 imports those classes? (d) Where does USC-expression live, given its subject is a document level and not a type? (e) Does the model grow an anchor-resolving check (V8I-XREF-real), which would also close the live RAT-PUBPRIV defect?"
  :adjudication-items ("ADJ-DDI2-IDENTITY-FAMILY: four classes carry the SAME payload (identity + version + canonical pointer) under three key vocabularies — V1.6 define-reference :canonical/:identity/:version/:owner-wp (V1.6:92-150), V1.7 define-reference :canonical/:identity/:version (V1.7:34-39,257-258), V1.8 define-reference :canonical-file/:identity/:version/:locator (V1.8:107,345-352) and V1.8 define-canonical-identity (V1.8:425-432, batch DDI-1, deferred-imports.sexp:59). ONE fact family must be decided in DDI-1 before any of the three DDI-2 reference classes can be imported." "ADJ-V18-REF-1 (V1.8 dossier): identity seats compete — LegalIR/1 (V1.6:96 vs V1.8:345 vs V1.8:425), TrustBundle/1 (V1.6:143 vs V1.8:346 vs V1.8:426), CognitionResult/1 (V1.7:39 vs V1.8:348 vs V1.8:428), DeclassificationReceipt/1 (V1.6:147 vs V1.8:349 vs V1.8:427)." "ADJ-V18-REF-2 (V1.8 dossier): five references anchor their canonical file INSIDE migration sources (files-and-roles.sexp:441,447 CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT) that DDI-2 imports — the pointer must move or become stale." "ADJ-V18-REF-3 (V1.8 dossier): RightsMatrix/1 has two document anchors (V1.7:126 via V1.8:352; LAWMAX-LICENSE-POLICY.md:44 via V1.8:248 and ISR:87)." "ADJ-DDI2-USC-SUBJECT: USC-expression's subject is a document level, not a type; the identity family as shaped by V1.8:425-432 cannot name it. Widen the family or seat it in `rationale` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:182-184)." "ADJ-DDI2-ANCHOR-CHECK: :V8I-XREF-real (V1.8:353-357) demands a check that opens the canonical file and finds the locator; no such check exists on either path, and the same absence lets the live RAT-PUBPRIV dangling anchor stand (rationale-references.sexp:7; orchestrator-notes.md N17).")
  :topological-position 5 :atomic-groups (1)
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "NOT-APPLICABLE" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart "nonexistent file / locator absent / wrong identity or version => typed FAIL (V8I-XREF-real V1.8:353-356; V8I-XREF-identity mutations V1.8:440-441) | invariant: no fabricated identity, no silent pass (V1.8:438-440 HARD_PRE_FREEZE_BLOCKER) | fallback: return typed error value (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:24)" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE" :package-asdf-boundary "a :CODE locator is a package-qualified exported symbol: MemoryEvent/1 -> orchestrator.memory:record-episode (source/memory.lisp:24-27 exports record-episode; SEAT-MEMORY AM/seats.sexp:56-57); document locators (LegalIR/1 -> LAWMAX-LEGAL-IR-SEMANTIC-CONTRACT.md 'Counterproof'; TrustBundle/1 -> MLTP 'TrustBundle') are DOCUMENT_SEAT anchors; 5 references point INTO migration sources V1.6/V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp (V1.8:348-352) that DDI-2 retires from authority (ADJ-V18-REF-2) | invariant: one seat per concept; seat path unique (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:305-308) | fallback: document anchor (rationale doc+anchor MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:182-184)" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE" :compile-time-validation "the two-part resolution (V1.8:433-441: part A identity+version inside the block; part B canonical-file exists and contains locator) as a build gate; for :CODE anchors the structural form is find-symbol + fboundp/exported-p in the named package rather than a textual grep (AM/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:9 'No regex, no grep, no substring is structural proof') | invariant: V8I-XREF-identity (V1.8:433-441) | fallback: grep of the canonical file (the current audit mechanism, V1.8:353-356)" :runtime-validation "NOT-APPLICABLE (identity resolution is a build property)" :python-in-cl-risk "MEDIUM. Naive import: (:canonical-file STRING :locator STRING) pairs checked by a grep — textual proof that a later rename of record-episode would break only at gate time, and the 5 pointers into V1.6/V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp go stale the moment DDI-2 imports those records. CL-native: canonical-identity facts with :seat an L3 ref to a `seat` fact (path owned by the seat) and, for code, :package + :symbol fields verified structurally at build; document anchors as (doc, anchor) with a resolver (N17 shows today's rationale anchors are unresolved)." :future-freedom "NO constraint on S04/S19/JTMS/S20. Binding MemoryEvent/1's identity to the symbol record-episode in source/memory.lisp is a meaning->tool binding tolerated because memory.lisp is the ONE memory seat (V7I-MEM-one-owner V1.7:115-118; SEAT-MEMORY); replacing the function name would be a seat change, not a canonical-identity change, if the fact references the seat rather than the string. Competing identity seats (ADJ-V18-REF-1) are a one-seat adjudication.")
  )

