  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "NEW `cog-node-type` (id <graph>__<NODE>; :node ref cog-node; :in ref type; :out ref type|TERMINAL) — 20 facts. L3 status of the endpoint names (verified against AM/interfaces-and-types.sexp): 5 of 17 distinct names are model `type` facts — PerceptionEnvelope/1 (:39, S02), ClarifiedInterpretation/1 (:18), CognitionResult/1 (:19), ClarificationRequest/1 (:16), ClarificationResponse/1 (:17) (S04); 12 are NOT model types and NOT ISR interfaces — NormalizedDocument/1 (V1.7:45), SegmentSequence/1 (:48), TokenStream/1 (:51), MorphLattice/1 (V1.6:183; V1.7:35 ref), PackedParseForest/1 (V1.6:186; V1.7:36), ReferenceGraph/1 (V1.7:54), DiscourseState/1 (V1.6:192; V1.7:37), LegalEntityGraph/1 (V1.7:58), LegalSemanticAlternativeSet/1 (V1.7:62), InterpretiveProfileEvaluation/1 (V1.7:66), ClarificationDecision/1 (V1.7:70), PromotionEvidence/1 (V1.6:201; V1.7:38); TERMINAL (V1.8:380-383) is a sentinel with no definition anywhere — needs a declared pseudo-type or an `:out` enum (L1 forbids NIL, AM/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:6). Edge typing rule (verified by reading V1.8:57-63 against :363-383): all 13 flow, 2 branch and 4 terminal edges satisfy out(src)=in(tgt); the resume edge CLARIFY-SUSPEND→CLARIFY-RESUME is type-INCOMPATIBLE (out ClarificationRequest/1 V1.8:378 vs in ClarificationResponse/1 V1.8:379) and legal only by the prose rule V1.8:384-385 via ClarificationResponse/1.resume_binding_ref (V1.8:38) — a NEW `resume-binding` fact (:request-type :response-type :via-field) is needed to make the exemption data."
