  :adjudication-items ("ADJ-V18-NT-1 / ADJ-V17-REC-1 / ADJ-V17-REF-1 (12 endpoint types unseated, ownerless)" "ADJ-V18-NT-2 (TERMINAL sentinel)" "ADJ-V18-NT-3 (resume edge type-incompatible by construction; exemption is prose)" "ADJ-V18-NT-4 / ADJ-V17-CO-2 (V1.7 stage seats and flags dropped)" "A10 (ISR dossier): ClarifiedInterpretation/1 double-seated (V1.7:75 vs V1.8:40)" "A9 (V1.6 dossier): CognitionError vs CognitionErrorV7 binding of CognitionResult/1" "ADJ-DDI3-REQ-3 (DFT-07 / T8-COGLIFE seat)" "ADJ-DDI3-MOD-1: module NAME for the DDI-3 function layer is stated three ways by the dossiers — 'decisions-and-projections.sexp' (V1.5 dossier) vs 'decision-functions' (V1.7 and V1.8 dossiers) vs 'cognition-graph' (V1.8 dossier, for the graph) — one name per module must be fixed once; every NEW module is auto-classified CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT by AM/classification-rules.sexp:39-41 (R-008) and must be pinned in AM/ROOT.sexp:12-28 (:module-count 14 today) under L7." "ADJ-DDI3-EXEC-1 (= dossier ADJ-V18-EXEC-1, widened to every DDI-3 class): the only program that has ever executed a DDI-3 contract is V1.8-VERIFY.py / V1.5-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, AM/files-and-roles.sexp:436,453; AM/LEGACY-AUDIT-DISPOSITION.md:10 'never a blocking or sufficient acceptance gate'); the model's harness universe executes laws L1-L7 only (AM/verification-corpus.sexp:24-58,122-125; KERNEL:346). Which harness (existing COMPONENT harness with new schema-derived checks, or a NEW harness fact) executes imported decision/graph contracts, or are they imported as inert data with a declared reason?")
  :topological-position 34 :atomic-groups (2 3)
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "20 `cog-node-type` facts (graph, node, in TYPE-ref, out TYPE-ref | TERMINAL) — TERMINAL is a sentinel, not a type (V1.8:380-383); L1 forbids NIL so 'no output' needs one declared token (ADJ-V18-NT-2); plus one `resume-binding` fact (from-type ClarificationRequest/1, to-type ClarificationResponse/1, via resume_binding_ref) making the resume exemption typed (dossier candidate) | invariant: :V8I-COG-typed-edges (V1.8:386-391) | fallback: alist of (node in out)" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "the (node, in, out) rows ARE the method-signature table of the per-node generic function of the graph: :in is the specializer of the node's method, :out its declared result type — standard CLOS eql/class specializers (cognition.lisp:101-118 pattern), no MOP; method existence per node checked at build with standard `find-method` | invariant: contract:21 'dispatch is total or errors typed' — a node without a method is a build failure, not a runtime surprise | fallback: single dispatch function" :condition-restart "the resume edge is type-INCOMPATIBLE by construction (CLARIFY-SUSPEND :out ClarificationRequest/1 V1.8:378 vs CLARIFY-RESUME :in ClarificationResponse/1 :379) and legal only by prose (V1.8:384-388; ADJ-V18-NT-3) — in CL that discontinuity IS the restart boundary: SUSPEND's :out is the slot type of the signalled condition, RESUME's :in is the argument type of the restart (trace-core.lisp:272-277 provide-trace takes a typed argument), so the 'exemption' is structural instead of a hard-coded skip (V1.8-VERIFY.py:1639) | invariant: V1.8:384-388 resume rule; contract:24 | fallback: typed error value" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE" :protocol "the 20 rows are the node protocol of the graph; a `resume-binding` fact types the SUSPEND->RESUME binding; only 5 of the 17 endpoint types are model `type` facts today (PerceptionEnvelope/1 :39, ClarificationRequest/1 :16, ClarificationResponse/1 :17, ClarifiedInterpretation/1 :18, CognitionResult/1 :19 in interfaces-and-types.sexp) — the remaining 12 have no ISR entry, no model type and no stated owner (ADJ-V18-NT-1) | invariant: :V8I-COG-typed-edges; L3 closed refs (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:24-25) | fallback: prose rule (the present state)" :package-asdf-boundary "each :in/:out must resolve (L3) to a `type` fact carrying owner-subsystem (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:148-152) — blocked for 12/17 until DDI-2 seats the intermediate cognition records (NormalizedDocument/1 ... PromotionEvidence/1, V1.7:45-62 records); the V1.7:81-94 :seat column is the only existing node->file binding (ADJ-V18-NT-4) | invariant: L3 closed references; contract:31 | fallback: type names as strings (loses L3)" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE" :compile-time-validation "build-time laws: L3 of every :in/:out into `type`; out(src)=in(tgt) over `cog-edge` x `cog-node-type` for flow/branch/terminal families; the resume edge checked against the `resume-binding` fact instead of exempted by name; method existence per node (standard find-method) — read-verified by the dossier: all 13 flow, 2 branch, 4 terminal edges compatible, resume edge incompatible by construction | invariant: :V8I-COG-typed-edges | fallback: runtime check" :runtime-validation "check-type of the incoming value against the node's :in at entry (capability-registry.lisp:54-59 fail-closed idiom); TERMINAL nodes accept and emit nothing | invariant: :V8I-COG-typed-edges | fallback: reject to TERM-ERROR" :python-in-cl-risk "HIGH. Naive import = list of dicts {node,in,out} with 'TERMINAL' as a magic string and the resume exemption as an `if node == ...` branch (V1.8-VERIFY.py:1632,1639 mutations name the rows textually). CL-native alternative: the table becomes method specializers + a typed restart argument; TERMINAL is a declared enum token; the resume binding is a fact — every 'special case' becomes a type, so no imperative validator exists to drift." :future-freedom "S04 cognition: importing the 12 unowned intermediate type NAMES (NormalizedDocument/1, SegmentSequence/1, TokenStream/1, MorphLattice/1, PackedParseForest/1, ReferenceGraph/1, DiscourseState/1, LegalEntityGraph/1, LegalSemanticAlternativeSet/1, InterpretiveProfileEvaluation/1, ClarificationDecision/1, PromotionEvidence/1) as canonical `type` facts would fix S04's intermediate representations before the language-cognition design is decided; importing them as strings preserves freedom but loses L3 — adjudication ADJ-V18-NT-1 decides which. S19/JTMS/S20: NONE.")
  )

(ddi-class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-cardinality-table
  :batch DDI-2 :source-file "V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp" :fact-class "define-cardinality-table" :source-count 1 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms (("clarified-interpretation-cardinality" :line 394 :sha16 "8f69eed47da08ee1"))
  :source-file "V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp"
  :source-forms 1
  :current-authority-seat "V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp §17 'EXECUTION CONTRACTS (VR repair — machine-readable, executed)' (header L358), sub-header L393 ';; ---- VR-06: ClarifiedInterpretation conditional-cardinality TABLE + fixtures (rules EXECUTED) ----', form L394-397 (3 rows). Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:56 (DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE, DDI-2, :source-count 1). Traceability row: TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:386 (DFT-06, S04, legal-dialectic.lisp, T8-CLARIFY, WP-08)."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "The SAME module as the `field` family (ADJ-DDI2-FIELD-SEAT) — a conditional-cardinality rule is a statement ABOUT fields and must sit beside them, not in a third place. It must also be the same module that takes V1.5-SCHEMAS__define-cardinality-matrix (V1.5:45-62, deferred-imports.sexp:15), which is the other cardinality dialect in the same batch."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "NEW fact type `field-rule` (:id-space TOKEN-SPACE :required (record when-field when-value field cardinality) :optional () :types ((record SYMBOL) (when-field SYMBOL) (when-value SYMBOL) (field SYMBOL) (cardinality SYMBOL)) :enum ((cardinality field-cardinality)) :ref ((record type) (when-field field) (when-value enum-value) (field field))) with a NEW enum `field-cardinality` (NULL ONE ANY ALL_PRESERVED). Flattening rule: 3 rows x 3 columns = 9 facts, ids `ClarifiedInterpretation/1__<WHEN>__<COLUMN>`; the :when keywords become bare symbols (ABSTAIN, EXPLICIT_SELECTION, EXPLICIT_MERGE) and the column values null/one/any/all-preserved become NULL/ONE/ANY/ALL_PRESERVED. The model's own define-conditional (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:26-30, instances at :293-316) is the exact schema-level analogue — it is a state-dependent field rule kept as DATA so both paths enforce one specification. Generalising it from the model's own fact types to imported record types is the natural design; whether that generalisation is admitted is the decision. no `enum`/`enum-value`/`field`/`primitive`/`cardinality`/`ref-class`/`adapter`/`canonical-identity` fact type exists among the 34 fact types (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:84-288); `define-enum` there is schema syntax for the model's own closed domains only (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:18,47-76); L1 forbids keywords, nested lists and NIL as values (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6) and the closed field set forbids adding keys to `type` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:9-13,148-152)"
  :owner "S04 — inherited, not declared. The form carries no :owner key. Its constrained record ClarifiedInterpretation/1 is owned by S04 (ISR:117; interfaces-and-types.sexp:18; subsystems.sexp:8 owner-seat SEAT-LEGAL-AST, seats.sexp:32 BUILT source/legal-ast.lisp), and TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:386 assigns DFT-06 to S04. Two independent sources agree; no source contradicts."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — a cardinality rule is a declaration about a record's fields, not a store. No registry names a writer. The instances it constrains would be written by S04's seat, which owns the legal-ir store (stores-and-authorities.sexp:9, writer SEAT-WRITE-AUTHORITY)."
  :classification "PUBLIC — it constrains the PUBLIC type ClarifiedInterpretation/1 (interfaces-and-types.sexp:18), its owner S04 is PUBLIC (subsystems.sexp:8), and no private member is named."
  :dependencies ("SCHEMA FIRST: `field-rule` + `field-cardinality` (or a generalised define-conditional) and the schema-version bump (X74-X76 verification-corpus.sexp:354-370)" "SAME BATCH, STRICTLY FIRST: V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-record — the three constrained fields selected_alternative_ref, merged_result_ref, input_provenance_refs (V1.8:43-45) must exist as `field` facts before :field/:when-field can be typed refs" "SAME BATCH, STRICTLY FIRST: V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum MergeSemanticsV8 (V1.8:31) — the three :when values are its members; :when-value cannot be a closed ref before the enum-value facts exist" "DECISION FIRST: which ClarifiedInterpretation/1 field set is canonical (V1.7:75-79 vs V1.8:40-46) — the table is TRUE of the V1.8 record and FALSE of the V1.7 one, because V1.7:77 types selected_alternative_ref as a plain `ref` (mandatory) while the table requires it null for ABSTAIN and EXPLICIT_MERGE" "DECISION FIRST: one cardinality family or two dialects (V1.5:45-62 field x profile with :R/:F/:C codes vs this mode x column table)")
  :consumers ("V1.8 define-fixtures clarified-interpretation-fixtures (V1.8:398-405, DDI-4) — 7 test vectors that are exactly the table's rows plus invalid cases" ":V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality (V1.8:47-51, DDI-4) — the prose twin of the same rule, ending 'Audit V8-CLARIFY with a mutation that makes ABSTAIN carry a selection'" "the record comments themselves (V1.8:43-44) state the rule a third time" "legacy executor V1.8-VERIFY.py:1037-1095 g_clarify (parses the :when rows at :1047-1050; duplicate-rule check at :1052-1054; mutation at :1646-1652) — HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:453), and LEGACY-AUDIT-DISPOSITION.md:1-6 declares it 'never a blocking or sufficient acceptance gate'" "CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:30-32 (DFT-06); TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:386" "dag.json: NO class references this one and it references no class (both edge sets empty)" "no tracked source/ or systems/ file names any record/enum id of the six registries (git grep at RO = 0); the only mechanical readers are the legacy audits/harness classified HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE (files-and-roles.sexp:436,440,444,450,453)")
  :identity-version-rule "ONLY-VERSION. define-cardinality-table occurs only in V1.8 and only once (classes.md row 62; my own grep), and the name clarified-interpretation-cardinality is unique across the six registries and the 14 model modules. It is NOT the same class as V1.5's define-cardinality-matrix (V1.5:45-62): different head, different shape (field x assurance-profile with :R/:F/:C codes vs merge-mode x column with null/one/any/all-preserved), different constrained record (SemanticAdmissionEvidence/1 vs ClarifiedInterpretation/1). Two dialects of one concept, both DDI-2, neither superseding the other."
  :migration-rule "IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL — 9 flat facts, one seat, an uncontested owner, and it is the only machine-readable statement of the VR-06 rule. It is the strongest IMPORT candidate in DDI-2. It is nevertheless gated by two same-batch prerequisites (the `field` facts and the MergeSemanticsV8 enum-value facts) and by the ClarifiedInterpretation/1 field-set decision, so the import ORDER inside DDI-2 is: enums -> records/fields -> this table."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "MEDIUM. (1) The rule is stated THREE times in V1.8 alone — the table (L394-397), the invariant prose (:47-51) and the record comments (:43-44). Importing the table as canonical while DDI-4 later imports the invariant would create a second seat unless the invariant import explicitly cites the table rather than restating it. (2) Two cardinality dialects in one batch (ADJ-V18-CARD-1). (3) Column-to-field binding is by NAME CONVENTION only: the columns are :selected / :merged / :input-provenance and the fields are selected_alternative_ref / merged_result_ref / input_provenance_refs (V1.8:43-45) — there is no typed reference between them, and the legacy guard hard-codes the mapping (V1.8-VERIFY.py:1058-1065). Any import must MAKE the binding typed or it imports a convention as if it were a reference. (4) The table contradicts V1.7:77 (selected_alternative_ref mandatory) — a rule true of one twin and false of the other."
  :requirement "R-129 via req-map S04__WP-08 :test Q08 :wp WP-08 (requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:70) is the only model chain that reaches S04. The source's own binding is DFT-06 / T8-CLARIFY / WP-08 (TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:386); T8-CLARIFY is NOT a model `test` fact (requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:30-50; orchestrator-notes.md N1/N7) and DFT-06 is not a model `requirement`. WP-08 IS a model `wp` (:60), so one third of the source's chain resolves."
  :invariant "L1 (nested row lists and keyword :when values cannot be values — MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6), L3 (:record, :when-field, :when-value and :field all closed refs — this is what turns the name convention into a typed binding). Source invariant: :V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality (V1.8:47-51). Model analogue: define-conditional (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:26-30), whose stated purpose — 'a state-dependent field rule, kept as DATA so both paths enforce one specification rather than two hand-written implementations' — is precisely this form's purpose, one level down."
  :qualification-test "NEW. Executable one-liner: for each of the 3 MergeSemanticsV8 members there are exactly 3 `field-rule` facts (one per constrained field), every :field resolves to a declared `field` of ClarifiedInterpretation/1, every :when-value resolves to a declared `enum-value` of MergeSemanticsV8, and no (record, when-value, field) triple appears twice — a completeness + uniqueness check, matching the duplicate-rule check the legacy audit already performs (V1.8-VERIFY.py:1052-1054). Pin the 9 with a property-family so a lost row is a named failure."
  :falsifier "REPLACE `:cardinality NULL` with `:cardinality ONE` on the row (ClarifiedInterpretation/1, ABSTAIN, selected_alternative_ref) — must be REJECTED, because it makes ABSTAIN carry a selection, which is the mutation :V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality itself names (V1.8:51 'Audit V8-CLARIFY with a mutation that makes ABSTAIN carry a selection'). APPEND `(fact field-rule ClarifiedInterpretation/1__ABSTAIN__no_such :record ClarifiedInterpretation/1 :when-field merge_semantics :when-value ABSTAIN :field no_such_field :cardinality NULL)` — both paths must reject: kernel-reason 'resolves to no declared field', checker-reason 'L3'. This is the falsifier that proves the column binding is typed and not conventional. APPEND a duplicate row for (ABSTAIN, selected_alternative_ref) with a different :cardinality — must be rejected as a duplicate rule (the check V1.8-VERIFY.py:1052-1054 performs and the model does not)."
  :rollback "delete the imported facts of this class and the fact-type/enum declarations added to MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp for it, re-run build_root.py so ROOT.sexp re-pins the 14 modules (ROOT.sexp:12-27; L7), and restore the ledger row to DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT / AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE (deferred-imports.sexp) so the source file is authoritative again; the source registry is never edited by the import (V1.7-SCHEMAS.sexp:256 'v1.5 files are NOT edited' is the precedent)"
  :batch-reason "DDI-2 because build_deferred.py maps define-cardinality-table to DDI-2, materialised at deferred-imports.sexp:56. AGREES. dag.json records NO in-edges and NO out-edges for this class — nothing in the six registries references it and it references no other class by symbol. Its real dependencies (the MergeSemanticsV8 members and the three ClarifiedInterpretation/1 fields) are both in the SAME batch, which is exactly what DDI-2 is for. The only caveat is intra-batch ordering: enums and record fields must be imported before the table."
  :decision-kind "SCHEMA_EXTENSION"
  :decision-question "(a) One cardinality family for both dialects (V1.5:45-62 field x profile R/F/C and V1.8:394-397 mode x column) or two families? (b) Is the model's define-conditional (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:26-30) generalised from the model's own fact types to imported record types, or is a separate `field-rule` family created? (c) Is the column-to-field binding made typed (:field -> `field` fact) rather than the current name convention? (d) Which harness EXECUTES an imported EXEC-MODEL contract — verification-corpus.sexp:122-125 declares two harnesses, both run_corpus.py, both for model laws L1-L7 (ADJ-V18-EXEC-1)?"
  :adjudication-items ("ADJ-V18-CARD-1 (V1.8 dossier): two cardinality dialects are both DDI-2 — V1.5:45-62 define-cardinality-matrix (deferred-imports.sexp:15) and V1.8:394-397 define-cardinality-table (deferred-imports.sexp:56); one fact family must express both or two families coexist." "ADJ-V18-CARD-2 (V1.8 dossier): column -> field binding is by name convention (V1.8:43-45); the legacy guard hard-codes it (V1.8-VERIFY.py:1058-1065). An import must make it typed or import a convention as a reference." "ADJ-V18-CARD-3 (V1.8 dossier), cross-ref ADJ-V18-REC-1: the table requires selected_alternative_ref nullable, which V1.7:77 forbids — the table can only be true of the V1.8 record, so importing it PRESUPPOSES the ClarifiedInterpretation/1 decision." "ADJ-V18-EXEC-1 (V1.8 dossier, shared with define-fixtures / define-reliance-aggregation / define-dimension-policy / define-cognition-node-types): the only program that executes this EXEC-MODEL contract is V1.8-VERIFY.py (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, files-and-roles.sexp:453; LEGACY-AUDIT-DISPOSITION.md:1-6 'never a blocking or sufficient acceptance gate'); the model's harnesses execute model laws only (verification-corpus.sexp:122-125). Which harness executes imported EXEC-MODEL contracts, or are they inert data?" "ADJ-DDI2-RULE-RESTATEMENT: the same rule is stated by the table (V1.8:394-397), the invariant (:47-51) and the record comments (:43-44); DDI-4's invariant import must cite the table rather than restate it, or the model gains a second seat for one rule.")
  :topological-position 50 :atomic-groups (5)
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "NOT-APPLICABLE" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE (rule data)" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE (one total evaluator over data; no dispatch)" :condition-restart "violation => typed condition naming (record, :when value, field, expected cardinality) (kernel conditional-violation pattern AM/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:1-3 (*read-eval* nil, standard readtable, no eval), :23 *enums*, :24 *conds*, :56-60 reader, :243-257 law5-isolation *conds*) | invariant: ABSTAIN => no hidden winner; EXPLICIT_MERGE => all input provenance preserved (V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality V1.8:47-51) | fallback: return typed error value (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:24)" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE (must stay DATA — MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:26-30 define-conditional is the schema-level analogue and 'could be generalised' per the V1.8 dossier)" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE" :package-asdf-boundary "NOT-APPLICABLE (data of the ClarifiedInterpretation/1 module; evaluator with the S04 seat legal-dialectic.lisp per TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:386 DFT-06)" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE (the :ABSTAIN row is the cardinality face of the JTMS :undefined status — mechanism in class 16)" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE" :compile-time-validation "build-time: rows == MergeSemanticsV8 members (exactly 3, each once — the V1.8-VERIFY.py:1055-1057 duplicate-rule check made structural via define-unique MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:34-36); column -> field binding as L3 refs to `field` facts instead of name convention (ADJ-V18-CARD-2); the 7 fixtures (V1.8:398-405, DDI-4) executed as PASS/FAIL corpus rows (AM/verification-corpus.sexp:24-39 fixture discipline) | invariant: V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality; exactly one rule per mode | fallback: runtime check (deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/LAWMAX-COMMON-LISP-NATIVE-CONSTRUCTION-CONTRACT.md:32)" :runtime-validation "at decode of a ClarifiedInterpretation/1: read :merge_semantics, apply the row (null => field absent/NIL-rendered, one => exactly one ref, all-preserved => input_provenance_refs covers every input) — a data-driven conditional, the CL twin of MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp define-conditional; declarative shapes as in source/shacl-validator.lisp:6-10 (shapes are data, not a bespoke checker); :115-130 property-shape / node-shape structs | invariant: V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality | fallback: reject input" :python-in-cl-risk "HIGH. The imperative validator ALREADY exists: deployment/collab/design/OMEGA2/CHANGE-PROPOSAL/V1.8-VERIFY.py:1050-1075 hard-codes the column->field binding (':selected_alternative_ref', 'selected-not-nullable' :1069) and walks parsed forms by hand — HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE per AM/files-and-roles.sexp:453 / LEGACY-AUDIT-DISPOSITION.md:10, never a gate. Naive import copies that into Lisp. CL-native: one flat fact per (mode, field) cell (field-rule :record :when-field :when-value :field :cardinality NULL|ONE|ANY|ALL_PRESERVED) with typed refs, evaluated by ONE generic conditional evaluator — the design MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:26-30 already states ('one specification rather than two hand-written implementations')." :future-freedom "NO constraint on S19/JTMS/S20. It constrains S04's ClarifiedInterpretation/1 by design and is TRUE only of the V1.8 record (V1.7:77 makes selected_alternative_ref mandatory — ADJ-V18-CARD-3), so it forces the ADJ-V18-REC-1 one-seat decision. Which harness executes imported EXEC-MODEL contracts (ADJ-V18-EXEC-1) is UNKNOWN: the model's harness universe executes L1-L7 only (AM/verification-corpus.sexp:24-39).")
  )

(ddi-class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-fixtures
  :batch DDI-4 :source-file "V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp" :fact-class "define-fixtures" :source-count 1 :authority AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE
  :forms (("clarified-interpretation-fixtures" :line 398 :sha16 "2fe8caba1d5d86b1"))
  :source-file "V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp"
  :source-forms 1
  :current-authority-seat "V1.8-SCHEMAS.sexp §17, comment ';; ---- VR-06: ClarifiedInterpretation conditional-cardinality TABLE + fixtures (rules EXECUTED) ----' (V1.8:393), form define-fixtures clarified-interpretation-fixtures at :398-405 — 7 test vectors, 3 :valid and 4 :invalid, over the table clarified-interpretation-cardinality at :394-397 (DDI-2, deferred-imports.sexp:56). Ledger seat: deferred-imports.sexp:61 (:source-count 1, DDI-4, AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE). Also registered at TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:386 (T8-CLARIFY) and PUBLIC-OBSERVATORY-QUALIFICATION-TESTS.md:1162-1163, where T8-CLARIFY is predeclared and UNEXECUTED."
  :proposed-canonical-target-module "verification-corpus.sexp (EXISTING) IF an executor exists — that module is the declared universe of 'everything that tests this model' (vc:1) with fixtures, property families, harnesses, falsifiers and floors; adding domain record fixtures there without an executor would put inert rows into the one module whose whole purpose is that every declared member is executed and counted (vc:10-13). OTHERWISE the same NEW module as its table (DDI-2), so the vectors sit beside the rule they test. The choice is the executor question, not a filing preference."
  :canonical-type-or-fact-family "NEW `record-fixture` :id-space TOKEN-SPACE :required (rule expect mode) :optional (selected merged provenance-preserved source-file source-line note) :types ((rule SYMBOL) (expect SYMBOL) (mode SYMBOL) (selected INTEGER) (merged INTEGER) (provenance-preserved SYMBOL) (source-file STRING) (source-line INTEGER) (note STRING)) :enum ((expect fixture-expectation) (provenance-preserved yes-no)) :ref ((rule <the DDI-2 cardinality-table fact>)). Flattening rule MANDATORY: the form is 7 nested row lists (V1.8:399-405), not an L1-legal value (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6) -> 7 flat facts with synthesised ids (e.g. CLARIFY-FX-01..07). TWO renderings must be declared: (a) `t` / `nil` (:provenance-preserved, V1.8:399-405) are not permitted values (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:6) and must become the existing yes-no enum YES/NO (:71); (b) the modes are BARE SYMBOLS here (ABSTAIN, EXPLICIT_SELECTION, EXPLICIT_MERGE, V1.8:399-405) but KEYWORDS in the table they test (:ABSTAIN etc., V1.8:395-397) — one file, two renderings of one enum; the legacy guard strips the colon (V1.8-VERIFY.py:1049). NOTE the model already has a `fixture` fact type (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:217-220) — but it is FILE-based (:path :expect :law) and its instances test model LAWS L1-L7 (vc:24-39); reusing that id space for domain records would collide conceptually and, if the same ids were used, under L2."
  :owner "S04 — inferred, not declared: the record under test, ClarifiedInterpretation/1, is a model `type` (interfaces-and-types.sexp:18) with :owner-subsystem S04, ISR:117 registers it to S04, and TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:386 records the row's subsystem as S04. The form itself carries no owner. Marked as an inference."
  :writer "NO_WRITER — no store (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:155-158). If the fixtures join verification-corpus.sexp, the relevant authority is the HARNESS that executes them, and the model's two harnesses both name run_corpus.py (vc:122-125), which executes model-law falsifiers only."
  :classification "PUBLIC — ClarifiedInterpretation/1 is PUBLIC (interfaces-and-types.sexp:18) and the vectors contain only counts and mode symbols. No private member."
  :dependencies ("FIRST (hard): the DDI-2 class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-cardinality-table (V1.8:394-397, deferred-imports.sexp:56) — the fixtures are meaningless without the rule they test, and the :rule :ref cannot close without it [typed reference; satisfied by DDI-4 running after DDI-2]" "FIRST: the DDI-2 record fields of ClarifiedInterpretation/1 (V1.8:40-46) and the enum MergeSemanticsV8 (V1.8:31) [field/enum references]" "FIRST: the EXECUTOR decision — which harness evaluates a domain-record fixture; the model's harness family (vc:122-125) runs model-law falsifiers, and the only program that executes these vectors is V1.8-VERIFY.py:1080-1094 (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE files-and-roles.sexp:453; NON_AUTHORITATIVE LEGACY-AUDIT-DISPOSITION.md:1-6) [execution dependency]" "FIRST: the t/nil -> YES/NO and keyword/bare-symbol rendering conventions [L1 dependency, shared with class 8]" "IF filed in verification-corpus.sexp: a universe-floor for the new family (cf. UF-FIXTURE minimum 8, vc:60-61), because an undeclared family can shrink silently [floor dependency]")
  :consumers (":V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality (V1.8:47-51) — DDI-4 class 14, same batch; its demanded mutation ('a mutation that makes ABSTAIN carry a selection') is literally row 4 of this form (V1.8:402)" "the DDI-2 table clarified-interpretation-cardinality (V1.8:394-397) is the rule under test" "legacy executor V1.8-VERIFY.py:1040,1080-1094 (evaluates each fixture through the parsed table; '<7 fixtures' fails at :1085) with mutations at :1647-1649 — HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, NON_AUTHORITATIVE" "TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:386 (S04 / DFT-06 / T8-CLARIFY / WP-08); PUBLIC-OBSERVATORY-QUALIFICATION-TESTS.md:1162-1163 (T8-CLARIFY predeclared, UNEXECUTED)" "CANONICAL MODEL: none — 0 hits for 'clarified-interpretation-fixtures' in the 14 modules; T8-CLARIFY is not a model `test` fact (rtw:30-50)")
  :identity-version-rule "ONLY-VERSION — define-fixtures occurs once in the whole corpus (classes.md row 63; no fixtures form in any other registry; V1.5:123 define-gate is a different head). The model's `fixture` family (vc:24-39) is NOT a prior version of it: those 8 fixtures are FILES under FIXTURES/ that test model laws, a different concept sharing a word."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION — the blocker is not representation (the 7 rows flatten cleanly once the two renderings are declared) but EXECUTION: importing executable vectors that no admitted harness runs produces facts that are parsed and ignored, which the model's own doctrine names as silent loss (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:12). With an executor the rule becomes IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL (7 `record-fixture` facts + a floor); without one, the honest value is SKIP-WITH-PROOF and the proof must say that the vectors remain authoritative at source because the model has no law under which to evaluate them."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "MODERATE. (i) Name collision of CONCEPT with the model's `fixture` family (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:217-220; vc:24-39) — two things called fixtures, one testing model laws and one testing a domain record; a shared family would silently widen UF-FIXTURE (vc:60-61) and make the law-fixture floor satisfiable by domain rows. (ii) The mode vocabulary is written twice in one file with two renderings (:395-397 keywords vs :399-405 bare symbols), so an import must canonise one and record the rename. (iii) The only existing executor is NON_AUTHORITATIVE, so 'imported and tested' would be a stronger claim than the repository can support."
  :requirement "NEW — TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:386 registers the row under DFT-06 with test T8-CLARIFY and WP-08; neither DFT-06 nor T8-CLARIFY is a model `requirement`/`test` fact (rtw:5-50), and T8-CLARIFY is declared predeclared-UNEXECUTED (PUBLIC-OBSERVATORY-QUALIFICATION-TESTS.md:1162-1163; orchestrator-notes.md N7). WP-08 IS a model `wp` fact (rtw:60), so the WP end of the chain closes and the requirement/test end does not."
  :invariant "L1 (nested rows are not values; `t`/`nil` are not values — MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-6,71), L2 (synthesised ids; and no collision with the existing `fixture` id space), L3 (:rule must resolve to the DDI-2 table fact), L6 (requirement->seat->test->WP: only the WP end resolves today). Source invariant: :V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality (V1.8:47-51). Model doctrine engaged: 'a parsed-but-ignored field is silent loss' (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:12) and 'a family that silently shrinks to zero is a failure' (:221-222)."
  :qualification-test "NEW — QT-DDI4-CLARIFY-FIXTURES-EXECUTED. Executable one-liner: `for each record-fixture, evaluate (mode, selected, merged, provenance-preserved) against the cardinality-table facts and assert the result equals :expect; assert exactly 7 fixtures exist for rule clarified-interpretation-cardinality` — the cardinality clause mirrors V1.8-VERIFY.py:1085 ('<7 fixtures' fails) and the evaluation clause is what makes the import non-inert. This test cannot be satisfied by declaring the facts alone; it requires the executor decision (ADJ-V18-FIX-1)."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact record-fixture CLARIFY-FX-08 :rule clarified-interpretation-cardinality :expect PASS :mode ABSTAIN :selected 1 :merged 0 :provenance-preserved YES)` — must be REJECTED by QT-DDI4-CLARIFY-FIXTURES-EXECUTED: the vector violates the table's :ABSTAIN row (:selected null, V1.8:395) so :expect PASS is wrong; this is the abstain-with-selection mutation :V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality demands (V1.8:51) and it is row 4 of the source form (:402) with the opposite expectation. REPLACE `:provenance-preserved NO` with `:provenance-preserved nil` — must be REJECTED, checker-reason 'MALFORMED-FACT' (NIL is not a value kind, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:6). DROP one of the 7 imported fixtures — must be REJECTED by the cardinality clause and by a universe floor; without a floor the deletion reads as a smaller success, the exact defect vc:58-61 records."
  :rollback "Delete the 7 record-fixture facts and any floor; remove the fact type from MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp and move :version (:37 / ROOT.sexp:9); re-run build_root.py; build_deferred.py restores deferred-imports.sexp:61. If a floor was added, lowering or removing it later needs a base-anchored universe-authorization (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:268-279) — plan the floor before the import, not after."
  :batch-reason "DDI-4 because build_deferred.py:102 maps `define-fixtures` to DDI-4 ('normative invariants / rules / prose'). AGREES — the dependency evidence does NOT contradict the placement; what is wrong is the batch TITLE, not the order. Order: the fixtures depend on the DDI-2 cardinality table (V1.8:394-397, deferred-imports.sexp:56) and DDI-4 runs after DDI-2, so the dependency is satisfied; dag.json records no order violation for this class. Theme: the batch title is 'normative invariants / rules / prose' and this class is neither prose nor a rule — it is executable test data (the source comment says 'rules EXECUTED', V1.8:393), so the batch title mis-describes it. The V1.8 dossier records this as a batch mismatch (ADJ-V18-FIX-2); on the mechanical evidence the ORDERING is correct and the LABEL is not, and those are different defects — so this row is NOT counted among the batch disagreements."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "Which harness executes a domain-record fixture? The model's fixture/harness universe (verification-corpus.sexp:24-39,122-125) executes model laws L1-L7 only, and there is no law among L1-L7 under which a ClarifiedInterpretation cardinality vector can be evaluated (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:64); the only program that executes these vectors, V1.8-VERIFY.py:1080-1094, is HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE and NON_AUTHORITATIVE. Import them inert, import them with a new law and a floor, or hold them at source? And which mode rendering is canonical — the table's keywords (:395-397) or the fixtures' bare symbols (:399-405)?"
  :adjudication-items ("ADJ-V18-FIX-1 (V1.8 dossier): executor seat — the only executor is NON_AUTHORITATIVE; importing without one makes the vectors inert, which the model calls silent loss (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:12)" "ADJ-V18-FIX-2 (V1.8 dossier), REFRAMED here: the ORDER is satisfied (DDI-4 after DDI-2) — the defect is that the batch TITLE ('prose') mis-describes executable data, and build_deferred.py:101-103 batches by head name, not by content or dependency" "ADJ-V18-FIX-3 (V1.8 dossier): two renderings of one enum inside one file (keywords in the table, bare symbols in the fixtures; V1.8-VERIFY.py:1049 strips the colon) — orchestrator-notes.md N12" "ADJ-MX4-NIL-RENDERING (new, shared with class 8): `t`/`nil` must render as the yes-no enum (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:71) under one declared convention" "ADJ-MX4-FIXTURE-NAME (new): the model already owns the word `fixture` for FILE-based model-law fixtures (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:217-220, vc:24-39, floor UF-FIXTURE vc:60-61) — a domain-record family must not share that family or its floor")
  :topological-position 51 :atomic-groups (5)
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "NEW `record-fixture` facts (:rule ref cardinality-table id, :expect PASS|FAIL from fixture-expectation ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:65, :mode SYMBOL constrained to MergeSemanticsV8 (V1.8:31) as a define-enum, :selected INTEGER, :merged INTEGER, :provenance-preserved YES|NO from yes-no :71) — 7 facts, hash-pinned | invariant: L1 (no NIL, closed enums, ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:5-7) + :V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality (V1.8:47-51) | fallback: leave in V1.8 as AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE — but NOT as an inert model fact (ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:12 forbids parsed-but-ignored data)" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart "NOT-APPLICABLE" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE" :package-asdf-boundary "NOT-APPLICABLE" :persistent-event "NOT-APPLICABLE" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE" :temporal-index-projection "NOT-APPLICABLE" :compile-time-validation "executed at gate time by a DECLARED harness (harness facts verification-corpus.sexp:122-125; run_corpus.py is the ONE runner per S15-M1 :118) with EXACT cardinality 7 and a universe-floor (UF-FIXTURE pattern :60-61) so a dropped row is a named failure; the executor evaluates the DDI-2 cardinality table AS DATA (as law2-unique evaluates define-unique data, ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:190) — each :invalid row must FAIL for the cell its comment names (V1.8:402-405) | invariant: :V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality 'Audit V8-CLARIFY with a mutation that makes ABSTAIN carry a selection' (V1.8:51) = the :invalid ABSTAIN row (V1.8:402) | fallback: NONE that is honest — an unexecuted fixture is silent loss; either executed or not imported (ADJ-CL4-08)" :runtime-validation "the SAME table is the production-time validator of ClarifiedInterpretation/1 instances at the RESOLVE node (V1.8:375; record V1.8:40-46): a data-driven cardinality check (selected/merged null|one, provenance all-preserved per :merge_semantics); the fixtures are its regression vectors (WP-08.md:23 'sbcl inference fiveam suite') | invariant: :V8I-CLARIFY-cardinality | fallback: reject the record (fail-closed)" :python-in-cl-risk "YES — the sharpest in DDI-4: t/nil → NIL (an L1 violation) or Python True/False; :valid/:invalid → strings; bare ABSTAIN vs :ABSTAIN in the table (V1.8:395 vs :399) reconciled by stripping colons in Python (the legacy guard V1.8-VERIFY.py:1049 per the dossier); the executor written as one imperative Python function per fixture. CL-native alternative: yes-no + fixture-expectation enums, mode symbols validated against the MergeSemanticsV8 define-enum, and ONE data-driven evaluator of the cardinality table implemented independently by each verification path (kernel and checker share the specification, never evaluator code — ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:1-2) and reused as the production validator's specification (one seat for the rule, two independent evaluations)." :future-freedom "CONSTRAINS S04's RESOLVE output (ClarifiedInterpretation/1) to the three merge semantics — intended (no hidden winner). Batch order: these DDI-4 fixtures depend on the DDI-2 table (V1.8:394-397; dossier ADJ-V18-FIX-2) — importing them before DDI-2 is impossible. No S19/JTMS/S20 constraint.")
  )

