  :consumers ":V8I-RASTATUS-product V1.8:97-103 (DDI-4); TM:390 DFT-10; QT:1163 T8-RASTATUS; CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:49-52; SUPERSEDED-REGISTER.md:286-287 ('4^8 = 65,536 root-authority product'); V1.8-VERIFY.py:1191 parses it, MUT :1656-1673 (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE). 0 canonical-model consumers."
  :identity-version-rule "id = `reliance-of` (TOKEN OK). ONLY-VERSION (unique to V1.8). Conceptual predecessor: :V7I-RA-qual-revocable V1.7:249-252 with the scalar RootAuthorityState enum V1.7:241 (auto_downgrade_on_expiry) — superseded in concept by the product state (V1.8:73-74) but RootAuthorityQualification/1 stays a live model type (AM/interfaces-and-types.sexp:53; ISR A10). Third decision dialect at source beside V1.5:229 / V1.7:259 (ADJ-V18-AGG-2)."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION (formula-as-string vs structured rule; executor; one family with the decision functions)."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "The semantics would have three copies: the V1.8:413 string, EXPECTED_AGG_RULE in V1.8-VERIFY.py:548-549 (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE) and the Python re-implementation :1223-1232; a model string value adds a fourth textual copy with no evaluator (AM/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:12 'parsed-but-ignored ... silent loss'). A structured `:rule-kind` removes the string but requires a NEW evaluator seat."
  :requirement "R-102 (S14 req-map :80). Source DFT-10 (TM:390) NOT a model fact — NEW."
  :invariant "L1 (:self-qualification enum REJECTED-only; :total/:deterministic YES-only), L2 (one aggregation-order per value via id), L3 (refs). Source guard: :V8I-RASTATUS-product V1.8:97-103 (derived, total, deterministic, preserves ALL causes, mandatory/advisory separated, forbids self-qualification). Totality/determinism/monotonicity over the 4^8 product are NOT model laws → NEW check RELIANCE-AGG (evaluate the structured rule over the full product of 8 DimensionState fields = 65536 combinations, SUPERSEDED-REGISTER.md:286-287)."
  :qualification-test "Existing: Q27 (:80). Source: T8-RASTATUS (TM:390; QT:1163 UNEXECUTED); legacy V8-RASTATUS 4^8 product (V1.8-VERIFY.py:1233-1240). NEW executable statement: T-DDI3-RELIANCE-TOTAL — over all 65536 RootAuthorityStatus dimension-state combinations, reliance-of yields exactly one RelianceClass; every combination with a MANDATORY dimension in {FAILED, DEGRADED, UNKNOWN} yields the minimum (by `aggregation-order`) failure class of those dimensions and lists every such dimension in blocking_dimensions; combinations where only ADVISORY dimensions fail yield FULL_RELIANCE with those dimensions in advisory_dimensions."
  :falsifier "(fact falsifier D3-10-SELF-QUALIFICATION-ACCEPTED :harness COMPONENT :intent \"the aggregation permits self-issued qualification evidence\" :mutation REPLACE :module \"decision-functions.sexp\" :replace-from \":self-qualification REJECTED\" :replace-to \":self-qualification ACCEPTED\" :kernel-reason \"outside enum self-qualification domain\" :checker-reason \"L1\") — legacy 'self-qualification-allowed' (V1.8-VERIFY.py:1657) made an L1 row. Companion (needs the NEW RELIANCE-AGG check): REPLACE ':rule-kind MIN-OVER-MANDATORY-FAILING' → ':rule-kind ALWAYS-FULL' must be rejected as 'RELIANCE-NOT-TOTAL-OVER-FAILURES' (legacy 'held/aggregation-always-full' :1667)."
  :rollback "Drop the `aggregation` + 4 `aggregation-order` facts, rebuild ROOT.sexp (L7), flip AM/deferred-imports.sexp:68 back; roll back with row 8 (the policy it reads)."
  :batch-reason "DDI-3 by BATCH map (AM/build_deferred.py:98 'define-reliance-aggregation':'DDI-3'; ledger :68). AGREES: inputs are DDI-2 enums/records and the same-batch policy table; nothing earlier references it."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "Is the aggregation body imported as the formula string of V1.8:413 (an inert canonical value that only HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE code can evaluate, V1.8-VERIFY.py:548-549,1223-1232) or restructured into typed facts (:rule-kind MIN-OVER-MANDATORY-FAILING + `aggregation-order`) that a model-side check evaluates over the 4^8 product; which harness is that evaluator's seat (the COMPONENT harness AM/verification-corpus.sexp:122 executes laws only); and is it one fact family with V1.5/V1.7 define-decision-function (ADJ-V18-AGG-2)?"
  :adjudication-items ("ADJ-V18-AGG-1 (formula string pinned byte-exactly only by the legacy guard)" "ADJ-V18-AGG-2 (one family for three decision dialects)" "ADJ-V18-AGG-3 (bare-symbol :order vs keyword enum members — rendering)" "ADJ-DDI3-EXEC-1 (executor seat)" "ADJ-V18-DIM-1 (via the policy it reads)" "A10 (ISR dossier): RootAuthorityQualification/1 (V1.7) still live beside the product state" "ADJ-DDI3-REQ-4 (DFT-10 / T8-RASTATUS seat)" "ADJ-DDI3-ENUM-1: no enum / enum-value fact family exists in AM/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:84-288 (34 fact types); every DDI-3 clause value, :output, :failure, :order and :result-when-insufficient is an enum member of a DDI-2 define-closed-enum / define-frozen-enum-reference form. Until DDI-2 seats enums as facts, DDI-3 values can only be bare SYMBOLs with no L3 closure (KERNEL:196-210 checks :ref targets only)." "ADJ-DDI3-MOD-1: module NAME for the DDI-3 function layer is stated three ways by the dossiers — 'decisions-and-projections.sexp' (V1.5 dossier) vs 'decision-functions' (V1.7 and V1.8 dossiers) vs 'cognition-graph' (V1.8 dossier, for the graph) — one name per module must be fixed once; every NEW module is auto-classified CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT by AM/classification-rules.sexp:39-41 (R-008) and must be pinned in AM/ROOT.sexp:12-28 (:module-count 14 today) under L7.")
  :topological-position 55 :atomic-groups (6)
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "`aggregation` fact (output-enum RelianceClass, total=YES, deterministic=YES, preserve-causes=YES, advisory-never-blocks=YES, self-qualification=REJECTED) + 4 `aggregation-order` facts (enum value, ordinal) + a STRUCTURED rule (rule-kind MIN-OVER-MANDATORY-FAILING, policy -> root-authority-dimensions, failing-states {FAILED DEGRADED UNKNOWN} as typed refs into DimensionState V1.8:75) instead of the formula STRING (V1.8:413; ADJ-V18-AGG-1) — the :order bare symbols vs RelianceClass keywords (ADJ-V18-AGG-3) unify under L1 rendering (note N12) | invariant: :V8I-RASTATUS-product 'DERIVED, total, deterministic, preserves ALL simultaneous causes' (V1.8:100-101) — a min over a declared total order of a closed enum is total by construction | fallback: string + external executor (the present state: V1.8-VERIFY.py)" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart "self-issued qualification evidence (issuer = subject) is rejected at evidence intake by a typed condition under a typed hierarchy — pattern source/jws-authority.lisp:62-68 (jws-error > key-not-found / invalid-signature) — never silently downgraded; UNKNOWN on a mandatory dimension is NOT an error: it maps to that dimension's failure class as a VALUE (V1.8:409) | invariant: :self-qualification :rejected (V1.8:414); V8I-RASTATUS 'forbids self-qualification' (V1.8:102) | fallback: typed error value" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE" :protocol "RootAuthorityStatus/1 -> RelianceProjection/1 with :derived a CONSTANT true (V1.8:87 '(member :true)') — the projection is never stored truth; both types are model facts owned by S14 (interfaces-and-types.sexp:46,54); consumers read RelianceProjection only and the causes are preserved in blocking_dimensions/advisory_dimensions (V1.8:86-87) | invariant: RelianceProjection DERIVED, not stored (V1.8:84); preserve-causes | fallback: n/a (signature fixed by the two model types)" :package-asdf-boundary "S14 package as define-dimension-policy (subsystems.sexp:18 SEAT-CAPABILITY-API; TRACEABILITY:390 'provider_registry' NOT FOUND — CL-DDI3-A8); the fold and the policy live in ONE package so there is exactly one reader of the policy | invariant: contract:31; one seat | fallback: monolith package" :persistent-event "the projection is never journaled as truth; the stored status (with policy_epoch, measured_at, signature V1.8:82) and the per-dimension recovery events are (V1.8:101-102, journal.lisp:507); every projection carries as_of (V1.8:87) | invariant: :derived constant true (V1.8:87) | fallback: n/a" :truth-maintenance-dependency "NOT-APPLICABLE" :temporal-index-projection "as_of (V1.8:87) + measured_at + policy_epoch (V1.8:82) key every projection; policy epoch = invalidation epoch (contract:30) | invariant: deterministic per (status, policy epoch, as_of) | fallback: no cache" :compile-time-validation "the full 4^8 = 65,536 product (SUPERSEDED-REGISTER.md:286-287; V1.8-VERIFY.py:1233-1240) enumerated at model build as a `property-family` of EXACT cardinality 65536 (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:221-223) executed generically by BOTH verification paths — replacing the Python-only executor (V1.8-VERIFY.py:1222-1240, HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE files-and-roles.sexp:453; ADJ-V18-EXEC-1); the flags total/deterministic/preserve-causes are PROVED by the enumeration, not stored booleans compared as strings (V1.8-VERIFY.py:1203-1213 `!= 't'`) | invariant: :V8I-RASTATUS-product; V1.8:414 flags | fallback: runtime check" :runtime-validation "every DimensionState value in its closed enum (V1.8:75) and the status's policy_epoch matching the loaded policy, else a typed condition (capability-api.lisp:35 pattern) | invariant: L1; no silent reinterpretation | fallback: reject" :python-in-cl-risk "HIGHEST in the batch. The executable semantics ALREADY live in Python: V1.8-VERIFY.py:1222-1232 `project()` re-implements the rule, pinned to a byte-exact string (EXPECTED_AGG_RULE :548-549; :1200-1202). A naive CL import copies the string into a fact and re-implements the loop beside it — two seats plus a 'parsed-but-ignored' value (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:11-13 forbids that). CL-native alternative: structured `aggregation` + `aggregation-order` facts + ONE explicit fold in S14 (min over the declared ordinals across MANDATORY dimensions whose state is in the declared failing set, else FULL_RELIANCE); the formula string survives only as a `rationale` pointer; the exhaustive product is a generic property family, not a bespoke executor." :future-freedom "S04/S19/JTMS: NONE. S20 / V8I-02: NONE. Constraint: this is the third 'decision' dialect at source (ADJ-V18-AGG-2) — first-match ordered clauses (V1.5/V1.7) vs min-over-order; a single `decision` family cannot express both without a :kind discriminator, so the import must decide one family with kinds or two families (CL-DDI3-A9); method combination (contract:22) is NOT requested — an explicit fold is the ceiling here because the dimension set is closed (8), so there is no open method set to combine.")
