  :dependencies ("EXISTING type facts ×7 (interfaces-and-types.sexp:10,20,42,29,31,14,58) — 2 of them CANDIDATE_DEFINITION at source (JurisdictionNamespace/1 V1.8:452; ISR:173) yet unmarked canonical in the model (ISR dossier A8)" "EXISTING subsystem facts ×5 (subsystems.sexp:29,15,22,19,30)" "requirement facts RA8-EPOCH RA8-CONT RA8-CORR RA8-JURNS RA8-MARK RA8-K RA8-SIDE — NOT model facts (N1; TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:391-397)" "test facts T8-EPOCH T8-CONT T8-CORR T8-JURNS T8-MARK T8-K T8-SIDE — NOT model facts (PUBLIC-OBSERVATORY-QUALIFICATION-TESTS.md:1162-1163 predeclared UNEXECUTED)" "wp facts: WP-06 (:58), WP-12 (:63), WP-13 (:64), DEFERRED (:52) exist in requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp; 'FUTURE_BOOK' does not (ADJ-V18-WP-1)" "DDI-2 V1.8 define-record for the 7 seat types (V1.8:110,140,160,452,207,179,193) — structure, not a prerequisite for the binding (dag.json 7 refs)" "Decision ADJ-V18-DELTA-2 (type-as-seat vs artifact seat)")
  :consumers (":V8I-RA-DELTA-seats (V1.8:455-458, DDI-4) — 'Exactly SEVEN … Zero or multiple seats for any delta ⇒ failure'" "CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:54-85 (7 deltas in prose; :84-85 places RA-JUR-NS INSIDE CanonicalCitationURI/1 — contradicts row L448)" "TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:391-398 (8 RA8-* rows incl. RA8-FROST; balance :400 says 7)" "V1.8-VERIFY.py g_radeltas (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, files-and-roles.sexp:453)" "no canonical-model consumer (0 hits for RA8- / T8- ids in ARCHITECTURE-MODEL/*.sexp per dossier)")
  :identity-version-rule "ONLY-VERSION — unique to V1.8 (V1.7 has no delta-seat form; its RA layer is TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:344-366 + V1.7 capability seats). Ids: the :delta symbols (RA-EPOCH …) are TOKEN-legal; the anonymous form's class id must be synthesised (N11). Requirement ids RA8-* / tests T8-* exist only in prose."
  :migration-rule "BLOCKED-PENDING-DECISION — (a) N1 (RA8 / T8 universe); (b) seat kind (type vs artifact seat, ADJ-V18-DELTA-2); (c) 7 vs 8 deltas (ADJ-V18-DELTA-3); (d) RA-JUR-NS own seat vs dimension of CanonicalCitationURI/1 (ADJ-V18-DELTA-4); (e) RA-SIDE private seat (ADJ-V18-DELTA-5); (f) WP per delta (ADJ-V18-DELTA-6). Once decided: IMPORT-AS-CANONICAL (7 rows + 7 requirement + 7 test facts)."
  :conflict-duplicate-seat-risk "(1) `requirement` / `test` would gain a second origin beside the define-subsystem derivation (N1 / N8 — the same second-origin problem N2 names for wp); (2) RA-JUR-NS: own record JurisdictionNamespace/1 (V1.8:448,452) vs 'typed dimension carried by CanonicalCitationURI/1' (CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:84-85) — two seats for one delta; (3) TRACEABILITY:398 RA8-FROST (S10, CryptoSuiteRegistry/1 + RecoveryEpoch/1) as an 8th delta the form excludes; (4) TRACEABILITY's 'owner seat' column (canonical-uris.lisp, 'MLTP governance', boundary schemas, ai-citation-strategy.lisp, INTERFACE_ONLY, LAWMAX-LICENSE-POLICY.md; :391-397) names artefacts other than the model owner-seats."
  :requirement "NEW ×7: RA8-EPOCH RA8-CONT RA8-CORR RA8-JURNS RA8-K RA8-SIDE RA8-MARK (TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:391-397) — none a model fact; TRACEABILITY:394 cites invariant :V8I-JURNS-namespace which does not exist in V1.8 (ADJ-V18-INV-4)."
  :invariant "L6 (requirement→seat→test→WP closure; kernel law6-reqmap KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:256-266 also requires seat = owner-seat) + L3; source :V8I-RA-DELTA-seats (V1.8:455-458)."
  :qualification-test "NEW — T8-EPOCH / CONT / CORR / JURNS / K / SIDE / MARK predeclared UNEXECUTED (PUBLIC-OBSERVATORY-QUALIFICATION-TESTS.md:1162-1163; TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:391-397), none a model test fact. Executable statement: exactly 7 delta facts; each :seat-type resolves to a `type` whose :owner-subsystem equals :owner; each :requirement / :test / :wp resolves (L3); no two deltas share a seat type; a count ≠ 7 fails (V1.8:455-458)."
  :falsifier "APPEND `(fact delta RA-FROST :seat-type CryptoSuiteRegistry/1 :owner S10 :requirement RA8-FROST :test T8-FROST :wp WP-06)` (the TRACEABILITY:398 8th row) — must be rejected: kernel-reason 'delta count 8 ≠ 7' or 'resolves to no declared requirement' (L3). REPLACE `:owner S25` of RA-EPOCH with `:owner S13` — rejected 'seat type CanonicalCitationURI/1 is owned by S25, not S13' (owner / type agreement rule)."
  :rollback "Delete the imported facts and any new fact-type/field declaration from MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp (schema-version must move, X74-X76 verification-corpus.sexp:354-372); re-run build_root.py so ROOT.sexp pins the restored modules (L7); build_deferred.py regenerates the ledger row as DEFERRED_DATA_IMPORT :batch DDI-1. The source registry is never edited (authority stays AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE until the batch is independently reviewed, deferred-imports.sexp:73-76)."
  :batch-reason "DDI-1 by build_deferred.py:88 ('seats'). Prerequisite order AGREES (targets are existing types and subsystems); the entry criterion DISAGREES (N1: 0 of 7 requirement ids and 0 of 7 test ids exist; no WP in the form) — the requirement / test universe decision must precede or be part of DDI-1."
  :decision-kind "ARCHITECTURAL_DECISION_REQUIRED"
  :decision-question "(a) Where are RA8-* / T8-* seated (TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md is AUTHORED_NORMATIVE_PROSE, not a migration source — N1)? (b) Is a delta's seat the TYPE (V1.8:445-451) or the owner subsystem's artifact seat (as req-map / L6 require)? (c) Seven deltas (V1.8:455-458) or eight RA8 requirements (TRACEABILITY:391-398)? (d) May RA-SIDE have its one canonical seat in a PRIVATE type / subsystem? (e) Which WP closes each delta? (f) RA-JUR-NS: own record (V1.8:448,452) or dimension of CanonicalCitationURI/1 (CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:84-85)?"
  :adjudication-items ("ADJ-V18-DELTA-1 (= N1)" "ADJ-V18-DELTA-2" "ADJ-V18-DELTA-3 / ADJ-V18-INV-4" "ADJ-V18-DELTA-4 / ADJ-V18-REC-6" "ADJ-V18-DELTA-5" "ADJ-V18-DELTA-6 / ADJ-V18-WP-1" "A8 (ISR dossier): JurisdictionNamespace/1 and SidecarSourceProfile/1 are CANDIDATE_DEFINITION contracts unmarked in the model")
  :topological-position 54 :atomic-groups (7)
  :cl-native (:immutable-record "NOT-APPLICABLE" :clos-class "NOT-APPLICABLE" :generic-function "NOT-APPLICABLE" :condition-restart "L6 closure failure (a requirement with zero or multiple seats / no test / no WP) is a kernel-law violation → typed; no restart | invariant: L6 requirement→seat→test→WP (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:176-181); :V8I-RA-DELTA-seats 'Zero or multiple seats for any delta ⇒ failure' (V1.8:455-458) | fallback: typed error value" :macro-dsl "NOT-APPLICABLE" :protocol "NOT-APPLICABLE" :package-asdf-boundary "A delta's home is the PACKAGE/SEAT of its owner subsystem, not a type: RA-EPOCH/RA-JUR-NS/RA-MARK → S25 SEAT-CANONICAL-URIS (seats.sexp:62; :orchestrator.uris canonical-uris.lisp:12); RA-K → S15 SEAT-CITATION-AUTHORITY (seats.sexp:52); RA-CORR → S18 SEAT-BOUNDARY-SHAPES DOCUMENT_SEAT (seats.sexp:73); RA-CONT → S11 SEAT-SECURITY-CELLS DESIGN_TARGET (seats.sexp:79, no path allowed MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:297-298); RA-SIDE → S26 SEAT-TENANT-PROFILE INTERFACE_ONLY (seats.sexp:97) — i.e. RA-SIDE has NO public package by construction (its seat type SidecarSourceProfile/1 is PRIVATE interfaces-and-types.sexp:58) | invariant: L5 (public/private isolation); :V8I-PUBPRIV-all-families; seats.sexp:15-19 (design targets/interface-only never dressed as files) | fallback: monolith" :persistent-event "RA-CORR's seat PublicCorrectionEvent/1 (V1.8:447) is an EVENT record: appended and hash-chained (journal.lisp:507 chained-append), carrying no re-published content (deployment/LAWMAX-THREAT-MODEL.md:101-102 'no re-published content and no PII') | invariant: :V8I-CORR-privacy (V1.8:168) | fallback: full replay" :truth-maintenance-dependency "RA-CORR: a public correction RETRACTS a previously published belief and every conclusion that depended on it — JTMS retraction (legal-inference-engine.lisp:395 tms-retract-premise; :347 recompute-beliefs, well-founded) rather than an ad-hoc republish | invariant: contract L28 'belief revision is monotone-audited'; :V8I-CORR-privacy | fallback: full recompute" :temporal-index-projection "RA-EPOCH (CanonicalCitationURI/1 + MultiCommitment/1 + ReAnchoringManifest/1, V1.8:445; TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:391) is an EPOCH-indexed identity: any cached derivation over a citation names its epoch and is invalidated on re-anchoring (contract L30 'a cache entry names its validation epoch; epoch change invalidates') — the contract's epoch seat (shacl-validator.lisp / mltp3:ontology-bundle) is NOT FOUND by grep ('epoch' 0 hits in shacl-validator.lisp; 'ontology-bundle' 0 hits in source/) | invariant: :V8I-EPOCH-one-expression (V1.8:128) | fallback: no cache" :compile-time-validation "L6 closure at kernel-law time requires facts that do not exist: 7 `requirement` (RA8-*) + 7 `test` (T8-*) — none in requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:5-50 (N1) — and a `wp` per row, absent from the form (V1.8:445-451 has no :wp; TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:391-397 supplies FUTURE_BOOK×3 / WP-06 / WP-12 / WP-13 / DEFERRED, and FUTURE_BOOK is not a `wp` fact: only FUTURE_BOOK_REVISION requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:53); also :seat is a TYPE while req-map :seat is a `seat` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:178-181) — a type-seat notion or a mapping to the owner seat is a schema decision (ADJ-V18-DELTA-2) | invariant: L6; :V8I-RA-DELTA-seats | fallback: n/a — cannot close today" :runtime-validation "NOT-APPLICABLE" :python-in-cl-risk "MEDIUM. Naive import yields 7 dict rows from an anonymous nested form (N11: id must be synthesised) with :seat kept as a string because it is a type, not an artifact seat. CL-native alternative: pure traceability facts — either req-map rows (:seat = owner subsystem's `seat`, plus a new optional :type L3 ref) or a `delta` fact type (:seat-type→type :owner→subsystem :requirement :test :wp) — nothing imperative; the only 'code' is the kernel's L6 closure. The tempting shortcut (a string :seat 'CanonicalCitationURI/1') is exactly the 'arbitrary string is not a seat' error (V1.7:354)." :future-freedom "CONDITIONAL. RA-SIDE is seated in a PRIVATE type owned by PRIVATE S26 with TRACEABILITY wp 'DEFERRED' (V1.8:451; TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:396) — a root-authority delta of the PUBLIC candidate whose one canonical seat lies outside the public build (ADJ-V18-DELTA-5); in package terms it has no public package, so the public build cannot even name it without a declassification edge. RA-CORR/RA-EPOCH pull in JTMS retraction and epoch invalidation — these are freedoms the contract already reserves (L28, L30), not constraints. Seven-vs-eight (RA8-FROST, TRACEABILITY-MATRIX.md:398 vs :V8I-RA-DELTA-seats) and RA-JUR-NS own-seat vs 'typed dimension of CanonicalCitationURI/1' (ADJ-V18-DELTA-3/4) are adjudications, not CL questions. No S04/S19/S20/LLM constraint.")
  )

