(adjudication ADJ-110 :class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-reference :item "ADJ-DDI2-IDENTITY-FAMILY: four classes carry the SAME payload (identity + version + canonical pointer) under three key vocabularies — V1.6 define-reference :canonical/:identity/:version/:owner-wp (V1.6:92-150), V1.7 define-reference :canonical/:identity/:version (V1.7:34-39,257-258), V1.8 define-reference :canonical-file/:identity/:version/:locator (V1.8:107,345-352) and V1.8 define-canonical-identity (V1.8:425-432, batch DDI-1, deferred-imports.sexp:59). ONE fact family must be decided in DDI-1 before any of the three DDI-2 reference classes can be imported.")
(adjudication ADJ-111 :class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-reference :item "A2 (V1.6 dossier): LegalIR/1 canonical pointer — V1.6:97 + ISR:15 name legal-ast.lisp AND the contract .md; V1.8:345 names the .md alone.")
(adjudication ADJ-112 :class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-reference :item "A3 (V1.6 dossier): DeclassificationReceipt/1 has no structure seat anywhere; V1.8:349 references the V1.6 reference block (reference-to-a-reference) and V1.8:274 derives edges from fields that exist only in a :note string.")
(adjudication ADJ-113 :class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-reference :item "A4 (V1.6 dossier): CandidateInterpretation/1 and ActionIntent/1 point at identifiers (neural-candidate/1, cockpit_intent) absent from all tracked Lisp.")
(adjudication ADJ-114 :class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-reference :item "U1 (V1.6 dossier): the '(L12)' locator in Approval/1 :canonical (V1.6:132; ISR:27) is unresolved — release-authority.lisp line 12 is header prose.")
(adjudication ADJ-115 :class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-reference :item "ADJ-DDI2-OWNER-WP-VS-REQMAP: a type's :owner-wp (V1.6:95,99,130,134,146,150) and its owner subsystem's req-map :wp (requirements-tests-workpackets.sexp:67-95) are two independent WP bindings with no reconciliation rule.")
(adjudication ADJ-116 :class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-mapping :item "A13 (V1.6 dossier): id charset violation, composite string seats, field/invariant used as seats, and 9 mapped files with no seat fact — one adjudication with four limbs, all cited above.")
(adjudication ADJ-117 :class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-mapping :item "ADJ-DDI2-CAPABILITY-SPLIT: cognition capabilities (V1.6, DDI-2) and RA capabilities (V1.7/V1.8, DDI-1) are the same concept in two batches; one family, one batch, or an explicit reason for two.")
(adjudication ADJ-118 :class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-mapping :item "A14 (V1.6 dossier): the casegrammar split is declared twice — V1.6:247 define-rule and SUBSYSTEM-REGISTRY.sexp:130-134 define-file-disposition (both DDI-4); the map depends on whichever wins.")
(adjudication ADJ-119 :class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-mapping :item "U4 (V1.6 dossier): source/legal-casegrammar.lisp carries no [general]/[private] marker, so 'legal-casegrammar.lisp[general]' is a seat that cannot be located in the artifact it names.")
(adjudication ADJ-120 :class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-ref-classification-v6 :item "A12 (V1.6 dossier): the form names SignedPublicRelease, ProofCarryingInterface, SensorAdapter, EmbodimentAdapter and ActuatorCapability, which are defined in NO registry; and it is superseded by two DDI-1 classes — successors import before the predecessor.")
(adjudication ADJ-121 :class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-ref-classification-v6 :item "N11 (orchestrator): anonymous form — its identity is the (file, head) pair only; the id-synthesis convention is a schema-level decision shared with 6 other anonymous forms.")
(adjudication ADJ-122 :class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-ref-classification-v6 :item "ADJ-DDI2-ROOTS-VS-L5: the model's public/private law is per-`consumes`-edge (KERNEL/model-law-kernel.lisp:243-254); a `closure-root` family would be a second, root-based statement of the same boundary. Which is authoritative?")
(adjudication ADJ-123 :class V1.6-SCHEMAS__define-ref-classification-v6 :item "N17 (orchestrator), inherited: RAT-PUBPRIV (rationale-references.sexp:7) is the declared rationale of every private seat and its :anchor string does not occur in deployment/LAWMAX-THREAT-MODEL.md — the boundary's stated justification is a dangling anchor no counted check opens.")
(adjudication ADJ-124 :class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum :item "ADJ-DDI2-ENUM-SEAT: the four DDI-2 enum classes (V1.5 16 enums/83 values, V1.6 8/71, V1.7 8/61, V1.8 9/37 — my own reader over the six registries) must share ONE module (one seat per concept); the dossiers disagree — V1.5/V1.6 propose interfaces-and-types.sexp, V1.7/V1.8 propose a NEW 'enums' module. No winner is picked here.")
(adjudication ADJ-125 :class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum :item "ADJ-V17-ENUM-1 (V1.7 dossier): CognitionError (V1.6:177, bound by CognitionResult/1.errors V1.6:207) vs CognitionErrorV7 (V1.7:40, bound by nothing).")
(adjudication ADJ-126 :class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum :item "ADJ-V17-ENUM-2 (V1.7 dossier): PublicMemoryScope/MemoryScope (V1.6:282,288) vs MemoryScopeV7 (V1.7:105, replacement declared only in the comment at V1.7:104) while MemoryEvent/1 and MemoryProjection/1 are not re-typed.")
(adjudication ADJ-127 :class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum :item "ADJ-V17-ENUM-3 (V1.7 dossier): RootAuthorityState (scalar, V1.7:241) vs DimensionState x RelianceClass (V1.8:75,83, DFT-10) — retire or keep as a projection domain?")
(adjudication ADJ-128 :class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum :item "ADJ-DDI2-ENUM-OWNER: no V1.7 enum declares an owner; if `enum` mirrors `type` (:owner-subsystem required, MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:148-152) the class is unimportable as-is.")
(adjudication ADJ-129 :class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum :item "ADJ-DDI2-PRIVATE-ENUM (shared): MemoryScopeV7's :USER_PRIVATE/:SERVICE_INTERNAL members sit inside an enum used by a public memory policy, against :V7I-PUBPRIV-acyclic (V1.7:297-299), and the model has no law that can see it.")
(adjudication ADJ-130 :class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-record :item "ADJ-DDI2-FIELD-SEAT: the four DDI-2 record classes (V1.5 18/181 fields, V1.6 22/190, V1.7 25/227, V1.8 19/179 — my own count) must share ONE `field` seat; the dossiers propose interfaces-and-types.sexp (V1.5/V1.6) vs a NEW module 'record-fields'/'schemas' (V1.7/V1.8). No winner is picked here.")
(adjudication ADJ-131 :class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-record :item "ADJ-V17-REC-1 (V1.7 dossier): 11 V1.7 records are absent from ISR although :ISR-V6-closure (ISR:177-180) demands definition there exactly once with an owner, and V1.8 binds 8 of them as cognition node types.")
(adjudication ADJ-132 :class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-record :item "ADJ-V17-REC-2 / ADJ-V18-REC-1: ClarifiedInterpretation/1 defined twice with the same version and different fields (V1.7:75 vs V1.8:40).")
(adjudication ADJ-133 :class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-record :item "ADJ-V17-REC-3 / ADJ-V18-REC-2: CitationSupremacyMetric/1 vs CitationMetricV8/1 and RootAuthorityQualification/1 vs RootAuthorityStatus/1 — both members of each pair are live model types and live ISR rows.")
