(adjudication ADJ-135 :class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-record :item "ADJ-V17-REC-5 / A20: the field-type vocabulary (id semver ref sha256 sig instant uncertainty keyword url text mime span usc-id anchor scope duration) has NO definition seat in any registry — a `field :domain` cannot be L3-closed until a primitive seat exists.")
(adjudication ADJ-136 :class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-record :item "ADJ-DDI2-CITATIONPANEL: CitationPanel/1 is referenced by V1.7:193 and V1.8:180 but defined only at V1.7:188 and registered in no registry — referenced-but-undefined, which ISR:177-180 calls an architecture-gate FAIL.")
(adjudication ADJ-137 :class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-record :item "ADJ-DDI2-INLINE-MEMBER: 18 inline (member ...) sets in this class alone (7 of them in TenantProfile/1, V1.7:227-239) need a single encoding rule — anonymous enum ids or STRING literals — decided once for all four record classes.")
(adjudication ADJ-138 :class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-reference :item "ADJ-DDI2-IDENTITY-FAMILY: four classes carry the SAME payload (identity + version + canonical pointer) under three key vocabularies — V1.6 define-reference :canonical/:identity/:version/:owner-wp (V1.6:92-150), V1.7 define-reference :canonical/:identity/:version (V1.7:34-39,257-258), V1.8 define-reference :canonical-file/:identity/:version/:locator (V1.8:107,345-352) and V1.8 define-canonical-identity (V1.8:425-432, batch DDI-1, deferred-imports.sexp:59). ONE fact family must be decided in DDI-1 before any of the three DDI-2 reference classes can be imported.")
(adjudication ADJ-139 :class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-reference :item "ADJ-V17-REF-1 (V1.7 dossier): MorphLattice/1, PackedParseForest/1, DiscourseState/1 and PromotionEvidence/1 are referenced by V1.7 and V1.8 cognition graphs but absent from ISR (violating :ISR-V6-closure ISR:177-180) and from the model; `type` requires :owner-subsystem (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:148-152).")
(adjudication ADJ-140 :class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-reference :item "ADJ-V17-REF-2 (V1.7 dossier): CognitionResult/1 is referenced at V1.7:39 (prose canonical) and V1.8:348 (canonical-file + locator, audit-opened by :V8I-XREF-real) — is V1.7:39 retired?")
(adjudication ADJ-141 :class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-reference :item "ADJ-DDI2-ENUM-SUBJECT: two of the eight references have an ENUM as subject (V1.7:257,258); the V1.8 identity shape names a type. Widen the family or refuse the two forms.")
(adjudication ADJ-142 :class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-reference :item "ADJ-DDI2-STALE-ANCHOR (shared with V1.8 define-reference ADJ-V18-REF-2): all 8 :canonical values point into V1.5/V1.6-SCHEMAS.sexp, which files-and-roles.sexp:441,447 classify CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT and which DDI-2 imports — the anchors become stale by construction.")
(adjudication ADJ-143 :class V1.7-SCHEMAS__define-reference :item "UNKNOWN: census_coverage_state's locator 'V1.5-SCHEMAS.sexp:184' names a line INSIDE the form (the :members line) rather than the form head at V1.5:182 — a line-number anchor with no stability guarantee.")
(adjudication ADJ-144 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum :item "ADJ-DDI2-ENUM-SEAT: the four DDI-2 enum classes (V1.5 16 enums/83 values, V1.6 8/71, V1.7 8/61, V1.8 9/37 — my own reader over the six registries) must share ONE module (one seat per concept); the dossiers disagree — V1.5/V1.6 propose interfaces-and-types.sexp, V1.7/V1.8 propose a NEW 'enums' module. No winner is picked here.")
(adjudication ADJ-145 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum :item "ADJ-V18-ENUM-1 (V1.8 dossier): ClarificationLifecycleState (V1.8:28) and ContinuityRole (V1.8:139) are used by no record field in any registry — orphan enums.")
(adjudication ADJ-146 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum :item "ADJ-V18-ENUM-2 (V1.8 dossier): three seats for clarification state across registries (V1.6:200 ClarificationState/1.status, V1.7:40-43 CognitionErrorV7, V1.8:28 ClarificationLifecycleState) — none declares supersession.")
(adjudication ADJ-147 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum :item "ADJ-DDI2-INLINE-MEMBER (shared): MergeSemanticsV8 is the precedent that an inline (member ...) set becomes a named enum (V1.7:78 -> V1.8:31); the encoding rule for the other 53 inline sets across the four record classes must follow it or declare why not.")
(adjudication ADJ-148 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum :item "ADJ-DDI2-ENUM-OWNER (shared with V1.7): no V1.8 enum declares an owner; a required :owner-subsystem would block the class.")
(adjudication ADJ-149 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-closed-enum :item "ADJ-DDI2-RESTRICTED-VALUE: MetricAssuranceClass :INDEPENDENTLY_AUDITED_RESTRICTED and ReproTier :T3_SEALED_RESTRICTED name a RESTRICTED handling class that the model's two-valued `classification` enum (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:47) cannot express; ISR uses :RESTRICTED as a classification (ISR:151,159) and build_model.py maps it to PRIVATE.")
(adjudication ADJ-150 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-record :item "ADJ-DDI2-FIELD-SEAT: the four DDI-2 record classes (V1.5 18/181 fields, V1.6 22/190, V1.7 25/227, V1.8 19/179 — my own count) must share ONE `field` seat; the dossiers propose interfaces-and-types.sexp (V1.5/V1.6) vs a NEW module 'record-fields'/'schemas' (V1.7/V1.8). No winner is picked here.")
(adjudication ADJ-151 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-record :item "ADJ-V18-REC-1 (V1.8 dossier): ClarifiedInterpretation/1 defined twice with the same version and different fields (V1.7:75 vs V1.8:40); both DDI-2 AUTHORITATIVE_AT_SOURCE; ISR:117 points at V1.8.")
(adjudication ADJ-152 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-record :item "ADJ-V18-REC-2 (V1.8 dossier): predecessor types stay canonical beside their v1.8 successors — RootAuthorityQualification/1 (interfaces-and-types.sexp:53) vs RootAuthorityStatus/1 (:54, ISR:112 names v1.7 as rollback); CitationSupremacyMetric/1 (:15) vs CitationMetricV8/1 (:14).")
