(adjudication ADJ-154 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-record :item "ADJ-V18-REC-4 (V1.8 dossier): status vocabulary — :DEFERRED_PRIVATE / :SPECIFICATION_ONLY / CANDIDATE_DEFINITION / :RESTRICTED / INTERFACE_ONLY across V1.8, ISR and TRACEABILITY-MATRIX; MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:62 knows six seat statuses and none of SPECIFICATION_ONLY/CANDIDATE_DEFINITION.")
(adjudication ADJ-155 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-record :item "ADJ-V18-REC-5 (V1.8 dossier): CryptoSuiteRegistry/1 / RecoveryEpoch/1 vs MACHINE-LEGAL-TRUST-PROTOCOL.md §14.1/§14.2 (:1349, :1360-1368) — EXTEND or second seat; ownership S10 vs S11 vs the MLTP root.")
(adjudication ADJ-156 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-record :item "ADJ-V18-REC-6 (V1.8 dossier): RA-JUR-NS seat — own record (V1.8:448,452; ISR:173) vs a dimension of CanonicalCitationURI/1 (CHANGE-PROPOSAL-v1.8.md:83-85).")
(adjudication ADJ-157 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-record :item "ADJ-V18-REC-7 (V1.8 dossier): ISR :future-wp FUTURE_IMPLEMENTATION_BOOK_PACKET_REQUIRED (ISR:112,115,129,138,142,145,160,164,175) is not a model `wp` — req-map rows for these types cannot be written until the WP token vocabulary is unified.")
(adjudication ADJ-158 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-record :item "ADJ-DDI2-CONSTANT-MEMBER: 17 inline (member ...) sets in this class, several of them one-value constants used as guarantees (V1.8:86 ':derived :type (member :true)', EmergencyFreeze/1 x3, PublicCorrectionEvent/1 x4). A constant-true guarantee encoded as a string is unfalsifiable; encoded as a one-value domain it is checkable. The encoding rule decides which.")
(adjudication ADJ-159 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-record :item "UNKNOWN/count divergence: the V1.8 dossier states 146 fields for this class; my own reader counts 179 over the same 19 records. The importer must re-count rather than trust either figure.")
(adjudication ADJ-160 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-reference :item "ADJ-DDI2-IDENTITY-FAMILY: four classes carry the SAME payload (identity + version + canonical pointer) under three key vocabularies — V1.6 define-reference :canonical/:identity/:version/:owner-wp (V1.6:92-150), V1.7 define-reference :canonical/:identity/:version (V1.7:34-39,257-258), V1.8 define-reference :canonical-file/:identity/:version/:locator (V1.8:107,345-352) and V1.8 define-canonical-identity (V1.8:425-432, batch DDI-1, deferred-imports.sexp:59). ONE fact family must be decided in DDI-1 before any of the three DDI-2 reference classes can be imported.")
(adjudication ADJ-161 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-reference :item "ADJ-V18-REF-1 (V1.8 dossier): identity seats compete — LegalIR/1 (V1.6:96 vs V1.8:345 vs V1.8:425), TrustBundle/1 (V1.6:143 vs V1.8:346 vs V1.8:426), CognitionResult/1 (V1.7:39 vs V1.8:348 vs V1.8:428), DeclassificationReceipt/1 (V1.6:147 vs V1.8:349 vs V1.8:427).")
(adjudication ADJ-162 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-reference :item "ADJ-V18-REF-2 (V1.8 dossier): five references anchor their canonical file INSIDE migration sources (files-and-roles.sexp:441,447 CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT) that DDI-2 imports — the pointer must move or become stale.")
(adjudication ADJ-163 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-reference :item "ADJ-V18-REF-3 (V1.8 dossier): RightsMatrix/1 has two document anchors (V1.7:126 via V1.8:352; LAWMAX-LICENSE-POLICY.md:44 via V1.8:248 and ISR:87).")
(adjudication ADJ-164 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-reference :item "ADJ-DDI2-USC-SUBJECT: USC-expression's subject is a document level, not a type; the identity family as shaped by V1.8:425-432 cannot name it. Widen the family or seat it in `rationale` (MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:182-184).")
(adjudication ADJ-165 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-reference :item "ADJ-DDI2-ANCHOR-CHECK: :V8I-XREF-real (V1.8:353-357) demands a check that opens the canonical file and finds the locator; no such check exists on either path, and the same absence lets the live RAT-PUBPRIV dangling anchor stand (rationale-references.sexp:7; orchestrator-notes.md N17).")
(adjudication ADJ-166 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-cardinality-table :item "ADJ-V18-CARD-1 (V1.8 dossier): two cardinality dialects are both DDI-2 — V1.5:45-62 define-cardinality-matrix (deferred-imports.sexp:15) and V1.8:394-397 define-cardinality-table (deferred-imports.sexp:56); one fact family must express both or two families coexist.")
(adjudication ADJ-167 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-cardinality-table :item "ADJ-V18-CARD-2 (V1.8 dossier): column -> field binding is by name convention (V1.8:43-45); the legacy guard hard-codes it (V1.8-VERIFY.py:1058-1065). An import must make it typed or import a convention as a reference.")
(adjudication ADJ-168 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-cardinality-table :item "ADJ-V18-CARD-3 (V1.8 dossier), cross-ref ADJ-V18-REC-1: the table requires selected_alternative_ref nullable, which V1.7:77 forbids — the table can only be true of the V1.8 record, so importing it PRESUPPOSES the ClarifiedInterpretation/1 decision.")
(adjudication ADJ-169 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-cardinality-table :item "ADJ-V18-EXEC-1 (V1.8 dossier, shared with define-fixtures / define-reliance-aggregation / define-dimension-policy / define-cognition-node-types): the only program that executes this EXEC-MODEL contract is V1.8-VERIFY.py (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, files-and-roles.sexp:453; LEGACY-AUDIT-DISPOSITION.md:1-6 'never a blocking or sufficient acceptance gate'); the model's harnesses execute model laws only (verification-corpus.sexp:122-125). Which harness executes imported EXEC-MODEL contracts, or are they inert data?")
(adjudication ADJ-170 :class V1.8-SCHEMAS__define-cardinality-table :item "ADJ-DDI2-RULE-RESTATEMENT: the same rule is stated by the table (V1.8:394-397), the invariant (:47-51) and the record comments (:43-44); DDI-4's invariant import must cite the table rather than restate it, or the model gains a second seat for one rule.")
(adjudication ADJ-171 :class V1.5-SCHEMAS__define-decision-function :item "V5-A2 (superseded decision kept live: SR:36 names V1.5 id; V1.7:260 supersedes)")
(adjudication ADJ-172 :class V1.5-SCHEMAS__define-decision-function :item "V5-A3 / ADJ-V17-DF-2 (V1.7:274 :VALID_AUTHORITATIVE_FRESH is a member of no enum)")
(adjudication ADJ-173 :class V1.5-SCHEMAS__define-decision-function :item "ADJ-V17-DF-1 (canonical coverage decision = V1.5:229 or V1.7:259)")
(adjudication ADJ-174 :class V1.5-SCHEMAS__define-decision-function :item "V5-A15 (V5R-*/V5Q-* universe not in model — L6 for every V1.5 fact)")
(adjudication ADJ-175 :class V1.5-SCHEMAS__define-decision-function :item "ADJ-V18-AGG-2 (one fact family for all three DDI-3 decision dialects: V1.5/V1.7 define-decision-function vs V1.8 define-reliance-aggregation)")
(adjudication ADJ-176 :class V1.5-SCHEMAS__define-decision-function :item "ADJ-DDI3-INPUT-1: the 8 decision inputs (V1.5:230) bind to enums only by naming convention (V1.5 dossier unknown #5) — a `decision-input :enum` declaration must be authored, by whom?")
(adjudication ADJ-177 :class V1.5-SCHEMAS__define-decision-function :item "ADJ-DDI3-MOD-1: module NAME for the DDI-3 function layer is stated three ways by the dossiers — 'decisions-and-projections.sexp' (V1.5 dossier) vs 'decision-functions' (V1.7 and V1.8 dossiers) vs 'cognition-graph' (V1.8 dossier, for the graph) — one name per module must be fixed once; every NEW module is auto-classified CANONICAL_MODEL_INPUT by AM/classification-rules.sexp:39-41 (R-008) and must be pinned in AM/ROOT.sexp:12-28 (:module-count 14 today) under L7.")
(adjudication ADJ-178 :class V1.5-SCHEMAS__define-decision-function :item "ADJ-DDI3-ENUM-1: no enum / enum-value fact family exists in AM/MODEL-SCHEMA.sexp:84-288 (34 fact types); every DDI-3 clause value, :output, :failure, :order and :result-when-insufficient is an enum member of a DDI-2 define-closed-enum / define-frozen-enum-reference form. Until DDI-2 seats enums as facts, DDI-3 values can only be bare SYMBOLs with no L3 closure (KERNEL:196-210 checks :ref targets only).")
(adjudication ADJ-179 :class V1.5-SCHEMAS__define-decision-function :item "ADJ-DDI3-EXEC-1 (= dossier ADJ-V18-EXEC-1, widened to every DDI-3 class): the only program that has ever executed a DDI-3 contract is V1.8-VERIFY.py / V1.5-CONTRADICTION-OMISSION-AUDIT.sh (HISTORICAL_EVIDENCE, AM/files-and-roles.sexp:436,453; AM/LEGACY-AUDIT-DISPOSITION.md:10 'never a blocking or sufficient acceptance gate'); the model's harness universe executes laws L1-L7 only (AM/verification-corpus.sexp:24-58,122-125; KERNEL:346). Which harness (existing COMPONENT harness with new schema-derived checks, or a NEW harness fact) executes imported decision/graph contracts, or are they imported as inert data with a declared reason?")
(adjudication ADJ-180 :class V1.5-SCHEMAS__define-algorithm :item "ADJ-DDI3-OWN-1: owner of control-domain-partition — S10 (V1.5:263 MLTP §10; ISR:63) vs S11 (SR:68-70) — no registry states it (V1.5 dossier unknown)")
